:: Quaver Wants a Band {"position":"2700,1550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): These halls deserve a darker sound tonight,
Four stolen instruments should set them right.
START LOG: He raised these halls from centuries of silence, stone, and spite,
Now music ought to sharpen every shadowed feast at night.
Four instruments will found a proper courtly band for him,
Each voice must serve his iron hand when halls grow dim.

A drum may thunder while the strings hiss sharp and low,
A pipe may mock the final breath of every foe.
Bring four unlike, let every stolen timbre earn its place,
Then Quaver judges which deserve to serve his darker grace.

His Tower needs more music than Brown claws on stone,
A proper doom should march in rhythm from his throne.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Bring four distinct instruments for his hall,
Let each have different voice when shadows fall.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Four voices rise; the hall has learned a tune,
But seven more must join the racket soon.
COMPLETION LOG: Four instruments now answer loudly when he crosses through the hall,
A modest storm of menace rises gladly at his call.
The drums can bite, the strings can scrape and sneer in tune,
Enough to make approaching fools regret arriving much too soon.

Yet four alone make only half the boast he deserves,
A tyrant's court requires more noise from trembling lesser nerves.
Eleven instruments will make the full collection sing,
Each different voice conscripted gladly for one darker king.

He built the Tower; Quaver builds the proper sound around,
Bring seven more, and let these waiting stone walls resound.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/quaver_wants_a_band · working title "A Band for the Dark Tower" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 100.47

[[Eleven Instruments. Why.]]

Quaver Request


:: Nobody Mapped This {"position":"3500,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): A castle off every map, Sire! Imperial hypocrisy came with battlements.
START LOG: Now this is delicious, Master! The Empire's own maps forgot a castle. Hard to misplace, really. Its noble court hid the place with enchantment. Yes, enchantment, Sire, while those fine people publicly feared magic! Privately, magic was splendid when consequences knocked outside. Solarius always kept standards for somebody else. Explore the castle and see what survived. Three centuries of hiding rarely improve courtly manners. They certainly do not improve claims to treasure. If the old nobles still object, remind them history has already overruled their appeal... rather thoroughly!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Explore the concealed castle and find what remains inside.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): The court survived, after a fashion! Hypocrisy preserves wonderfully.
COMPLETION LOG: Oh, this is excellent, Sire! Forbidden magic hid them perfectly. The court condemned enchantment, then wrapped itself in it. Their nobles and retainers still infest these halls. Undead, raiders, squatters, all wearing Imperial leftovers! They hid from enemies and vanished from allies. Yet somehow the privilege survived! Clear them out, Master. A secret castle is wasted on creatures this irrelevant! Their greatest victory was avoiding history long enough to become clutter. You are very good at removing clutter. Once the Lost Court stops objecting, we can inspect what its principles were really protecting.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/nobody_mapped_this · working title "A Castle Off the Map" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 502.20

[[Courtiers, Long Dead]]

Lost Castle Found


:: Just a Collar Now {"position":"4100,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): A collar remains. Its bearer does not. Death visited, Sire.
START LOG: A collar. No companion. Keep it, Sire. Service leaves an imprint. Flesh fails. Bonds may persist. I keep such records. The grave keeps others. This one still carries weight. Not every death should reverse. Not every bond should fade. Read what remains. Judge the thread, not grief alone. Death is no insult. Memory is no resurrection. Yet memory can guide a rite. A path may still exist. Walk it only with purpose. The dead deserve precision.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Keep the collar, Sire. Learn what still answers.
EMOTION (complete): Stricken
POPUP (complete): The bond persists. A road may remain.
COMPLETION LOG: The collar still answers, Sire. That matters. Memory clings to service. Service clings to form. A rite can follow that thread. The return may be imperfect. The body may change. The bond may not. Do not confuse possibility with permission. Choose with care. I tend graves, not fantasies. Yet a true bond deserves hearing. If work remains, call once. If nothing answers, close the grave. Balance first. Sentiment second. Service always.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/just_a_collar_now · working title "A Collar Left Behind" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O2 NW_B TOUR.GRAVE3

[[Not Quite Dead, Fido]]

Pet died


:: Finally, a Proper Horde {"position":"1600,2800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Look at them, Master! Four tribes and one wonderfully noisy Horde.
START LOG: Look at them, Sire! Browns, Reds, Greens, and Blues are awake and pointed roughly the same way. The Exodus scattered the Hives, Master, and the Silence left three tribes sleeping. Browns alone waited on, gnawing furniture and preserving tradition. Now muscle, flame, knives, and healing answer one Master again! Minions are your deadliest weapons, my Lord, especially in large and badly supervised groups. Take a moment and admire the muster. They certainly admire themselves! Oh, listen to that racket, Sire... the old Horde has found its voice again!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read this muster, Sire. The Horde deserves one moment of admiration.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): A proper Horde at last, Master! Silence has lost.
COMPLETION LOG: A proper Horde at last, Master! Browns bash, Reds burn, Greens stab, and Blues return the fallen to service. The old fourfold rhythm beats beneath the fifth Overlord, Sire! The Netherworld is noisy with it again, which is exactly as it should be. They will squabble, steal, boast, and occasionally ignite one another. Point them toward your enemies, my Lord, and priorities become wonderfully clear! This is your Horde, Sire, your fists, flames, knives, and second chances. Enjoy the noise! Silence had the Tower long enough. Perhaps keep a few alive until supper.
CODER NOTES: overlord:prologue_and_horde/finally_a_proper_horde · working title "A Complete Horde" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 205.30

Complete Horde Entry


:: Feed the Cradle {"position":"2300,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): A heart needs somewhere to matter, Sire. Give the flesh a cradle!
START LOG: A core by itself is merely an organ looking important, Sire! Set a primordial cradle in the chamber and give living matter somewhere to gather, feed, and develop. The word "cradle" sounds embarrassingly tender. "Flesh trough" tested poorly with visitors. Once established, it can support growth ordinary workshops would reject as unhygienic. Imagine their lack of vision! They also lack drains, which matters more than one expects. Give the core somewhere to work, Master. Let us see what begins pulsing! If the furniture starts breathing, my Lord, we shall call that progress!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Set a primordial cradle in the chamber, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There it goes, Master... pulsing. Charming, in a damp sort of way.
COMPLETION LOG: The cradle pulses, Sire! Feed it properly and living materials can grow into forms worth using. That is where biomancy becomes more interesting than butchery. Any fool can cut flesh apart! It takes study to make flesh remain useful afterward! Keep the chamber supplied, and keep curious Browns from poking anything moist. If the cradle develops teeth, tell me before Gristle names it. He has a distressing habit of seeing dinner where I see research. Master, we are building a laboratory, not a stew with architectural ambitions! Standards must survive somewhere!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/feed_the_cradle · working title "A Cradle for Flesh" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 Wastelands 130.30

[[It Twitched!]]


:: Dead Dragons Don't Fly {"position":"2200,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): A dead dragon flying? Oh, that is untidy, Sire!
START LOG: Ashlord was dead, Sire! Properly, usefully, reassuringly dead! Yet something hauled the carcass upright and taught it wings again. That reeks of old Cataclysm magic, not ordinary necromancy. I remember the ruin left by that disaster... unpleasantly well. Search the creature's tower, Master. Look for carvings, offerings, armour, anything left by worshippers. Dead monsters rarely keep records! Their admirers keep absolutely everything! What devotion. If someone prepared Ashlord for this return, they left marks behind. Find them, and perhaps we learn who wanted a corpse airborne.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter Ashlord's tower, Sire, and investigate the raised dragon.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): There! I know that mark. The Kindred were here, Sire.
COMPLETION LOG: The skull carries the Kindred mark, Master! A Minion cult, and an old embarrassment. They worshipped the extinct Dragon-Kin and tried restoring them themselves. Sensible Minions stopped at stealing, burning, and occasional treason. These little zealots wanted dragons! Their rites did not raise Ashlord, though they prepared him carefully. The Great Cataclysm supplied what their worship could not. Its released magic struck the dead beast and finished their work. How efficient of catastrophe! So Ashlord's return was no accident, Sire. The Kindred prepared the corpse. The Cataclysm made it stand up!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/dead_dragons_dont_fly · working title "A Dead Dragon Flies" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 412.10

[[Kindred, Still Meddling]]


:: Brew on Purpose {"position":"2100,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): random brew fun once... now bottle obeys, Sssire.
START LOG: random brew... funny once. not funny tomorrow. need same poison, same bite, same victim. so I use known recipe, known essence... no guessing. measure little. sniff twice. heat slow. if green smoke comes, know why it came. if tongue goes numb... also know why. suspicious mixture can wait. today bottle does what I meant. quiet success, yes? quiet still kills nicely. that makes me smile... small smile. face feels stiff on left side.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): brew one known formula... no guessing this time.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): it obeyed... unsettling. good. I like unsettling.
COMPLETION LOG: known things in... known potion out. much better. less waste, less screaming at bottle. control means poison reaches right throat, not nearest throat. important detail. formula can change later... stronger, slower, nastier. first make it reliable. I will taste less now. maybe. tiny taste still counts as science... probably. copper flavour means stop, yes. next I master one formula until no secret bubbles remain. then bottle and I understand each other. poor bottle.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/brew_on_purpose · working title "A Deliberate Formula" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_CantPoison

[[Perfected Poison]]


:: Salvage the Salvagers {"position":"5700,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): They salvage ruins, Master. Let us salvage the Den.
START LOG: Kobolds built their lives on taking what abandoned powers left behind. Admirable! Now make the principle reciprocal, Sire. Kill their Captain and ten Kobolds. Do not waste time arguing whether the tunnels belong to Dwarves, Kobolds, or worms. Once resistance is broken, they belong to whoever can use them. Their own philosophy should make that comforting, my Lord! The Captain's death breaks the Den's centre. Ten more deaths ensure nobody mistakes it for an accident. Salvage is simply conquest performed after somebody else has done the building. Go on, Master. Show the scavengers how efficiently an Overlord can reuse a settlement!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the Kobold Captain and ten Kobolds, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Salvaged, Master! The Den finally understands its own philosophy.
COMPLETION LOG: The Captain is dead, ten Kobolds with him, and the Den has lost the confidence that made it theirs. Excellent! They spent the Silence converting abandoned Dwarf tunnels into a home. Now you have converted that home into a warning. It is almost educational, Sire! Their tools, passages, and useful scraps remain. Ownership does not! Take whatever merits keeping, Sire. The Dwarves may even call this justice, which would be amusing if anyone asked them. We did not. The salvagers have been salvaged, Master. I do appreciate a policy that explains itself!
VARIANT [escalated_kobolds=yes]: They once supplied you or worked beneath you, Master. Razing the Den afterward proves usefulness earned tolerance, never permanence.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/salvage_the_salvagers · working title "A Den Worth Razing" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_kobolds=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_kobolds=yes · VOICE: O1 EXP_D2_Abyss 350.20

Destruction Path


:: I Know That Stride {"position":"2200,2300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): That warrior moves like an old memory, Sire... and I dislike it.
START LOG: Watch that warrior below, Master! The stance is wrong for a common brute. The weight shifts before every strike, then settles hard. I have seen that discipline before... long ago. Memory can be treacherous, particularly after several dead Masters! Do not trust mine yet. Take the arena key from him, Sire. If this place was rebuilt by whoever I suspect, the lock should open more than a door. It may open an old chapter as well. Kill him cleanly! I should like one useful clue left intact for once!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the underworld arena, Master, and obtain its key.
EMOTION (complete): Stricken
POPUP (complete): The key fits old work, Master. Someone rebuilt a very familiar hall.
COMPLETION LOG: The key confirms the workmanship, Sire! This arena copies an old Tower hall almost lovingly. The proportions are right! The approach is right! Even the cruel little sightlines are right! Someone remembered how an Overlord received enemies and rebuilt the lesson underground. That warrior's style was another piece of it. I will not name the hand yet, Master. Old memories deserve better than guesses. But this was not built by a scholar reading ruins. Whoever ordered it knew one of my old reigns from the inside. Open the hall! Let us see whose nostalgia has teeth!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/i_know_that_stride · working title "A Familiar Weight Below" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 Tower_ThroneRoomMisc 301.20

[[He Rebuilt the Hall]]


:: It's Still Warm {"position":"2300,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Still warm, Sire! That is either promising or deeply unhygienic.
START LOG: Ah, my little biological diversion lives on! We need a primordial core, the dense living centre from which more ambitious work can grow. Think of it as a heart before sentiment ruins the concept. Obtain one intact, Sire! Flesh is troublesome material because it insists on warmth, feeding, repair, and other opinions. A core makes those arguments manageable. Once we have it, the chamber can acquire a proper pulse... and perhaps something worth feeding later. Do try not to squeeze it, Master. Living things take encouragement from the strangest gestures!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Bring a primordial core to the chamber, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): It is warm, Master! Delightfully, inconveniently alive.
COMPLETION LOG: There it is, warm and unpleasantly alive! A primordial core is exactly what my old work needed. Concentrated life, Sire, without the tiresome personality attached. It can feed structures that grow rather than merely stand there, which gives flesh possibilities stone and iron cannot manage. Do not think of it as meat. Meat has finished having ambitions! This is raw biological potential waiting for instructions, Master! Oh, I knew keeping those notes would pay off. Several assistants suggested burning them. Those assistants displayed very little imagination, my Lord... and eventually very little else worth preserving!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/its_still_warm · working title "A Fleshy Core" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 Wastelands 130.40

[[Feed the Cradle]]


:: Their Fire Is Yours {"position":"4500,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Their forge is excellent, Sire. The owners are optional.
START LOG: Dwarves understand fire, Master. Let us separate the useful part from the beards! Kill three Dwarven Warriors and the Forger who centres their craft. Do not ruin the forge itself, my Lord. Destruction should have standards! Their old realm built weapons enough to trouble nations, and this Hold still clings to that inheritance. Take the inheritance without the argument. Three warriors prove their defenders can fall. The Forger proves their continuity can be cut. Then the fire remains, Sire, waiting for hands less attached to ancestry. Ah, acquisition by subtraction! Brutal, efficient, and blessedly free of contracts.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill three Dwarven Warriors and the Dwarven Forger, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): The beards are quieter, Sire. The forge still burns. Perfect!
COMPLETION LOG: Their warriors are dead, the Forger is gone, and the forge still burns! Excellent work, Master! You took the one part worth preserving and removed the mouths arguing about ownership. The Successor Hold wanted history to guarantee possession. History has now changed hands, Master! Keep those fires hot, Sire. Dwarven craft deserves survival even when Dwarven authority does not. There is something almost charitable about preserving useful industry after killing its leadership. Almost! Do not dwell on it, Sire. The forge owes its fire to the power that kept it standing, and that power is yours.
VARIANT [escalated_successor_hold=yes]: They once received your recognition or served as your vassal, Master. Taking the forge afterward teaches that even honoured arrangements remain yours to revoke.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/their_fire_is_yours · working title "A Forge Owes Its Fire" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_successor_hold=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_successor_hold=yes · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 200.10

Destruction Path


:: Dragons Make Great Bellows {"position":"3300,1100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Dragon fire! Giblet wants hotter forge. Much hotter.
START LOG: Forge good. Dragon work hotter. Much hotter! Giblet wants Dragon Forge core. Beast flame goes there. Metal listens. Common fire too soft. Dragon fire bites. Good bite! Set core when beast ready. Giblet handles metal. Dragon handles flame. Eyebrows maybe survive. No promises. Hot forge. Hard metal. Proper work. Giblet approves danger when danger useful. Master brings core. Giblet makes forge worthy. Good danger makes good forge. Giblet likes forge that threatens back.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Set Dragon Forge core here, Master. Giblet handles hammer!
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Dragon Forge hot! Good hot. Giblet approves.
COMPLETION LOG: Dragon Forge stands. Heat bites back. Good! Giblet respects fire with temper. Common forge makes common metal. This makes angry metal. Feed right stuff. Let dragon flame work first. Hammer comes after. Giblet knows order. Keep dragon mouth away from Giblet face. Forge Master needs eyebrows. Mostly. Next, DragonSteel. Giblet wants one ingot fresh from heat. Then hammer asks questions. Metal answers. Bad metal breaks. Good metal sings. Giblet listens.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/dragons_make_great_bellows · working title "A Forge for Dragons" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_F INTRO.20

[[Steel That Screams]]

DragonForge Restoration


:: Wear Their Faces {"position":"7400,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Take a mask, Sire. Let worship look up and see its new authority.
START LOG: The Umvuthana follow masks, symbols, and their sun spirit's authority. Very obliging! Obtain one of their masks and turn that obedience toward yourself, Master. Do not kill the god yet. Submission is more amusing when worship remains intact but command comes from elsewhere. Wear the face they recognise. Let the followers answer! They may still pray upward while marching where you point! Ah, such theological flexibility. Symbols are wonderful things, Sire. People pour obedience into them, then act surprised when someone stronger picks one up. Take the mask and let the Grove discover a Master beneath its god.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain an Umvuthana mask and claim its authority, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The mask obeys you, Sire. More importantly, so do the faces behind it.
COMPLETION LOG: The mask is yours, Master, and the Umvuthana recognise the authority it carries. Their god remains above the grove, shining and receiving worship. Yet the followers answer to you. Delicious! Such a proud little theology, reduced to a chain of command with you inserted near the top. They may call Umvuthi divine, Master! Let them! Gods can have worshippers, Sire! Overlords have subjects! If the distinction troubles anyone, the mask should help explain it. Keep their rites, their dances, their feathers. Obedience is the only ornament we actually needed.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/wear_their_faces · working title "A God Beneath a Master" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_grove=Submission · VOICE: O1 D3_MAIN 804.60

Submission Path


:: Lovely, Stolen Gold {"position":"1400,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Gold, Sire! At last, a decorating principle worth respecting.
START LOG: Gold, Sire! Now the Tower is speaking sensibly. A Dark Tower needs a hoard, Master, though not for mystical reasons. Large piles make visitors understand priorities immediately, especially former owners! Start this chamber with a proper pile, my Lord. Stolen gold is best. Tribute is acceptable, and inheritance will do. Honestly earned gold rather spoils the atmosphere! Wealth should glitter, intimidate, and be inconveniently heavy, Sire. Otherwise it is merely accounting. We are not Dwarves, thank Evilness!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Place a pile of gold in the treasury, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Lovely, Master! The hoard has begun.
COMPLETION LOG: Lovely, lovely gold, Master! One pile is not a hoard, of course, but it is a beginning. Every mountain starts with something shiny another person wanted to keep, Sire! Let this chamber swell with coin, gems, relics, and trophies. Scholars may claim such things belong in museums, my Lord. A museum is merely a hoard with labels! Here we are more honest about greed and much less apologetic. Everything belongs to you, Sire. If the floor groans beneath the weight, consider that applause! Then add another pile.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/lovely_stolen_gold · working title "A Golden Start" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D4_SD5_TheRoyalHalls 200.10

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Hoard Restoration


:: Let the Straw Work {"position":"2900,600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): tiny workers good, Masta! now give me big straw brute!
START LOG: Tiny hands do tiny work, I need big helper! Make Hay Golem, Masta, straw shoulders, no lunch break, no fingers in stew! Let it haul sacks, lift baskets, carry boring things while Browns bash something useful. Keep fire away, hear me! Dry straw catches fast, very fast, embarrassingly fast. My kitchen flame stays where I tell it. Field flame does not get invitation! Straw works, crops move, nobody becomes bonfire. Good plan, loud plan, do it!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Make Hay Golem, Masta! Keep flame off straw!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Ha! Straw got arms, and still got no appetite!
COMPLETION LOG: Hay Golem works, Masta, big straw arms, empty belly, beautiful! It carries, stacks, hauls, never steals turnip for helmet. Keep it dry, keep fire far, farther, no, farther than that! I burned one scarecrow once, on purpose... different reason. Next I want whole estate tested. Crop Critters harvest twenty crops, no Minion hands. I count every one! Browns claim they helped? Check pockets, then helmets, then mouths. Missing carrots always confess. I want clean rows, full baskets, no excuses!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/let_the_straw_work · working title "A Harvest Worth Automating" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.BurnBurn

[[Twenty Crops, Zero Minions]]


:: Flowers Want Hearts? {"position":"3900,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): A heart for the altar, Master! These flowers are improving already.
START LOG: Bring the shrine its Orchid Heart, Sire. I expected petals or moonlit nonsense. Instead it wants a heart! Much more respectable! Place it on the altar and be ready. The guardian tied to this elven growth should answer. Evernight's reborn magic gets defensive around sacred arrangements! You have never possessed a gardener's gentle touch... thankfully! The heart may be key, meal, or both, and blood improves rituals enormously! Feed the shrine, Master. Then let us see what this decorative patch has been hiding behind all those petals.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Bring the Orchid Heart here, Sire, and feed the altar.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): There she is! Tall, sharp, floral, and already objectionable.
COMPLETION LOG: The heart called out its guardian, Master! Queen of Orchid, indeed. Mantis shaped, elegant, and thoroughly dangerous. Evernight's reborn magic clings to every blade and petal. The title is ceremony, not an elven crown! No hidden court is taking orders from her. This shrine is not the source of Evernight's return either. She simply grew from that old magic's resurgence! Quite a bloom, Sire! Now cut her down. Gardening is only conquest with poorer screams. Besides, anything with that many blades has clearly volunteered for pruning.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/flowers_want_hearts · working title "A Heart for the Altar" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 1100.10

[[Weed the Garden]]


:: Resin for Peace {"position":"7600,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Leave the hive alone, Master, provided it pays in something sticky.
START LOG: Myrmex resin has value, Sire, which immediately makes restraint more attractive. Obtain resin from the colony and leave the hive to itself in exchange. No friendship, no cuddling, no absurd insect diplomacy. Merely terms! They remain in their mound, Sire. You receive something useful! Everyone avoids being trampled! I can accept this! Peace is less offensive when it comes packaged as material gain. Take desert or jungle resin, Master, whichever colony answers first. Then let the insects continue their busy little lives with the comforting knowledge that continued existence has acquired a price.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain Myrmex resin and leave the colony undisturbed, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Resin received, Master! The ants have purchased breathing room.
COMPLETION LOG: The resin is yours, and the colony remains intact. A neat exchange! The Myrmex continue digging, breeding, hauling, and pretending their tiny empire matters. You gain what you wanted without wasting time crushing every soldier. That is not kindness, Master. It is efficient pricing, Sire! Their peace lasts because resin makes their survival useful. Let the colony understand that distinction if it is capable of understanding anything beyond pheromones and hierarchy. If not, no matter, my Lord! The arrangement still works! Evil need not always destroy, Master. Sometimes it sends an invoice and waits outside the mound!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/resin_for_peace · working title "A Hive Left its Own" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_myrmex=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D4_SD2_TempleConstruction 101.10

Peaceful Path


:: Bees. Endless Bees. {"position":"3100,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Bees, Sire, endless bees and cheerful flowers... my loyalty suffers.
START LOG: What a revolting little paradise, Master. Bees everywhere, honey underfoot, and flowers where decent fungus ought to grow! The whole realm hums with productive sweetness. I can feel my scales tightening already. This place survived the Empire's old cleansing attempts. A pocket of light magic slipped their grasp! Almost admirable... almost, so explore the hive, Sire! Find whatever passes for authority among these insects. Any realm this cheerful must produce something worth stealing. If not, we can still crush something ceremonial. Please do hurry. I fear prolonged exposure may make me appreciate the colour gold.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Explore the endless hive, Master, and find its ruler.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): A Queen! Of course sweetness becomes political eventually.
COMPLETION LOG: The hive goes on and on, Sire! Golden caverns, flowers, workers, honey everywhere. Enough cheerfulness to make a dungeon feel medicinal. Yet the place has order, Master! The bees gather around a Queen like any court. A throne with wings is still a throne! Approach her and inspect this ridiculous monarchy. Do not bow! Do not accept a flower crown. If she offers honey, test it for useful magic first! We endured all this sweetness for a reason. I refuse to leave an entire sticky kingdom without exploiting at least one valuable substance.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/bees_endless_bees · working title "A Hive Without End" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.20

[[Her Majesty, the Bug]]

Bee Nest Found


:: Something Chews Up North {"position":"2200,1700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Something large is feeding in the frozen North, Sire. How considerate!
START LOG: The northern trace ends in a frozen hideout, Master. Something inside has been feeding very well! The snow carries blood, bone, and that same spoiled tang. I can hear enough chewing through the netherrock to dislike the creature already. Skor, they call it! A Yeti with an appetite larger than its manners. Search the lair, Sire! I want whatever remains after its meals, especially anything that should have stayed dead. Corruption leaves patterns in what it ruins! Frozen meat preserves evidence beautifully... and dinner, if one has sufficiently low standards. The Minions usually do!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter Skor's frozen hideout, Sire, and investigate the corrupted lair.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Frozen corpses, Master... and some refuse to remain corpses!
COMPLETION LOG: There we are, Sire. Skor has been feeding on corrupted remains. The cold preserved more than meat! Several frozen skeletons still twitch beneath that foul influence, as though death misplaced the final instruction. Skor did not create this power. He found it, ate around it, and grew enormous on the leftovers. Charming! Destroy the animated remains, Master. If the corruption can keep dead bones moving after Skor has finished chewing, I want to know how stubborn it truly is. Five clean kills should tell us enough. Then we can deal with the glutton himself!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/something_chews_up_north · working title "A Hunger In The Frozen North" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 200.10

[[Frozen Leftovers]]


:: Pointy End Out, Sire {"position":"1600,2000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Browns are waiting, Master! Claim the Staff and give one something to follow.
START LOG: The Browns never slept, Master! Tough, loyal, and wonderfully uncomplicated, they waited in the Netherworld with all their old enthusiasm intact. Now they finally have a Master again! Your Master Staff is the old sceptre of command. It calls Minions and settles arguments about authority. Claim it, Sire, then call one Brown to you. He will cheer, salute, and seek something larger to hit! Ah, such dependable instincts. Point the little fellow in a useful direction, my Lord. That is usually enough. Soon we shall have more servants, more noise, and considerably more broken furniture!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Claim the Master Staff, Sire. Call one Brown to your side.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Good, Master! One Brown, one Staff, and the beginnings of a proper Horde.
COMPLETION LOG: There we are, Master! The Staff rests in the proper hand, and a Brown has answered your call. Look at the little brute, Sire! Teeth, fists, devotion, and scarcely enough thought for hesitation. Browns are the Horde's muscle, always volunteering for unpleasant impacts. Admirable, really! One Minion does not make an army, my Lord, but it does make a beginning. The others can be woken in time, once suitable violence reminds them who they are. For now, you have a servant, and he has a Master again! Try not to let him headbutt anything structural. He looks eager enough to try.
CODER NOTES: overlord:prologue_and_horde/pointy_end_out_sire · working title "A New Master" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 202.10

[[Sit, Sire. Brood.]]

[[The World Won't Ruin Itself]]

[[Fire, Fury, No Sense]]

Brown Quest


:: Holy or Bloody? {"position":"3100,600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Enough preparation, Sire! Let one grand tradition shake the ceiling.
START LOG: Enough preparation, Sire! Cast a Blood spell or Holy spell at its highest order. I do not care whether the power arrives through veins or sanctity. Both become wonderfully persuasive when strong enough! Reach the tenth circle in either art and let the study feel it. Priests will insist the distinction matters terribly. Victims may agree! An Overlord should ask the useful question: does it obey? Make one of those great traditions answer, Master. We have copied, forged, and refined long enough. Now give the room something worth being frightened of!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Cast a level-ten Blood or Holy spell, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Ah! That is spellcraft worth reinforcing the ceiling for.
COMPLETION LOG: Now that is spellcraft, Master! Blood or holiness, one great tradition answered at its highest order. Priests may argue over the source, but the important part is obedience. The spell came when called, Sire! Your study has travelled from copied words to forged scrolls, refined tools, and power capable of shaping a battle by itself. Very respectable! Keep learning, Sire. Mastering one dangerous height does not make everything below it harmless. It merely gives you a better view of what else deserves conquering. And what a lovely view that should become, my Lord!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/holy_or_bloody · working title "A New Power Balance" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_TR IMAGIC.70


:: Loot Deserves Drawers {"position":"1400,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Master, the loot is becoming geological! Give greed some shelves.
START LOG: Conquest produces possessions, Master, and possessions produce piles! Piles produce Browns sleeping on them. Unacceptable, Sire. We need somewhere proper for lesser spoils before the corridors disappear beneath them. Restore this chamber with a drawer controller, my Lord. Then iron can find iron, cloth can find cloth, and loot can stop hiding beneath Minions! Gold deserves admiration. Trophies deserve display. Useful materials deserve finding before someone eats them! Order is not virtue, Sire, perish the thought. It is greed with shelves, which makes it perfectly respectable.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Set a drawer controller in the storage chamber, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Ah, order! Not virtue, Master, just organized possession.
COMPLETION LOG: Ah, proper storage, Sire! The Tower can swallow lesser treasures again without burying the corridors under anonymous junk. No more archaeological expeditions through Minion rubbish, Master! Drawers for useful goods, packs for what travels, and fewer onions inside helmets. Do not mistake this for tidiness, my Lord. Tidiness is virtuous, a horrible word. This is conquest catalogued! You should know exactly how much belongs to you, Sire. More importantly, know how little belongs to everyone else. Greed becomes much easier when properly indexed!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/loot_deserves_drawers · working title "A Place for Everything" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 204.10

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Storage Restoration


:: The World Won't Ruin Itself {"position":"1800,1800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Look outside, Sire! The world has been comfortable for far too long.
START LOG: Look beyond the Tower, Sire! The land has enjoyed nearly three hundred years without an Overlord. Disgraceful, Master, absolutely disgraceful! The netherrock beneath your home blighted the earth around it. Sensible locals avoid that cursed belt, which shows uncommon good sense. Beyond it lie towns, ruins, beasts, fools... opportunities! Cross out of the Tower's shadow, my Lord, and inspect your inheritance. I am almost curious what people built without us. Almost. There may be green fields and birdsong out there. Steel yourself, Sire! We shall endure the pleasantness together, then find something worth spoiling.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Cross beyond the cursed ground surrounding the Dark Tower, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Hideous, Master! Green fields, birdsong, and opportunities everywhere.
COMPLETION LOG: Hideous, is it not, Master? Birds singing, fields green, people wandering about without permission! Still, there is promise beneath all that pleasantness, Sire. Old roads lead to new settlements, fat little markets, and ruined powers left holes for smaller ones. Comfortable communities always produce someone worth robbing! The fifth Overlord has crossed the cursed ground, my Lord. This land no longer remembers what an Overlord means. Oh, what a delightful failing! Let them smile a little longer... then educate them, Sire. Nothing improves local memory like a proper reign of terror!
CODER NOTES: overlord:prologue_and_horde/the_world_wont_ruin_itself · working title "A Reign Unfolds" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 100.20

