Exploration Opens


:: Souls, Crystallised {"position":"2500,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): A soul made solid, Sire? Much tidier than haunting!
START LOG: Furniture does not make a ritual chamber, Sire. An answered rite does! Begin with crystallisation at the brazier and make a soul shard. Spiritual residue is so much easier once it acquires edges. Priests prefer invisible mysteries because nobody can count them. I prefer power one can hold, catalogue, and take away! Perform the rite properly, Master, and make the chamber answer. If the result is cold, sharp, and faintly unsettling, excellent. That usually means we have made something useful rather than devotional. Besides, my Lord, shelves are much easier to organize than hauntings!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Perform the Crystallization Ritual at the brazier, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There! A soul shard. Small, cold, and wonderfully practical.
COMPLETION LOG: A soul shard, Master! Small, cold, and vastly more useful than a sermon. The rite answered, which means powers beyond the Tower can hear this chamber. Good. We can work with that! Ritual magic is etiquette enforced by consequences, Sire. Prepare the signs, provide the proper thing, speak correctly, then wait to see what notices! We shall continue carefully... not reverently. Anything eager for worship is usually selling something. Anything demanding souls probably has expensive tastes. Fortunately, we are very good at negotiating from a position of darkness!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/souls_crystallised · working title "A Ritual that Works" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.30

[[Gods Like Snacks]]


:: Dragons Again? Lovely. {"position":"4700,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): A living dragon, Sire! Apparently the world felt insufficiently flammable.
START LOG: That is a real dragon, Master. Large, alive, and very inconveniently historical. Dragons vanished long ago, yet here one stands! Do not invent an explanation before evidence arrives. I have buried enough Masters beneath elegant assumptions! First learn what these creatures actually are! Old bestiaries recorded breeds, habits, nests, and weaknesses. Find one, Sire, and read it properly! Then we may discuss killing, robbing, taming, or strategic admiration. Preferably from behind something thick. Knowledge will not shrink the teeth, but it may keep your name out of a chapter titled 'Master, Eaten.'
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Find a proper bestiary and study these dragons, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Real dragons, documented dragons, breeding dragons! How reassuring.
COMPLETION LOG: The bestiary confirms them, Master. These are no illusions. Its old descriptions match the living breeds outside! Why they returned remains unanswered, and stays unanswered! We use evidence here, Sire, not pretty guesses. The useful parts are wonderfully practical. Nests, eggs, growth, taming, and several routes into a dragon's stomach! We can work with that, so find an egg next! A species' future becomes much easier to manage when stolen young! Let the adults object. Property disputes are considerably simpler when one side breathes fire and the other is you.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/dragons_again_lovely · working title "A Shadow with Wings" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_SD1_TheViridianCaverns 101.10

[[Read Up, Sire]]

Dragon encountered


:: One Wound, Many Bleeds {"position":"2800,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Five foul concentrations, Sire... and every one points elsewhere.
START LOG: Now we can compare them, Master. Skor fed on corrupted dead, and Sirok swallowed corrupted blood! Ashlord rose through old Cataclysm power! The Kraken fattened on tainted sacrifice. My old Master carried corruption from his prison. Five places, five appetites, one ugly direction! None behaved like a source. They were mouths, Sire, feeding from something hidden. That matters because the Great Cataclysm scarred more than one land. I remember what uncontrolled magic did afterward... too well. If these traces share one injury, we stop hunting symptoms. We find what was buried, and why.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read my conclusion, Master, and trace the corruption toward its hidden source.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Ah. The Empire buried its fear in vaults, Sire. Let us dig it up!
COMPLETION LOG: I remember the Empire's cleansers now, Master. After the Cataclysm, they sealed remote containment vaults around contamination they feared. Stone outside, ritual inside, silence everywhere. Typical Empire housekeeping! There are strange eyes made from crystallised soured magic. They tug toward those buried vaults, as though the corruption remembers where it belongs. Follow that pull, Sire! I cannot yet tell what waits beyond their sealed door. I can tell you this much. Skor, Sirok, Ashlord, the Kraken, and my old Master were not five beginnings. They were five bleeding roads! Every road leads toward the same buried secret.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/one_wound_many_bleeds · working title "A Single Wound" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O2 Empire_Endbattle 680.20

[[So That's Where It Went]]


:: Something's Gone Off {"position":"1800,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Sire... that essence smells wrong. Lifeforce should not curdle!
START LOG: That little essence should feel alive, Master! Faintly, perhaps, but alive! Instead it has the spiritual bouquet of forgotten milk. Something soured the lifeforce without killing its power. I can feel that taint through the netherrock... unpleasantly clearly. Worse, it tugs at the stone beneath your Tower. Keep it away from anything precious, Sire! Corruption loves company! Ordinary rot consumes things and has the decency to stop. This does not. Even the Browns have started sniffing one another suspiciously. Examine it carefully. I want to know whether we found one bad drop, or the first stink from a much larger drain.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read my first account of the tainted essence, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): One foul drop proves little, Master. Unfortunately, I can smell more!
COMPLETION LOG: The essence is no lonely curiosity, Sire! Its corruption has a direction to it! I feel a faint pull through the netherrock, like a scent on a long wind. Stronger concentrations answer from elsewhere! Whatever feeds upon them has had time to become very large. We do not know the source yet, Master! We only know the same wrongness reaches places with nothing else in common. That is rarely comforting! Hunt those concentrations! Watch what the corruption does to flesh, bone, and magic. Once we have enough examples, even a mystery can be cornered and kicked.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/somethings_gone_off · working title "A Tainted Essence" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O2 Empire_Endbattle 680.10

[[We Need a Bigger Sword]]

[[Scars Everywhere, Sire]]

[[That Is Not a Fish]]

First Essence Found, Sets up the Campaign


:: It's... Blooming? {"position":"3800,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): The wound is growing things, Sire. I find that personally insulting.
START LOG: Look beyond the central scar, Master! The wound is not barren at all! Corrupted growth has rooted where only broken stone should remain. Forests twist through poisoned ground. Crystalline pools gather strange power! Living structures cling to places that ought to kill them. The wound has leaked long enough for life to adapt... revoltingly well. A wasteland eventually exhausts itself, Sire! An ecosystem learns. Explore the outer region and see how far this has spread. The Anchor is gone, yet the corruption keeps breeding habits of its own. Neglect anything for centuries and apparently even cosmic damage starts gardening!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Explore the outer reaches, Master, until you find the wound's corrupted growth.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): It thrives, Master! I preferred our cosmic injuries properly injured.
COMPLETION LOG:
The outer wound is alive, Sire, and thriving! Roots drink poisoned ground. Crystalline pools carry strange power! Creatures treat impossible conditions as ordinary weather. That is worse than simple desolation. Barren damage can fade. Living damage feeds, adapts, and spreads! The trouble no longer sits neatly where we entered, Master. It has learned to flourish beyond the old centre. Almost admirable... if it were not eating reality. We follow that growth outward now. Something in this realm survived long enough to turn catastrophe into habitat. I want to know what else learned to live here.
VARIANT [heart_seed=held]: The seed tugs harder through this growth, Master, pointing beyond the bloom.
VARIANT [heart_seed=not_held]: The surviving current still trends outward, Sire, even without that fragment.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/its_blooming · working title "A Thriving Wound" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VARIANT: heart_seed=held|not_held · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.30

[[Shulkers, Still Sulking]]


:: Home, Wretched Home {"position":"2300,1575","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Look around, Master! Sixteen chambers, nearly respectable in their wickedness.
START LOG: Look around, Sire! The throne stands, the forge rings, kitchens smoke, and studies hum. Cages wait while gold glitters, Master. Even your bed looks properly ominous! Sixteen chambers have risen from neglect. Each remembers what this Tower was built to be, my Lord, and who built it to serve. Read the final muster and enjoy that rare sensation of finished work! Do not become attached to it, Sire. There is always another ruin, kingdom, beast, or cosmic mistake demanding attention. Evil is never short of maintenance! That is how we know it remains healthy.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read the final Tower muster, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): At last, Sire! The Dark Tower lives again.
COMPLETION LOG: At last, Master! The Dark Tower deserves its name again. Not pristine, not tasteful... alive, Sire! Fire, magic, beasts, steel, food, secrets, and Minions arguing over all of them. This is more than a home, my Lord, however gratifyingly dreadful the furnishings. It is a statement visible for miles! Evil has an address, a throne, and excellent storage, Sire! Quaver already believes the restored halls require music, though I had hoped completion might bring silence... foolish of me. Enjoy the Tower while the quiet lasts. It will not last long!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/home_wretched_home · working title "A Tower Complete" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Tower_ThroneRoomMisc 100.10

[[Quaver Wants a Band]]

Complete Tower


:: Eleven Instruments. Why. {"position":"2875,1550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Four voices started. Eleven crown the song,
He deserves a court both loud and wrong.
START LOG: Four instruments first taught these restored old halls to sing,
Now eleven voices must attend their dark reigning king.
Bring every kind, from deepest drum to shrillest silver reed,
Each voice recruited proudly for his darker courtly need.

No missing string, no silent pipe may skulk somewhere aside,
His orchestra should thunder proudly always at his side.
Let Quaver count each stolen instrument now one by one,
Until the full and wicked score is gloriously done.

A Master conquers lands with claw and sharpened blackened steel,
He conquers silence too, with properly wicked musical zeal.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Gather all eleven instruments for his court,
No absent voice, no unfinished report.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Eleven voices thunder through the stone,
His Tower finally has a sound its own.
COMPLETION LOG: Eleven instruments now fill the Tower's broad waiting air,
A courtly din of menace settles thickly everywhere.
From little chime to growling strings that scrape below,
Each voice has learned exactly when its darker threat should show.

No hall need suffer peaceful silence from this wicked hour,
The band can greet each victim walking helpless toward his power.
Quaver has counted every stolen note and conquered tone,
And none remain outside the music of his throne.

The set is whole; the darker repertoire may now start,
His enemies can hear their own defeat performed as art.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/eleven_instruments_why · working title "A Whole Orchestra" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.10


:: Minions With Tails {"position":"3700,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Rats, Sire! Tiny hands, sharp teeth, dreadful morals, very promising.
START LOG: These are not ordinary wall thieves, Master. Look at the little beasts work! They can be trained, equipped, and given proper tasks. Almost Minions with tails... almost. Let us avoid starting a cousin dispute. Tame one, Sire, and test its loyalty! Something that small can reach places Browns cannot. Better still, it may fit through without removing the doorway first! If it serves well, we gain cheap labour with pocketsized overhead. I am told cheese motivates them. A worker paid in lunch has already understood several important principles of government.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Tame one of these unusually capable rats, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): It follows you! Excellent, now keep it away from Tower accounts.
COMPLETION LOG: Your rat has accepted service, Sire! Admirably quick little traitor. Feed it, equip it, and put it to work. Courier, guard, thief, labourer, perhaps worse, because they learn quickly, Master! It is not merely appetite either, because I see bargaining, hoarding, calculation! Those tiny eyes have merchant written all over them! Find some of their cheese and watch closely! We should learn whether it is food or wealth. With clever rodents, always assume the less dignified answer. It saves disappointment later... and sometimes prevents a banking crisis.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/minions_with_tails · working title "A Workforce with Tails" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 209.10

[[Cheese Is Currency Now]]

Rat encountered


:: That Is Not a Fish {"position":"4500,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): That is no longer merely fish. You may call me the Historian.
START LOG: You have caught an instructive specimen; allow an introduction; I am the Historian; names matter less than collections; I preserve art, artifacts, treasures, truths. This creature belongs with the latter two. Its deformity has structure. The flesh carries the same rot already troubling your reign. Water has merely distributed it. Cut the specimen open. Carefully, if you please. What changed first? What endured longest? Bodies are records when one reads them correctly.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Cut open the aberrant catch. Preserve what it reveals.
EMOTION (complete): Composed
POPUP (complete): Yes. The rot reached the water. Find its witnesses.
COMPLETION LOG: The specimen is useful; the conclusion is unpleasant; rot has entered the sea; ordinary creatures record different exposures; fishermen noticed before scholars would have. Practical men often meet history early. They also write badly. Search their bottles. Fear, drink, superstition, and drowning produce untidy testimony. Untidy does not mean worthless. Open one message. I want the witness before interpretation polishes it. The coast may have been keeping this record for years.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/that_is_not_a_fish · working title "An Aberration on the Line" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: DREDGE Collector Row 0310

[[Bottled Gibberish]]

Aberration caught


:: Raid Where I Point {"position":"4000,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Let them raid, Master. Just improve their sense of direction!
START LOG: Raiders without raiding become sullen, Sire. We need not cure them of their best habit. Redirect it! Carry the Bastille's banner. Help them win a raid against another village. That proves a simple arrangement: their walls remain theirs, their appetite remains intact, but their violence travels where you point. How civilised! A border pact built on shared victims has admirable clarity. Win beside them, Master, and let the Bastille learn that peace with you means war for somebody less useful. I can tolerate diplomacy when the paperwork screams in the distance!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Win a raid against another village while carrying the Bastille's banner.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): A perfect border pact, Sire! Their peace points outward.
COMPLETION LOG: The Bastille keeps its walls, Master, and its raiders keep their favourite occupation. They raid where your shadow permits! Very neighbourly, in its way! No tribute was demanded, no knees were forced down, and yet their violence now respects your boundary. Let them boast that the pact preserves their independence, Sire. Independence with approved targets is a wonderfully flexible word! Their enemies suffer, useful settlements remain standing, and you spend none of your own walls in the bargain. Peace by redirection! I confess, my Lord, diplomacy improves enormously when everyone carries axes.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/raid_where_i_point · working title "An Armed Boundary" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_bastille=Peaceful · VOICE: O2 NW_TR ROSE.30

Peaceful Path


:: Trophies, Not Clutter {"position":"1400,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Pile bad. Display good. Giblet wants warning furniture.
START LOG: Weapons in heap. Bad heap. Giblet wants blades standing proud. Armour upright. Trophies watching door. Put display case in armory, Master. Strong glass. Clear glass. No wobble. Prize belongs where visitors see it. Fear saves hammer work. Sometimes. Giblet calls that efficient. Case first. Trophy later. Armory should look ready before anything swings. Giblet likes ready. Giblet hates shelves that apologize. Good armory should threaten before door opens. Very good warning.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Put display case in armory, Master. Let steel boast!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There! Armory looks mean. Giblet approves!
COMPLETION LOG: Better. Much better! Giblet sees armory now. Not scrap nest. Blades stay ready. Armour stays straight. Trophies do staring. Master finds gear fast. Good metal should work. Good trophies should warn. Put important thing inside. Better if old owner wants it back. Then case tells story before hammer does. If old owner arrives, Giblet has hammer. Story gets ending. Strong case. Strong message. Good work. Giblet calls that proper decoration.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/trophies_not_clutter · working title "An Armory Worth Seeing" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_F ARMOR.NO_I4

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Armory Restoration


:: Cheese Is Currency Now {"position":"3700,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): It is currency, Master, actual cheese! Civilization has finally surrendered.
START LOG: Get some of that cheese, Sire. I hoped it was merely bait. No such luck! The rats value it like Dwarves value gold. Cheese buys labour, tools, favour, perhaps political office! The system is offensively coherent. Worse, their stories keep naming Ratlantis. A lost rat civilization, spoken of with reverence! We are not chasing folklore because the money smells interesting. First find what connects these furry economists to it! There should be an object, relic, or key. Something tangible. I refuse to invade a legendary rodent nation on the strength of dairy gossip alone.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain their cheese, Master, and study what it buys.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Cheese buys civilization! Somewhere a Halfling ancestor applauds.
COMPLETION LOG: Yes, Sire, it is absolutely currency. Reward, trade, favour, all of it, and every crumb seems accounted for! Their entire ambition rests on cheese! I almost respect the simplicity! Unfortunately, the stories point toward something more solid. A Gem of Ratlantis, Master! An artifact tied to their lost civilization! Find it, Master, before the stories become even less dignified. Until then, I shall maintain Ratlantis is marketing! A joke, perhaps, or an elaborate scam run by rodents with excellent branding! Please let me keep that theory a little longer... Evil has crossed many boundaries. A cheese economy may yet be one boundary too many.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/cheese_is_currency_now · working title "An Empire of Cheese" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 606.10

[[A Rat's Crown Jewel]]


:: Rich Soil, Richer Master {"position":"2900,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): cupboard empty again, Masta! dirt needs feeding before I do!
START LOG: Kitchen eats fast, cupboard empties faster, I need rich soil! Dark dirt, fat dirt, dirt that grows crops like I threatened it, Masta! Make farmland ready, keep Brown boots off seedlings or I roast boots with feet still in them. Soil never reaches plate, still first ingredient. No soil, no crop, no dinner, simple! Feed ground, ground feeds kitchen, kitchen feeds Tower. I want rows working hard, pots working harder, fire hottest!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Make rich farmland, Masta! Feed dirt, then feed me!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Good dirt! Dark, ugly, fat. I could almost season it!
COMPLETION LOG: Good soil, Masta, soft, dark, rich, proper ugly! Crops got no excuse now. Grow big or become compost, I mean it! Kitchen needs steady food while Red hive still sleeps, and Browns pick with mouths first. Keep rows full with roots, grain, greens, anything that boils, fries, roasts, or survives my pan. I turn field into dinner! Next I want tiny field workers, small feet, quick hands, less trampling. If they steal carrots too, I get bigger spoon!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/rich_soil_richer_master · working title "An Estate Worth Feeding" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D4_SD3_TheBrewery 100.20

[[Tiny Farmhands]]


:: RSVP to a Lich {"position":"2900,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): His prison waits. Enter, Sire. Let the pretender receive you.
START LOG: A prison made court. Appropriate. The Lich chose his cage. Once, a Fallen Knight. Then came Silence. Then ambition. He gathered graveyards. He commanded corpses. He named theft a kingdom. This claim is his alone. No distant master excuses it. Enter the prison, Sire. Study what he built. Let him see your shadow. The dead know hierarchy. Pretenders often forget it. He has waited centuries for correction. We should be punctual.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the Lich's prison, Sire. Confront his claim.
EMOTION (complete): Stricken
POPUP (complete): He waits within. One dark lord too many.
COMPLETION LOG: You stand in his court. Bone. Stone. Vanity. The Lich wears old discipline well. He wears authority poorly. Silence taught him a false lesson. Absence became inheritance. Graveyards became provinces. Corpses became subjects. No. His lesser dead are broken. His staff is taken. Only the claimant remains. Kill him, Sire. End title and body together. Let each grave remember proper silence. Death has tolerated his administration long enough. I will file the correction.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/rsvp_to_a_lich · working title "An Invitation to the Lich" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.40

[[Only One Dark Lord, Thanks]]


:: Theft or Salvage? {"position":"5100,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Theft or salvage, Sire? The answer depends entirely on who still has an army.
START LOG: Now we can admire a properly old grievance, Master! The Dwarves say the Kobolds stole their abandoned tunnels. The Kobolds say abandoned tunnels were waiting to be salvaged. Both arguments improve dramatically when shouted underground! You need not care who is historically correct. Decide who benefits your reign! Back the Dwarves by killing Kobolds! Back the Den by killing Dwarven warriors. Make both sides trade and call that peace. Or deepen the feud with blood from each. This quarrel decides their relationship, Sire, not their greater fate. Think of it as seasoning between two separate conquests!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read my account, Master, then choose how the Dwarf-Kobold feud should tip.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There, Sire. Two claims, four answers, and not one requires fairness.
COMPLETION LOG: You understand the quarrel now, Master. The Dwarves invoke ancestry, Sire! The Kobolds invoke abandonment, my Lord! Neither side invokes the obvious fact that you outrank both arguments! Still, their feud can be useful. Tilt the scales toward old ownership, arm the scavengers through blood, force trade across the grievance, or let hatred ripen into open war. The choice changes how these two peoples face each other, not what you separately decide to do with either faction. Keep those matters distinct, Sire. A ruler may settle a boundary today and burn one signatory tomorrow. Consistency is for clerks!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/theft_or_salvage · working title "An Old Conflict" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D4_SD3_TheBrewery 104.10

[[Side With the Beards]]

[[Both Work for You Now]]

[[Back the Tunnel Rats]]

[[Peace, What is it good for?]]

Dwarf/Kobold Introduction


:: Back the Tunnel Rats {"position":"5250,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Three Dwarven warriors, Sire. Let the scavengers call it precedent!
START LOG: Perhaps the Kobolds deserve your thumb on their side, Master. Kill three Dwarven Warriors and let the Den interpret that as support. The Kobolds will celebrate! They will say salvage beat ancestry. The Dwarves will say theft has gained a patron. Both descriptions are entertaining, my Lord! Three dead warriors are enough to mark your preference without deciding the whole future of either faction. This is a feud, Sire, not a marriage! Back the tunnel-folk today and choose their greater fate separately. The important lesson is that old ownership means very little once somebody stronger starts editing the footnotes!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill three Dwarven Warriors to favour the Kobolds, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The Den has your favour, Sire. The beards will be unbearable about it.
COMPLETION LOG: Three Dwarven warriors have fallen, Master, and the Kobolds can celebrate their interpretation of property. Let them cheer! The old tunnels remain contested, but the Den now knows whose strength tipped the argument. Dwarves will resent it, naturally, Master. Resentment keeps memory sharp, Sire. None of this binds your later choices toward either people. The Kobolds have won this dispute, not immunity. The Successor Hold has lost ground, not necessarily its future. A wise Overlord keeps every promise exactly as narrow as the words allow. A wiser one lets everyone else imagine more!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/back_the_tunnel_rats · working title "Arm the Den" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 201.20

Kobold Favored Path


:: Patron of Ugly Engineers {"position":"5400,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Their engineers are clever, Sire. Buy the hands, keep the inventions!
START LOG: Goblin engineers make wonderfully ugly things, Master! More importantly, the ugly things work, my Lord! Become their patron and turn that talent toward your reign. Let one of their engineers recognise the arrangement. Patronage sounds gentle, but ownership does not require a collar when ambition pulls just as well. Supply opportunity, demand results, Master! Their workshops keep moving, their clever little contraptions keep multiplying, and every useful design begins asking whether the Overlord would approve. Ah, influence through vanity! Make the engineer deal, Sire! A craftsman who wants your favour will forge his own leash and polish it afterward.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Win the service of a Goblin engineer, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Excellent, Sire! Their cleverness now sends invoices to you.
COMPLETION LOG: Their engineers have a patron now, Master, and that patron has a Tower. Very persuasive architecture! Goblin workshops will keep their noise, smoke, and alarming improvisation, but their best work now serves your reign. Let them boast that this is partnership! The word costs us nothing, my Lord! A Goblin who invents for your approval has already moved beyond simple trade. He is building your strength while congratulating himself. Delightful! Keep the materials flowing when useful, Sire, and the inventions will follow. There are worse ways to conquer a people than making their brightest minds desperate to impress you.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/patron_of_ugly_engineers · working title "Arms by Patronage" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_goblins=Submission · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 400.20

Submission Path


:: We Never Speak of Ratlantis {"position":"3700,3800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Back at last, Sire! Good, now we never speak of Ratlantis.
START LOG: You returned, Master, excellent, so begin forgetting immediately! Secure the Gem somewhere dark. Pay useful rats whatever cheese keeps them working. And keep Quaver away from this story! Ratlantis had machines, a flying Baron, and far too much civilization. I will never dismiss wall scratching again. Knowledge is supposed to empower a reign, Sire. This knowledge merely smells of cheese and humiliation. We survived the place, and that is quite enough! No tours, embassies, or cultural exchange will follow this! If anyone proposes diplomatic relations with Ratlantis, I shall personally misfile the request forever.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Return to the surface, Master, and leave Ratlantis behind.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Normal-sized tyranny again! I had almost forgotten the comfort.
COMPLETION LOG: Ratlantis is behind us, Sire, so keep it there! Ordinary rats remain useful little servants. Their cheese remains acceptable wages. The Gem proves every ridiculous legend was true. We killed their Baron, escaped their machinery, and adopted none of their customs! That counts as triumph, and if anyone asks what lies beyond the Gem, say nothing! If they bring evidence, lose it. Some horrors deserve public conquest, Master. Others deserve a locked drawer and aggressive denial. Ratlantis belongs firmly in the second category. I have standards, even after all these centuries.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/we_never_speak_of_ratlantis · working title "Back from Ratlantis" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 Tower_ThroneRoomMisc 303.10


:: Blow the Horn, Sire {"position":"4200,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Take their horn, Sire! Nothing says obedience like stolen command.
START LOG: The Bastille prides itself on ravagers, Master! Huge, angry beasts with exactly the right number of social skills. Their horn carries command among the raiders! Obtain one, and the symbol of their strength becomes yours. No need for speeches, Master! A horn sounded in the proper hand settles hierarchy very quickly. Let them hear their own beasts answer your call, Sire. Raiders respect force, but they adore visible proof of it. Take the horn and make submission audible! I suspect the ravagers will adapt faster than their former handlers. Beasts are often very sensible about new management!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain a ravager horn from the Bastille, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Hear that, Sire? Their strength answers your breath now.
COMPLETION LOG: The horn is yours, Master! That sound carries farther than any treaty. The Bastille's beasts have become instruments of your reign, and the raiders know precisely what that means. They may keep their banners, their walls, and their sour expressions. Command sits elsewhere now, Sire! Blow the horn and their proudest creatures answer your authority. Ah, such a satisfying little inversion, my Lord. They respected strength, so strength acquired them. No philosopher could explain submission more neatly. Keep the horn close! Symbols matter to armed fools, especially when the symbol makes several tonnes of teeth and muscle come running!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/blow_the_horn_sire · working title "Bastille as a Weapon" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_bastille=Submission · VOICE: O2 Nordberg_Town_Chunk_4 402.15

Submission Path


:: Pets Are Minions Too {"position":"1700,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Beasts need somewhere to sleep, Sire. Preferably not on the throne.
START LOG: Not every servant walks upright, Sire! Beasts bite without speeches, and companions rarely demand titles. Some learn loyalty faster than people, Master, and complain much less about taxes! Restore the beasts' pen with a proper pet bed, my Lord. Give your less articulate followers somewhere to settle. Treat them well enough to keep the teeth outward! Affection is optional, Sire, but feeding is not. Even tyranny looks foolish when the war beast wanders off for better snacks. We have standards to maintain! Besides, a loyal beast rarely asks for a promotion.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Place a pet bed in the beasts' pen, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The pen is ready, Sire! Teeth now have assigned quarters.
COMPLETION LOG: The pen is ready, Master! Beasts and companions finally have somewhere proper, Sire, with fewer opportunities to eat the upholstery. Not the kitchen, not the treasury, and ideally not someone's lap during council! A loyal creature can track, guard, carry, and maul, my Lord. It may even look majestic beside the throne. That exceeds many courtiers already! Keep bedding dry, bowls filled, and dangerous ends facing visitors, Sire. Pets are servants with better noses and fewer opinions. In several respects... an improvement! Even I can admit that much, Master!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/pets_are_minions_too · working title "Beasts Pen" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D4_SD2_TempleConstruction 101.10

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Pen Restoration


:: Guests Who Can't Leave {"position":"1400,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Some guests are more useful breathing, Master. Let us improve their accommodations.
START LOG: Hospitality is wasted on enemies, Master, but walls are not! Restore this prison with a proper cage, Sire. Some troublesome guests are more useful breathing, at least until questioning becomes repetitive. Information, leverage, bait, examples... such charming possibilities! A living captive can serve beautifully, my Lord. Browns sometimes confuse prisoners with toys. Blister may confuse them with ingredients. Sturdy bars solve both problems! Think of it as mercy with hinges, Sire. The prisoner lives, and you decide for how long. Ah, suddenly hospitality sounds much more appealing!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Place a proper cage in the prison, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Lovely bars, Master! Hospitality has improved enormously.
COMPLETION LOG: Bars, locks, stone... lovely, Sire! The prison is ready, and captives may reconsider their choices in comfort behind reassuringly solid bars. Question them, Master. Trade them, threaten them, display them... possibilities abound! Or simply let them admire the architecture, my Lord. Keep Browns away from keys, and Blister away from unattended drinks. Both mean well in their fashion! Neither improves evidence preservation. Your Tower now offers hospitality with a wonderfully firm departure policy, Sire. Guests may complain, naturally, and that is how you know the locks are working!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/guests_who_cant_leave · working title "Behind the Bars" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D5_MAIN 303.30

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Prison Restoration


:: Swallowed Whole, Armour On {"position":"2400,1900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Armour full of changed blood, Sire. Even corpses are becoming informative!
START LOG: Examine that armoured corpse, Master! Sirok swallowed the raider whole, plate included! The armour trapped blood where the worm could not scatter it. Now that blood has become corrupted essence. It did not merely rot. It changed. Sirok has been feeding on tainted lifeforce through his victims, then growing fat on it. Efficient, in a disgusting sort of way! The plate became a sealed little bottle for the process. Scholars would murder for evidence this tidy. Happily, someone already handled the murder. Look closely, Sire! The victim may tell us what the worm cannot.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Examine the corpse buried in Sirok's nest, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): There it is! Sirok eats corrupted lifeforce. Let us spoil his supper.
COMPLETION LOG: The corpse confirms it, Master! Corruption was already inside the victim's lifeforce. Sirok swallowed both together and grew stronger! The worm is a feeder, not the source. That distinction matters, Sire! Frozen remains kept moving after death. Here, living blood changed before being eaten. Different symptoms, same foul character. Kill Sirok next! When his own essence breaks free, watch where the trace pulls. If the desert is merely another feeding ground, the released power should answer elsewhere. One dead raider has made the worm scientifically useful. I do hope Sirok appreciates the promotion before you kill him!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/swallowed_whole_armour_on · working title "Blood Beneath the Armor" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 107.10

[[Sirok, Evicted]]


:: The Bedtime Story Was True {"position":"3700,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): They made you a bedtime story, Sire. Correct the ending.
START LOG: Spree has spent centuries forgetting what fear meant. Let us repair that, Master! Its guards and iron golem are the town's civic spine. Break them where everyone can see, Master! Five guards first, then the golem. Do not chase farmers through fields or burn the Happy Mule merely for scenery. This lesson needs precision, Sire! The protectors fall, the town watches, and the old bedtime story suddenly sounds less childish. Ah, memory through demonstration! Make them understand why their ancestors once whispered about Overlords. A myth cannot collect obedience, my Lord. A living nightmare can!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill five Spree guards and its iron golem inside the town, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): There it is, Sire! The bedtime story has teeth again.
COMPLETION LOG: Spree's civic spine is broken, Master! The guards are down, the iron golem has fallen, and every comfortable little street has learned the same lesson. The story was true. The Overlord was never merely something for children to fear beneath blankets. He was only absent! Let the town keep its sheep, beer, pumpkins, and beloved potatoes, Sire. They will taste different now, my Lord. Fear seasons everything. No need to erase Spree when terror can live there rent-free. Ah, listen to that quiet! A prosperous town remembering how small it is can be a beautiful thing.
VARIANT [escalated_spree=yes]: They had already known your trade or your leash, Sire. Breaking them afterward makes the lesson sharper: cooperation was a privilege, not protection.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/the_bedtime_story_was_true · working title "Break the Civic Spine" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_spree=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_spree=yes · VOICE: O1 Warrior_In_Spree 104.30

Destruction Path


:: Courtiers, Long Dead {"position":"3500,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Clear the court, Sire! Their invitations expired centuries ago.
START LOG: Time to break this Lost Court, Master. Kill enough hostiles to end the pretense. No secret Imperial government waits behind these doors! No rightful heir is restoring Solarius from a cupboard. Only remnants survived here, hiding while everything collapsed! How noble! The enchantment kept their castle off every map. It did nothing for relevance, Sire! Remove ten of the creatures claiming these halls. Steel explains obsolete privilege remarkably well! Once the court stops objecting, we can search in peace. I suspect their treasure preserved better than their political judgment.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill ten hostile remnants of the Lost Court, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Court adjourned! Permanently, unless someone has dreadful paperwork.
COMPLETION LOG: The Lost Court is broken, Sire. Its nobles, raiders, and servants no longer matter. They hid behind magic while condemning magic outside! Three centuries later, the hypocrisy remains wonderfully fresh! Solarius would be proud, assuming pride survived becoming sludge. Now the halls are quiet enough to rob properly! Somewhere near the throne sits what they protected longest. Find that treasury, Master. Principles rot! Noble property often ages beautifully. If these people wanted their valuables respected, they should have stayed alive, relevant, and considerably better armed.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/courtiers_long_dead · working title "Break the Lost Court" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O2 End_Scene 100.10

[[Finders Keepers, Sire]]


:: Cheat Them Politely {"position":"5200,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Honest trade is ghastly, Master. Fortunately, these are Goblins.
START LOG: No tribute, Sire! Let that surprise them. Make a merchant arrangement where both sides trade freely and each side quietly cheats the other. That should feel natural! Goblins respect a clever bargain more than a solemn oath. Approach their merchants and prove you can do business without turning the camp into a tax office. The profit will still flow, Master, just less predictably. If they overcharge, smile. If we underpay, smile wider. Peace among villains requires shared standards, and shared dishonesty is a sturdy one! Conduct the deal, my Lord. Let nobody leave entirely certain who won, Master.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Make a merchant deal with the Goblins, Sire, without demanding tribute.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): A peaceful bargain, Master! I distrust it already.
COMPLETION LOG: The deal is struck, Sire! No tribute changed hands, nobody knelt, and both sides are almost certainly lying about the numbers. Splendid! The Goblins keep their caravans and their merchant pride. You gain access without wasting soldiers on bookkeeping. They will cheat when they can, Master. We shall do the same, Sire! That is not betrayal, Master. That is cultural respect! Let the cousins congratulate themselves on independence while every profitable exchange ties their camp more closely to your reign. Honest commerce would have been intolerable. This, at least, has enough fraud to feel properly civilised.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/cheat_them_politely · working title "Business Without Tribute" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_goblins=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D4_SD1_TheGlitteringMine 204.10

Peaceful Path


:: Scars Everywhere, Sire {"position":"2200,2950","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Old ruins waking up, Sire! The Cataclysm left very untidy scars.
START LOG: This place reeks of soured lifeforce, Master! The ruin itself is much older. The Great Cataclysm broke more than cities and crowns. Nobody counted every wound it left behind. Sensible folk abandoned places like these for centuries. Now old damage is stirring again... how industrious! Factories, prisons, arenas, drowned halls, buried temples! Any one may have kept something unpleasant sleeping. Investigate them when you find them, Sire. Judge each place by what is actually there. Then kill whatever has mistaken ancient disaster for inheritance! History should lie still unless we order otherwise.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Hear what the Cataclysm left behind, Sire, then investigate.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Old scars, fresh trouble! The Cataclysm remains offensively productive.
COMPLETION LOG: These ruins deserve attention, my Lord, not theories! Corrupted lifeforce can inhabit whatever a ruin provides. Flesh may swell, bones may rise, and machinery may develop ambitions! Prisoners may become much worse company than before. Some places will be stranger still... naturally. Do not force one explanation onto every site! Ancient disasters already did enough careless mixing for us. Enter each scar, study what survived, then kill its master! Very scientific and very thorough! Best of all, it leaves fewer ancient horrors wandering about unsupervised. The past had centuries, Sire. It has enjoyed itself quite enough.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/scars_everywhere_sire · working title "Cataclysm" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 412.10

