Corruption Investigation Path


:: Shulkers, Still Sulking {"position":"4000,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Cities in the wound, Sire! Even here, someone invented neighbours.
START LOG: There are cities at this realm's edge, Master! Actual cities! Towers climb over emptiness while Shulkers cling to every wall. Whoever built here expected the world itself to attack. Sensible people, at last. The place reminds me of creatures driven from safer homes by old Empire purges. I cannot prove these builders were among them, Sire. So we shall inspect before history grows legs and runs away with us. Enter one city! See what endured here, and how long. Ruins remember occupation badly. Occupied ruins can still bite anyone asking rude questions!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter one of the cities at the wound's edge, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Occupied, armed, and still sulking in boxes. Civilization survives everything!
COMPLETION LOG:
The city still lives, Master! Shulkers guard walls above open nothing! Bridges hang where sensible roads refuse to exist. Every stone says its builders expected another disaster. Perhaps they were right, Sire! These settlements are not the wound's source! They prove its margins supported refuge and stubborn life for ages. The Empire once drove magical creatures from one shelter after another. Some survivors may have fled farther than anyone guessed. I will not pretend the stones confess names. They do confess fear! Someone built where even Imperial cleansers would hesitate to follow... and then stayed!
VARIANT [heart_seed=held]: The seed ignores these city walls, Sire, and pulls farther outward.
VARIANT [heart_seed=not_held]: The corrupted current thins here, Master, but still runs beyond.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/shulkers_still_sulking · working title "Cities at the Edge" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VARIANT: heart_seed=held|not_held · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 417.10

[[More to Conquer, Sire]]


:: The Staff Says Obey {"position":"7800,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Find their command staff, Sire. Insects do adore hierarchy!
START LOG: A Myrmex colony lives by command, Master. Better still, it carries that command in a staff! Obtain one and spare us the trouble of teaching every insect individually. Their hierarchy already knows how to obey. We merely replace the voice at the top. Beautifully economical! Desert staff or jungle staff, either will do. Once it rests in your hand, Sire, the colony's order becomes a tool rather than an obstacle. Let the workers work, my Lord. Let the soldiers march. No need to ruin a useful machine simply because it has too many legs. Take the handle and keep the machine!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain a Myrmex command staff, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Staff in hand, Sire! The mound has discovered management.
COMPLETION LOG: The staff answers to you now, Master, and through it the colony's precious hierarchy bends. Wonderful! Myrmex society is built to obey signals without debate, hesitation, or tedious moral reflection. One could almost envy the efficiency, Master. Almost! Keep the Queen where she is, Sire. Keep the soldiers useful! Keep the workers busy. The difference is who directs the pattern. Evernight's magic helped these insects build something larger than themselves. You have done the more important thing and placed yourself above it! Order is so much prettier once it belongs to Evil.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/the_staff_says_obey · working title "Command of the Resin" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_myrmex=Submission · VOICE: O1 D3_MAIN 804.20

Submission Path


:: Turn This Into That {"position":"1900,600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): last trick... make thing stop being itself. cruel little lesson.
START LOG: last lesson, Sssire... real change now. not copy. not split. thing becomes other thing. need fermentation vat... deep enough to bubble, stink, think slow thoughts. put it low. I fell off shelf already... learned lesson. no drinking from vat, even when smell sweet. sweet smell lies. numb tooth confirms. set vat down... then matter loses right to stay itself. nasty? yes... useful too. I like useful nasty. vat whispers better from distance.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): put fermentation vat in lab... and no tasting.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): vat bubbles... old thing gone. new thing smells worse.
COMPLETION LOG: vat ready... warm bubbles, sour hiss. good. now matter changes proper. sulfur, salt, mercury... break, rebuild, repeat, then cross line. I keep notes with dry hand. wet hand makes letters crawl... maybe ink, maybe fumes. quiet vat looks safe. quiet vat lies. I know now. Theurgy goes farther here, Sssire... matter gets less stubborn. I get little dizzy, matter gets very cooperative. fair exchange. I watch from three steps back. four if purple smell returns.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/turn_this_into_that · working title "Crossing the Boundary" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WontBudge01


:: Weed the Garden {"position":"3900,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Weed the garden, Master! Mind the enormous bladed insect.
START LOG: Kill the Queen of Orchid, Sire. Pretty thing, in a murderous way. Like sharpened glass with petals! The reborn magic beneath this shrine will survive her. We are pruning one aggressive bloom, nothing more! That is quite enough for today. A Dark Lord should recognize excessive decoration on sight. Strike quickly and avoid those obvious blades. If Quaver sees the petals, we may never hear the end of it! Gardens are terrible battlefields, Master. Everything looks harmless until it has poison, teeth, or poetry. Fortunately, you are excellent with all three.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the Queen of Orchid and prune this shrine.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Much better! Fewer petals, fewer limbs, excellent improvement.
COMPLETION LOG: The Queen is dead, Sire, while the shrine remains rooted! Evernight's reborn magic will keep growing elsewhere! Forests are irritating that way! Defeat an army and soldiers stay gone. Defeat a garden and it plans next spring! Still, this particular bloom learned permanent manners while its altar and orchids survived! That is a perfectly respectable balance, Master. Beauty offered no protection, and sharp limbs offered only temporary protection! Consider the garden properly pruned. If it grows another monarch, we shall bring larger shears.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/weed_the_garden · working title "Cut Down the Queen" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 701.20


:: Off With Her Head {"position":"7700,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): One Queen, Master. So many dependants. How convenient!
START LOG: Every great hierarchy has a neck somewhere, Sire. The Myrmex call theirs Queen, my Lord! Kill her! The colony's workers and soldiers may look numerous, but all that industry circles one royal centre. Remove it and the mound loses more than a ruler. It loses its future, Master! Very efficient! No need to stamp every tunnel flat when one death can turn order into collapse. Reach the Queen and cut the crown from this insect empire. Evernight's old magic, running wild again, made the colony ambitious. Let us teach it the danger of putting too much importance in one abdomen!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the Myrmex Queen, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Crown removed, Master! The mound has lost tomorrow.
COMPLETION LOG: The Queen is dead, Sire, and the mound's great hierarchy has been cut through at its centre. Excellent! Workers may still scurry, my Lord! Soldiers may still bite! But the colony's future has been severed with one life. That is why crowns are so convenient! Evernight's magic inflated these insects into something almost political. You answered with the oldest political correction available, Master. Let the tunnels empty in their own time. We need not chase every leg. A dead Queen has already done the important work. Ambition looks much smaller once its nursery is gone.
VARIANT [escalated_myrmex=yes]: They once purchased peace with resin or obeyed through their staff, Sire. Killing the Queen afterward proves every arrangement ended where your patience did.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/off_with_her_head · working title "Cut Off the Crown" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_myrmex=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_myrmex=yes · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 604.30

Destruction Path


:: Calamari, Sire? {"position":"2600,2500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Enough worship, Sire! Kill the calamari before it wants an encore.
START LOG: Nerakyss has eaten enough sacrifices, Master! Beast, cult, and corrupted lifeforce now share one dreadful pantry! Kill the Kraken and end this little maritime religion. Avoid the tentacles where possible. I know, excellent advice! When the beast dies, watch what leaves it, Sire. The other concentrations have behaved like feeders, not sources. If Nerakyss does the same, five separate horrors become one very awkward pattern. The cult supplied bodies, blood, and devotion! They forgot lemon, table manners, and basic suspicion. Correct their oversight with violence!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill Nerakyss the Kraken, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Calamari, Sire? No? Wise. The corruption ruins the flavour!
COMPLETION LOG: Nerakyss is dead, Master, and the essence pulls away! It does not settle in the sea. The cult, the captain's changes, and those sacrifices were all downstream effects. Another mouth, not another source. Five concentrations now share that same insistence, Sire. Frozen graves, desert blood, a dead dragon, an ancient prisoner, and this overfed squid all answer elsewhere. Coincidence has officially become too expensive to believe! We have enough evidence now! Bring the traces together and compare them properly. Whatever soured this lifeforce can reach very different places, and it has been doing so for a very long time.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/calamari_sire · working title "Cut the Ocean's Threat" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 Warrior_In_Heavens_Peak 206.10

