:: Their Forges, Our Metal {"position":"6600,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Depth Metal, Sire! Let the drowned Elves forge upward.
START LOG: The Mermorphs forge Depth Metal, Master, which is far more useful than their ancestry. Obtain one of their ingots and make the arrangement plain. Their underwater craft serves your reign now! The village may keep its forges, songs, lanterns, and old memories. We want output! Submission does not require stripping every custom from a people. It requires deciding which direction the useful things travel. Let their smiths work beneath the waves, Sire. Let the metal rise to your hand. A forge that answers on command is a much better monument than another dead Elf!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain a Depth Metal ingot from the Mermorphs, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Their Depth Metal rises to you, Sire. Proper tide!
COMPLETION LOG: Depth Metal is in your hand, Master, and the Mermorph forges have found their proper customer. The sea people remain in their village, but their best craft now answers upward. Excellent! Let them call it duty, treaty, necessity, or anything else that helps them sleep underwater. The metal still comes! Their ancestors once stood outside Everlight's gates and paid terribly for it. Their descendants now stand beneath your authority and keep their forges. A softer history, perhaps, but still yours to shape. Keep the ingots coming, Sire! Sentiment corrodes faster than good metal!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/their_forges_our_metal · working title "Depth Metal on Call" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_mermorphs=Submission · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 300.30

