:: Just a Little Prick {"position":"2300,400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Just a little prick, Sire... followed by entirely different flesh!
START LOG: We have grown flesh, fed flesh, and reduced flesh. Now we tell it what to become! Use a bio-injector to impose a chosen change upon living material, Sire. One small prick, one prepared compound, then the body receives new instructions. Wonderful, my Lord! Bodies become terribly obedient once you bypass the part that objects. This is where biomancy stops resembling gardening and starts resembling command. I almost envy the simplicity... almost. Apply the injector carefully, Master. Random change is nature's hobby, and nature has produced Elves. We can surely manage better than that!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Use a bio-injector to direct a living change, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): There! One little prick, and life takes orders.
COMPLETION LOG: There! Directed life, delivered without speeches, votes, or appeals. Biomancy can now move beyond collecting living matter into shaping what that matter actually does. Use the privilege deliberately, Master. Random mutation is nature's hobby, and its record contains some truly embarrassing work! We can do better, Sire! At minimum, our mistakes will be labelled, contained, and kept away from the kitchen. My little project has become a proper discipline, Sire... which is both gratifying and slightly alarming. Exactly how worthwhile research should feel! If nothing occasionally escapes a jar, my Lord, one is probably not being ambitious enough!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/just_a_little_prick · working title "Directed Life" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 800.10


:: Steel That Screams {"position":"3300,900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Forge ready! Giblet wants DragonSteel. Real metal.
START LOG: Forge ready. Giblet wants DragonSteel now! Not spoon metal. Not cup metal. Not soft trinket metal. Bring one ingot, Master. Giblet checks weight. Ring. Heat. Edge. Then hammer. One hit maybe. Stubborn metal gets more. Truth comes out under hammer. If metal sings, good. If screams, better. If breaks, somebody lied. Giblet remembers liars. Hammer hears truth faster than mouths. Giblet wants honest answer. Bring hot one. Giblet tests before metal cools.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Bring DragonSteel ingot, Master. Giblet tests proper!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): DragonSteel! Strong. Angry. Giblet approves!
COMPLETION LOG: DragonSteel. Good metal! Strong. Rare. Mean. Proper forge stuff. Common steel looks sleepy beside it. Forge restored. Ingot made. Hammer gets worthy work. Giblet respects old craft. New fire matters too. Bring hard armour. Big beasts. Stubborn metal. Anything worth shaping. Giblet makes stronger answers. Metal remembers right hammer. Giblet makes sure it remembers. DragonSteel gets no easy treatment. Good ingot earns more hammer, never less. Hammer should leave memory in every edge.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/steel_that_screams · working title "DragonSteel" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_F FORGE.I_AMB2

