:: Sirok, Evicted {"position":"2600,1900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): The worm has eaten enough, Sire. Evict it from the desert!
START LOG: Sirok has turned corrupted blood into bulk, Master. Very impressive, if one admires enormous digestive failures! The corpse showed what he has been eating. Now kill the Sand Worm and watch what leaves him. Try not to become another armoured sample, Sire. I should hate explaining how the fifth Overlord became a bowel obstruction. When Sirok dies, the corruption may finally show its direction. Worms are simple creatures! Eat, grow, burrow, repeat. That makes them useful witnesses! Remove the witness violently, and let the evidence do the talking!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill Sirok the Sand Worm, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Sirok is evicted, Master! The desert may keep its sand.
COMPLETION LOG: Sirok is dead, Sire, and his essence pulls elsewhere! It shares the northern trace's broad direction instead of settling here. Another feeding ground, then. Another creature swollen by borrowed corruption. The desert gave us blood altered before consumption. The North gave us dead bones moving afterward. Different symptoms, same rotten undertone! I dislike coincidence, Master! It always arrives dressed as innocence. Keep this trace in mind while we test the others. Suspicion is useful! Conclusions are better. With enough dead monsters on the table, even a hidden cause eventually starts looking nervous!
