:: It Twitched! {"position":"2300,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): It twitched, Sire! Progress always looks better when it moves.
START LOG: The cradle can sustain growth. Now prove that growth can leave it! Obtain living flesh, something that has crossed the delightful line between ingredient and participant. Do not worry if it twitches. Worry if it waves. Living material can repair, adapt, and carry functions dead matter cannot. Very useful! It also develops appetites and opinions if given too much freedom, so keep whatever you find securely contained. We are cultivating usefulness here, Master... not founding another faction in the basement. If it learns politics, I am setting fire to the notes!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain living flesh for the chamber, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): It lives, Sire! More importantly, it remains useful.
COMPLETION LOG: It lives! More importantly, it remains useful while living. That distinction has ruined many promising experiments. Living flesh can become material, reagent, vessel, or foundation for things that repair themselves! Delightfully efficient, Sire! The difficulty is appetite. Everything alive wants something, and eventually it starts asking loudly. Our next device solves that problem from the other direction. Give unwanted organic matter something else to chew it first... preferably something without conversation, demands, or teeth pointed at us. If it complains anyway, Master, we shall know the experiment has become far too educated, my Lord!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/it_twitched · working title "Flesh Reborn... Almost" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 Wastelands 140.10

[[Chew, Don't Complain]]


:: Feasts Are for Gloating {"position":"2700,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): one plate? insult! I want table groaning, Masta!
START LOG: One plate too small, make feast, Masta! Meat, roots, pies, stews, stack table edge to edge, let steam hit corridor and smell reach throne! I want Browns staring with wet eyes and both claws visible. Master eats first, everybody learns patience! Black crust means flavour. Black middle means... deeper flavour, yes, exactly. Nobody argues with cook holding cleaver! Build feast worthy of Tower, big enough to make enemies hungry before we kill them!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Make Tower feast, Masta! More dishes, more fire!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Now table looks dangerous! Hot, heavy, beautiful!
COMPLETION LOG: That is feast, Masta, big, hot, loud enough to smell! Good feast looks like victory spread over wood. Named servants get share, Browns get watched share, sleeping tribes get nothing until they wake. Their problem! I keep pans moving and portions larger than excuses. Smoke under rafters happened on purpose. Very advanced smoke. Master eats first, everybody else waits or meets spoon! I guard leftovers like treasure, because leftovers are treasure, only tastier and easier to hide from Browns!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/feasts_are_for_gloating · working title "Food Shaman" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_B RES.RED1


:: Trolls Below, Giants Above {"position":"4900,3800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Trolls below, giants above! At last, government by height.
START LOG: Push through the trolls and reach those giants, Sire. This forest has exhausted nearly every sensible scale. Serpents, towers, hydras, ghosts, frozen palaces... now giants! Queen Fay's refuge has become wonderfully undisciplined. The giants sit above the trolls as though altitude grants sovereignty! Correct that assumption, Master. Reach their heights and make yourself known. Anything tall enough to look down on an Overlord should learn better posture! Do not be distracted by the view. Magnificent vistas are merely battlefields seen before someone starts screaming. I find they improve enormously afterward.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Pass the trolls, Master, and reach the giants above.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Giants reached! Perspective has been corrected satisfactorily.
COMPLETION LOG: You reached the giants, Sire. The Sanctuary has no higher excuse left. Its old refuge survived the Empire, but order did not! Guardians, beasts, and territories hardened into private dangers. Queen Fay's elves remain gone or hidden. Sensible of them, perhaps! You crossed their refuge anyway, Master. Old keepers fell, towers emptied, and ice broke beneath you! Now even the giants have met your shadow. That is quite enough introduction! Let the realm remember who came through! Elves always choose elaborate hiding places. You have a gift for making those places much less private.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/trolls_below_giants_above · working title "Giants Above" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 602.10


:: I May Have Dabbled {"position":"2300,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): A private project, Sire... entirely respectable by my standards!
START LOG: There is one chamber I omitted, Sire. Entirely accidental, naturally! I spent some of the Silence studying living matter, Master. Flesh, growth, organs, adaptation... all that soft machinery lesser minds call disgusting. I call it promising! The notes survived, my Lord, although most specimens did not survive their more ambitious improvements. That may be for the best. Read what I left here, Sire. We might yet persuade life itself to become useful. Oh, do not look so surprised! An old Minion needs hobbies during a Silence that long, especially hobbies with jars.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read my surviving notes, Master. Try not to touch anything damp.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): You found it, Sire! Now try not to look so alarmed.
COMPLETION LOG: So, you found my little project, Master! Nothing scandalous, I assure you, merely flesh made more cooperative, Sire, under the strictest available standards. Very strict indeed! This chamber can continue that work, my Lord, with rather better ventilation this time. Living matter has advantages over iron: it grows, repairs, feeds, and occasionally screams when something goes wrong! Very considerate. We shall begin simply, Sire. Simple by my standards, naturally... which should make everyone else nervous. Do keep an open mind. Preferably not literally. That became messy last time!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/i_may_have_dabbled · working title "Gnarl's Secret Project" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 Wastelands 130.40

