:: Family We Don't Mention {"position":"6900,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Piglins, Master. We do not discuss the family resemblance at dinner.
START LOG: Ah... Piglins! There are old family stories involving Minions and a pig, Sire. We do not discuss them. Ever. Unfortunately, the descendants have built villages, fortresses, and an entire culture around gold, which makes ignoring them impractical. Their pride is considerable. Their taste in relatives is worse. Plant your banner, Master, and keep the genealogy out of conversation. We can barter honestly, shameful though that sounds. We can empty their treasury and establish who truly owns the gold. Or we can remove enough of the family that future gatherings become pleasantly small. No questions about great-grandmothers!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner among the Piglins, Sire. Ask nothing about ancestry.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Banner planted, Master. If anyone says "cousin," deny everything.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner stands among the Piglins, and I have heard no genealogical questions yet. Excellent! Gold gives us three respectable distractions from the family embarrassment, Sire! Trade for it and let everyone pretend commerce has dignity! Take their treasury and teach them who owns wealth beneath your reign. Or break their pride by thinning the village until even the brutes stop boasting. All perfectly sound, my Lord! What matters, Master, is that the Piglins become useful, obedient, or fewer. What does not matter is exactly how Minion ancestry entered the story. Some histories improve when buried very, very deep, Master!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/family_we_dont_mention · working title "Gold in the Netherworld" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 402.10

