Piglin Introduction


:: Honest Barter. Disgusting. {"position":"6800,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Honest barter, Sire. I feel dirty merely saying it.
START LOG: Piglins adore gold, Master! That much, regrettably, may run in the family. Distract one with gold and barter without theft. Yes, honestly! Try to contain your shame, Sire! A peaceful arrangement leaves their pride intact while making their appetite useful. Gold crosses one way, goods cross the other, and nobody needs to admit kinship. There are worse outcomes, my Lord. I am struggling to name one just now, but there must be! Make the exchange, Sire. Let the Piglins discover that dealing with the Overlord can be profitable. Do not let them mistake profit for equality. That would make the next family gathering unbearable.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Barter honestly with a Piglin using gold, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): You bartered honestly, Sire. I shall recover in time.
COMPLETION LOG: The bargain is done, Master, and no one stole the gold back immediately. Remarkable restraint! Piglins can now trade beneath a peace built on the one language they trust completely. Gold. Let them keep their villages and their pride. Let goods pass between us while everyone carefully avoids asking why Minions find them vaguely familiar. The arrangement is useful, Sire, and usefulness excuses many indignities. Even honesty, apparently! If the Piglins begin calling you a trusted partner, change the subject. Preferably to prices. Nothing restores proper distance like haggling over something shiny.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/honest_barter_disgusting · working title "Gold without Theft" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_piglins=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D4_SD5_TheRoyalHalls 200.10

