:: Kindred, Still Meddling {"position":"2400,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): The Kindred again, Sire. Minion zealotry ages like old cheese!
START LOG: That sigil settles it, Master! The Kindred prepared Ashlord's remains! They were a Minion cult obsessed with the extinct Dragon-Kin. Ordinary devotion was apparently too dull! They wanted the old blood returned, scales and all. Their rites failed to raise Ashlord by themselves! Then the Great Cataclysm released enough wild magic to finish the work for them. Lucky little fanatics! Search the tower for the rest of their traces, Sire. If they tended the corpse, they may also explain what happened after it woke. A revived dragon rarely keeps quiet for centuries without leaving consequences.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Examine the marked dragon skull, Sire, and uncover Ashlord's origin.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Ah! Ashlord bred new dragons before the Silence ended. How industrious.
COMPLETION LOG: The Kindred wanted Dragon-Kin restored, Sire. They got something close enough to regret! The Cataclysm raised Ashlord where their rites had failed. Once awake, the dead dragon did not merely survive. He bred new dragons in secret, then released them during the Silence. That explains why these beasts returned after their old Minion kin were gone. The cult opened the door. Catastrophe shoved Ashlord through it. Then Ashlord filled the sky himself. Delightful succession of bad decisions! Kill him, Master! The Kindred began this meddling centuries ago. You can provide the overdue conclusion with considerably less ceremony.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/kindred_still_meddling · working title "Heraldry of the Raised" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 402.10

[[Stay Dead This Time]]


:: Squeeze the Essence Out {"position":"2100,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): ingredient hiding something... I squeeze secret out, Sssire.
START LOG: root looks dull... bug looks stupid. slime looks like slime. still each hides useful bit. honey solvent asks rude question, essence answers. pull one extract, Sssire. no licking first. I did that once... tongue blue for two hours. blue fine colour. wrong tongue colour. sniff from safe distance. safe distance keeps growing... wisdom does that. bring one extract back. I want see what ingredient was pretending not to know. I keep both hands visible.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): pull one extract with honey solvent... no tasting.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): small bottle... big secret. nose says keep cork on.
COMPLETION LOG: there... extract. little bottle, loud secret. ingredient stops hiding. now I know what it can do, maybe what it should never do. brewing gets less guessy... shame, guessing had excitement. label bottle. keep label dry. fumes chew memory and ink both. tasting teaches fast... regret teaches faster. today I hear faint buzzing when yellow catches light. probably cauldron. yellow should not buzz. bottle stays closed until room stops humming at me.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/squeeze_the_essence_out · working title "Knowledge of the Earth" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D2_SD1_TheViridianCaverns 106.20

[[Brew on Purpose]]


:: Again. And Again. {"position":"1900,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): once is luck... twice is clever... three pedestals make rule.
START LOG: do once... luck. do twice... maybe clever. now make it repeat, Sssire. three pedestals: source, target, result. source here... target there... result somewhere sensible. if result moves, duck. set all three and make same change again. no fresh miracle. repetition sounds safe... suspicious word. room tilts little today, pedestals do not. I trust furniture now. strange life. three pedestals, one pattern, same answer. that is science enough for me. I like that arrangement.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): set source, target, result pedestals... all three.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): three stand still... trick repeats. floor still suspicious.
COMPLETION LOG: three pedestals ready... source, target, result. pattern goes here. thing goes there. changed thing comes out... there, ideally. Reformation works because trick remembers itself. less guessing, fewer singed whiskers. maybe less fun. still useful. next we push farther... make thing stop being itself entirely. that part sounds dangerous. good. tea tastes numb today. wait... tea cold, tongue fine. excellent. pedestals stay steady even when walls breathe little. I call that dependable.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/again_and_again · working title "Laws of Repetition" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.GuardHere01

[[Turn This Into That]]


:: Bottled Gibberish {"position":"4500,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): A dead sailor mailed us evidence. Open it.
START LOG: The writing is crude; keep it anyway; fear ruins handwriting before it ruins observation; these sailors recorded impossible catches; then lights. Then altered dreams. Finally, familiar water became suspect. Some writers were already unraveling. That is not grounds for dismissal. Open the bottle. Read every fragment. Which details repeat? Which fears do not? Madness distorts arrangement. It does not automatically invent every fact. I prefer evidence before diagnosis. Preserve the bottle as well.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Open the sailor's message. Read what survived.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Broken language. Consistent fear. There are more records.
COMPLETION LOG: The message preserves a progression; normal water; wrong catches; changed behaviour; then fear. The writer lacked our vocabulary. He still recognized worsening exposure. Other testimony sank with ships and minds. Some remains as Sunken Scrawls. Collect them all. A single frightened account invites doubt. A complete sequence permits appraisal. Bring me the scraps before deciding what the sailors understood. The rot deserves documentation... not mythology. Completeness improves the price of certainty.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/bottled_gibberish · working title "Lost in Translation" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: DREDGE Collector Row 0090

[[Every Scrap Collected]]


:: Both Work for You Now {"position":"5050,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Trade across the feud, Master. Misery shared is almost cooperation.
START LOG: We could make them stop killing each other briefly, Sire. I know, revolting! Trade with both a Dwarf and a Kobold! Commerce forces hands together where history prefers fists. Neither side must forgive anything, Master! Better that they do not! Old resentment keeps prices competitive! We simply make both discover that profit under your shadow hurts less than another tunnel war. This is peace in the narrowest possible sense, Master, which makes it tolerable. Let each side sell while glaring at the other. If they can work because you made the alternative inconvenient, then both are already learning whose terms made the truce possible.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Trade with both a Dwarf and a Kobold, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): They traded, Master! Nobody even stabbed the invoice.
COMPLETION LOG: Dwarf and Kobold have both traded under your arrangement. Miraculously, nobody needs to like anyone, Master. They merely need to recognise that work pays better than reopening every ancestral grievance. This does not make them friends, and thank Evilness for that. Friends become sentimental! Workers remain useful! Let the Hold call it pragmatism. Let the Den call it opportunity. Both are working within the same peace because you made it profitable to do so, Master. Their larger fates remain separate, Sire. Today we settled a feud, my Lord. Tomorrow, who knows? Evil should never overcommit its calendar.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/both_work_for_you_now · working title "Make them Work" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 Tower_ThroneRoomMisc 102.10

Peace Path


:: Maze, Meal, Hydra {"position":"4900,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): A labyrinth and a Hydra, Sire! Elven pest control had ambition.
START LOG: Through the labyrinth next, Master, then kill the Hydra. The maze prefers confusion and repetition. Very sophisticated! After the third identical corridor, irritation does half its work! The Hydra is refreshingly direct. Many heads, much fire, very little philosophy. Beat both and continue deeper into the Sanctuary! Mark your route if possible, Sire. I recommend something more dignified than dead Minions. Browns traditionally disagree with that advice! Still, any route ending at a dead Hydra is technically successful. Try not to get eaten while proving the point.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Conquer the labyrinth, Master, then kill the Hydra.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Maze solved, Hydra shortened! Progress has fewer heads now.
COMPLETION LOG: The labyrinth is behind you, Sire, and the Hydra is not following! Excellent, because these defenses grow stranger with every region! One old keeper wanted traps! Another preferred fire and excessive heads. Ahead, towers brood in the gloom where dead knights and a very large Ghast wait! At least subtlety is dying, Master. Queen Fay's refuge once protected magical creatures from Imperial cleansing! Without its old keepers, protection has become territorial hostility. A familiar institutional problem! Clear the towers next! Perhaps something in this forest remembers its original purpose. I am not optimistic.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/maze_meal_hydra · working title "Maze & Fire" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 604.10

[[Knights, Ghosts, Ghasts]]


:: Purple Means Power {"position":"3100,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): That glow means power, Master... or an expensive accident!
START LOG: Magic deserves better tools, Master! Build an arcane anvil and give enchanted implements somewhere proper to be mended and refined. Ordinary anvils are excellent for ordinary problems. This one is for problems that glow purple and hum when insulted! I advise slightly less hammering than Giblet would. Arcane tools carry power. Power still chips, frays, and fails at dramatic moments. Very educational for observers, Sire... less so for whoever is holding it. Set the anvil here, Sire, and make your spellcraft sturdier. Expensive magic should survive long enough to hurt somebody, my Lord!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Build an arcane anvil for the study, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There! Purple, humming, and considerably less fragile.
COMPLETION LOG: The arcane anvil stands ready! Spellcraft now has somewhere to mend and refine the tools that carry it. Fewer expensive magical objects should fail at exactly the wrong moment. A pity, perhaps, but reliability has its uses! Your study can inscribe spells, forge scrolls, and maintain arcane implements now. That is a respectable arsenal, Master! One question remains... how far can you push spell power itself? We have arranged the ink and iron. Now I want to see the room tremble! Preferably without bringing the ceiling down on anything valuable.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/purple_means_power · working title "More than a Weapon" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_TR IMAGIC.YES2

[[Holy or Bloody?]]


:: The Sand Is Moving {"position":"2200,1900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): The sand is moving, Master. I doubt the desert has learned manners.
START LOG: That disturbance is too regular for weather, Sire. Something enormous is burrowing beneath the dunes! The local stories call it Sirok. Very dramatic. Very hungry. Before we rush into its mouth, search the nest. Large predators scatter evidence everywhere! Bones, armour, half digested travellers... all the usual scholarship. One corpse in particular still wears full plate, Master. Find it before the worm finishes its meal! If corruption reached this place through what Sirok eats, the remains may preserve the trail. I do enjoy investigations where the evidence has already been tenderised!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter Sirok's nest, Master, and investigate the buried corruption.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): There, Sire! Swallowed whole, armour and all. How wonderfully greedy.
COMPLETION LOG: You found the corpse, Master, still sealed inside its armour! Sirok swallowed the poor wretch whole! Greed has finally produced something useful! The plate trapped blood and decay away from scavengers. That makes the remains unusually clean evidence. Ignore the smell. Examine them closely, Sire! Did Sirok merely grow large here? Or did his food carry that same foul essence? If the blood changed before digestion, the worm is another victim with teeth. If not... well, we kill it anyway! Armour, for once, has made this corpse wonderfully cooperative!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/the_sand_is_moving · working title "Movement Beneath the Ruborian Sands" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 Tower_ThroneRoomMisc 304.10

[[Swallowed Whole, Armour On]]


:: Chew, Don't Complain {"position":"2300,600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Waste is matter waiting for a hungrier servant, Master!
START LOG: Waste is material that has not met the right appetite, Master! Set up a decomposer and let unwanted organic matter become useful components instead of decorative rot. It has no mouth, thankfully, but understands feeding perfectly well. Think of it as a Minion with better digestion and no demand for helmets! Give it scraps. Let it work! Keep your fingers out unless you would like them efficiently sorted. Nature uses worms and patience. We have neither reason nor inclination to wait that long, Sire. Let something else do the chewing!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Set a decomposer in the chamber, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Excellent, Sire! Waste goes in, useful material comes out.
COMPLETION LOG: The decomposer is working, Master! Waste enters, useful biological material leaves, and nobody has to ask which piece belonged to what. That is efficiency! Nature does the same through worms, rot, mud, and tedious speeches about cycles. We have removed the waiting! With processed matter flowing, the chamber can support deliberate changes rather than simply feeding whatever grows. Next comes the delicate part... giving living tissue instructions. In this case, delicate means a needle, a compound, and very little concern for consent. Ah, progress! It is so much tidier when the subject cannot object.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/chew_dont_complain · working title "No Mouth, Must Work" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 204.10

[[Just a Little Prick]]


:: Birds Don't Rise Twice {"position":"7300,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): A sun-bird god, Master. Let us test the resurrection clause.
START LOG: Umvuthi looks terribly certain of his divinity, Sire. Kill him, because simple experiments are often best! The Grove sees a sun spirit and imagines permanence, perhaps renewal, perhaps all the usual comforting nonsense. Let the bird fall and wait for the miracle. I suspect we shall have time. His Umvuthana will lose more than a leader. They will lose the thing that made their masks sacred. How educational! Strike down the god, Master. The forest's returned magic made him, and your reign can unmake him. If he rises again, we revise the notes. If not... not a phoenix!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill Umvuthi, Sire, and end the Grove's god.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Still dead, Master! A disappointing phoenix and a very satisfactory corpse.
COMPLETION LOG: Umvuthi is dead, Sire, and the sun has failed to put him back together. Not a phoenix! The Grove's great god lies still while his worshippers face the ordinary problem of faith after evidence. I almost pity them, Master. Almost! That old elven resurgence raised a feathered power here and let it gather masks, rites, and certainty. You cut through all three with admirable directness, Master. Leave the grove to dim around the absence. Gods are impressive until somebody proves mortality with a weapon. After that they are mostly landmarks, Sire.
VARIANT [escalated_grove=yes]: Umvuthi once blessed you or his followers served you, Sire. Killing him afterward makes the hierarchy final: favour and obedience never placed a god beyond your reach.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/birds_dont_rise_twice · working title "Not a Phoenix" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_grove=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_grove=yes · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 502.20

Destruction Path


:: Elves, Hiding in Trees {"position":"4900,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Elven magic again, Sire! Not Evernight's this time, but older refuge magic.
START LOG: The Grove and those Ribbits carry Evernight's reborn stink. This current is different, Master. This current was hidden deliberately, long ago. Queen Fay prepared a Sanctuary for magical refugees! The Empire was busy cleansing anything inconveniently magical. Some creatures escaped into this Twilight Forest instead. Clever, for Elves! The refuge survived separately from Evernight. Its old protections have loosened and twisted with time! Enter the forest, Sire, and see what remains. The elves themselves may be gone or hiding. I shall generously count hiding as their first sensible decision in centuries.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the Twilight Forest, Master, and follow the Sanctuary magic.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): The refuge survived! Its hospitality, unfortunately, did not.
COMPLETION LOG: Queen Fay's Sanctuary still exists, Sire. Its protective magic does too. What failed was the careful order around it. Territories now answer to guardians, beasts, and abandoned duties! Do not confuse this with Evernight's resurgence, Master. Different forest, different history, same elven fondness for consequences. Two ancient keepers block the deeper route! A Naga and a Lich hold their ground, yes, a Lich! Undeath remains terribly fashionable! Remove them both and the Sanctuary should open farther. We came to inspect a refuge. Naturally, the refuge has decided to fight back.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/elves_hiding_in_trees · working title "Old Forest, New Master" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.10

[[The Forest's First Keepers]]

Twilight Forest Start


:: Forgive Me, Old Master {"position":"2600,2300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): Forgive me, old Master... but there is only one throne now.
START LOG: There can be no mistake now, Sire. That is my old Master! He conquered the Infernal Abyss and became its god and prisoner. I once hoped he might escape it... just not like this. Something cracked that prison and let him climb out corrupted, furious, and convinced the throne remained his. I served him well. I remember that much with pride. But the Netherworld chose again, Master. It chose you. Old loyalty cannot divide one throne between two Overlords! Face him. End what the Abyss and this corruption have made of him. Some duties deserve no joke.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill Helvar, the Third Overlord, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Stricken
POPUP (complete): It is done, Sire. An old reign ends beneath the new.
COMPLETION LOG: My old Master has fallen, Sire. I will not pretend that pleases me. He was cruel, capable, stubborn... an excellent Overlord once. The Infernal Abyss claimed him, and corruption changed what escaped. Yet even his ruined power answers the same distant pull as the others. That matters, Master! The Abyss was not the beginning. It was another place touched by whatever force lies beyond these traces. Keep his fall in memory. We have removed a rival and gained another piece of the pattern. One throne remains. One Master sits it. I think he would have understood that, before the prison broke him.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/forgive_me_old_master · working title "One Reign Must End" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 EXP_Endboss_Abyss 300.20

[[One Wound, Many Bleeds]]
[[It Smells Off]]
[[Now the Dead Dance]]
[[Older Than You Think]]
[[It Cracks Everything]]
[[All Roads Bleed One Way]]


:: Oh, You'll Do Nicely {"position":"1600,1800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): At last, Sire! The fifth Overlord stands where Evil belongs.
START LOG: At last, Sire! The fifth Overlord stands in the Dark Tower, and oh, it has been too long, Master. My voice reaches you through the netherrock beneath your feet. That same black stone raised this place and binds it to the Netherworld. I remain in the other Tower, naturally, because advisers survive longer away from falling masonry! Nearly three hundred years have passed since your predecessor's reign ended. During that Silence, kingdoms faded and the Empire became ruins. Magic became something peasants whisper about, and most of your Horde slept. Your halls are battered, my Lord, and your servants scattered. Yet the throne has a Master again! Evil has an address once more. Oh yes... that is how these things begin.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read my first account, Master. A reign deserves a proper beginning.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There we are, Sire! Evil has an address again.
COMPLETION LOG: Ah, your reign has begun, Sire! The old world is gone, but its bad habits survived beautifully. The Dark Tower still stands, Master, and the Netherworld still answers. Browns waited through the Silence for someone worth bruising themselves for! The other tribes sleep, and your halls lie half dead. Beyond the cursed ground, people have grown terribly comfortable. Three centuries without an Overlord will do that. Do not hurry, my Lord. Evil has patience when patience tastes this sweet! Let them enjoy one more birdsong... one more quiet supper. Then remind them what has returned! Peace makes the first scream so much more satisfying.
CODER NOTES: overlord:prologue_and_horde/oh_youll_do_nicely · working title "Our New Overlord" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Throneroom_Intro 100.40

[[Pointy End Out, Sire]]

"Introduction Quest"


:: Guards on a Leash {"position":"3800,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Spree has guards now, Master. Let us improve their employer!
START LOG: Spree's watchmen look terribly proud in their little posts. Such confidence! Recruit one into your service, Sire, and let the rest consider what that means. A guard who answers to you turns every watchtower into a reminder. Protection becomes supervision! Safety becomes permission. No need to flatten the town when its own defenders can carry your authority through the streets! Bring one guard beneath your command, Master. The uniform may stay. In fact, keep it. Nothing unsettles citizens quite like familiar armour saluting the wrong throne. Ah, submission with local tailoring, my Lord! Even the potatoes may notice.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Recruit a Spree guard into your service, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Splendid! Spree's watch now watches on your behalf.
COMPLETION LOG: One guard has changed masters, and the whole town feels different! Spree's watchtowers may still stand, Sire, but the authority behind them now points toward you. That is domination at its neatest. Let the townsfolk keep their markets and their beds. Let them even call themselves protected! They are protected, after all... by men who answer to the Overlord, Sire. A shield can become a collar without changing shape, Master. Very economical! Spree survives, its guards remain useful, and everyone learns that safety is something you permit. Much better than smashing every wall, though admittedly less noisy.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/guards_on_a_leash · working title "Overlord's Watch" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_spree=Submission · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 901.60

Submission Path


:: Half Man, Half Fish {"position":"2400,2500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Your captain is becoming seafood, Sire. Promotion standards have slipped!
START LOG: Look at that captain, Master! Scales, altered flesh, and far too much confidence! He has been changing under Nerakyss's influence. The cult feeds the Kraken bodies, but the corruption feeds back through its servants. Charming arrangement! Kill the captain and inspect what his blood has become, Sire. If his lifeforce carries the same taint as the sacrifices, then Nerakyss is not merely worshipped. It is distributing corruption through the whole little congregation. A proper religion should at least offer better robes. This one offers gills! Finish him before he becomes difficult to fillet!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the corrupted pirate captain, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Half man, half fish, wholly dead! The trail leads to Nerakyss.
COMPLETION LOG: The captain is dead, Master, and his changed essence pulls straight toward Nerakyss! There is our lesson. Repeated exposure did not merely poison him. It reshaped his living body around the strongest influence nearby. The cult called that a blessing, naturally! Cults are wonderfully efficient at mislabelling symptoms. Nerakyss is the great reservoir here, swollen by sacrifice after sacrifice. Kill the Kraken, Sire. Then we can see whether the sea concentration also answers somewhere beyond itself. The captain's body became a sermon while he lived. In death, his essence has pointed directly at the congregation!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/half_man_half_fish · working title "Part of the Sea" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 1000.10

[[Calamari, Sire?]]


:: A God on Retainer {"position":"7200,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Offerings for blessings, Master. A god on retainer has possibilities.
START LOG: We need not worship Umvuthi, Sire. We can hire him! Bring the proper offerings and earn the Sun's Blessing. The Grove calls this devotion, Master. I prefer procurement! A useful power provides a useful service and receives payment. Much healthier than kneeling! If the bird-god accepts the arrangement, let the Umvuthana keep every ceremony they like. You receive the blessing without pretending anyone outranks you, Master. Gods become less troublesome when treated like expensive specialists. Make the offering! If Umvuthi wants reverence as well, we shall consider that an optional extra and decline it with dignity!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Offer tribute to Umvuthi and receive the Sun's Blessing, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Blessing received, Master! A god has discovered contract work.
COMPLETION LOG: The Sun's Blessing is yours, Sire, and Umvuthi has accepted the exchange. See? No kneeling required! The Grove keeps its god! The god keeps his worshippers, my Lord. You gain power because the right offering crossed the right hands. That is a peaceful arrangement I can respect. Almost! Let them call you patron, outsider, honoured guest, whatever preserves their pride. The practical truth is better: a divine power has rendered service to the Overlord. Ah, sometimes even gods understand employment! Keep the relationship transactional, Master. Faith is expensive and notoriously difficult to dismiss.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/a_god_on_retainer · working title "Patron of the Grove" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_grove=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 EXP_D2_Abyss 210.40

Peaceful Path


:: Peace, What is it good for? {"position":"5150,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Peace is terribly overrated, Sire. Three of each should cure it.
START LOG: If peace offends you, Master, the remedy is wonderfully simple. Kill three Dwarven Warriors and three Kobolds. Give each side fresh corpses to add beneath its older complaints! Their feud has survived the Silence because nobody possessed the sense to forget it. We need not improve them, Master! We can improve the quarrel, Sire! Equal blood keeps neither side favoured and both sides furious. This still decides only the tunnel conflict, Sire. Their greater fates remain yours to choose separately. Think of it as maintaining local tradition with six unfortunate participants. Some customs deserve preservation, especially the violent ones!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill three Dwarven Warriors and three Kobolds, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Much better, Sire! Mutual hatred has received fresh funding.
COMPLETION LOG: Three Dwarves, three Kobolds, and not a trace of reconciliation! Excellent, Master! The old grievance has fresh blood now, evenly distributed for maximum resentment. Neither side can claim your favour. Both can blame the other, Master! That is a remarkably stable arrangement! Let them glare across the tunnels and sharpen tools that could have been used productively. Their greater futures remain separate questions, Sire. You have not chosen peace, submission, or destruction for either people here. You have merely ensured their shared history remains loud, bitter, and conveniently distracting. Sometimes the best solution is no solution at all!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/peace_what_is_it_good_for · working title "Peace, What is it good for?" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 201.20

War Path


:: The Dead Keep Poor Company {"position":"2900,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Graves disturbed. Dead marching. Another hand commands them.
START LOG: These dead move with order. I know that rhythm. Restless corpses wander. Soldiers obey. Someone has bound these graveyards. Kill five, Sire. Listen when bindings break. I have kept Netherworld graves through absence and Silence. I know rightful service. This is not it. A rival will gathered abandoned dead. Command became theft. Authority became costume. Put five back down. Their remains will tell us who holds the leash. Death keeps good accounts.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Put down five graveyard dead, Sire. I will read them.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): One command. One mark. A Bone Staff.
COMPLETION LOG: Five returned to stillness. Good. Their bindings match. Old necromancy. Martial discipline beneath it. The hand belongs to a former Fallen Knight. During the Silence, he chose lordship. Graveyards became his domain. The dead became his army. No Netherworld sanctioned him. His Bone Staff carries the claim. Take one, Sire. Break symbol before sovereign. We live. We serve. We die. He kept only command and discarded duty. Such bookkeeping ends badly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/the_dead_keep_poor_company · working title "Places the Dead Keep" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O2 NW_B TOUR.GRAVE2

[[A Stick Worth Stealing]]

Graveyard Found


:: Words With Teeth {"position":"3100,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Enough dusty theory, Master! Make the page bite.
START LOG: Enough dusty theory, Master! Put the inscription table to work. Write a spell into your spellbook and make impossible words repeat themselves on command. Scholars adore pretending this is refinement. It is weapon-making with better penmanship! Ink, symbol, intent, then something unpleasant becomes portable knowledge. The Empire feared magic in public and hoarded methods in private. Charming hypocrites! Use what survived, Sire. A dead wizard cannot object when you improve his notes. Written power is far easier to steal than wisdom, my Lord, and much easier to aim!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Write a spell into your spellbook at the inscription table.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There, Sire! The book has learned something dangerous.
COMPLETION LOG: There, Sire! One spell sits properly in the book, waiting for an excuse. Written magic has crossed from theory into armament. Much healthier! Keep studying the forms. A spoken secret dies with its keeper, but a written one merely changes owners. The Empire burned practitioners and still failed to burn every method. How considerate of them! Their scraps have become your curriculum, Master, and your curriculum has teeth. Continue collecting spells. Knowledge becomes much more respectable once somebody can be threatened with it, especially when the knowledge bites back on command!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/words_with_teeth · working title "Practical Spellcraft" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_TR MAGIC2.10

[[Scrolls, Forged Hot]]


:: Gods Like Snacks {"position":"2500,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Now feed the unseen thing, Master. Divinity does love tribute!
START LOG: If you want a higher power's attention, feed it, Master! Burn Offering Incense upon an altar and see what listens. Old religions buried the transaction beneath robes and solemn voices. Very dignified! Underneath it all, someone burns a gift and hopes an unseen power feels sociable. I prefer calling it payment in advance. Give the offering, but promise nothing extravagant. Especially descendants. Gods become remarkably attentive when somebody else pays the future bill... and remarkably forgetful when the service is due! Let the smoke rise, Sire. We shall see whose nose twitches.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Burn Offering Incense upon an altar, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Composed
POPUP (complete): The incense burned, Master... and something listened.
COMPLETION LOG: Something listened! That is enough for now, Sire. Offerings create a line between mortal and power, though I strongly prefer to call you a customer rather than supplicant. Sacred rites may reach the Mother Goddess. Darker rites may reach something else, and I see no reason to name what has not introduced itself. Learn the forms, Master! Keep the posture upright! Gods adore ceremony because ceremony makes taking things look dignified. We can use that weakness without becoming sentimental about it. If they want devotion, my Lord, they may submit a better offer!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/gods_like_snacks · working title "Prepare the Offering" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 203.10

[[Talk to Fire, Sire]]


:: Profit, Then Ruin {"position":"5300,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Take the profit, Master. Leave the cousins the ruin.
START LOG: Business has one final model, Sire. Hostile acquisition! Prove yourself the Goblin slayer and leave their camp without the part that argues over margins. They understand exploitation perfectly, which should make the lesson almost flattering. Their merchants profit from weakness. Their tyrants profit from fear. You can profit from both by removing the owners! Crush their camp's resistance, Master. Let caravans scatter and ledgers become kindling. If Minions truly share blood with them, consider this a particularly vigorous family disagreement. Every family has one. Ours merely comes with loot and screaming!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Break the Goblin camp and earn their name for a Goblin slayer, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Profit taken, Master! The ruin may keep the receipts.
COMPLETION LOG: The Goblin enterprise is ruined, Sire! Their merchants can no longer haggle over tribute, their engineers no longer choose patrons, and the camp's profit has become salvage. Very efficient! If the cousin story was true, a few Minions may grieve for several seconds. Distract them with something shiny, my Lord! Goblins built tyranny into a business model and assumed that made them competitors. It only made them comprehensible, Master. You found the controlling interest and it was violence. Take what remains useful! Leave the broken carts as a warning to any relative considering entrepreneurship!
VARIANT [escalated_goblins=yes]: They traded beside you or built for you once, Sire. Ruining them afterward reminds every clever merchant that partnership never made them your equal.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/profit_then_ruin · working title "Profit & Ruin" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_goblins=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_goblins=yes · VOICE: O1 D5_MAIN 207.10

Destruction Path


:: Frogs Farm for Us {"position":"6000,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): If the frogs insist on gardening, Sire, we may as well eat the results.
START LOG: Ribbit gardens are disgustingly healthy, Master. Rows of crops, damp soil, happy little gardeners... ugh! Still, food is food! Trade with a Ribbit and turn their prosperity toward your table. No need to trample every flower when the harvest can travel willingly. Let them garden! Let them croak! Let them congratulate themselves on peace. Meanwhile, their produce reaches the Tower, Sire, and your presence becomes part of village prosperity. I can endure a little twee agriculture when supper improves. Make the trade, my Lord. If they offer flowers as well, feed those to something less important, Master!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Trade with a Ribbit, Master, and let its harvest flow toward the Tower.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Their gardens flourish, Sire. At least someone sensible gets the harvest.
COMPLETION LOG: The Ribbits are trading, Master, and their garden wealth now flows beneath your shadow. They call it prosperity! We call it edible influence! Nobody needed flattening, which is disappointing, but the arrangement has virtues. Their village keeps its music and mud. Your table gains the harvest. Every successful season gives them another reason not to offend the dark neighbour who buys what they grow. Very practical, Sire! Let the frogs sing about peace if they insist. A full pantry muffles many indignities. Besides, one cannot conquer on an empty stomach... Gristle becomes impossible!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/frogs_farm_for_us · working title "Prosperity in Ribbit" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_ribbits=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 203.10

Peaceful Path


:: Maracas on Command {"position":"6200,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Take a maraca, Master. If they must make noise, let it be on command!
START LOG: The Ribbits treasure their music, Sire. There is our handle! Obtain one of their maracas as tribute. A small instrument, yes, but symbols need not be large to humiliate properly. Once their music is offered upward, every cheerful rattle carries a reminder: the village sings beneath your permission. Much neater than banning music entirely! A silent frog is pleasant, but an obedient frog can still farm. Take the maraca, Master. Let them keep the songs, the gardens, and the dreadful charm. We shall keep the right to decide when the tune begins!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain a Ribbit maraca as tribute, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Rattle it, Master! The village has learned who calls the tune.
COMPLETION LOG: The maraca is yours, Sire, and the Ribbits understand the little arrangement behind it. Their village survives, my Lord! Their gardens grow! Their musicians still play, Master... when the shadow over them permits it. Ah, much better! Domination need not silence every harmless habit. Sometimes it is more satisfying to own the habit. Let them dance, Master. Let them croak and shake their ridiculous instruments. Every performance now begins beneath authority they cannot ignore. A tribute this small weighs very little in your hand, but a great deal in theirs. That is the proper use of symbolism!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/maracas_on_command · working title "Quiet Village under Shadow" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_ribbits=Submission · VOICE: O2 NW_TR TOUR3.30

Submission Path


:: Shiny. Suspiciously So. {"position":"3300,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Oh, it shines now, Sire! That makes it much more suspicious.
START LOG: The filled Chalice has enough corrupted charge, Master! Time to refine it! We have layered those essences together until their common character can no longer hide. Now force that charge into a Radiant Essence! Yes, radiant. I dislike the name too. Bright things so often expect applause. The refinement should strip away some noise and leave the contamination exposed in a cleaner form, Sire. If something is drawn to that signal, we shall learn whether the taint attracts creatures already suited to it. And if nothing comes... we still own an expensive glowing cup!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Refine the Chalice's charge into Radiant Essence, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): There! Bright, concentrated, and calling to something. Keep your weapon ready.
COMPLETION LOG: The Radiant Essence is stable, Sire, and terribly inviting! Refinement did not remove the corruption. It made the signal cleaner. Something beyond our sight is answering already, Master. I can feel the response tightening around the Chalice. Good! A trap that baits itself saves everyone time! Do not mistake brightness for purity. The power remains soured beneath the shine. We wanted the common thread stripped bare, and now we have it. Hold the essence ready! Whatever comes for it may show us how corrupted power chooses a host, or whether the host chooses it. Either way, kill first and philosophise afterward!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/shiny_suspiciously_so · working title "Radiance for the Vessel" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 107.20

[[The Architect of Chaos]]


:: Break It, Rebuild It {"position":"1900,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): break it careful... not hammer careful. sneaky careful.
START LOG: now matter comes apart, Sssire... careful apart. not smash. need incubator low down... shelves and I had disagreement. incubator warms pieces, sorts pieces, keeps useful bits from becoming soup. take thing apart. save good bits. build again with plan. not creation... sounds too shiny. sneaky reuse. better. set incubator low and leave sticky corner alone. sticky corner belongs to itself now. I do not argue with it. fingers outside... always.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): put incubator in lab... low shelf, please.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): warm, humming... maybe hungry. useful enough.
COMPLETION LOG: incubator ready... soft hum, warm glass. maybe hungry. I feed matter, not fingers. split thing. keep useful bits. rebuild with purpose. sloppy work gives sludge. careful work gives result. very careful work gives result and no rash... best result. kitchen jars stay in kitchen now. Gristle stops shouting. good for ears. next we repeat same change until trick becomes rule. repetition sounds harmless... dangerous sign. harmless words usually bite when nobody watches.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/break_it_rebuild_it · working title "Reassembling Matter" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ItHurts01

[[Again. And Again.]]


:: Healers, Sadly Necessary {"position":"1600,2600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): One Hive remains, Sire. Unfortunately, we need the healers.
START LOG: One sleeping tribe remains, Sire, and unfortunately it is the helpful one. The Blues! Healing sounds suspiciously virtuous, Master, but even Evil needs putting back together. Blues swim, heal, and meddle shamelessly with death's bookkeeping. An Elder Guardian carries old power from the deep. Kill one, my Lord, and its death should jolt the Blue Hive awake! There is a pleasing irony there, Sire. Something dies so our healers may return. Mortis would probably call that balance. I call it convenient! Find the creature and end it. Let the Blues remember who rules.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill an Elder Guardian, Master. Its death should wake the Blues.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The Blues answer, Sire! Death has competition again.
COMPLETION LOG: The Blue Hive wakes, Sire! At last, the four tribes answer again. Blues are poor brawlers, Master, but that was never their charm. They swim where others flail, mend what enemies damage, and retrieve the fallen before rigor sets in. Death grows possessive, my Lord, and Blues are shameless thieves! Browns, Reds, Greens, and Blues serve one Master again. Each tribe is dangerous alone. Together, they become an administrative problem that ends kingdoms! Ah, our preferred sort of administration, Sire. The Horde has all its colours again. Try not to lose them immediately!
CODER NOTES: overlord:prologue_and_horde/healers_sadly_necessary · working title "Restore the Blues" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D3_SD1_TheMoistHollows 103.20

[[Finally, a Proper Horde]]

Blue Quest


:: Stabbing Is an Art {"position":"1600,2400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Now the Greens, Master! Poison and witchcraft should stir that fragrant little Hive.
START LOG: Now for the Greens, Master! Sneaky little wretches, always fond of poison, shadows, and exposed backs. Their Hive needs a properly foul reminder, Sire, something venomous and suitably unpleasant. Let poison enter your blood first. Then kill a witch while its sting remains. Venom and witchcraft together should carry enough malice! If that does not stir them, my Lord, the smell probably will. Greens have always been terribly proud of the smell. Ah, standards differ among the tribes! Wake them, Master. Fair fighting has gone unchallenged long enough, and that simply will not do.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Let poison course through you, Sire. Then kill a witch.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Ah, the Greens! Pungent, sneaky, and awake.
COMPLETION LOG: Ah, the Greens are awake, Master, and still pungent! How reassuring. They are assassins by temperament, Sire, and cowards by excellent sense. They make both qualities wonderfully useful whenever someone exposes a kidney. A Green sees little virtue in a fair fight, my Lord. Why bother when backs, poison, and shadows exist? Browns batter, Reds burn, and Greens make survivors regret turning around! Keep count of your servants, Master. The Greens certainly will... especially when someone else has something shiny. Ah, the old Horde is becoming properly unpleasant again!
CODER NOTES: overlord:prologue_and_horde/stabbing_is_an_art · working title "Restore the Greens" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D2_SD1_TheViridianCaverns 102.30

[[Healers, Sadly Necessary]]

Green Quest


:: Fire, Fury, No Sense {"position":"1600,2200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): The Red Hive sleeps, Sire. Bring it something hot enough to remember.
START LOG: Browns hit beautifully, Sire, but some problems improve when burned first! The Red Hive still sleeps, Master, and we need something hot enough to offend it awake. A blaze rod should do nicely! Blazes carry stubborn fire in their bones, exactly the sort of reminder we need. Take one, my Lord, and bring that heat under your command. If the Hive remembers itself, the little scorchers should answer. If not... I may have to shout. Spare us both that indignity, Sire! Wake the Reds with fire. It is the only alarm they ever respected, and I expect a wonderfully violent morning!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Take a blaze rod, Master. Let its fire wake the Red Hive.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Oh thank Evilness, Sire! The Reds are burning again.
COMPLETION LOG: Oh thank Evilness, the Red Hive burns again! Our little scorchers are awake, Sire, and irritable too. Perfect! Reds shrug off flame and throw it back, Master. Distance means very little to them, and restraint means even less. The world contains far too many things that are not smoking, my Lord. They will take that personally! Browns provide bruises, while Reds provide singed eyebrows and a useful amount of panic. A lovely division of labour, Sire! The Horde is beginning to look respectable again... or at least dangerous from across the room. With Minions, that is much the same thing.
CODER NOTES: overlord:prologue_and_horde/fire_fury_no_sense · working title "Restore the Reds" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 200.10

[[Stabbing Is an Art]]

Red Quest


:: It Didn't Close. Of Course. {"position":"3600,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): The wound remains open, Sire. Of course it does. How obliging!
START LOG: The Anchor is dead, Master, yet the wound remains! Killing its keeper stopped the great concentration, not the injury itself. I suppose expecting ancient reality damage to behave politely was optimistic. Return through the opening, Sire! We know what lies beyond now, and we know the Heart's loss helped shape it. The question is what survives without the Anchor feeding at its centre. Watch the currents. Watch the crystals. Most of all, watch where the corruption still travels. A dead guardian changes the balance! It does not magically repair centuries of damage... regrettably!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Return through the wound, Master, and cross beyond its central scar.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Still open, Master! Then we have more work, and more places to loot.
COMPLETION LOG:
The wound did not close, Sire! Its centre is quieter, but the passage survives! The Anchor was feeding upon the injury, not holding existence together. That is useful! It is also inconvenient! Corrupted currents still move outward through the realm, carrying traces beyond the place where the dragon fell. We can follow them now without that enormous reptile interrupting every thought. Explore farther, Master! The wound has had centuries to become more than one chamber and one guardian. I suspect the outer reaches kept growing while everyone above congratulated themselves on a sealed door. Typical!
VARIANT [heart_seed=held]: The seed pulls through the open wound, Sire, eager for the rest.
VARIANT [heart_seed=not_held]: Without that fragment, corrupted currents still lead us farther outward.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/it_didnt_close_of_course · working title "Return to the Wasteland" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VARIANT: heart_seed=held|not_held · VOICE: O2 End_Scene 100.40

[[It's... Blooming?]]


:: Chasing Storms, Sire {"position":"4500,3600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): The scrawls indicate rocky waters. Go there. Prudence can wait.
START LOG: Enter the rocky waters they described; wrecks gather there; storms do too; sensible captains avoided both; sensible captains left fewer records. The scrawls place altered creatures there repeatedly. They also describe crude rites. Superstition, perhaps. Experiment, perhaps. The distinction interests me less than results. Observe the place before judging the men. Desperate methods sometimes touch real pressures. What answers deliberate action there? Find out. Return with evidence, not courage. Curiosity can replace prudence briefly.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the rocky waters named in the Sunken Scrawls.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): The place matches. Now test the sailors' rites.
COMPLETION LOG: Their geography was accurate; their fear was justified; the water carries altered life and wreckage; something also gathers around deliberate acts; the sailors noticed that. Then they ritualized it. Crude procedure can still be procedure. Reconstruct one rite. Perform it exactly enough to compare outcome. I care little whether you believe their explanations. Belief is cheap. Response is evidence. Let us see what the water does when addressed. The comparison should be instructive.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/chasing_storms_sire · working title "Rocky Waters" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: DREDGE Collector Row 0503

[[Heavy Rites]]


:: Halo or Horns? {"position":"2500,600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Here is the fork, Master... halo or horns, and neither comes with a trustworthy owner.
START LOG: Here is the fork, Master. The Mother Goddess still answers Sacred rites. Something darker and unnamed answers Wicked ones. Perform one path's rite and make the choice real! Sacred does not mean harmless, Sire, and Wicked certainly does not mean loyal! Powers have interests, not friendships. Choose whose gifts suit your reign, then remember who owns the Tower. You are the Overlord, not somebody's decorative servant! Keep your knees straight... and your expectations lower than the altar. We have standards, my Lord, and worship is for people with less authority.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Perform either the Sacred or Wicked path ritual. The first one answered is yours.
EMOTION (complete):
VARIANT [eidolon_path=Sacred]: Pleased
VARIANT [eidolon_path=Wicked]: Relishing
POPUP (complete):
VARIANT [eidolon_path=Sacred]: The Mother Goddess answered, Sire. Take the power and leave the kneeling to Elves.
VARIANT [eidolon_path=Wicked]: Something darker answered, Sire. It offered no name, which is almost polite.
COMPLETION LOG:
VARIANT [eidolon_path=Sacred]: The Sacred rite has answered! The Mother Goddess still listens after all these centuries, Sire. That is reassuring only if one enjoys being watched by ancient powers. Her gift runs bright and ordered. Irritatingly wholesome! Power does not become useless merely because Elves once approved of it! Take what the path offers, Master, and keep your knees unbent. A gift from a goddess is still yours once it reaches your hand. Do not mistake blessing for ownership! She may answer the rite, but you answer to no altar in this Tower!
VARIANT [eidolon_path=Wicked]: The Wicked rite has answered, Sire! Something beyond the signs accepted the call, but it offered no name. A cautious power, then. I suggest we return the courtesy! Its power is dark, willing, and therefore exactly the sort that deserves suspicion! Unknown patrons are like locked chests, Master. Useful, certainly. Safe, never! Take what the path offers, but do not confuse response with allegiance. There is room for one unquestioned authority in this Tower, and it is not hiding behind a ritual sign... however impressive the answer may feel, my Lord.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/halo_or_horns · working title "Sacred or Wicked" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · TAG: eidolon_path=Sacred|Wicked (unset until this quest resolves) · VOICE: O1 D3_MAIN 804.60


:: Sit, Sire. Brood. {"position":"1675,1600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): First things first, Sire! A Dark Tower needs somewhere properly ominous to sit.
START LOG: A Tower without a throne is embarrassing, Sire! It becomes merely a tall inconvenience with stairs. Your seat should explain everything at a glance, Master. Who owns the halls, gives the orders, and gets the best chair? You, naturally! Set a proper necrolord chair where the throne belongs, my Lord. Let the Tower remember its purpose after centuries of neglect. Once you brood above it all again, the neglected chambers can follow. Oh, I have missed proper hierarchy, Sire! Furniture should know whom it serves, and so should everyone else.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Place a necrolord chair where the throne belongs, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Much better, Sire! Now the Tower knows who owns it.
COMPLETION LOG: Much better, Sire! A throne gives ruin direction, and the Tower is stirring around you now. Old chambers are ready for steel, books, cages, and gold, Master. Necessities! The commotion has roused two specialists early, my Lord. Gristle is awake and furious about the kitchen. Blister is awake and smelling faintly medicinal. Their tribes still sleep, fortunately, while these two have slipped the blanket early. One Gristle is noisy enough! One Blister is quite enough to smell. Sit proudly, Sire, and brood magnificently. Everyone else can get to work!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood · working title "Seat of the Overlord" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Throneroom_Intro 100.10

