:: Kill the Big Lizard {"position":"3200,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): There is your Anchor, Sire! Break its crystals, then break it.
START LOG: That dragon is the Anchor, Master, and those crystals feed it! The shards are crystallised magic from the old disaster, gathered around the creature like armour with opinions. Destroy them first. Then kill the dragon! Simple instructions are so refreshing! Do not waste time admiring the scenery, Sire! Every crystal you leave standing keeps power flowing into the beast. Once the Anchor falls, whatever it has wrapped around itself should finally be exposed. I cannot sense clearly through that storm of corruption... not yet. Break the supports, then the reptile. We can investigate the corpse after it stops trying to eat you!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Destroy the Anchor's support, Sire, and kill the great dragon.
EMOTION (complete): Stricken
POPUP (complete): Sire... I can feel it now. The Tower Heart is in there!
COMPLETION LOG: Master... that is the Tower Heart! I know its pull. I know it as surely as the Netherworld knows you. The fourth Master fired it at Empire City, and its released power tore through something already cracked by the Cataclysm. Then the Heart vanished. We never knew where! Now I do! The Anchor crystallised around it and buried its presence beneath centuries of soured magic. With the dragon dead, that noise has fallen silent. Most of the Heart lies deeper in this wound, Sire. But something remains here, close enough to touch. Search what the Anchor left behind.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/kill_the_big_lizard · working title "Sever the Anchor" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O2 Empire_Assault 460.40

[[Evil Always Finds a Way]]
[[A Piece of Home]]


:: Scrolls, Forged Hot {"position":"3100,1000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): A spell on parchment, Sire! Trouble should travel well.
START LOG: Now make the danger portable, Sire! Build a scroll forge and give your magic somewhere to leave the study. A spell fixed on parchment can wait quietly until somebody has a truly dreadful afternoon. How civilized! Shape mana into scrolls, and preparation becomes opportunity. Power made earlier can become catastrophe later, with no need for the victim to appreciate the craftsmanship. I have always admired delayed unpleasantness. It shows patience... and lets one prepare several unpleasantnesses in advance! Put the forge to work, Master. Magic should travel as readily as bad news.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Build a scroll forge in the study, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Excellent! Magic has learned to travel folded.
COMPLETION LOG: Excellent, Master! The scroll forge is ready, and magical trouble need no longer stay home. A scroll stores intent until the proper moment, which is delightfully sneaky for parchment. Keep useful ones close and experimental ones somewhere Browns cannot reach. Bright warning marks sometimes slow them down. Sometimes! Your study can now inscribe spells and press them into portable form, Sire. Much improved! Next we need better tools around the magic itself, because even sorcery becomes embarrassing when its equipment falls apart. Nothing ruins menace, my Lord, like a priceless implement breaking before the screaming begins!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/scrolls_forged_hot · working title "Shape the Mana" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_TR MAGIC1.20

[[Purple Means Power]]


:: Skor's Last Supper {"position":"2600,1700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Skor has chewed his last corpse, Master. Time for dessert to bite back!
START LOG: The frozen dead told us enough, Sire. Skor feeds where corruption has already touched the remains! The Yeti did not create that power. He grew on it, bite by dreadful bite. Now kill him and watch what spills free. A creature that large should make a wonderfully obvious sample! Keep clear of the claws, Master! I prefer my Overlords in one piece, particularly the current one. When Skor falls, the essence should either settle here or pull elsewhere. That distinction matters more than his appetite. Still, do make the death memorable. Gluttons hate leaving leftovers!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill Skor the Yeti, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Skor is finished, Sire! And his corruption is already pulling away.
COMPLETION LOG: Skor is dead, Master, and the freed essence does not remain north! It pulls away with the same wrong insistence we have sensed before. So the frozen hideout was another feeding ground. The animated bones were symptoms, not beginnings. Excellent! One enormous nuisance removed, one useful comparison gained. Keep that direction in mind, Sire! We need every concentration before I trust the pattern. Corruption is slippery when cornered! It loves coincidence, superstition, and frightened people making speeches. We shall give it none of those comforts. We shall give it measurements... and several more dead monsters!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/skors_last_supper · working title "Silence the North" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 101.10

