[[It Smells Off]]
[[Now the Dead Dance]]
[[Older Than You Think]]
[[It Cracks Everything]]
[[All Roads Bleed One Way]]


:: Blessed Silence {"position":"6100,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Ten frogs, Sire. Think of the silence afterward!
START LOG: I have tolerated the croaking admirably, Master. Enough! Kill ten Ribbits and let the swamp learn what quiet actually sounds like. No ancient grievance hides beneath this. No forgotten crime requires vengeance, my Lord! They are simply part of Evernight's latest burst of elven rot, and they have maracas. Surely that is sufficient! Strike the village until song turns to absence, Sire. Gardens without gardeners become wonderfully untidy. Music without musicians becomes blessed memory. Ten deaths should settle the matter. I may even enjoy the swamp afterward... assuming nothing else begins singing!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill ten Ribbits, Master, and silence the village.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Ahhh, Sire. Hear that? Exactly!
COMPLETION LOG: Ten Ribbits are dead, Master, and the garden has finally stopped performing at us. Blessed silence! No maracas. No croaking. No tiny cheerful gardeners asking whether turnips need encouragement. The swamp feels almost respectable now, Master. Evernight's revived forest magic produced these creatures, and you have reminded it that growth is not the same thing as permission. Let the empty beds overgrow, Sire. Let reeds reclaim paths and mud swallow instruments. I will remember the village fondly now that it has stopped making noise. Distance improves so many relationships, Sire!
VARIANT [escalated_ribbits=yes]: They once traded peacefully or played beneath your command, Sire. Their silence now makes the lesson unmistakable: tolerance was yours to grant and yours to end.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/blessed_silence · working title "Silent Garden, At Last" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_ribbits=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_ribbits=yes · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 701.20

Destruction Path


:: Tiny Farmhands {"position":"2900,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Brown hands steal harvest! I want tiny hands, smaller stomachs!
START LOG: Fields need hands, Masta, but Brown hands eat half harvest and call it inspection! Make Crop Critter, tiny worker, tiny feet, hopefully tiny appetite. Let it pick and carry without stuffing onions in helmet. I watch first one close! Cute things steal too, never trust cute near pantry. If it works, good. If it bites tomato and runs, I catch it, season tomato, maybe not worker. Bring one to estate! Small jobs need small hands and I need full shelves!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Bring Crop Critter to field, Masta! I watch every bite!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Ha! Tiny thing works! Browns, observe and feel shame!
COMPLETION LOG: Ha, tiny thing works, Masta! Picks crop, carries crop, no boasting, no helmet full of onions. Better than some Browns, and I want them hearing me! Small hands fit small work. Keep helper moving, keep kitchen full! Cute comes second, useful comes first. Next I want bigger helper, straw body, strong arms, no belly at all. Perfect worker if nobody lights it. NOBODY LIGHTS IT! I am cook, not field arsonist... today. Tiny worker earns place by working, not by looking snack-sized!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/tiny_farmhands · working title "Small Hands for Small Work" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_B RES.RED4

