:: Spree, Still Sheepish {"position":"3700,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Spree, Master! Still sheep, still pumpkins, and somehow considerably fatter.
START LOG: Spree survived, Sire! That little farming settlement has swollen into a prosperous town while nobody sensible was watching. The sheep remain, the pumpkins remain, and the Happy Mule still serves drink. Even the potatoes appear loyal! What Spree has lost is memory! The old Overlords have become bedtime stories, the sort told to frighten children into behaving. How charming! Plant your banner inside the town and let the story acquire armour again. Its fields are rich, its guards confident, and its people comfortable. Comfort makes such lovely leverage. Let us see whether they prefer business, obedience, or a much shorter civic tradition!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner inside Spree, Sire, and make the old story real again.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There, Master! Spree has remembered that bedtime stories sometimes walk back in.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner flies over Spree, Sire! The town has finally placed its old nightmare beside the market stalls. It even has excellent posture! Now choose how the lesson continues! Spree can prosper by feeding your Tower until dependence feels like friendship. Its guards can serve you and turn protection into ownership. Or the town can learn through broken watchmen and a fallen golem, which is wonderfully concise! No path requires them to remember the old Overlords correctly, Master. They need only understand the fifth one. Ah, history is so much easier when the subject is still alive to be frightened by it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/spree_still_sheepish · working title "Spree, Again" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 404.40

