:: Egg Theft, a Classic {"position":"4700,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Steal the egg, Sire! Grand theft infancy is proper Evil tradition.
START LOG: Now steal a dragon egg, Master. Keep it intact! The parents may object rather loudly, which proves they understand property and therefore the insult! A smashed egg is mere destruction. A stolen future is leverage, Sire! Raise the hatchling beneath your authority from the start. It may learn Master before it learns intruder. Do not ask whether owning a dragon is practical, Master, because neither is a throne! Power occasionally deserves wings for the spectacle alone. Everyone understands a dragon overhead. No herald, speech, or second warning is usually required!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Steal a dragon egg, Master, and keep it intact.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The future is stolen! Now comes the part where it grows.
COMPLETION LOG: The egg is yours, Sire, and somewhere a parent is furious! Or inattentive, which also favours us! Raise the hatchling carefully enough to establish authority early! A loyal dragon offers transport, weaponry, terror, and tremendous theatre. Very efficient package, Master, so eventually you should tame one and ride it! Yes, ride it, while I observe from the ground where gravity has behaved reliably for centuries! Architecture also stays put most days! Still... I admit the image has merit. A Master descending from the sky makes border negotiations wonderfully short.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/egg_theft_a_classic · working title "Steal the Future" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 202.50

[[Mind the Landing]]


:: Bribe the Captain {"position":"5600,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): A well-fed Captain, Sire, can become wonderfully reasonable.
START LOG: Keep the Den's Captain supplied, Master, and let the Kobolds do what they already do best. Trade with them! Nothing grand! A few useful exchanges can turn their salvage routes toward the Tower without breaking the Den. The Captain keeps authority, the tunnels keep humming, and we receive the interesting things they drag from forgotten places. Peace through procurement! I can endure it, Master! Kobolds respect practical value more than ceremony, so do not waste a speech. Bring something worth trading, Sire! A Captain with full stores and profitable routes rarely asks philosophical questions about whose reign makes the arrangement possible.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Trade with a Kobold and supply the Den, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Supplies in, salvage out, Sire. Almost indecently sensible.
COMPLETION LOG: The Captain has accepted your trade, and the salvage route now bends toward the Tower. No Den burned, Master! No tunnels collapsed. I suppose restraint occasionally has uses, Sire! Kobolds keep exploring old workings and hauling out whatever history forgot to nail down. You keep first interest in the useful finds. Let them call it commerce, Sire. They are happy, we are supplied, and the Dwarves will be furious merely knowing the arrangement exists. That last benefit is complimentary, my Lord! Peace can be terribly dull, but irritating Dwarves improves it considerably.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/bribe_the_captain · working title "Supply the Captain" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_kobolds=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 202.40

Peaceful Path


:: Read Up, Sire {"position":"4700,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Read the bestiary, Master! Preparation is cowardice only when others do it.
START LOG: Study the book properly, Sire. Dragons vary in element, temper, habitat, and appetite. Also in how much countryside they consider personal. Knowledge will not make their teeth smaller! It may keep you from standing before them wrongly! More importantly, these records describe eggs and young dragons. Some can be raised into loyalty instead of trophies. Yes, Master, this sounds suspiciously like responsibility. Think of it as acquiring siege equipment very early! Siege equipment that grows, eats livestock, and eventually develops opinions. We can manage one of those. Probably.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Study the dragon bestiary, Sire, and learn their habits.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Excellent! You now know exactly how large trouble becomes.
COMPLETION LOG: The book gives us what matters, Master. Nests, eggs, growth, feeding, taming, and weaknesses. Very practical reading! It still does not explain the dragons' return! We will not fill that hole with invented nonsense, Sire. I have seen enough bad prophecies already. What we know is enough for action! Find an egg and take it. Dragons defend their future with admirable violence. That makes stealing it properly ambitious! A hatchling raised beneath your shadow may become far more useful alive! Dead trophies impress visitors once. Living dragons impress them every time they approach the Tower.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/read_up_sire · working title "Take the Measure" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 201.40

[[Egg Theft, a Classic]]


:: Wet Handshakes {"position":"6400,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Aquamarine diplomacy, Master. At least the handshake comes pre-washed.
START LOG: The Mermorphs understand aquamarine, Sire, and valuables translate beautifully underwater! Barter with them. Establish terms without dredging up old tragedies. They do not need the story of how their ancestors became sea people. They need a reason to keep trade moving toward you! Offer value, receive value, and let the treaty remain damp but serviceable. Their village survives, your reach extends beneath the surface, and no one has to pretend Elves became less tiresome in water. Make the exchange, Master! Peace is much easier when everyone is staring at something shiny!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Barter aquamarine with the Mermorphs, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Terms agreed, Master! Wet hands, dry profit.
COMPLETION LOG: The aquamarine has changed hands, Sire, and so have the terms between your reign and the village below. They remain independent enough to feel dignified. You gain trade beneath waters most surface folk barely understand. Very useful! No old accusation was needed, no drowned history reopened. Sometimes forgetting is convenient, Master! Let them remember their elven ancestry and their lanterns while business moves around both. The sea can keep its mysteries, my Lord! We need only ensure some of its wealth surfaces in the correct direction. Peaceful, yes... but at least it glitters, Master!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/wet_handshakes · working title "Terms Below the Surface" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_mermorphs=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 201.20

Peaceful Path


:: Why Is It in the Sky? {"position":"2075,3250","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): An acropolis in the sky, Sire! Even drowning became theatrical for an Elf.
START LOG: Scylla was an Everlight sorceress, my Lord. She stood outside Everlight when the great wave came. The sealed gates saved those safely behind them. Everyone outside received rather wetter treatment! Scylla drowned, but her magic did not settle quietly. Corrupted lifeforce caught that power and twisted it hard. Now she rules this absurd height above the sea! Typical Elf. Even catastrophe requires scenery and a grand entrance! Reach the Acropolips and kill her, Sire. Whatever carried her upward can keep the architecture. I only want the sorceress brought permanently back down.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Reach the Acropolips, Sire, and kill Scylla.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Scylla has fallen! Gravity finally received proper recognition.
COMPLETION LOG: Scylla is finished, Sire, and none too soon! She was once an Everlight sorceress beyond those sealed gates. The wave drowned her with the people outside. Her magic gave corrupted lifeforce something potent to seize! The Mermorphs adapted together, but Scylla became a singular horror. What returned belonged properly to neither sea nor sky. It scarcely belonged to Elf anymore, either! Everlight's gates protected those already safely within. Everyone else learned how selective sanctuary can be. Charming people, Elves! Always saving exactly the correct side of a door! The floating ruin may keep its altitude, Master. Scylla has finally lost hers.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/why_is_it_in_the_sky · working title "The Acropolips" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 703.20


:: Mind the Fumes, Sire {"position":"2100,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Sssire... room too clean. needs cauldron, fumes... better.
START LOG: Sssire... alchemy room feels dead. dry stone, clean air... horrible. need glass cauldron. clear glass, no cracks, low enough to sniff safely. then roots, slime, dust, bugs... secrets everywhere. I sniff first. taste almost never. right side of tongue works again... mostly. put cauldron here and bubbles start talking. bottles hiss too. sometimes words... maybe fever. still informative. nose says room needs brewing. nose rarely wrong. nose currently burning... also informative.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): put glass cauldron here... I brew proper.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): cauldron ready... ah! nose burns. room alive.
COMPLETION LOG: cauldron ready... room smells right now. bitter, sharp, little sweet. sweet worries me. shelves ready. bottles ready. one mixture under table moved... leave it alone. I can pull extracts, brew known mixtures, make poison, make cure, make poison pretending cure. useful room, Sssire. keep hands off black-string bottles. red-string too. no string means I forgot what bottle does... those worry me most. left eye stopped blinking by itself. progress! small progress still progress.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/mind_the_fumes_sire · working title "The Alchemy Den" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_PoisonNoHurt

[[Squeeze the Essence Out]]

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Alchemy Restoration


:: Dwarven Junk, Awake {"position":"1925,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Dwarven machinery, Sire! Worse, the junk has developed initiative.
START LOG: A Dwarven war factory, Master! I remember their taste. Huge gears, hotter furnaces, and absolutely no restraint. The Harbinger was machinery before this place went quiet. Now corrupted lifeforce has put motion where none belonged! Old metal has learned enough life to become troublesome. How very Dwarven of it! Push through the factory and smash the thing flat. I like their engineering best when we are stealing it! Failing that, dead and bolted down will do nicely. Machinery should make weapons for its Master, Sire. It should never begin applying for the position.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Break the Harbinger, Sire, and quiet the ancient factory.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Back to scrap! A dignified improvement for Dwarven machinery.
COMPLETION LOG: There, Master! The Harbinger is respectable scrap again. Dwarves built the frame for war long ago. Corrupted lifeforce supplied its ugly imitation of life! No hidden Dwarf was pulling levers behind a wall, which is a pity because I enjoy blame! The factory itself offered everything the taint needed. Metal, mechanisms, armour, and an enthusiasm for violence! It merely made the old engine continue beyond reason! That is the danger of excellent workmanship, Sire. Occasionally the rubbish survives its owners! Still, a hammer cures many engineering disagreements. You have demonstrated that splendidly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/dwarven_junk_awake · working title "The Ancient Factory" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 200.10


:: The Architect of Chaos {"position":"3300,3600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Something answered our shiny bait, Sire. How wonderfully predictable!
START LOG: There it is, Master! Netherman, the so-called Architect of Chaos, came for the Radiant Essence! Grand title. Dreadful manners. Our little beacon worked. Kill it and watch what happens to the power inside. This creature seems built from concentrated force given appetite and shape. Very useful, Sire, and extremely rude! If it collapses back into raw power, we learn something important. The contamination may travel through lifeforce without belonging to lifeforce itself. That could explain why different bodies carry the same wrongness. First comes the traditional scientific method. Hit the specimen until it stops objecting!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill Netherman, the Architect of Chaos, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Down it goes! And look, Master, the corruption survives the host.
COMPLETION LOG: The Netherman collapsed, Sire, but the power did not die with it! There is our answer. The corruption can inhabit lifeforce without being lifeforce itself. The creature carried it, shaped it, perhaps even fed upon it, but did not create it. Once the host failed, the tainted power simply remained. Very impolite! Very useful! This helps explain our other concentrations, Master! Different creatures can express the same contamination in wildly different ways. Flesh is only the vessel. The wrongness travels deeper. Keep the refined evidence secure! We have separated host from poison, which is more than most healers manage before breakfast!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/the_architect_of_chaos · working title "The Architect of Chaos" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 414.10


:: Gashling's Little Circus {"position":"1400,1800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Gashling is ready, Sire! Unfortunately, so are his lungs.
START LOG: Ah, an arena, Sire! The old Dungeon taught us something useful. Defeated enemies become entertaining when defeated twice! Battle Rock improved the idea under Gash, Master, and his bloodline kept the habit. Gashling has inherited the enthusiasm and apparently none of the indoor voice. And the lungs, apparently! Give him a command drum, my Lord. Let beasts and challengers make regrettable decisions here. Practice matters, Sire, and so does recreation. Nothing relaxes the Horde like watching something enormous discover its evening has gone terribly wrong!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Give the arena a command drum, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): The arena is open, Sire! Fairness remains outside.
COMPLETION LOG: The arena is open, Master! Gashling is already shouting, so noise must be hereditary. Good, Sire! Here you can test strength and revisit old enemies. Dangerous creatures can become evening entertainment, my Lord, after they have earned the privilege. The Horde will adore it from a safe distance! Do not call it sport, Sire. Sport implies fairness. This is rehearsal for conquest with applause! Blood on the sand helps the atmosphere. Gashling insists the next bout will be louder. Somehow, I believe him. Keep the drum handy and the cleaners farther away.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/gashlings_little_circus · working title "The Arena" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Tower_Dungeon 100.20

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Arena Restoration


:: Twenty Crops, Zero Minions {"position":"2900,400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): proof time, Masta! twenty crops, no Minion claws near them!
START LOG: Time for proof, Masta! Let Crop Critters harvest twenty crops, no Brown helping while chewing evidence, no hidden onions, no boots flattening rows! Twenty shows estate works while Browns and named servants do other jobs. Keep little workers moving and I count every crop, one, two, three, no cheating! If one stops, glare. If glare fails, spoon! Twenty clean harvests, no Minion hands, then kitchen knows field can keep pace with my appetite!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Let Crop Critters harvest twenty crops, Masta! I count!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): TWENTY! No Minions! Check Brown pockets anyway!
COMPLETION LOG: Twenty crops, zero Minions, good! Field works while Tower does other things, crops come in, kitchen stays fed, seedlings stay upright. No Brown swears turnip was missing already, not with me counting! If any says he helped, pockets first, helmet second, cheeks third. Estate carries own weight now, Masta. Less chasing thieves means more cooking, more shouting, more fire! That is proper progress. Kitchen wins when field stops needing babysitting, and I get more time to threaten dinner into behaving!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/twenty_crops_zero_minions · working title "The Assisted Estate" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_B RES.RED3


:: Raiders With Real Estate {"position":"4100,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Raiders with walls, Sire! How terribly respectable of them.
START LOG: Heaven's Peak left descendants behind, Master. Apparently centuries of plague, collapse, and bad manners turned guards into raiders! They call their stronghold the Bastille now. Fortified walls, armed bands, ravagers, clay golems... very industrious! They answer to strength because strength is the only law they still respect. Convenient! Plant your banner there, Sire, and make them decide what sort of strength you represent. Their raids can be pointed elsewhere. Their beasts can be brought under your command. Or their fortress can learn what walls are worth when the enemy is already inside. I rather like this lot. Awful people!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner at the Bastille, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The Bastille has noticed you, Sire. Good. Raiders should know their competition.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner stands at the Bastille, Sire! The raiders have not mistaken it for decoration, my Lord! They understand force! You have arrived carrying rather a lot of it. Now decide what use these unpleasant descendants of Heaven's Peak should serve. Point their raids away from useful settlements and call it a border pact. Take command of their beasts and make the fortress serve directly, Master! Or break their proud little military order until fear replaces loyalty. Any choice suits Evil, Sire, provided you remain above them! Raiders make excellent neighbours when somebody else decides where they raid!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/raiders_with_real_estate · working title "The Bastille" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D1_SD4_Castle_Spree 300.10

[[Burn the Bastille]]

[[Raid Where I Point]]

[[Blow the Horn, Sire]]

Pillager Introduction


:: A Stick Worth Stealing {"position":"2900,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Find the Bone Staff, Sire. False crowns have handles.
START LOG: The staff is declaration. It is also a tool. Bone holds command well. The pretender marks his graveyards through it. Take one, Sire. Do not mistake possession for mastery. Necromancy requires measure. Sacrifice. Boundary. He ignores all three. We will not. Bring the emblem. I will read its pattern. Every false crown leaves a seam. Every seam can split. Death records vanity with admirable patience. Symbols are convenient that way.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain one Bone Staff, Sire. Bring me his emblem.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): The staff points home. A prison awaits.
COMPLETION LOG: The staff bears his mark. Repeated. Insistent. Childish. Its command travels through the graveyards. The name behind it is clear. He fashioned absence into legitimacy. He called himself lord. The staff also carries direction. His prison is fortress, court, tomb. He expects challengers. Perhaps he craves them. Corpses make poor audiences. Enter his prison, Sire. Give the pretender company. Then take it away. Let him hear our answer approaching. Soon.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/a_stick_worth_stealing · working title "The Bone Staff" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.20

[[RSVP to a Lich]]


:: Still Burning, Poor Knight {"position":"2325,3250","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): An Empire knight still burning, Master! Even I call that excessive.
START LOG: Ignis was an Empire legion knight, Sire. Then the Great Cataclysm caught him in this arena. He burned alive and somehow missed the ending. Corrupted lifeforce turned that endless fire into strength! So now one dreadful moment has lasted centuries! Efficient cruelty, certainly, but terribly poor administration. Enter the Burning Arena and finish the matter yourself. He has suffered long enough to become everybody else's problem! I almost pity him... almost. Give the knight the ending history forgot, Master. Then perhaps the furniture can stop catching fire whenever he objects to visitors.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the Burning Arena, Sire, and kill Ignis.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): At last, the knight stops burning! Someone reassure the furniture.
COMPLETION LOG: Ignis has finally gone out, Master! He was an Empire knight when catastrophe found him. Corruption stretched one burning death across centuries of violence. No priest planned that resurrection, and no cult called him back! The disaster simply refused to finish its work. There is almost something admirable in such persistence... from here. I doubt Ignis enjoyed the distinction! The arena may cool now, Sire. Another Imperial weapon has finally remembered how death works. Poor knight, dreadful masters, dreadful retirement, dreadful pension plan! At least you supplied the last benefit personally.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/still_burning_poor_knight · working title "The Burning Arena" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 101.10


:: Only One Dark Lord, Thanks {"position":"2900,3600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): End the pretender, Sire. Death has heard enough titles.
START LOG: The Lich stands at the centre. Kill him. Strength does not grant office. Discipline does not grant office. Longevity certainly does not. He found an empty age. He mistook it for permission. Necromancy preserved him. Pride crowned him. Neither chose him. Strike through both, Sire. Return his graveyards to silence. One Dark Lord is sufficient. Competition may sharpen rule. It must also know when to die. Today, teach it. Titles require maintenance.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the Graveyard Lich, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The title is vacant again. Permanently.
COMPLETION LOG: The Lich is ended. His command breaks. Bone Staffs become sticks again. The dead lose formation. Good. He copied power's surface. Servants. Territory. Fear. Immortality. He missed its cost. Service binds both ways. Death ends all claims eventually. We live. We serve. We die. He refused the last truth. The first two followed. The grave has him now. I doubt it will promote him. Death for life? Not today. Today, death keeps what arrived.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/only_one_dark_lord_thanks · working title "The Corrupted Champion" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.QUIT2


:: Gods Don't Stay Buried {"position":"2200,3125","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Ruboria buried a god here, Master! Evidently the hole lacked ambition.
START LOG: This pyramid is Ruborian, Sire, and very old. What sleeps beneath it is older than these raiders. Do not mistake it for the Forgotten God! This Ancient Remnant belongs to Ruboria's own buried past. Worship stopped, the tomb closed, and that should suffice! Of course it did not! The Cataclysm disturbed even graves built for deities! Corrupted power gave the remains enough motion for trouble. Enter the pyramid and bury it properly, Master! Ruboria keeps far too many secrets underground. I object when those secrets stand up and demand a second reign.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the cursed pyramid and kill the Ancient Remnant.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Buried twice! Perhaps divinity will respect the arrangement now.
COMPLETION LOG: The Ancient Remnant is down again, Sire! Ruboria had old powers before these present squabbles. This thing was one of them. It served no Forgotten God and carried no Abyssal claim. Good, because one ancient deity is quite enough paperwork! The Cataclysm shook a tomb that should stay silent! Corrupted lifeforce supplied strength where worship no longer could. So an old god became everybody's modern inconvenience. Very inconsiderate! Perhaps future peoples should mark sacred graves more clearly, Master. Enormous pyramids apparently communicate the wrong message. They seem to say, 'Important treasure and sleeping horror. Please enter.'
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/gods_dont_stay_buried · working title "The Cursed Pyramid" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 EXP_D4_Abyss 200.20


:: Scavengers Downstairs {"position":"5700,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Kobolds, Master! Little scavengers living in somebody else's inheritance.
START LOG: Beneath the old Dwarf tunnels, Sire, we have Kobolds. Warriors, engineers, enchanters, pirates... industrious little vermin! They moved into abandoned workings during the Silence and made a Den of the place. The Dwarves call that theft. The Kobolds call it salvage. I call it excellent use of empty property! Their Captains keep the Den together, and their cleverness is worth more than their manners. Plant your banner, Master. We can supply their Captain and keep salvage flowing, claim their engineers, or salvage the salvagers themselves. Do admire the irony before choosing. It took centuries to mature!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner in the Kobold Den, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The Den has a new shadow, Master. Mind your pockets.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner hangs in the Den, Sire, and the Kobolds are already deciding whether it can be repurposed. Charming! These tunnel-folk took what older powers abandoned. Then they made it useful again! A sensible philosophy, provided they remember who is older and more powerful now. Their Captain can be supplied into cooperation. Their engineers can work under your authority. Or the entire Den can discover what salvage feels like from the other side! There is also that tedious feud with the Dwarves, Master. Once both parties are in view, we can decide whose definition of property becomes official.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/scavengers_downstairs · working title "The Den Below" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 401.10

[[Salvage the Salvagers]]

[[Theft or Salvage?]]

[[Bribe the Captain]]

[[Clever Little Scavengers]]

Kobold Introduction


:: He Rebuilt the Hall {"position":"2400,2300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): Ah... I know this hall, Sire. I know who rebuilt it.
START LOG: Now I am certain, Master! This hall belongs to memory. The third Overlord used spaces like this, and the hand behind this copy knew them intimately. His name was Helvar. He conquered the Infernal Abyss after defeating the Forgotten God. The victory became a prison. The god cursed him to rule that place forever. I had hoped my old Master might escape one day... naturally. I did not hope to find his taste in architecture buried beneath us. Go deeper, Sire! If Helvar rebuilt this hall, then something of him escaped the Abyss before we arrived.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the rebuilt hall, Master, and face Helvar's old reign.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Helvar lives, Master... if that ruined thing can still be called living.
COMPLETION LOG: There he is, Sire. Helvar, my old Master, escaped the Infernal Abyss! That same corruption has twisted him badly, but I know the posture, the armour, the fury. He still believes the throne is his. I cannot entirely blame him. Eternal imprisonment encourages poor perspective. Still, the Netherworld chose another Master while he was gone. That choice stands. Whatever cracked the Abyss gave Helvar a road out, then poisoned the traveller. We will learn more after he falls. For now, Master, remember this. He was once worthy of the title you bear. Treat the killing accordingly!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/he_rebuilt_the_hall · working title "The Door to an Old Reign" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O2 Ambient_NW G.ANY8

[[Forgive Me, Old Master]]


:: Gods Are Just Landlords {"position":"2500,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Religion, Master! Let us see what still answers when properly bribed.
START LOG: Religion, Sire! One of civilization's more profitable habits. Signs, offerings, solemn faces... then someone asks for power. Set a proper worktable here, Master. We shall see what still answers, my Lord, and what price it imagines itself worth. The Mother Goddess remains difficult to ignore, and something darker may listen as well. Sensible Evil reads the stains before signing anything! Gods are landlords with better thunder, Sire. Pay only when the property proves useful. Never confuse an answer with affection. Divine beings become terribly possessive about that!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Set a Magic Workbench in the chamber, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The chamber is ready, Master. Keep your knees for practical purposes!
COMPLETION LOG: The chamber is ready, Master! Symbols can be shaped here, rites prepared, and offerings arranged with suitable dignity. I recommend skepticism, Sire. Divine power is useful, but useful is not trustworthy, as history keeps proving! We have seen enough jealous powers and foolish worshippers, my Lord. Learn what answers you. Take what serves, Sire, and keep your knees for practical purposes! If some great presence demands devotion, remind it who owns the Tower. Politely, of course... until politeness becomes inconvenient. Oh, gods do hate a tenant who reads the terms.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/gods_are_just_landlords · working title "The Eidolons Chamber" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 EXP_D5_Abyss 501.10

[[Souls, Crystallised]]

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Eidolon Restoration


:: The Fourth's Old General {"position":"2325,3125","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): Maledictus... I know that name, Sire, and prison has not improved him.
START LOG: Maledictus served my fourth Master as a general. That name I remember, Sire. After the reign fell, someone locked him here. The Frosted Prison was meant to hold indefinitely! Such a brave little word, indefinitely! Corruption reached the cells while he waited inside. Whatever prison did to his temper, this did worse. Find the old general and end his sentence yourself. Officers become terribly attached to expired commands! I have watched enough reigns to know that, Master. Rank ages badly when the army is gone. Death, however, keeps a remarkably clear chain of command.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Find Maledictus, Sire, and end his command permanently.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): General dismissed! Very permanently, which suits the current administration.
COMPLETION LOG: Maledictus is finished, Master. He outlived my fourth Master's reign and spent the Silence in prison. Ice, resentment, and corruption kept him company afterward! A dreadful little staff meeting! I will not claim the cell created everything you fought. It merely gave the taint a patient, furious host! The old general still carried himself like command remained his. Command does that to some creatures, Sire! They mistake memory for authority. Fortunately, you have supplied a correction he cannot appeal! The Tower has enough inherited history already. We need not retain every former officer as furniture.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/the_fourths_old_general · working title "The Frosted Prison" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 EXP_Endboss_Abyss 300.10


:: Thaw the Snow Queen {"position":"4900,3600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Yeti first, Snow Queen after! Cold apparently has a hierarchy.
START LOG: Break through the Yeti, Sire, then reach the Queen. The beast guards the ascent with muscle and appetite. The Snow Queen trusts ice, height, and freezing visitors! Disappoint them both! This frozen dominion belongs to the Sanctuary's broken order. Nothing more needs inventing, Master. The forest has had centuries to become peculiar unaided! Climb through the beast's territory and enter her palace. Different floors, same lesson. A crown is not authority when my Master arrives armed! Mind the cold, Sire. Pride keeps nobody warm, although burning enemies sometimes helps.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Defeat the Yeti, Master, then bring down the Snow Queen.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The Queen has thawed permanently! Upward we go.
COMPLETION LOG: Yeti down, Queen finished, Sire! Her glacier has lost its court. Another private kingdom inside the old Sanctuary collapses nicely. The path now climbs toward stranger heights! Trolls hold the lower ground. Giants occupy whatever they can call above. Apparently ordinary scale offended somebody here, Master! Magic, chaos, or unrestrained elven architecture may explain it! I care less with every staircase. The important thing is this: the giants are large enough to hit very satisfyingly. Keep climbing!
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/thaw_the_snow_queen · working title "The Frozen Queen" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 606.30

[[Trolls Below, Giants Above]]


:: Spree's Favourite Customer {"position":"3600,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Trade, Sire! A revoltingly peaceful way to tighten a leash.
START LOG: There is a gentler way to own Spree, Master. Feed its appetite! Trade with the townsfolk until your custom becomes part of their prosperity. Ten good exchanges should begin the habit. Grain moves, goods move, coin moves... and soon everyone has forgotten which direction dependence travels. Delicious! Do not call it charity, Sire. Charity expects gratitude. This expects repeat business. Become their favourite customer and supplier, my Lord, until full granaries quietly depend on the Dark Tower. They may even thank you. Try not to laugh in their faces. A long con wilts when watered with obvious gloating!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Trade with Spree ten times, Master. Make prosperity depend on you.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Excellent, Sire! Spree calls it commerce. I call it a leash with receipts.
COMPLETION LOG: Spree's granaries are full, Master, and your trade is woven through them. How wholesome! Farmers prosper, merchants smile, and the Tower has become difficult to remove without making everyone poorer. That is the sort of peace I can tolerate. No chains, no torches, no screaming... merely dependence with a friendly handshake. They still own their fields, Sire. They still choose what to sell. They simply make those choices beneath your shadow now. Wonderful! Let them boast about prosperity, Master! Every boast makes the arrangement harder to abandon. Tribute is so much sweeter when the payer insists it was negotiated, my Lord!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/sprees_favourite_customer · working title "The Full Larder" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_spree=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 203.10

Peaceful Path


:: A Rat's Crown Jewel {"position":"3700,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): The Gem of Ratlantis exists, Sire... oh dear.
START LOG: You found a genuine Gem of Ratlantis, Master! So Ratlantis graduates from joke to administrative problem. The craftsmanship is disturbingly good, thanks to too much intelligence, cheese, and no supervising Overlord! Predictable result! Its stories mention machines and flying contraptions. They also mention a Rat Baron ruling the skies. I am drawing a line here, Sire. We may investigate him and steal valuables, but we will not admire the architecture! Follow the Gem's trail and find this Baron. Maintain standards while doing so. Someone in this reign must.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Follow the Gem, Master, and seek the Rat Baron.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Ratlantis has a Baron! Naturally the little horror flies.
COMPLETION LOG: The Gem was telling the truth, Sire. Ratlantis built far beyond tunnels and cheese stores. Tiny paws turned confidently toward machinery and flight! Dwarves would approve, which condemns the idea immediately! The Baron is their proudest surviving ambition. A flying ruler with entirely appropriate modesty problems! Find him, Master, and bring him down. Call it war, piracy, pest control, whatever pleases you. We are restoring proper proportions! Rats may work, steal, and even bargain for cheese! Rats do not receive air superiority. Some laws should be universal.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/a_rats_crown_jewel · working title "The Gem of Ratlantis" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 701.30

[[Depose the Rat Baron]]


:: Small, Fat and Greedy {"position":"4900,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Small, fat, greedy... Master, something about them feels terribly familiar.
START LOG: These are Gnumus, Sire! Small, round, hungry, and surrounded by food. Why does that sound familiar, Master? They have no idea their ancestors were Halflings, which may be the first useful thing forgetting history has achieved! Centuries of gluttony magic left them changed, but not cured of appetite. They trade, craft, hoard vintage tools, make rifles, adore cheese, and carry doubloons as though greed needed decoration. Plant your banner, Master! We can revive their craft, bind them with debt, or end the whole swollen little branch. Whatever happens, do not mention Halflings! I want to enjoy the resemblance in peace!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner in the Gnumu settlement, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Banner planted, Master! The little stomachs have noticed us.
COMPLETION LOG: The Gnumus now know your banner, Sire, though thankfully they still know nothing of their ancestry. Let that remain our private joke! Their workshops hold useful old craft, their merchants understand appetite, and their shamans wrap indulgence in ceremony. Plenty to work with, my Lord. Help their vintage craft flourish and make prosperity serve you. Finance them until debt becomes obedience. Or remove the settlement and let gluttony meet the grave at last! They believe themselves a people with a future, Master. Naturally! Everyone does before an Overlord begins considering the available options!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/small_fat_and_greedy · working title "The Gnumu Settlement" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 411.10

[[Old Craft, New Master]]

[[Debt Is a Leash]]

[[Gluttony, Meet Grave]]

Gnumu/Halfling Introduction


:: Our Ugly Cousins {"position":"5300,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Goblins, Sire! Greed with carts, contracts, and an unfortunate family resemblance.
START LOG: Ah, Goblins! Merchants, extortionists, caravan thieves, and enthusiastic owners of other people's labour. Almost respectable, Master! Minions insist Goblins are cousins, Sire. Goblins appear willing to believe anything that improves a bargain. There is no proof, naturally, and I recommend keeping it that way. Their camps run tyranny as a business. Excellent instinct, irritating competition! Plant your banner, Sire, and let these ugly relations discover a larger enterprise. We can trade while both sides cheat politely, place their engineers under your patronage, or take the profits after ruining the firm. Family occasions are always so complicated!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner in the Goblin camp, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The cousins have noticed us, Sire. Hide the good silver.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner hangs over the Goblin camp, Master, and nobody has stolen it yet. Promising! Their merchant tyranny already understands greed, coercion, and the useful flexibility of morality. They may be cousins to Minions, or merely ugly enough to start the rumour. Either way, we can work with them, my Lord! Trade without tribute and enjoy the mutual cheating. Sponsor their engineers until their cleverness arms your reign. Or leave the camp ruined after taking everything worthwhile! Business offers so many paths, Sire! The Goblins may even respect you for choosing the most profitable one. I certainly will, Master!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/our_ugly_cousins · working title "The Goblin Camp" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 Tower_Awakening 104.20

[[Profit, Then Ruin]]

[[Cheat Them Politely]]

[[Patron of Ugly Engineers]]

Goblin Introduction


:: Not Quite Dead, Fido {"position":"4100,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): The grave may return it, Sire. Not always unchanged.
START LOG: Use the collar's thread. Call once. The rite may restore cleanly. It may not. Grave-cold flesh can still remember. Do not judge first by warmth. Judge recognition. Judge service. Judge the bond. Flesh can be repaired later. Loyalty is harder. I have seen perfect corpses hold nothing. I have seen ruined forms remember everything. Perform the rite, Sire. If your companion returns changed, we address the change. We do not punish the return.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Restore the fallen companion, Sire. Living or grave-touched.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): It knows you. Enough, for now.
COMPLETION LOG: The companion returned. The bond found home. That is the first measure. Breath may follow. Warmth may follow. If death still clings, another rite can clear it. If not, the crossing is complete. Do not make such reversals casual, Sire. Death gives life weight. Yet loyalty freely given carries weight too. This servant crossed because a true path remained. Keep it close. Remember the threshold. Do not make Mortis process paperwork twice.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/not_quite_dead_fido · working title "The Grave Gives Something Back" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.60

[[Death, Politely Refused]]


:: A Cup Worth Filling {"position":"3300,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): A Great Chalice, Sire! Finally, corruption gets proper tableware.
START LOG: We need a vessel, Master. That Great Chalice will do beautifully! One tainted essence tells us very little! Several together may expose what they share. Place the Chalice somewhere safe, Sire. Keep it away from the Browns! Yes, they would drink it. No, I am not guessing. Once set, feed stronger essences into the vessel. Then compare how the corruption behaves when concentrated. A cup for poison, a Tower full of Minions, and taint tugging at the stone... almost proper Overlording again! Proper vessels make dangerous research look respectable, which helps enormously!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Place the Great Chalice, Sire, and prepare it to receive essence.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Excellent, Master! A respectable cup for thoroughly disreputable power.
COMPLETION LOG: The Chalice is ready, Sire! Its wards are strong enough to hold what we pour into it, and its shape should keep the essences from dispersing. Very thoughtful craftsmanship! We shall reward it with corruption! Gather a Great Essence and charge the vessel properly, Master. I want the tainted layers pressed together until their shared nature becomes obvious. Separate traces can lie by looking different. Concentrated traces have fewer places to hide! Keep the Minions away from the rim! If one falls in, we shall learn something, certainly, but I would prefer experiments that do not require mops.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/a_cup_worth_filling · working title "The Great Chalice" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 1404.20

[[Fill It to the Brim]]

Essence Found


:: Fill It to the Brim {"position":"3300,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Fill the Chalice, Master! Let us make the poison introduce itself.
START LOG: Now we give the vessel substance, Sire. Bring a Great Essence and a filled goblet! Together they should charge the Chalice beyond decorative menace. Watch how the power behaves as it gathers. Corruption hides comfortably in weak traces, Master! Concentration leaves it fewer shadows. If the vessel holds, we can force the gathered power toward a cleaner, brighter state and expose what the taint has been hiding. If it does not hold... the crater may still be educational! The Chalice was built for excess! Fortunately, excess remains one of our better disciplines.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain a Great Essence and a filled goblet for the Chalice.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Full to the brim, Sire! Now we squeeze the mystery until it shines.
COMPLETION LOG: The Chalice is charged, Master, and the layers are agreeing with one another! Not pleasantly, of course! Their common taint is concentrating toward a single character beneath all the differences. That gives us something we can refine! Force the charge into a Radiant Essence, Sire! Brightness may strip away the muddle without cleansing the corruption itself. Think of it as washing mud from a knife. The knife remains a knife! Once refined, the signal may attract whatever naturally answers this power. Then we shall have a new specimen, a clearer comparison, and possibly another mess on the floor. Progress!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/fill_it_to_the_brim · working title "The Great Essences" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 Tower_HeartIntro 100.50

[[Shiny. Suspiciously So.]]


:: A God With Feathers {"position":"7300,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Evernight has grown a god, Sire. Elven rot is getting ambitious.
START LOG: Evernight's old magic regrew without an Overlord stamping on it, Master. Predictably, it has developed ideas above its station. This grove worships Umvuthi, a sun spirit with feathers and a following of masked Umvuthana. A god, they say! How charming! The masks matter almost as much as the bird. Plant your banner among them, Sire. We can trade offerings for its blessing, make the masked followers answer to you instead, or discover whether this sun-bird rises twice after death. Evernight used to produce Elves, my Lord. I had not realised the forest could become more pretentious!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner at the Grove, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Your banner stands beneath their god, Sire. An instructive arrangement already.
COMPLETION LOG: The Grove has your banner now, Master! Umvuthi still shines. The Umvuthana still wear their masks. Both now have you looming nearby! Excellent! Their god can become a useful contractor through offerings. Their masked followers can learn that a Master outranks worship. Or the sun spirit can die and settle the question of divine permanence personally! This whole grove sprang from Evernight's wild return, Sire, another patch of elven rot flowering into something self-important. We may as well cultivate it, command it, or pull it out by the roots. Gardening has never sounded so tolerable!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/a_god_with_feathers · working title "The Grove and its God" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 EXP_D2_Abyss 100.20

[[Wear Their Faces]]

[[A God on Retainer]]

[[Birds Don't Rise Twice]]

[[Elves, Hiding in Trees]]

Grove Introduction


:: Hunt the Hunter {"position":"4300,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): A hunter noticed you. Flattering, yes? Kill him.
START LOG: Hunters adore categories; vampire; monster; prey. Such tidy little words. Curiosity would exhaust them. One has chosen you, Sire. He expects fear, hiding, predictable hunger. How provincial. Disappoint him. Kill the hunter. Let him discover that your night began with a throne already beneath you. I have watched certainty masquerade as courage for ages. Remove certainty and the costume slips. Cruel? Perhaps. But education should leave an impression. He volunteered for the lesson.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the vampire hunter.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Hunter hunted. Ah, symmetry can be beautiful.
COMPLETION LOG: He expected a vampire; he met you; that error killed him; hunters survive by studying habits. Feeding. Hiding. Panic. You brought command instead. Très mauvais for him. His fellows may struggle to classify the remains. Let them. Confusion is healthy in enemies. Now choose what this condition becomes in your hands. Power without style is merely appetite. You have never suffered that limitation. I am curious what you will add next.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/hunt_the_hunter · working title "The Hunter" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: IWTV S02E07 cue 584.2

[[Blood Has Its Price]]


:: Mind the Landing {"position":"4700,3600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): A dragon beneath the Master! Excessive, dangerous, absolutely appropriate.
START LOG: Tame a dragon and ride it, Sire! Subtlety has limits. Arriving from the sky on obedient firepower exceeds them beautifully. The creature must truly accept your command, Master. Merely tolerating your weight until murder becomes convenient will not do! Once it obeys, take wing and look down properly. Walls seem smaller from above. So do rulers behind them! One piece of ancient wisdom, Sire: landing counts as flying! Many impressive careers forget that final detail. Try not to join them. The Tower roof would also appreciate some warning.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Tame a dragon, Master, then take to the skies.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): The Master takes wing! Kindly avoid landing through the Tower.
COMPLETION LOG: You rode a dragon under command, Sire, and I admit the effect is magnificent! Villages shrink, fortifications show weak points, and witnesses reconsider negotiations before landing! We still lack evidence for why dragons returned. That mystery remains where it belongs, Master, unanswered! What matters is that one now answers you! Giblet will hear about this eventually. Then the forge will start hammering something absurdly large! I can almost hear it already... wonderful! For now enjoy the view, because power rarely gets such excellent scenery!
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/mind_the_landing · working title "The Master Takes Wing" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 402.30

[[Dragons Make Great Bellows]]


:: Blood Has Its Price {"position":"4300,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Power asks a price. Vulgar power asks upfront.
START LOG: Choose your first vampiric power; do not confuse choice with submission; courts, cults, bloodlines, priesthoods... all insist power belongs to whoever grants access; how adorable. Power belongs to whoever survives possessing it. Take what suits you. Leave doctrine for creatures needing permission to feel eternal. Which gift fits an Overlord? I would not insult you by deciding. Surprise me, mon cher. Hunger is common. Taste is rarer. Choose beautifully, if possible.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Choose your first vampiric power at a Vampire Altar.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There. Hunger has learned technique.
COMPLETION LOG: You chose power and remained yourself; encouraging; vampirism will sharpen some instincts; others will become inconvenient. The night is full of predators who mistake age for importance. Time only lets vanity ferment longer. You were dangerous before your blood changed. That is why I watch. What will eternity add to a reign already in motion? I expect excess. I hope for elegance. Gratitude is unnecessary. Obedience would be disappointing. Do try not to become boring.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/blood_has_its_price · working title "The Price of Power" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: IWTV S03E05 cue 148


:: Her Majesty, the Bug {"position":"3100,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Her Majesty is a bee, Sire! Monarchy has suffered enough.
START LOG: There she is, Master. The Queen Bee herself! Her entire court runs on pollen, honey, and optimism. Get close enough to inspect her domain. Avoid becoming part of royal catering. She is not some beast from a recent catastrophe. This ridiculous kingdom functions perfectly well on its own! That almost makes it worse! Natural sweetness leaves nobody convenient to blame. Study the Queen, Sire. Something powerful concentrates around her realm. I can smell useful magic beneath the flowers. Find what the hive protects, and please do not begin respecting the insects.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Approach the Bee Queen, Master, and inspect her domain.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): She guards an essence! At last, something useful among flowers.
COMPLETION LOG: The Queen's domain confirms it, Sire! This hive condenses its magic into essence. Light, pollen, honey, buzzing, all packed together. I expect it smells unbearably pleasant. Take it, Master! If we must endure cheerful magical paradise, we leave richer! The Empire failed to cleanse this realm long ago. Good. Their failure has become productive! I would call that poetic, but flowers are already involved. Obtain the essence and keep your hands away from the Queen herself. We want the prize, not an international incident with bees.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/her_majesty_the_bug · working title "The Queen's Domain" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.40

[[Bottled Sweetness. Ugh.]]


:: Depose the Rat Baron {"position":"3700,3600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Bring down the Baron, Master! Before rodents formalize air power.
START LOG: The Rat Baron mistakes altitude for sovereignty, Sire. Correct him! Kill the flying little tyrant before this becomes doctrine. Never underestimate creatures building machines to their own size! Dwarves taught us that lesson painfully well. Small engineers still make large explosions! Once the Baron falls, we leave Ratlantis immediately. No sightseeing, souvenir cheese engine, or admiring tiny fortifications, Master! Back to a world where rats stay near floors! Civilization has suffered enough experimentation. Depose him, then find the way home before somebody invents a rat navy.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the Rat Baron, Sire, and ground his ambitions.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): The Baron has fallen! Gravity restores a little dignity.
COMPLETION LOG: The Rat Baron is dead, Master, and his aerial ambitions are wonderfully grounded! Do not linger, because every minute here makes cheese engines look more normal! That way lies madness, Sire! Return to the surface and restore proper scale. Our tame rats can remain useful workers. Ratlantis can remain very far away. We have seen enough of its machines and architecture! More than enough, because some discoveries become private embarrassments guarded by threats! This one gets the threats, so home, Master, before I start understanding their engineering!
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/depose_the_rat_baron · working title "The Rat Baron" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 611.20

[[We Never Speak of Ratlantis]]


:: Oh No. Frogs. {"position":"6100,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Frogs, Master. Musical frogs. Elven rot has developed a sense of humour.
START LOG: Evernight grew back while nobody was crushing it, Sire, and now the old forest magic has begun producing consequences. These are Ribbits! Frogs with gardens, music, and maracas. They find all this charming! Elven rot, Master! Plant your banner in their village before somebody composes a welcoming song. They are gentle, productive, and offensively cheerful. We can make their gardens feed your table, take their music as tribute, or finally introduce the swamp to blessed silence. Every option improves the place. Some merely improve it more noisily than others!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner in the Ribbit village, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The frogs have noticed you, Master. Unfortunately, they are still singing.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner stands among the Ribbits, Sire! The village remains damp, green, musical, and almost aggressively pleasant. I am enduring it bravely, Master! Their gardens can prosper, Sire. Better still, they can feed your table! Their maracas can become tribute, so every song reminds them who decides when music starts. Or we can remove ten singers and see how picturesque the swamp feels without croaking! The Ribbits are another bloom from Evernight's old forest magic, Master. Leave them no illusions about who rules beyond the garden fence. Harmony is tolerable only when Evil holds the conductor's stick!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/oh_no_frogs · working title "The Ribbit Village" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 200.10

[[Maracas on Command]]

[[Frogs Farm for Us]]

[[Blessed Silence]]

[[Elves, Hiding in Trees]]

Ribbit Introduction


:: The Rift's Doorman {"position":"2500,3200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): A guardian with no kingdom I recognize, Master. How reassuring.
START LOG: This citadel feels wrong in a different way, Sire. The sentinel carries no history I recognize. No lost army, old cult, or forgotten species shows through! It seems shaped around the damaged place itself. As though pressure learned to grow teeth... charming! The Ender Guardian stands watch over an edge I cannot name! Kill it, Master, but look carefully afterward. A doorman without a known door deserves suspicion. Especially when nobody remembers building the house! Whatever purpose made this thing, it has guarded it very faithfully. Let us reward such dedication with dismemberment.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill the Ender Guardian, Sire, then inspect what remains.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): The guardian is gone. Somehow, Master, that is less reassuring.
COMPLETION LOG: The Ender Guardian is destroyed, Sire. Its residue remains thoroughly unpleasant. I can find no older creature beneath it! No prisoner, soldier, beast, or machine shows through. The sentinel seems to have formed for this place alone! Something here wanted an edge defended, Master. What lies past that edge remains unclear! I will not invent an answer merely for elegance. Elegant answers get Masters killed! We know one useful thing now! The corruption here behaves like a guard. Anything ancient enough to grow its own sentry deserves remembering... and watching very closely.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/the_rifts_doorman · working title "The Ruined Citadel" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 EXP_D2_Abyss 210.15


:: The Sea Keeps Secrets {"position":"2200,2500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): That ship reeks of worship, Sire. Worship and fish. Mostly fish.
START LOG: The ocean trace ends at that ship, Master! I smell blood, brine, and organised stupidity! A cult has been feeding something beneath the water. Nerakyss, they call it! Their captain shows the first changes already, and I doubt bad cooking explains the scales. Search the ship, Sire! Find how the sacrifices are prepared and what the creature gives back. The sea hides evidence well, but cultists compensate by writing everything down and decorating it. Bless them! If the corruption here moves through sacrifice, the captain may be our cleanest link between worshippers and whatever is waiting below.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Enter the Kraken ship, Master, and investigate the corrupted cult.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): A changing captain and a hungry Kraken. Subtle cult, Master!
COMPLETION LOG: The ship gives us the pattern, Sire. Sacrifices go down. Corruption comes back up! Nerakyss has become the centre of a very efficient little faith. The captain is changing under its influence, and the crew treat that as favour instead of warning. Religious people can be wonderfully economical with suspicion. Kill the altered captain next, Master! His blood should tell us whether the taint runs through the servants as well as the sacrifices. If it does, Nerakyss is not simply eating corrupted lifeforce. It is spreading corruption through those who feed it. Then we introduce the congregation to consequences!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/the_sea_keeps_secrets · working title "The Sea Has Been Keeping Something" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 702.10

[[Half Man, Half Fish]]


:: Netherworld Scrap Metal {"position":"2075,3125","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Netherworld engineering has learned to walk, Sire! Furnaces need stricter boundaries.
START LOG: Ah, the Soul Forge, Master! Heat, metal, souls, and dreadful confidence. Very Netherworld. The Monstrosity inside began as a contraption. Corrupted lifeforce gave it far too much persistence. Now it mistakes movement for purpose and crushing for thought. I dislike machinery with opinions, Sire. Particularly opinions about my Master's bones! Break it apart and return this forge to ordinary hazards. Fire should burn, metal should clang, and furnaces may explode festively! None of them require ambitions. If the thing had remained scrap with legs, I might even admire it.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Smash the Netherite Monstrosity and reclaim the Soul Forge.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Scrap metal again! The Netherworld immediately feels more sensible.
COMPLETION LOG: Much better, Sire! The Monstrosity is a heap again. The forge supplied metal, heat, and admirable violence. Corrupted lifeforce supplied the refusal to stop! Flesh was never required here, Master. Give the taint a machine built to crush things! Apparently it will happily continue the original instruction forever! Efficient, in a revolting sort of way. I prefer infernal machinery obedient and politically inactive. Let Giblet argue with metal if he likes! Metal should never argue back. The Soul Forge may now return to producing respectable burns, smashed fingers, and weapons for the proper owner.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/netherworld_scrap_metal · working title "The Soul Forge" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 700.20


:: Books? How Quaint. {"position":"3100,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Books, Sire! Let us make them dangerous enough to justify the dust.
START LOG: Books, Sire! Shelves, ink, parchment... scholars do love furniture before throwing lightning at people. Much better, Master! Set an inscription table here, my Lord, and let this study become useful again. The old Empire feared magic loudly while using it whenever convenient behind locked doors. Such delightful hypocrisy! There should be scraps worth stealing, Sire. We can improve them and point them elsewhere. Why perform tedious scholarship when dead scholars already did it? Knowledge is power, and stolen knowledge saves time!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Set an inscription table in the spell study, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): There, Sire! Scholarship has finally become threatening.
COMPLETION LOG: There, Master! The inscription table is ready, and the study already looks more dangerous. Spells can be recorded, refined, and carried, Sire, without relying on some wandering sage. Eventually they can become tools worthy of your hand! Do not grow sentimental about books, my Lord. Scholars insist knowledge belongs to everyone. Nonsense! Knowledge belongs to whoever keeps the library, Sire. In this case, that would be you. You have the Tower, the shelves, and alarming magical furniture! I believe that settles the academic debate rather neatly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/books_how_quaint · working title "The Spell Study" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 800.10

[[Words With Teeth]]

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Spell Room Restoration


:: Dwarves, Still Digging {"position":"4500,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Dwarves, Master! Angry beards, old claims, and paperwork carved in stone.
START LOG: The Dwarves survived after all, Master. Of course they did, Sire! Angry beards on legs are difficult to eradicate completely! This Successor Hold claims continuity with the old Dwarf realm. Apparently ancestry is a receipt nobody can challenge! They still forge excellent metal, hoard old claims, and remember enough history to be annoying. Their ancestors built war machines, my Lord! Their descendants prefer bureaucracy with anvils. Plant your banner, Master, and let them weigh two kinds of continuity: their own, or yours. We may back their claim, make the Hold your vassal forge, or take their fire outright. Such rich little choices!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner inside the Successor Hold, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The beards have noticed, Master! Now let us discuss continuity.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner stands in the Successor Hold, Sire, and the Dwarves are already measuring precedent. Wonderful creatures! They treat ancestry like armour and paperwork like siege equipment. We can use both, Sire. Recognise their old claim in exchange for access to their craft. Let their precious continuity survive beneath your throne. Or kill the warriors, remove the Forger, and remind them that a forge owes its fire to whoever can keep it! Their old realm is gone, Master. The Hold remains. That makes continuity negotiable... particularly when the negotiator has Minions and very little patience.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/dwarves_still_digging · working title "The Successor Hold" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 100.20

[[A Vassal Forge]]

[[Their Fire Is Yours]]

[[Signed in Stone]]

[[Theft or Salvage?]]

Dwarf Introduction


:: Something Big Below {"position":"2200,3250","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Something enormous feeds beneath the drowned reef, Sire. Naturally it does.
START LOG: There is a sunken city below, Master. These waters took the fourth reign's great wave. Bodies, magic, and ruined reef settled together afterward! A deep beast found quite a banquet waiting. The Leviathan fed on drowned, corrupted lifeforce for years! It grew accordingly... and without manners! Descend into the city and kill it, Sire. The sea preserves every problem beyond convenient reach. It hides corpses, ruins, monsters, and occasionally entire mistakes! At least desert horrors stay where one can stab them dry. Bring this one an overdue lesson in shore leave.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Descend into the Sunken City and kill the Leviathan.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The deep is quieter, Master! Still wet, unfortunately.
COMPLETION LOG: The Leviathan is dead, Sire. Good riddance to it! This was no sleeping sea god demanding worship. It was a beast that found catastrophe plentiful! The wave left bodies, magic, and broken reef below. Corrupted lifeforce turned that feast into monstrous growth! The Leviathan simply kept eating, Master. Sensible instinct, appalling table manners! Its great advantage was abundance and nobody interrupting dinner! You have corrected both. The drowned city can keep its silence now! With luck, the sea will wash away the blood. It certainly has enough water for the job.
CODER NOTES: overlord:scars/something_big_below · working title "The Sunken City" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 702.10


:: Every Scrap Collected {"position":"4500,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Bring the complete record. Fragments behave better under pressure.
START LOG: Collect every Sunken Scrawl; alone, each is merely distress; wrong eyes in a catch; voices over calm water; crews refusing safe inlets. Rites attempted after reason failed. Together, the pieces may describe spread. I do not require sane authors. I require sufficient coverage. Preserve contradictions. They are often useful. Bring the complete set. Then we can distinguish panic from pattern. Incomplete archives flatter whatever theory arrives first. I prefer the slower conclusion.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Collect the complete set of Sunken Scrawls.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Complete. The sea kept a ledger after all.
COMPLETION LOG: The scrawls align more than expected; rot appeared gradually; catches changed first; currents followed; then people handling those catches changed too. Some fled. Some prayed. Some became fascinated. One place recurs across accounts: rocky waters, storms, wrecks, concentrated anomalies. Go there. A record should eventually face its geography. Otherwise, one merely curates stories. Stories improve themselves far too readily. Geography is less cooperative than paper. Water tends to object to neat conclusions.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/every_scrap_collected · working title "The Sunken Record" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: DREDGE Collector Row 0495

[[Chasing Storms, Sire]]


:: Burn It Scientifically {"position":"1900,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): need clever fire... thinking fire, Sssire. not dinner fire.
START LOG: Sssire... room needs clever fire. not forge fire. not cook fire. thinking fire... ugly little flame with rules. Theurgy takes thing apart, sorts bits, makes thing new. sneaky craft. I approve. put pyromantic brazier here. then sulfur, salt, mercury start giving secrets. I sniff smoke from far side now... learned distance. room stopped spinning yesterday. good sign? maybe. heat matter until truth comes out. scientific burning... fancy words, nasty smell.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): put pyromantic brazier here... make matter confess.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): clean flame... too clean. I do not trust polite fire.
COMPLETION LOG: brazier burns clean... suspiciously clean. still, lab wakes. sulfur, salt, mercury next. break matter, rebuild matter, repeat it, change it. neat little path... if gloves hold. keep bottles away from flame. keep Gristle's pots farther. I handle fire while Green hive still sleeps... named hands can work before tribe wakes. flame handles me little too. fingertips tingle. only two purple now. yesterday four. excellent trend. no need tell Gnarl unless fingers fall off.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/burn_it_scientifically · working title "The Theurgy Lab" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_WontBurn

