Theurgy Restoration


:: Not the Heart. Yet. {"position":"1400,1600","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Master! Road stone! Not Heart, no, but still very good stone!
START LOG: Master, I found road stone, and no, not Heart, I know, too small, wrong hum, but waystone still good! It remembers places and I remember places and soon Tower remembers too! Put one here and home stays found, yes? Then I run far and come back and run farther and come back faster! Grubby dug Gates before roads knew where they went. I can do road-stone work too! Maybe not Grubby-fast yet, but I keep digging at problem until problem gives up!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Put waystone in Tower, Master! Make road remember home!
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Yes! Waystone set! Home stays found, easy!
COMPLETION LOG: Waystone set, Master, yes, Tower knows road now and I can go far and come back without losing home behind me! Not Heart, no, nobody fool me with that, but useful stone, very useful! More stones mean more paths and more paths mean more places and more places mean more holes, and I like holes! Grubby could find a Gate through anything. I find roads through things. Different work, still good work! Next route, Master, and I race it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/not_the_heart_yet · working title "The Tower Heart?" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 Hunting_Grounds 114.30

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Waystones Restoration


:: Elves, Somewhat Soggy {"position":"6500,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Elves, Sire... only wetter. Somehow they found a new indignity.
START LOG: These sea people remember being Elves, Master, which is already unfortunate. Long ago, when the fourth Overlord's rising seas struck the reef, Elves caught outside Everlight's closed gates drowned and changed. Their descendants became Mermorphs, my Lord! They remember the old blood, but not the Overlord or what caused their drowning. Better for everyone, Master! They keep a final spark of elven light alive beneath the water. Plant your banner in their village, Sire! We can trade in aquamarine, command their Depth Metal forges, or snuff that last light completely. Ah, Elves... even submerged, they manage to become a decision!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner in the Mermorph village, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The sea people have noticed you, Sire. Elves do take their time.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner marks the village, and the Mermorphs now face a power their ancestors forgot. Let them keep that ignorance, Sire! We gain nothing by explaining an old drowning they cannot undo. Their aquamarine can support peaceful terms, my Lord! Their Depth Metal can be forged on your command. Or their sea lanterns and lives can vanish together, ending the last little glow they carried from elven days. Three useful futures, Sire! Everlight itself remains sealed behind its gates, beyond this affair. These are the ones left outside. History was cruel to them once. You may decide whether it has developed restraint.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/elves_somewhat_soggy · working title "The Village beneath" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.10

