[[Their Forges, Our Metal]]

[[Snuff the Last Light]]

Sea People Introduction


:: A Vassal Forge {"position":"4600,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Continuity, Master! Let it continue beneath your boot.
START LOG: If they insist on continuity, Sire, give them continuity with improved management! Obtain one of their metal ingots and wear a complete suit of Dwarven armour. Let the Hold see its craft carried by the authority above it. No need to erase their identity. Submission is far more useful when the servants remain skilled! Their forge continues, their traditions continue, and their pride continues... beneath yours! Very tidy. Walk among them wearing their own work, Master. A vassal should recognise itself reflected in its ruler, especially when the reflection is taller and carrying a much larger weapon!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Obtain Dwarven metal and wear a complete suit of Dwarven armour.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Perfect fit, Sire! The Hold continues exactly where you put it.
COMPLETION LOG: There we are, Master! Dwarven metal covers you, and the Successor Hold has found the continuity it wanted. It simply continues as your vassal forge. Such a proud people, reduced to service... sometimes history has a sense of humour! Their smiths still hammer, their armour still bears old craft, and their halls still call themselves a Hold. Let them keep all that, Sire! Ownership does not require erasing the label. In fact, preserved traditions make obedience look almost respectable. The Dwarves wanted an unbroken line! You have kindly placed yourself at the end of it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/a_vassal_forge · working title "The Weight of Continuity" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_successor_hold=Submission · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 203.10

Submission Path


:: So That's Where It Went {"position":"3000,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): Sire... that sealed door opens onto the rift. So that's where it went.
START LOG: Now I understand, Master! This is the old injury itself! The Great Cataclysm cracked a rift between realms, small enough to escape notice. Years later, the fourth Master fired the Tower Heart's power at Empire City. That second release tore the crack fully open. Solarius's cleansers found the injury afterward and did what the Empire did best. They hid it! These strongholds became containment vaults around the wound, sealed with stone and ritual. The strange eyes were never leading to treasure, Sire. They were crystallised soured magic yearning back toward the break that made them. Charming little compass needles!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Cross the Empire's sealed threshold, Sire, and confront the realm beyond it.
EMOTION (complete): Stricken
POPUP (complete): One wound, Master. Five concentrations, countless scars... and an Anchor feeding inside.
COMPLETION LOG: Everything fits now, Sire! The five great concentrations drank corruption from this rift. So did the scattered scars and spoiled lifeforce. The Empire sealed the door, but sealing is not healing! Inside, Cataclysm magic crystallised into shards feeding a vast Anchor. That dragon has grown around the old wound for centuries. Corruption leaks outward while those crystals keep feeding it. Kill it, Master! Break the feeding crystals first, then the beast itself. The cleansers buried the problem and called that victory. We shall use the traditional remedy... find the largest thing involved and kill it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/so_thats_where_it_went · working title "The Wound Beyond the World" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O2 NW_TR prep2.20

[[Kill the Big Lizard]]


:: Salt, Sulfur, Smugness {"position":"1900,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): three nasty bits... sulfur, salt, mercury. mercury gets no kiss.
START LOG: three things first, Sssire... sulfur, salt, mercury. small names, nasty manners. bring clean sulfur, alchemy salt, mercury shard. I sniff. no taste. mercury lesson already learned... coins still haunt tongue sometimes. each piece says different thing about matter. what changes. what stays. what slips between. clever, yes? mostly we heat things until secrets squeal. bring all three... I ask rude questions. no licking. not even brave little lick. gloves stay on. both gloves.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): bring sulfur, alchemy salt, mercury shard... untouched by tongue.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): all three here... head buzzes. knowledge or fumes?
COMPLETION LOG: sulfur, salt, mercury... all here. no licking. very good rule. sulfur wants change. salt holds shape. mercury slips between... sneaky shiny thing. I respect sneaky things from distance. now lab stops guessing quite so much. pieces have names. names make rules easier... sometimes. next we take matter apart careful, keep useful bits, throw bad bits nowhere near kitchen. head buzzing again. probably fumes. if floor starts breathing... tell me before I step on it.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/salt_sulfur_smugness · working title "Three Principles" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O2 NW_B RES.GREEN3

[[Break It, Rebuild It]]


:: Knights, Ghosts, Ghasts {"position":"4900,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Phantom knights and a monstrous Ghast, Sire! The forest diversified.
START LOG: Clear both towers, Master. Phantom knights hold one. An enormous Ghast screams through the other. The knights are old duty without useful context. The Ghast is simply huge and miserable! More relatable, really! Break both strongholds and open the route upward. Queen Fay's Sanctuary once sheltered magical refugees from the Empire. Centuries later, its defenses attack anything breathing nearby. Institutional memory at its finest, Sire! If a guardian cannot remember whom it guards, dismissal becomes appropriate. Yours will involve considerably more steel than paperwork.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Defeat the phantom knights and the great Ghast, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Towers cleared! The gloom remains, but nobody important owns it.
COMPLETION LOG: The phantom order is broken, Sire, and the great Ghast is silent! Two more abandoned duties have lost their teeth! Perhaps those knights guarded refugees and the tower watched old approaches! Nobody remains to explain it, Master. Chaos reduced purpose to hostility long ago! The route climbs now toward frozen territory. A Yeti holds the lower path, and beyond waits a Snow Queen in her glacier! Another monarch, yes! Forests become kingdoms alarmingly fast without regular pruning. We shall provide the pruning ourselves.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/knights_ghosts_ghasts · working title "Towers in the Gloom" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 EXP_D4_Abyss 300.10

[[Thaw the Snow Queen]]


:: Signed in Stone {"position":"4400,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): They want recognition, Sire. Buy it cheaply and charge interest in steel!
START LOG: Dwarves adore old claims, Master. Let us sell them one they already believe! Trade until they entrust you with a rune, then put your weight behind their ancestral claim. In return, their forge works for your reign. Everyone leaves feeling dignified! Revoltingly peaceful, but profitable! The rune matters because Dwarves trust marks, stone, lineage, and anything difficult to alter after an argument. Give them recognition in writing, Sire, and take practical value in metal. We lose nothing! Their ancestors are too dead to complain about the terms, which makes them ideal partners in negotiation!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Trade with the Dwarves until they give you a rune, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Signed in stone, Sire! Their claim stands, and their forge serves.
COMPLETION LOG: The rune seals the arrangement, Master! The Successor Hold keeps its proud ancestral claim, and you gain the forge behind it. Everyone can pretend principle won. How pleasant! They call it recognition, Sire. We call it access. Their smiths work, their old story survives, and your reign gains Dwarven craft without wasting good metal on a siege. Let them carve the terms deeply. Stone makes people feel secure. The interesting part is what the agreement does, not what it says. Their continuity now has a patron... and patrons have expectations, Sire!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/signed_in_stone · working title "Two Claims" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_successor_hold=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 500.30

Peaceful Path


:: Old Craft, New Master {"position":"4800,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): Restore their vintage craft, Sire. Prosperity is so easy to redirect!
START LOG: The Gnumus have fragments of older craft, Master, buried beneath cheese and appetite. Help them improve that vintage work until their workshops thrive again. They need not know why you care, Master. Prosperity makes an excellent disguise, Sire! Once their makers can produce better wares, the Tower becomes their finest customer and patron. Everyone smiles, tools improve, and influence settles in quietly. How civilized! Encourage the revival, Sire. A workshop that owes its new success to your presence becomes remarkably reluctant to lose you. Peaceful arrangements are tolerable when gratitude grows into dependence without anyone noticing the roots!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Help the Gnumus restore and improve their vintage craft, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Their old craft lives again, Sire, under very convenient patronage.
COMPLETION LOG: The Gnumu workshops are humming again, Master! Vintage craft has returned to capable little hands, and those hands have learned exactly which patron made the revival possible. Let them prosper, Master! Let them sell tools, rifles, and whatever else their appetites inspire. The Tower gains wares, influence, and a settlement eager to keep business pleasant. No conquest required! Merely opportunity offered by the right dark benefactor. They think they restored something lost, Sire! In truth, they restored it beneath your shadow. That is the long con at its most elegant... almost enough to make honest work bearable!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/old_craft_new_master · working title "Vintage Work Restored" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_gnumus=Peaceful · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 601.10

Peaceful Path


:: Debt Is a Leash {"position":"5000,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Lend generously, Master. Debt remembers who fed it.
START LOG: Gnumus understand business, Sire, and business understands debt. Approach them as a financier. Give their ventures enough support that repayment becomes a horizon they never quite reach. No shackles needed! A ledger can pull surprisingly hard. Their workshops continue, their tables remain full, and every ambitious little merchant discovers that tomorrow's profit already has your name on it. Delightful! Make the arrangement, Master! A debt that can be repaid is merely commerce. A debt that lingers becomes obedience wearing respectable clothes. Even the fattest Gnumu can feel a leash once it is written in figures!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Finance the Gnumus through their business arrangement, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Excellent! They owe you more than coin now, Master.
COMPLETION LOG: The Gnumus have accepted your credit, Master, and the leash is already tightening. No guards marched in. No roofs burned. Nothing uncivilized at all! Their business now grows on money whose source they cannot ignore. Every expansion deepens the obligation, Sire. Every successful sale makes repayment possible in theory and less desirable in practice. Very clever, Sire! Let them call you investor, patron, benefactor... anything except owner. Ownership becomes much more useful when the owned insist on polite vocabulary. Their vintage workshops remain lively, their tables remain full, and their future has acquired a creditor with a throne.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/debt_is_a_leash · working title "Vintage on Credit" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_gnumus=Submission · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 606.10

Submission Path


:: We Need a Bigger Sword {"position":"2000,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): One bad essence, Master, and five stronger stinks answer it!
START LOG: That first tainted essence has company, Sire! Five stronger concentrations answer from very different places! One lies in the frozen North. Another crawls beneath the desert. A third gathers around a dead dragon's tower. One festers below in the Netherworld. The last waits out at sea. Delightful distribution! Do not charge at all five empty handed, Master. Prepare properly, then investigate each lair. We need evidence before slaughter becomes interpretation! Well... slightly before. If the same corruption truly feeds all five, each creature should reveal a different piece of the pattern. Then we can decide what deserves the bigger sword.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Read my warning, Master, and prepare for the five corrupted threats.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Good, Sire! Five foul lairs await, and none know how fortunate they are.
COMPLETION LOG: We have our targets, Master! Frozen hideout, desert nest, dragon tower, Netherworld depths, and a ship at sea! Five places with no sensible reason to share one taint. Take them in any order, Sire! The netherrock lets me follow each trace independently. Expect different symptoms! The North may preserve corruption in death. The desert may carry it through blood. The other three will tell their own stories. Kill what must be killed, naturally! But bring back understanding with the trophies. A mystery is much easier to dominate once all its ugly pieces have been properly surrounded!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/we_need_a_bigger_sword · working title "We Need a Bigger Sword" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 417.50

