[[The Sand Is Moving]]

[[Dead Dragons Don't Fly]]

[[I Know That Stride]]

[[The Sea Keeps Secrets]]

Boss Hideout Found


:: Heavy Rites {"position":"4500,3800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Perform the reconstructed rite. Ceremony is only useful when it answers.
START LOG: Reconstruct one sailors' rite; follow its form; spare me belief; ritual can be treated as procedure; the men who made these forms were frightened. Some were altered. Some expected death. None of that makes the structure meaningless. Perform it in the affected waters. Observe the response. What changes? What appears? What remains? I have seen respectable authorities understand less than doomed fishermen. Rank is not evidence. Results are. Procedure deserves that courtesy.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Perform one reconstructed rite in the affected waters.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): It answered. Good. Preserve the result and the uncertainty.
COMPLETION LOG: The rite produced a response; that matters; messages, scrawls, aberrant catches, storms, ceremonies: one record now binds them; rot spread through the sea and changed exposed life; the sailors discovered some interaction with it. We need not invent a name for every pressure they felt. Mystery... is still data. I will preserve the account. You may keep what the rite yielded. A fair transaction. Truth for collection. Artifact for labour.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/heavy_rites · working title "Weight of the World" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: DREDGE Collector Row 1033


:: Side With the Beards {"position":"4950,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Five Kobolds, Master. A small price for Dwarven gratitude.
START LOG: If the old claim amuses you, Sire, put weight behind it. Kill five Kobolds! No grand extermination, just enough bodies for the Successor Hold to call the scales corrected. Dwarves understand numbers when the numbers are casualties! The Den will understand too. This does not make the Hold peaceful, obedient, or safe. It merely says that in this one quarrel, their claim has your favour. Useful ambiguity! Let the beards enjoy the decision, Master. Gratitude is sweetest when recipients know it might be withdrawn at any moment. Five Kobolds should make the point without settling anything else for us.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill five Kobolds to favour the Dwarven claim, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The scales tip toward the beards, Master. Temporarily, of course.
COMPLETION LOG: Five Kobolds are down, Sire, and the Successor Hold will read that as vindication. Let them! Dwarves love seeing history confirm what they already believed! The Den has been checked, the old claim has gained weight, and neither faction's greater fate has been decided. Very useful! Keep the distinction sharp, Master! Supporting a claim does not promise friendship, protection, or future survival. It only tells both sides which way your thumb pressed the scale today. Tomorrow you may need that thumb for something else... perhaps crushing the scale entirely. Never let gratitude become expectation!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/side_with_the_beards · working title "Weight the Scales" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 EXP_D4_Abyss 301.10

Dwarf Favored Path


:: Burn the Bastille {"position":"4100,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Strength is their law, Master. Rewrite it in casualties.
START LOG: The Bastille believes strength settles ownership. Excellent! Let us accept their terms, Sire. Break ten of their fighters and destroy a clay golem. Leave enough fortress standing for witnesses. A ruin teaches less if nobody survives to describe the lesson! Their walls are not the true target, Master. Their certainty is. Legioners, skirmishers, archers, whatever proud title they use... cut through ten. Then break the construct they trust to hold the line. When strength is their law, destruction is merely a legal argument conducted properly, Master. Present your case, my Lord, with enthusiasm!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill ten Bastille fighters and destroy one clay golem, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Argument settled, Master! The Bastille has discovered stronger law.
COMPLETION LOG: The Bastille has bowed to the simplest evidence, Sire! Ten fighters are down, their clay guardian is broken, and the fortress has learned that walls do not make strength. They only concentrate targets, my Lord! Excellent! Let the survivors keep enough stone to remember what failed. Their pride was built on the belief that force alone decides who commands. You have not disproved them, Master! You have merely won the argument! Raiders understand that better than mercy. From now on, the Bastille is not a rival power. It is a warning with battlements.
VARIANT [escalated_bastille=yes]: They once raided by agreement or answered your horn, Sire. Their later destruction makes one point plain: service lasted only while you allowed it.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/burn_the_bastille · working title "What Bows After Fear" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_bastille=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_bastille=yes · VOICE: O1 End_Tower_Battle_Narrative 1507.10

Destruction Path


:: Finders Keepers, Sire {"position":"3500,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): The court hid its treasure too, Master! Open the treasury.
START LOG: The throne-room hoard is still sealed, Sire. Nobody qualified remains to object. Open it! The court survived enchantment, death, and centuries of irrelevance. Their treasure did even better! That makes ownership wonderfully simple. Abandoned wealth belongs to the Dark Lord who finds it after removing squatters! I may have simplified several legal traditions, Master. History will recover! Take what this castle kept. Wealth becomes much less embarrassing once removed from hypocrites. Especially hypocrites who hid behind forbidden magic while lecturing everyone else about it.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Open the throne-room treasure chest, Sire, and take everything.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Finders keepers! Imperial law was never this efficient.
COMPLETION LOG: The treasury is open, Master, and quite worth it! The court hid itself, condemned magic, then used magic. It outlived the Empire with astonishingly little dignity. Finally, it preserved this hoard for you! A satisfying chain of custody! Scholars may argue provenance later, Sire. Let them argue, because you found the castle, broke the court, and opened the treasure! That is perfectly adequate paperwork for the Tower. The Empire tried to hide from history! Its valuables have now escaped that mistake. Do have the Minions carry the heavy pieces.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/finders_keepers_sire · working title "What the Castle Kept" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O1 D1_SD1_WorkCamp 203.30


:: Frozen Leftovers {"position":"2400,1700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): The leftovers are standing up, Sire! Skor really should chew better.
START LOG: Those frozen skeletons are moving, Master! Very rude! Skor chewed the flesh, yet corruption still clings to the bones strongly enough to animate them. Destroy five and watch what remains. I want to know whether the power dies with its second host or simply moves on again. The cold has preserved this mess beautifully, Sire! Almost thoughtful of the climate! Do not let the bones surround you. Dead things have poor discipline but excellent persistence! Once we have tested enough of them, we can decide whether Skor is causing this... or merely eating from the same poisoned table.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Destroy five frozen skeletons in Skor's lair, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): Five down, Master! The corruption survives them. Skor is only feeding.
COMPLETION LOG: That is enough, Sire. The skeletons confirm the pattern! Their corruption persists after flesh, death, freezing, and Skor's teeth. Very committed stuff. The Yeti did not create it. He has been feeding where the taint already gathered, then growing larger on the meal. Kill Skor next, Master! His own essence should give us a stronger trace than these scraps. If it pulls away after his death, we know the North is another feeding ground rather than a source. I almost pity him. Imagine becoming enormous through mysterious corruption only to end as one of my measurements!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/frozen_leftovers · working title "What the Frost Made" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 201.20

[[Skor's Last Supper]]


:: Too Many Flowers {"position":"3900,3000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Orchids, Sire! Evernight's elven rot has learned decoration.
START LOG: This shrine reeks of Evernight's reborn magic, Master. Orchids everywhere! The altar sits beneath all that tasteful superiority. Elves always did confuse beauty with virtue. Examine it, Sire. A guardian is bound somewhere to this place! I can feel the connection, but not the creature. Apparently murderous flowers require invitations now. Touch the altar and see what offering it wants. I expect moonlight, poetry, or some other waste, yet... something sharper hungers beneath the petals! Perhaps this shrine has better taste than it looks.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Examine the orchid altar, Master, and learn its demand.
EMOTION (complete): Darkened
POPUP (complete): It wants a heart! Finally, a flower with sensible taste.
COMPLETION LOG: An Orchid Heart, Sire! That is the offering. No hymns, moonlit dancing, or contemplating dew required! Bring the heart back and feed the altar. Its magic should call the hidden guardian forward! Evernight's resurgence has grown many strange things from old elven power. This shrine feels particularly sharp, Master! Beautiful, certainly. Beauty is only danger after someone improves the lighting! Let us see what answers when properly fed. If it has petals and claws, I shall feel wonderfully vindicated.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/too_many_flowers · working title "Where the Orchids Gather" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 1100.20

[[Flowers Want Hearts?]]

Orchid Altar found


:: It's Our Gold Now {"position":"7000,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): A treasury full of gold, Master. I believe the ownership error is obvious.
START LOG: Piglins think gold belongs to them, Sire. Adorable! Enter one of their great fortresses and take its treasury. No complicated treaty is required. Possession is such persuasive law when backed by an Overlord! The Piglins may rage, bargain, snort, or wave weapons. Let them! Once their hoard sits in your hands, the hierarchy becomes very simple. They guard gold! You own what they guard. Take the treasury, Master, and make the family lesson clear without discussing family. Greed is one tradition we can all share without embarrassment, particularly when your share is everything worth carrying!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Loot a Piglin fortress treasury, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Lovely gold, Master! The Piglins have learned whose hoard it was.
COMPLETION LOG: Their treasury is yours, Sire! Gold has changed hands, and the Piglins now know who owns the wealth they were merely keeping warm. Much better! Submission becomes wonderfully easy when pride has a price tag. Let them continue mining, bartering, and admiring shiny things. They simply do so beneath the memory of their fortress being emptied by you. Ah, the educational value of theft, Sire! No need to destroy the villages, my Lord. Every gold-loving Piglin can look toward the missing treasure and remember the larger claim above them. Ownership, Master, is often just robbery that nobody can reverse.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/its_our_gold_now · working title "Who Owns the Gold" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_piglins=Submission · VOICE: O1 EXP_D4_Abyss 211.10

Submission Path


:: Talk to Fire, Sire {"position":"2500,800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Listen to the Blaze, Master! Preferably without becoming charcoal.
START LOG: A ritual asks. A chant can be rather more direct! Study a Blaze closely enough to learn the Chant of Flames, Master. Fire already knows what it is. We merely need its vocabulary! Research is such a gentle word for prying secrets from something dangerous. I approve immensely, Sire! Once you can call flame by sign and word, this chamber stops being merely devotional. It becomes useful. Religion improves enormously when it starts setting things on fire, Sire... especially when somebody else is standing nearest the altar. Learn the chant, my Lord, and make fire answer properly!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Study a Blaze and learn the Chant of Flames, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Well done, Master! Fire has learned to answer politely.
COMPLETION LOG: The Chant of Flames answers you! You studied a natural force and turned understanding into command. Priests may call that revelation. Scholars may call it research. We call it useful, Master! Signs and chants are tools, not loyalties. Learn what a power offers without belonging to it. That distinction matters now, because the chamber has reached a fork. Sacred or Wicked! The next proper rite will decide which path answers your hand first. Even gods enjoy reducing enormous questions to two inconvenient choices! Choose carefully, Sire, then make whichever answer remember who called it.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/talk_to_fire_sire · working title "Words that Answer" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 400.30

[[Halo or Horns?]]


:: Even Evil Sleeps {"position":"1400,2000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Even Evil sleeps, Sire! Preferably somewhere Browns cannot crawl into first.
START LOG: Even Evil sleeps, Sire! Preferably behind thick doors and away from snoring Browns. Your chambers should make rank obvious, Master, even to the dimmest visitor. Set a proper necrolord bed here, my Lord, and reclaim some privacy. Nobody should ask you for anything in this room! I cannot promise obedience. Browns regard closed doors as puzzles. Still, a Master deserves somewhere to remove armour peacefully. Finding three Minions under the blankets rather spoils that! Establish your chambers, Sire. Then rest just long enough to make everyone nervous.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Set a necrolord bed in your chambers, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Your chambers are ready, Sire. Do check beneath the bed.
COMPLETION LOG: Your chambers are fit again, Master! Dark bed, solid furniture, adequate gloom... almost civilized. Rest whenever you choose, Sire. Tyranny is tiring work, my Lord, especially when victims insist on resisting first! The room is yours alone, at least in principle, assuming the Browns understand privacy. Check beneath the bed occasionally, Sire. Browns hide treasure there, and pets hide bones there. History suggests Overlords attract stranger things than either! Still, close the door and ignore the scratching. If it starts speaking politely, then perhaps call me.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_dark_tower/even_evil_sleeps · working title "Your Chambers, Sire" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 1400.30

[[Home, Wretched Home]]

Bedroom Restoration


:: Death, Politely Refused {"position":"4100,3400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION (unlock): Pleased
POPUP (unlock): One stain remains. Clean it, Sire. Finish the return.
START LOG: Death still clings. Remove it. The body crossed back. The grave left residue. Cure that stain, Sire. Let living flesh finish the journey. Death is not jealous. Death is exact. A bond held. A rite was paid. A servant returned. That is not theft. I know theft. I catalogue it. Complete the cure. Let the collar become memory again. Let the companion stand whole. Balance restored. Service resumed. Grave closed.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Cure the returned companion, Sire. Remove death's residue.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Death refused. Politely. The bond remains.
COMPLETION LOG: The grave-stain is gone. Your companion lives whole. Remember the path. Collar carried memory. Memory carried bond. Bond carried the rite home. A simple chain. Not an easy one. Not every death leaves it intact. This one did. Keep the servant close, Sire. We live. We serve. We die. Sometimes, with cause and proper measure, service resumes before the final accounting. Death permits exceptions. It dislikes sloppy paperwork. I will close the entry.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/death_politely_refused · working title "A Death Reversed" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · STAT: side_lines_finished += 1 on completion · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.30


:: Stay Dead This Time {"position":"2600,2100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Ashlord already had one funeral, Sire. Let us improve the second!
START LOG: We know enough now, Master. The Kindred prepared Ashlord! The Cataclysm raised him. Then the old beast bred new dragons and released them during the Silence! Admirable persistence, dreadful consequences. Kill Ashlord and end this concentration properly. No rites this time. No worshippers hovering around the corpse. No helpful catastrophe waiting nearby! When he falls, watch the essence that leaves him, Sire. If it pulls away like the others, then even this spectacular resurrection was another symptom. Dead dragons should stay dead! I have always considered that one of death's more useful administrative features.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill Ashlord the infernal dragon, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Dead again, Master! Do try to make this funeral stick.
COMPLETION LOG: Ashlord is down, Sire, and the freed essence pulls elsewhere! So even his resurrection points beyond the tower! The Kindred prepared the corpse, and Cataclysm magic supplied the spark, but neither explains the corruption's continuing direction. Another concentration fed by something farther away. Excellent! We now have a dead dragon, a ruined cult, and one more trace for comparison. Keep it with the others, Master! When all five great concentrations are broken, we can stop guessing at isolated disasters and judge the pattern together. For the moment, enjoy the silence. Dragons are much less impressive when they stop breathing!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/stay_dead_this_time · working title "Undo the Resurrection" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 605.20

[[One Wound, Many Bleeds]]
[[It Smells Off]]
[[Now the Dead Dance]]
[[Older Than You Think]]
[[It Cracks Everything]]
[[All Roads Bleed One Way]]


:: Ants With Ambitions {"position":"7700,1400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Composed
POPUP (unlock): Insects with hierarchy, Sire. Evernight has been unsupervised far too long.
START LOG: Another gift from Evernight's untended resurgence, Master. Myrmex colonies grew fat on it and developed alarming ambition. Workers, soldiers, resin, royal chambers... the little crawlers have built themselves a society. How industrious! How unnecessary! Their Queen holds the colony together, while resin and command staffs offer more practical handles. Plant your banner near the mound, Sire. We can leave them alone in exchange for resin, seize a staff and command them directly, or remove the Queen and let the whole grand insect order discover how fragile hierarchy can be. I almost admire them! Almost! Ants should know when to stop organising!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Plant your banner at the Myrmex colony, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): The mound has noticed you, Sire. Try not to stand on anything diplomatic.
COMPLETION LOG: Your banner stands over the Myrmex claim, Master, and the colony now has something larger than itself to consider. Good! They offer three convenient weaknesses! Resin can buy peace without pretending anyone likes insects. A command staff can bend their strict hierarchy toward you. Or the Queen can die, taking the colony's future with her. Evernight's regrowth swelled these creatures beyond ordinary insect concerns, Sire. That does not make them exempt from Overlording. It merely gives us more interesting options than stepping on them one at a time!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/ants_with_ambitions · working title "The Mound-Dwellers" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 900.20

