[[The Staff Says Obey]]

Myrmex Introduction


:: Erase the Family Shame {"position":"6900,1200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Darkened
POPUP (unlock): Ten Piglins, two brutes, Sire. Fewer relatives means fewer awkward questions.
START LOG: There is one very direct solution to a shameful family branch, Master. Pruning! Kill ten Piglins and two of their brutes inside a Nether village. The ordinary fighters show the settlement can bleed. The brutes show even its proudest protectors cannot keep the family name standing. Do not shout about ancestry while doing it. Dignity, Sire! We are erasing embarrassment, not advertising it. Break the village's confidence and let surviving Piglins learn that gold, tusks, and pride do not make them your equals. Twelve relatives fewer! Ah, one can almost feel the holidays improving already!
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Kill ten Piglins and two Piglin brutes inside a Nether village.
EMOTION (complete): Relishing
POPUP (complete): Family gathering reduced, Master! Much more manageable now.
COMPLETION LOG: Ten Piglins and two brutes are dead, Sire. The village has lost enough pride to stop looking like a branch worth claiming. Excellent! Let the survivors keep their gold if they can hold it. Let them keep the ancestry too. We certainly do not want it back! Their brutes were supposed to embody stubborn Piglin strength. Now they embody something flatter. The family shame has not vanished from history, Master, but it has become quieter, and that is almost as good. Some bloodlines deserve monuments! Others deserve fewer witnesses! This one has received your editorial attention!
VARIANT [escalated_piglins=yes]: They once bartered with you or surrendered their treasury, Sire. Culling the village afterward proves even family arrangements survive only while you tolerate them.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_reign/erase_the_family_shame · working title "Break the Pig Pride" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 (intros) + part 4 (paths) · TAG: faction_piglins=Destruction · TAG when replacing Peaceful or Submission: escalated_piglins=yes · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 803.10

Destruction Path


:: The Forest's First Keepers {"position":"5050,3100","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Relishing
POPUP (unlock): Naga and Lich first, Sire! The forest arranged nuisances by seniority.
START LOG: Two old keepers block the deeper Sanctuary, Master. First the Naga. Enormous serpent, ancient duty, objectionable teeth! Then the forest's Lich in his tower. He was once part of this refuge's guarding order. Time and chaos twisted duty into territorial hostility! Very common management failure! Kill both, Sire. Their original purpose no longer matters if every visitor becomes prey. Queen Fay built a sanctuary, not a private menagerie of tyrants! Remove the first barriers and the deeper forest should open. Try not to become decoration in either lair.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Defeat the Naga and the Twilight Forest Lich, Master.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): First keepers removed! The Sanctuary remains strangely ungrateful.
COMPLETION LOG: The Naga is dead, Sire, and the Lich has lost his tower! Two old barriers are finally gone! Queen Fay's refuge did not become harmless when its elves vanished! Its keepers remained, Master, then warped around abandoned duties! Protection became possession and duty became hostility, a very tidy decline! The deeper regions are open now. Labyrinths and fire wait ahead, which sounds refreshingly honest! No philosophy required, just walls, monsters, and something flammable! I almost feel nostalgic.
CODER NOTES: overlord:tales/the_forests_first_keepers · working title "The Forest's First Keepers" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 1 (hooks) + part 3 · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 605.10

[[Maze, Meal, Hydra]]

Naga + Lich (NEW passage)


:: A Piece of Home {"position":"3200,2300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION (unlock): Stricken
POPUP (unlock): That egg is no egg, Sire... it is a piece of the Tower Heart!
START LOG: Look at what the Anchor left behind, Master. That shell is not an egg! It is a seed of the Tower Heart, a fragment crystallised around by the dragon. I can feel the old power inside it now. Faint, battered, unmistakable. Most of the Heart remains deeper in the wound, but this piece survived close to the Anchor. Take it, Sire! Bring a piece of home back to the Tower! The seed is not quiet either. It calls toward the rest of the Heart, tugging outward through the wound. A useful little homesick fragment... and perhaps our next compass.
OBJECTIVES (voiced): Take the Heart's seed into your possession, Sire.
EMOTION (complete): Pleased
POPUP (complete): Home again, little seed! And listen, Master... it is calling to the rest.
COMPLETION LOG: You have it, Sire! A seed of the Tower Heart rests in your hand, and I can feel its pull clearly now. The Anchor crystallised around this fragment while most of the Heart slipped farther into the wound. That explains the false egg. It was never offspring. It was armour grown around something older! Keep the seed safe, Master! It calls toward the missing Heart with the stubborn certainty of a Minion spotting unattended gold. We have recovered only a piece of home, but pieces can lead to wholes. When you are ready, follow where it calls. The Heart has been lost long enough.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/a_piece_of_home · working title "A Seed of the Heart" · trigger/objective: quest-specs part 2 + narrative-beats · TAG on completion: heart_seed=held · at credits if incomplete: heart_seed=not_held · VOICE: O1 Tower_HeartIntro 100.10

Dragon Egg = seed of the Tower Heart (NEW passage, optional for the credits)


:: It Smells Off {"position":"2900,1700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: One concentration gone, Sire... and the stink still points elsewhere.
LOG: The first great concentration is broken, Master! Good! Yet the corruption did not die with it! The freed essence pulls away, as though answering something beyond the place we just cleared. I will not name a source from one corpse and one direction. That is how priests are born. Still, Sire, the behaviour matters! A true origin should not look homesick for somewhere else. Keep that pull in mind. We have other concentrations to test. If each one dies differently but its corruption departs the same way, then we may finally have a pattern worth distrusting!
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/it_smells_off · working title "Gnarl's Suspicions I" · Rambling-style entry (popup + log, no completion) · spec: narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 EXP_D2_Abyss 210.15

Count-based: fires when the 1st gate is resolved, whatever the order (NEW passage)


:: Now the Dead Dance {"position":"2900,1850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Twice now, Master. Different horror, same pull. I am listening.
LOG: A second concentration has fallen, Sire, and again the corruption answers elsewhere! The creature, place, and manner of death differed from the first. The departing essence did not care. That is useful! Two examples are not proof, but they are enough to sharpen suspicion. Whatever this power is, it behaves less like local rot and more like something feeding through local hosts. Do not rush the conclusion, Master. Mysteries enjoy making clever people look stupid. We shall be clever more slowly! Break another concentration. If the same tug returns, coincidence will start running out of places to hide.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/now_the_dead_dance · working title "Gnarl's Suspicions II" · Rambling-style entry (popup + log, no completion) · spec: narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 EXP_D3_Abyss 500.20

Count-based: fires when the 2nd gate is resolved, whatever the order (NEW passage)


:: Older Than You Think {"position":"2900,2000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Three, Sire! This corruption was already at work by the Great Cataclysm.
LOG: Three traces now, Master, and the age finally shows! Some hosts were already marked by the Great Cataclysm. Yet the same foul pull runs through them. That puts this corruption centuries before your reign, Sire. It was working by the Cataclysm, perhaps around it. I will not pretend the exact hour is obvious. Ancient disasters rarely keep tidy little ledgers... irritating things! But this much is no guess. The taint had time to settle into old scars. It did not begin with your Tower's return. Whatever spoiled this lifeforce has been patient indeed. Break another concentration! Let us see what else survived history.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/older_than_you_think · working title "Gnarl's Suspicions III" · Rambling-style entry (popup + log, no completion) · spec: narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 416.10

Count-based: fires when the 3rd gate is resolved, whatever the order (NEW passage)


:: It Cracks Everything {"position":"2900,2150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Four, Master! Different bodies, same corruption. Something deeper is cracking through.
LOG: Four concentrations have broken, Sire, and four freed traces pull beyond themselves! That is no local disease. It crosses flesh, bone, old magic, and places that should share nothing at all. Something deeper is reaching through each concentration and cracking whatever holds it. I still will not name the hidden cause before we have the last comparison. Restraint is painful, Master! Appreciate the sacrifice! One concentration remains! Break it and watch the essence carefully! If the fifth behaves like the others, then we stop asking whether these horrors connect. We start asking what one injury could feed them all.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/it_cracks_everything · working title "Gnarl's Suspicions IV" · Rambling-style entry (popup + log, no completion) · spec: narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 602.10

Count-based: fires when the 4th gate is resolved, whatever the order (NEW passage)


:: All Roads Bleed One Way {"position":"2900,2300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Five, Sire. No more coincidence. Every foul road bleeds the same way.
LOG: That settles it, Master! Five concentrations, five different horrors, one departing pull! None was the true beginning. Each fed upon corruption arriving from elsewhere, then expressed it in its own charming fashion. We have been cutting mouths away from one hidden wound. Now we find the wound itself, Sire! Bring the traces together and compare what they share. Somewhere beyond these lairs is one cause broad enough to touch them all. I do admire a problem with ambition! We have finished counting symptoms. The next step is to follow the common direction and make the source regret being discoverable.
CODER NOTES: overlord:the_wound/all_roads_bleed_one_way · working title "Gnarl's Suspicions V" · Rambling-style entry (popup + log, no completion) · spec: narrative-beats · VOICE: O1 EXP_D3_Abyss 500.10

Count-based: fires when the 5th gate is resolved, whatever the order (NEW passage)


:: Flesh, Forged [rambling] {"position":"1000,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Ah, a forge with a pulse, Sire! Now that is organic craftsmanship.
LOG: Ah, a forge that wriggles beneath your hand, Sire! Much better than another cold iron box in the Tower, Master! Feed it flesh... and watch the ugly workshop mend itself! It heals between hammerings, which should save endless tedious repairs later. Ordinary forges crack, cool, and sulk when treated properly for years. This one may simply bite the apprentice who neglects it instead. Keep your splendid gauntlet clear of those eager teeth, my Lord. A workshop with a pulse deserves fear, respect, feeding, and distance. Oh, Giblet will be green with envy... metaphorically, I hope!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/flesh_forged · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/bio_forge` (in-game name "Organic Smithing") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 200.10


:: It's Spreading, Sire [rambling] {"position":"1150,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: It's spreading, Master... splendidly. Do keep it off the throne!
LOG: Oh, look at it spread across the Tower stone, Sire! The flesh has found ambition at last, Master! It creeps through every crack... rather eagerly, doesn't it, my Lord? Living growth never understands when enough should mean enough for anyone! Give it one wall, and it starts eyeing three more nearby. Give it three... and soon it starts eyeing you for dessert. Delightful appetite, provided we choose the boundaries ourselves. Keep it well away from the throne and Gristle's pantry! I prefer furniture that stays still when praised, mostly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/its_spreading_sire · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/malignant_growth` (in-game name "Malignant Growth") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 900.20


:: Stars Taste Better [rambling] {"position":"1300,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A Nether Star for dinner, Sire! Expensive tastes suit ugly things.
LOG: Now that is proper feeding: a Nether Star! Lesser scraps merely twitch, but this one truly feasts, Master! Look how eagerly the flesh answers such expensive nourishment before you! Power knows a rich meal when somebody generous offers one. Stars make terribly costly morsels, which only improves matters for Evil. Waste common scraps on common growth, my Lord, never grandeur itself. Save priceless offerings for something magnificently unpleasant and worthy instead. Ah, now the creature understands your standards... excellent work, Sire! Even hungry flesh knows quality when you provide it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stars_taste_better · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/nether_star_sacrifice` (in-game name "Superior Sacrifice") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 107.10


:: Spare Kidneys, Anyone? [rambling] {"position":"1450,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Spare kidneys, Master! At last, a market with useful merchandise.
LOG: Someone has put spare organs on sale... wonderfully practical! Hearts, glands, kidneys, all neatly priced and dripping, Master! Merchants have finally discovered a respectable use for anatomy after all! Why bury good parts with owners who already failed them completely? A liver needs neither sentiment, ceremony, nor a grieving widow nearby. An eye rarely asks awkward questions after changing hands, my Lord. Keep the freshest pieces close, my Lord, and haggle ruthlessly for bargains! Blister may even want the shrivelled ones... lucky little creature. Ah, commerce with a proper smell at last!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/spare_kidneys_anyone · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/organ_trader` (in-game name "Organ Trader") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_D3_Abyss 403.30


:: Holes. So Many Holes. [rambling] {"position":"1600,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Oh... holes, Sire. Far too many holes!
LOG: So many holes... far too many little holes everywhere! Some of them appear to breathe as well, Master! Do not stare too closely into that pattern, my Lord! Patterns like this encourage thoughts best left hungry and unfed. Still, what a fine ugly specimen you discovered here, Sire, today! It must have taken ages growing this thoroughly offensive to eyesight. One almost wants to... poke it and see what answers back. Preferably use something attached to somebody else! Your good hand deserves a safer curiosity, surely it does.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/holes_so_many_holes · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/primal_orifice` (in-game name "Trypophobia?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 107.10


:: The Cat Had It Coming [rambling] {"position":"1750,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Feline Felon! The whiskered menace misjudged its mark.
LOG: Hail, Feline Felon! Claws were drawn. Fur flew. The cat chose poorly. His dark hand chose better! Tiny tyrant toppled. Whiskers wilted. Pride remained gloriously intact. I applaud the victory, loudly. I also inspect nearby shadows. Cats hold grudges... and they fit beneath chairs. Such foes are beneath the Master, certainly. Yet ankles are very low targets. Salutations, Scourge of Soft Paws! Let no cushion conceal revenge. Quaver will keep both feet tucked safely beneath his stool tonight. Quiet now... cats hear footsteps.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_cat_had_it_coming · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/cat_killer` (in-game name "Kitty Cat Killer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles PEASANT_KILLS_1.JES


:: Endangered? Not Anymore. [rambling] {"position":"1900,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A rare beast fled beneath the sheltering bough / Its kind was scarce, and scarcer still is now!
LOG: There once was a beast, both precious and painfully rare / And it roamed beneath branches with magnificent soft silver hair! / The scholars begged mercy and pleaded to keep it alive / The Master went hunting, so fewer of those beasts survive. / And its cousins grow scarcer wherever dark hunters still roam / Soon one handsome new trophy is already travelling home! / I should sing a lament for the dearly departed breed / But rare beasts when butchered make splendid dark trophies indeed. / The keepers may count every footprint and track in despair / Our Lord counts one more fine pelt hanging safely there!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/endangered_not_anymore · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/poacher` (in-game name "Rare Animal Poacher") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.14


:: Fangs for the Collection [rambling] {"position":"2050,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Collector of Carnivore Cutlery! Teeth look better off the owner.
LOG: Greetings, Collector of Carnivore Cutlery! Fine fangs acquired. Ferocious owner dismissed! A predator once carried those teeth. Now the Master carries them better. Very tasteful. Very sharp. Very dead. I admire trophies with simple histories. Beast bites stranger. Dark Lord bites back harder! Still... perhaps hang them above eye level. A loose fang underfoot spoils a perfectly good entrance. Welcome, Warden of Wicked Whiskers! No, that title needs work. Keep the teeth. I shall keep the rhyme and a respectable distance from anything still attached to jaws. Teeth first, song second, distance always.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/fangs_for_the_collection · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/predator_killer` (in-game name "Predator Killer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D3_KAHN.JES


:: Reap What They Carry [rambling] {"position":"2200,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Good bits, Masta! Giblet wants all!
LOG: Giblet sees good bits! Good bones! Giblet sees scraps. Giblet sees value. Cut beast open! Take hard bits! Take sharp bits! Soft bits? Gristle gets those. Giblet wants horn. Giblet wants tooth. Maybe claw too. Master brings carcass. Giblet makes treasure! Waste nothing! Bad butcher drops things. Good butcher grabs all. Greedy? Yes! Greed keeps forge fed. Giblet knows that. Fifth knew too. Fifth lost hand. Still grabbed hammer! Good family. Very good family. Bring more beasts. Giblet sorts pieces. Bone here. Horn there. Metal-worthy bits here. Giblet hits later. Oh yes he will!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/reap_what_they_carry · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/greedy_butcher` (in-game name "Greedy Butcher") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ThatsMine01


:: The Cradle Likes It Raw [rambling] {"position":"2350,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: RAW? No! Fire fixes meat!
LOG: WHAT? Cradle wants raw? NO! Meat gets proper fire! Fire first, feeding after! Cradle spits cooked meat. Stupid hungry thing! Wants meat cold, wet, ugly. Makes me furious. I make crust! I make smoke! I make dinner behave! Bah, feed it raw. Good cuts stay mine! Those belong my pot. Meat goes cradle, no seasoning. Waste no spice! I save spice for mouths. Maybe cradle got no tongue. Sad little meat-hole. Still, Masta wants feeding. I do feeding. I complain LOUD! Cooked meat better. Always, always better.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_cradle_likes_it_raw · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/cooked_meat_sacrifice` (in-game name "Cooked Meat Disrelish") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_BurnBurn


:: Paste for the Pets [rambling] {"position":"2500,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Paste got no crust! I can fix!
LOG: I taste paste first. Ugh, warm mush! Smells almost like food. Almost! Digester chews all scraps. Spits out beast paste. I taste tiny dab. Too smooth. Needs salt. Needs heat. Needs CRUNCH! Pets maybe like warm slop. Pets eat paste then. Roast stays mine. Stir paste harder! No lumps hiding. Lumps mean lazy pot. I hate lazy pot. Add scraps, grind more. Good, goo moves right. Masta can feed beasts. I improve later. Fry paste flat maybe. Burn edge nice. Not burned wrong! Cooked bold. Big difference! Pot knows too.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/paste_for_the_pets · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/digester` (in-game name "Yummy Paste") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WhatAMess01


:: Every Meat, Sire [rambling] {"position":"2650,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: All meat! Bring hooks!
LOG: Meat! More meat! I see every kind. Raw, bloody, chewy, weird. Good meat pile! Mine eyes happy. Mine knife happier! I want roast each one. Slow one. Hot one. Char one. Sauce one. No cut escapes! Masta brings whole butcher-table. I judge fat first. Fat means flavour! Bone means broth. Skin means crisp. Tough bit gets hammer. Soft bit gets pan. Strange bit gets Blister? No! He licks anything. I cook first. If still moving, stab. If squeals, fresher! Every meat got purpose. Mostly eating purpose. I need more hooks. More salt. Bigger fire!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_meat_sire · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/raw_meat_collection` (in-game name "Collector of Raw Meats") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WeNeedMore01


:: Brewing With Guts [rambling] {"position":"2800,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Sssmell that... lovely guts.
LOG: Sssmell that... warm guts, sharp salt... lovely little mess. I stir slow... tissue curls, broth thickens... colour gets prettier. Not food... no, no... alchemy food maybe. I taste drop... tongue tingles left side... good sign. Another drop? ,maybe foolish. I do anyway, ears ring soft now. Master, this batch wants bone dust. Or tooth dust, hard tell. Bottle bubbles sideways, very polite poison. I keep lid loose, pressure gets moody. Gristle would shout, ruin whole mood. I whisper instead, ssso nice. Flesh, salts, little rot, all getting along beautifully.
