:: Meddling With Growth [rambling] {"position":"3100,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Growth twitches... yesss, Master.
LOG: Growth mix twitches... look close, Master... not too close. I feed one drop... stem swells wrong. Good wrong. Second drop... little teeth maybe?! ...no, just roots. I poke root... finger prickles. Gene stuff strange... tiny changes, big bodies. I like tiny causes. Less cleanup. Need more sample, not enough yet. Mix wants marrow, maybe slime. I sniff vial, eye starts twitching. Left eye only, right eye sensible. I mark that down, mentally. Paper got wet poison. Growth can be guided, nudged, bullied softly. Beautiful work. Dangerous work. Best kind, yesss.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/meddling_with_growth · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/genetic_compounds` (in-game name "Genetic Bio-Alchemy") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.NotEnough01


:: Secretions, Bottled [rambling] {"position":"3250,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Drip... drip... sssoft poison.
LOG: Drip... drip... lovely sound. Bottle fills slow... gland juice, slime... little clear ooze. I collect all... waste makes me sad. Master... this secretion smells sweet. Sweet usually lies. I touch drop... fingertip goes cold. Another jar smells rotten... much nicer. I breathe shallow... colours start humming. Hm... maybe lid tighter. Organic stuff gives itself freely, after squeezing enough. I whisper thanks, polite science. No need Gristle hearing. He calls everything sauce. This not sauce, probably. Could be sauce once. Bad sauce. Very interesting sauce. I cork jars, line them straight, keep sssoft one separate.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/secretions_bottled · fires on advancement `biomancy:biomancy/organic_compounds` (in-game name "Organic Bio-Alchemy") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 700.20


:: You Cured It? Why? [rambling] {"position":"3400,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: You cured it, Master? How alarmingly generous!
LOG: You actually cured it... deliberately, even, with your own hands! How very generous of your dark magnificence today, Master! Somewhere a priest just smiled without knowing the reason, my Lord! Do not let that become a regular habit, Sire. A curse reversed is still useful knowledge to possess for later. Today one wretch gets his miserable face restored completely by you. Tomorrow somebody less deserving may lose theirs instead... much better. Think strategically, kindness can still serve Evil very nicely! Once is research, and research sounds perfectly respectable to me!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/you_cured_it_why · fires on advancement `eidolon:cure_zombie` (in-game name "Curse Lifted") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 203.10


:: Chanting at Strays [rambling] {"position":"3550,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Cold at a word, Sire! Revenge should always travel well.
LOG: At last, cold magic earns its keep... revenge served properly! A few words, then winter bites somebody unpleasant, Master! I rather like that arrangement for clean little murders, my Lord! No furnace, fuel, or messy heap of kindling required anywhere nearby. Freeze toes, stiffen fingers, and spoil their courage nicely before striking. Very clean carnage... almost elegant enough for court, my Lord. Even snow becomes respectable when obeying your command properly. Ah, cold and screaming together, lovely work indeed! Do keep chanting until somebody important starts shivering hard!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/chanting_at_strays · fires on advancement `eidolon:frost_spell` (in-game name "Call of Winter") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Nordberg_Town_Chunk_4 310.30


:: Healing? Wash Your Hands. [rambling] {"position":"3700,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Healing, Master? Wash your hands before anyone sees!
LOG: That was a healing touch? Oh dear, wash your hands! That looked dangerously charitable for your dark magnificence, Master! Still, repaired flesh can suffer all over again later, my Lord! That makes healing useful, not virtuous, which is very reassuring to everyone sensible. Mend yourself first whenever somebody dents your magnificence, Sire. Mend servants when replacing them becomes bothersome and expensive instead. Leave sainthood to fools who enjoy marble statues and grateful peasants! Practical kindness is far less embarrassing when properly explained afterward. Ah... maintenance with warm blood, much better indeed!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/healing_wash_your_hands · fires on advancement `eidolon:lay_on_hands` (in-game name "Healing Touch") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Sys 200.20


:: Priests Teach Now? [rambling] {"position":"3850,4400","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Priests teaching you, Sire... how brave of them!
LOG: So, the Sacred Path has tutors now... brave little priests! Take every lesson those hopeful little creatures offer freely, Master! The Mother Goddess may bless whoever pleases her today, my Lord! She cannot choose what happens with that blessing afterward, fortunately. Bright power burns perfectly well in dark hands, Sire! Elves always confused beauty with goodness... tiresome creatures, every one. Priests make much the same mistake with blessings and obedience. Ah, let them teach you everything they know! Then demonstrate what their lessons become under proper management!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/priests_teach_now · fires on advancement `eidolon:sacred_path` (in-game name "The Sacred Path") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_D2_Abyss 210.40


:: A Goblet, Filled [rambling] {"position":"1000,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Blood in the goblet, Master! Now the ritual is paying attention.
LOG: The goblet is full of blood at last... proper ceremony! Warm, red, useful, and already measured for us, Master! The rite has surprisingly decent taste for religion, my Lord! A little life goes wonderfully far in ceremony and bargaining. Priests call it sacrifice with very solemn little faces, naturally. I call it efficient pouring in expensive robes, Sire. If something unseen answers, splendid... we have its full attention now! If it demands more, negotiate while armed and smiling! Never let a cup dictate terms to an Overlord!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_goblet_filled · fires on advancement `eidolon:sacrifice` (in-game name "Blood for the Dark One") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 415.10


:: Smiting Is Rude [rambling] {"position":"1150,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Holy smiting, Sire! Mortis may call that rude.
LOG: A holy smite in your hands... Mortis may raise one dignified eyebrow! Do it again, Master, because that worked beautifully just now! Light seems terribly offended by the dead, my Lord! Very judgmental stuff, holiness, always choosing sides so loudly and brightly. Still, a useful blast remains wonderfully useful in your hands. If some corpse defies you, smite it properly and loudly, Sire! Tools need not share their Master's morals, thankfully for us. They merely need obedient results... preferably smoking ones afterward. Ah, sanctity with proper direction at last!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/smiting_is_rude · fires on advancement `eidolon:smite_undead` (in-game name "The light's Fury") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Nordberg_Town_Chunk_4 440.20


:: One Fewer Peasant [rambling] {"position":"1300,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: One fewer peasant, Master! The altar appears satisfied.
LOG: There goes another peasant... the ritual seems thoroughly pleased! So am I, Master, rather more honestly than the altar! Villagers multiply quickly enough to spare one occasionally, my Lord! Sometimes one may even serve a grander purpose before supper, Sire. Blood, timing, altar... very respectable ingredients for serious ceremony. Priests call this a greater sacrifice, naturally enough. I call it better accounting with candles and fewer living witnesses! Random slaughter is recreation, this has paperwork, candles, and witnesses attached. Ah, civilization makes everything sound nicer!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/one_fewer_peasant · fires on advancement `eidolon:villager_sacrifice` (in-game name "A Greater Sacrifice") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 903.10


:: Witches Know Best [rambling] {"position":"1450,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Wicked Path, Sire... much more familiar surroundings!
LOG: Ah, the Wicked Path... much more familiar territory! Smoke, blood, whispers... proper educational surroundings, Master! Witches always understand useful stains, my Lord, especially permanent ones! They rarely scrub away the interesting parts afterward, sensible old creatures. Take whatever answers, but trust nothing that answers too eagerly. Dark powers have appetites too, Sire, sometimes enormous hungry ones! If a bargain grows flowery, burn it quickly before signing anything. If it grows useful, read every tiny word first. Then take the power and keep your name!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/witches_know_best · fires on advancement `eidolon:wicked_path` (in-game name "The Wicked Path") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 800.10


:: Soup, But Worse [rambling] {"position":"1600,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Sssoup murmurs... not normal.
LOG: Crucible murmurs... soup should not murmur. I lean closer... steam smells metal, ash... something sleepy. Nice. Spoon goes in... spoon comes out black. Still spoon? ...mostly. Master... alchemical sssoup thick today. I sip edge, very tiny sip. Teeth buzz, one ear whistles. Flavour starts bitter, ends somewhere purple. That not flavour word, but true. Add powder slowly, surface opens little eye. I blink first. Eye wins. Fine. Stir clockwise, then forget why. Soup wants more heat? ,maybe less me. I step back, bowl follows bubble. Gristle would boil harder. I prefer listening.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/soup_but_worse · fires on advancement `eidolon:crucible` (in-game name "Alchemical Soup") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WhatAMess01


:: The Dead Obey You [rambling] {"position":"1750,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The dead hear you, Sire. They obey.
LOG: The dead obey! That is proper. Breath is not required. Loyalty may outlast it. You have enthralled one, Sire. The corpse hears. The corpse serves. Command remains after pulse. Some call this unnatural. They misunderstand the grave. Death changes duties, not ownership. Still, keep the balance. A borrowed servant carries debt. Souls notice such accounting. Graves notice more. We live. We serve. We die. Some continue working afterward. Efficient, in its way. I approve of punctual corpses. Keep the command simple. The dead prefer certainty. Complicated orders decay faster than bodies.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_dead_obey_you · fires on advancement `eidolon:enthrall_undead` (in-game name "A New Servant") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.50


:: Harvest Season [rambling] {"position":"1900,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The scythe has work. Let it reap.
LOG: A scythe should reap. Yours has learned well. Grain falls. Flesh falls. Souls follow both. Hold it steady, Sire. A wild sweep wastes effort. Death dislikes waste. One clean cut settles matters. That is cleaner. The reaper needs no hurry. Everyone comes eventually. This blade merely improves the schedule. Do not fear its shape. I have carried one long. It is quite companionable. Better company than most living things. It never complains about the weather. Keep the edge clean. A dull reaper embarrasses everyone. Even corpses deserve competent harvesting.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/harvest_season · fires on advancement `eidolon:reaper_scythe` (in-game name "Reaping Time") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.45


:: Promoted to Zombie [rambling] {"position":"2050,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: One duty ended. Another rose.
LOG: One life ended. Another service began. You made a zombie, Sire. The flesh rose badly. The duty rose intact. That is enough. A corpse needs little comfort. It needs no wages or sleep. Opinions are also absent. There are virtues in death. There are odours too. Keep some distance. The balance still matters. Death for life. A life returned requires weight. Even crude resurrection leaves a mark. This one may shamble. It may groan. It may lose pieces. Promotion is rarely perfect. Give it simple work. Complex thought belongs elsewhere. A zombie performs best without promotion meetings. Keep it supervised.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/promoted_to_zombie · fires on advancement `eidolon:zombify` (in-game name "A New Recruit for the Dark") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.NO2


:: Someone's Crypt, Sire [rambling] {"position":"2200,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: A crypt, Master! Someone's privacy has just expired.
LOG: Someone buried this crypt deep... very private indeed! How unfortunate for them, Master, and fortunate for your curiosity! Old graves hide excellent secrets, my Lord, especially rich ones! Wards reveal exactly what frightened the owner most in life. Treasure reveals what they loved enough to hide underground from everybody. Bones reveal what eventually won the argument for good, Sire! Search every dusty corner... especially the locked ones. Dangerous or valuable, those are our favourite little categories in ruins. If something whispers your name, whisper back with steel!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/someones_crypt_sire · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/enter_catacombs` (in-game name "Dungeon Delving") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D3_SD3_TheUnderstreets 100.10


:: Ink Fit for a Tyrant [rambling] {"position":"2350,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Legendary ink, Sire! Finally, stationery worthy of tyranny.
LOG: Now this is stationery worthy of a tyrant... legendary ink! Do not waste it on shopping lists, Master, I beg you! This stuff deserves wicked words, preferably expensive ones, my Lord! Wizards adore precious supplies and endless little ceremonies around every scratch. Ink, vellum, quills, moonlight... such exhausting fuss for simple writing! Take the useful part and skip their posing entirely, Sire. Write something that bites back when opened by enemies or creditors. Ah, scholarship improves enormously beneath proper tyranny! Even the margins look more imposing in your hands.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/ink_fit_for_a_tyrant · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/ink_legendary` (in-game name "Premium!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 105.20


:: Follow the Needle [rambling] {"position":"2500,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: A compass toward trouble, Master! Much better than north.
LOG: This compass points toward trouble... much better than boring north! Follow the needle, Master, it looks almost eager for blood! Ordinary travelers ask where they are, poor little lost creatures! You ask what needs conquering next, my Lord, which is much healthier. That is why you wear armour while they carry maps! Peasant maps always flatter their own village shamelessly, Sire. This little needle flatters danger instead... charming device. If it finds treasure, excellent! If it finds danger, the treasure probably hired expensive guards to keep you out.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/follow_the_needle · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/make_wayward_compass` (in-game name "And so a Quest Begins!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 404.40


:: A Dead King's Diary [rambling] {"position":"2650,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A dead king's book, Sire! He is unlikely to ask for it back.
LOG: A dead king left you his spellbook... how considerate! Death has ended the ownership dispute, Master, very tidily indeed! Read everything, especially the forbidden bits, my Lord! Old rulers hoard the best tricks until burial, selfish old creatures with vaults. Immortality, curses, wards, revenge... predictable royal tastes, really. If his ghost complains, splendid news indeed, Sire! That means the book still matters after all. Nothing validates stolen scholarship like an angry former owner returning from death. Ah, inheritance without an heir, beautifully efficient, and wonderfully quiet!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_dead_kings_diary · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/spell_book_dead_king` (in-game name "Necronomicon") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 205.10


:: Bound in Dragon [rambling] {"position":"2800,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Dragon-bound spells, Master! Wizards do love expensive covers.
LOG: Wizards bound spells in dragon hide... expensive covers! Feel that hide, Master, terribly dramatic stuff in your hands! The contents had better deserve such extravagant vanity and expensive scales, my Lord! We need not solve every dragon mystery today, thankfully. We can still steal dragon scholarship quite happily, Sire! Read the elder spells and keep the book very close to the Tower. If the binding survives fire... excellent craftsmanship indeed. If the spells cause fire, even better! Knowledge wrapped in arrogance suits your library very nicely, beside darker things.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/bound_in_dragon · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/spell_book_dragon` (in-game name "Elder Power") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 200.10


:: Stolen From Illagers [rambling] {"position":"2950,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Stolen Illager magic, Sire! Theft improves most scholarship.
LOG: You stole an Illager grimoire... improved already! Raiders hate losing anything useful, Master, especially their magic! Their spells are noisy, theatrical, and terribly pleased with themselves, my Lord! Summon, gesture, shout... then hope somebody screams loudly nearby. Crude, yes, but effective in wicked hands like yours, Master. Read their tricks and keep the book! If they demand it back, laugh loudly first. Then test their own spells on them, educational and fair! Theft should always include a proper demonstration afterward, preferably on witnesses.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stolen_from_illagers · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/spell_book_evoker` (in-game name "Grimoire of Evokation") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 501.30


:: A Peasant's Prayer Book [rambling] {"position":"3100,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: A peasant prayer book, Master... try not to get hope on your gauntlet.
LOG: A peasant prayer book has become useful at last... try not to sneeze! It probably smells of bread and hope, Master, revolting little mixture! Do read it anyway, my Lord... carefully and privately! Peasants preserve useful little protections surprisingly well over many frightened generations. Wizards overlook anything that appears too simple for their towering pride, naturally. Their loss may become your considerable gain, Sire! Healing and warding still serve tyranny beautifully. Ah, virtue is wonderfully portable once stolen! Keep the prayer if the power proves worth the embarrassment, then hide the cover.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_peasants_prayer_book · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/spell_book_villager` (in-game name "Enlightenment") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 1000.30


:: Wizards Hate Sharing [rambling] {"position":"3250,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: You robbed a wizard, Sire! Ah, scholarship at its finest.
LOG: You stole from a wizard, Sire... excellent instincts, as ever! They become wonderfully educational when properly offended, Master! Gold can be replaced, my Lord, but private research hurts more! Take the scrolls, inks, and anything guarded with particular nervous fuss. Ignore lectures about scholarly property and professional courtesy entirely. Wizards stole half their wisdom from older graves! You merely improved the ancient tradition with much better timing. If he calls you a fool... steal something else! Nothing sharpens academic debate like losing another treasured possession.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/wizards_hate_sharing · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/steal_from_wizard` (in-game name "A Fool's Folly") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D5_MAIN 206.10


:: A Stick That Burns [rambling] {"position":"3400,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: FWOOSH! Giblet likes burn-stick!
LOG: FWOOSH! Stick burns! Hah! Giblet likes this. Not proper blade. Still burns good! Wood holds flame. Strange trick. Giblet taps it. Tap tap. No break. Good stick! Master waves it. Fire jumps out! Better than torch. Worse than sword. Maybe both together? Giblet thinks yes. Heat makes work. Sparks make happy. Fire makes metal listen. This stick brings fire. Giblet respects that. No old dragon tale. No silly legend. Just hot. Hot is enough. Keep grip tight! Burn enemy. Burn scrap. Burn nothing useful. Giblet knows useful. Oh yes he does!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_stick_that_burns · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/staff_pyrium` (in-game name "Ancient Beckonings") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_BurnBurn


:: Mouldy Magic [rambling] {"position":"3550,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Rot took the cover. Not the spell.
LOG: Rot has entered the book. The magic remains. Interesting. Mould feeds on neglect. Spells sometimes do the same. Turn pages carefully, Sire. Damp vellum tears easily. Old power does not. A rotten book may still bite. That is the useful part. The smell is less useful. Graveyards teach patience with odours. Libraries should learn the same. Keep it dry now. Let the decay stop here. Knowledge may age. Knowledge may sour. It should not become compost before reading. Wrap it in cloth. Keep worms away. They are excellent readers, but terrible librarians. Preserve what remains.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/mouldy_magic · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/spell_book_rotten` (in-game name "How long's this been here?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.QUIT4


:: Written in You [rambling] {"position":"3700,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Blood makes intimate ink. You do enjoy writing yourself into things.
LOG: You wrote blood into a book? Of course you did, because ink was never intimate enough. There is vanity in it. I rather admire that. A spell drawn from yourself feels different, does it not? Closer, hungrier, less polite. The old priests preferred words scrubbed clean of appetite. They were terribly afraid of honesty. You are not, and that interests me. Leave the book near tonight. Read it when the room is quiet... notice which passages seem to breathe back. If it stains your fingers, darling, do not wash too quickly. Some signatures deserve to linger.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/written_in_you · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/spell_book_blood` (in-game name "A piece of Yourself") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S01E01 1048


:: The Dead King's Sceptre [rambling] {"position":"3850,4550","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A dead king's sceptre suits you better than it suited him.
LOG: A dead king's sceptre. How very flattering. Power loves a corpse with accessories. Does it feel heavier than expected? It should, because blood remembers rank when kingdoms forget it. Hold it loosely while everyone else imagines the effort. You need not imitate the king who carried it. He is dead, after all. His taste may have been excellent. His timing clearly was not. I wonder whether he begged at the end? No matter. The sceptre has changed hands, which is the only royal ceremony worth attending. Take the old crown if there was one. The stick is better.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_dead_kings_sceptre · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/staff_blood_staff` (in-game name "Staff of Blood") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S03E01 317


:: An Old Codex, Restored [rambling] {"position":"1000,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The restoration is competent. Please keep the volume dry.
LOG: A restored codex deserves examination... before celebration. Age alone proves very little. What matters is survival. Ink persists where owners do not. Bindings endure longer than vows. This volume has endured remarkably well... once repaired. Note the margins. Someone expected later hands to read them. Perhaps yours. Perhaps mine. Do not assume the missing years are accidental. Gaps can be curated as carefully as pages. Keep the book dry and separate from common shelves. I would like to inspect the older repairs when convenient. Their workmanship may tell us more than the text.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/an_old_codex_restored · fires on advancement `irons_spellbooks:irons_spellbooks/spell_book_netherite` (in-game name "Ancient Knowledge") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until That Is Not a Fish (overlord:tales/that_is_not_a_fish) has UNLOCKED (the Collector's first appearance) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: DREDGE Row 1045


:: Pelting Raiders, Sire? [rambling] {"position":"1150,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A rotten tomato, Master! What a magnificently petty weapon.
LOG: You threw rotten produce at an armed raider... Oh, that is insulting in exactly the right way, Master! Anyone can answer steel with steel, my Lord, very dull and terribly expected! Rotten fruit attacks pride before it bruises anything important. Raiders build their authority from fear, banners, beasts, shouting, and swagger. Splatter one with rotten pulp and watch that swagger drip, Sire! Keep your weapon ready afterward... humiliation makes them energetic. Still, what a splendid use for spoiled produce! Even bad vegetables may serve Evil when thrown with confidence.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/pelting_raiders_sire · fires on advancement `farmersdelight:main/hit_raider_with_rotten_tomato` (in-game name "Boo! Hiss!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_D1_Abyss 402.10


:: A Knife Too Fancy [rambling] {"position":"1300,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Fancy knife. Giblet sees good edge!
LOG: Too fancy. Tiny knife! Too shiny. Giblet squints. Good edge though. Very good edge! Netherite bites clean. Handle fits hand. Blade stays mean. Giblet tests nail. Scratch! Good. Tests old plate. Scratch again! Better. Kitchen knife? Hah! Gristle gets jealous. Giblet not care. Knife cuts food. Knife cuts foe. Same edge. Different mess. Master should keep it. Fancy bits can stay. Edge matters most. Point matters too. Giblet made worse-looking blades. Those killed fine! Pretty no hurt. Pretty no help. Sharp helps. Giblet approves. Mostly. Needs one hammer tap. Maybe three!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_knife_too_fancy · fires on advancement `farmersdelight:main/obtain_netherite_knife` (in-game name "If You Can't Take the Heat...") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 102.20


:: Balanced Meals, How Dull [rambling] {"position":"1450,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Balanced? Bah! Add pepper!
LOG: Balanced? Who asked balanced? Sounds sleepy already. Bit grain, bit veg, bit meat. All behaving too nice. Kitchen needs anger. Where rage? Where scorch? Food should FIGHT BACK! I still taste it. Hm, good body. Good chew too. Annoyingly proper. Masta eats, stays strong. Hmph, I accept. But I add pepper. Then more pepper! Now meal wakes up. Nourishing can still hurt. That makes sense. I hate dull plates. Beige food insults kitchen. Give colour! Give smoke! Give knife marks! Meal smiles polite? Sear it! I want loud dinner. Masta deserves loud dinner.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/balanced_meals_how_dull · fires on advancement `farmersdelight:main/eat_nourishing_food` (in-game name "Nourishing!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Nice01


:: Ham, Freshly Liberated [rambling] {"position":"1600,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: HAM! Nobody touch mine!
LOG: Fresh ham! Mine! Big cut too. Good fat cap. Nice pink meat. I smell feast already! Whoever owned pig part before, too late. Ham liberated! I score skin. Salt deep. Hang near heat. Not too close. Yet. Let fat wake slow. Then FIRE! Skin pops loud. Skin listens! Good sound. I slap anyone touching. Mine kitchen, mine ham! Masta gets first slice. Thick slice. Juices run. Quaver gets end bit maybe. If sings nice. Giblet gets bone? No, bone for stock. No one steals stock bone. I count bones. I count hams. I count fingers near hams!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/ham_freshly_liberated · fires on advancement `farmersdelight:main/get_ham` (in-game name "Wild Butcher") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ThatsMine01


:: Fungus Farming [rambling] {"position":"1750,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Good fungus! Into pan!
LOG: I smell mushrooms spreading. Good dark crop! Good dark food! Fat caps crowd logs. Dirt smell, dinner smell. Some smell poison. Blister tests those. I cook safe ones! Butter first, heat after. Salt too. More heat! Mushrooms shrink too much. Rude little things! Need bigger basket. Need bigger colony. Let them crowd wood. Let them push dirt. I harvest hardest caps. Soft ones into stew. Tough stems chopped small. Nothing wasted. Masta gets pan full. Brown fungus, black crust, hot steam. Better than flowers! Flowers taste like apology. Mushrooms taste like dinner.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/fungus_farming · fires on advancement `farmersdelight:main/get_mushroom_colony` (in-game name "Fungus Among Us") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Treasure01


:: Every Dish, Devoured [rambling] {"position":"1900,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Empty plates! THAT means good!
LOG: Empty plates everywhere! GOOD! Means food worked. Means mouths busy. I know each bowl. I know each crust. Stew scraped clean. Roast picked bare. Sauce wiped up. That is praise! Quaver hears nothing. He writes song. Plate tells truth better. Empty means good. Full means insult. No insult here! Clean bowls shine. Masta ate whole spread. Fine appetite. Proper appetite. I want bigger table. Two pots boiling. Three pans screaming. Bread near fire. Meat over flame. Veg hides under meat. Feast grows meaner. I cook till table groans. Then cook more!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_dish_devoured · fires on advancement `farmersdelight:main/master_chef` (in-game name "Master Chef") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ThatWasFun01


:: Every Seed Planted [rambling] {"position":"2050,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Seeds today! Supper later!
LOG: Whole field planted! Tiny future food. Future soup everywhere! I like that. Not eating yet though. Annoying. Seed down, then wait. Water, then wait more. Sun, more waiting! Cooking faster. Still, crop comes later. Wheat, roots, herbs, greens. All become pot victims. I mark good rows. Mark spicy rows. Mark no-touch rows. Masta planted whole lot. Smart. Kitchen hates empty baskets. Fields fix baskets. I respect dirt work. Little bit. Grubbison likes dirt too much. Like what dirt gives me. Food! Harvest comes, no one eat raw! I am watching.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_seed_planted · fires on advancement `farmersdelight:main/plant_all_crops` (in-game name "Crop Rotation") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 104.10


:: A Pot Full of Mana [rambling] {"position":"2200,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Blue pot? Keep spoon back!
LOG: Keep spoon back! Pot glowing blue! I do not trust. Pot should glow red. Red means HOT! Blue means Blister nonsense. Mana smell wrong. Still, mana bubbles inside. Spoon hums too. Spoon should NOT hum! I stir anyway. Liquid pulls sparks around. Strange soup. Not soup? Everything in pot turns soup. I can season magic. Maybe. Add herb. Glow brighter. Hah! Add pepper. Pot spits, rude thing. I spit back. Masta gets mana brew. Not dinner. Bah. My ladle stays separate! No magic taste in stew. Touch wrong pot, lose hand! Simple rule.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_pot_full_of_mana · fires on advancement `farmers_spell:alchemist_pot` (in-game name "Brimming with Mana") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_FireNoHurt


:: Blood Tofu. Really. [rambling] {"position":"2350,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Blood tofu? I fry first!
LOG: I poke blood tofu. Wobble at me! Really, blood tofu? Blood belongs on meat. Blood still blood. This block steals blood. BIG insult! I fry it hard. HISS, now better! Edge darkens, middle stays soft. Maybe edible now. I taste corner careful. Hm, not terrible! Do not smile yet! I said not terrible. Add garlic, hot oil. Add more hot oil! Now thing got courage. Masta can eat it. Call it blood brick. Sounds much stronger. Tofu sounds weak. Inventor gets spoon thrown. Plate empty later? Then genius idea. Mine genius idea. Forget first part.
