:: Every Monster Carved [rambling] {"position":"2950,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Carver of Curious Carcasses! The menu has become a bestiary.
LOG: Hail, Carver of Curious Carcasses! Every strange beast has met the knife. Splendid work! The board groans. The platters glisten. The cookbooks may need stronger bindings. I prefer my monsters at a distance... or sliced very thin. Yet such a feast deserves a verse. / He carved through claw and horn with cheer, the rarest cuts all gathered here! / From crypt to cave the courses came, each butchered beast enlarged his fame! Salutations, Sovereign of Supper Specimens! If Gristle asks for a tasting singer, I have suddenly lost my appetite.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_monster_carved · fires on advancement `dungeonsdelight:main/all_knife_mob_drops` (in-game name "Gastrocryptozoologist") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 100.10


:: Who's the Monster Now? [rambling] {"position":"3100,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The monsters brewed their vilest poisons into bane / He wore them all and walked away again!
LOG: And each monster brought venom, corruption, fever, and poisonous flame / And the Master endured every foul and disgusting little game! / And their curses grew nastier, their draughts became terribly grand / Yet none of those horrors could stop where he'd stand! / I would have fainted before even one brew was done / I promptly claimed in the ballad that clearly I'd won! / The beasts mixed their vilest effects into one dreadful stew / Then he swallowed the trouble and calmly came wandering through. / A monster may season its victim with sickness and pain / And against such a Master, that recipe tastes rather plain!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/whos_the_monster_now · fires on advancement `dungeonsdelight:main/all_monster_effects` (in-game name "Monsters Smashed") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.13


:: An Entire Horse, Sire? [rambling] {"position":"3250,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Welcome, Devourer of Distinguished Destriers! The stable has filed a complaint.
LOG: Welcome, Devourer of Distinguished Destriers! One horse entered. No horse left. Astonishing appetite! Hooves vanished. Mane vanished. Dignity vanished shortly afterward. The Master has eaten feasts before, but this one once had a saddle. I salute such hunger from a smaller plate. Much smaller. Perhaps a biscuit. Perhaps half. Greetings, Galloper-Gobbler of Grand Proportion! The title is dreadful. The deed is worse. Still, a full horse is a full verse. I only beg that the next course lacks reins, shoes, and any chance of recognizing me. Stable doors closed... excellent.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/an_entire_horse_sire · fires on advancement `dungeonsdelight:main/eat_horse` (in-game name "How Hungry...?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D1_FOOD.JES


:: Yams Turned on Yams [rambling] {"position":"3400,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Tuber-Turner of Treacherous Yams! Their own filth joined the fight.
LOG: Hail, Tuber-Turner of Treacherous Yams! Their own foul muck became the weapon. Poetic enough! The yams advanced. The gunk flew. The field became dinner's revenge. I stood well back. Mud stains bells. / The yam struck yam with septic spray, and root fought root throughout the fray! / The Master watched the crop revolt, then sent each tuber to its jolt! Salutations, Sultan of Spoiled Starch! I may revise that later. Preferably after somebody washes the battlefield.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/yams_turned_on_yams · fires on advancement `dungeonsdelight:main/use_gunk_arrow_on_monster_yam` (in-game name "Septic Tank") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 100.20


:: The Cleaver of Heresy [rambling] {"position":"3550,4700","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Big cleaver, Masta! Giblet wants swing!
LOG: Give cleaver here! Now good. Heavy back. Mean edge. Giblet grabs handle. Nice weight! Chop once. Chop twice. Table cries. Good table test. Heresy? Big word. Giblet says meat-splitter. Bone-splitter. Helm-splitter too! Master swings better. Much better. Cleaver wants work. Giblet can hear it. Clang in head. Chop in hand. Simple. Good. Netherite holds shape. Bad steel curls. This one not curl. Giblet respects stubborn metal. Put no flowers on it. Put no gold curls. Leave ugly. Ugly works. Master likes works. Giblet likes works. Hit it until good! This already good!
