:: Well, That Collapsed [rambling] {"position":"1750,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: CRASH! Giblet says bad case!
LOG: CRASH! Case down! Bad case! Very bad case. Giblet looks down. Pieces everywhere. Glass sad. Frame bent. Trophy maybe squashed. Hah! What a mess. Good lesson though. Thin legs bad. Weak join bad. Too much shiny? Also bad. Giblet warned nobody. Falling case proves Giblet right! Master needs cases standing. Standing means strong. Strong means thick. Thick means heavy. Heavy means good! Giblet can fix. Hammer here. Brace there. More iron under. Less wobble. No dainty feet! Dainty feet die. Case should survive Brown bump. Maybe two Brown bumps. Giblet makes next one meaner. Hit until sturdy!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/well_that_collapsed · fires on advancement `display_case:collapse` (in-game name "The collapse") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WhatAMess01


:: A Case in a Case [rambling] {"position":"1900,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Case in case? Hah! Giblet likes!
LOG: Case in case? Hah! Giblet stares. Opens one. More case. Opens that. More? Hah! Clever box. Annoying box. Giblet likes both. Metal frame good. Hinges tiny. Tiny hinges still good! Master keeps treasure deep. Thief opens first. Finds second. Thief gets tired. Good plan. Giblet would use hammer. Thief maybe does too. Then cases need strength! Strong outside. Strong inside. Strong all way down. Giblet understands now. Box protects box. Box protects thing. Thing maybe another box! Hah! Good foolishness. Giblet wants make one. Needs much iron. Much glass. Much hammering. Good day!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_case_in_a_case · fires on advancement `display_case:infinity_case` (in-game name "To infinity and beyond") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Nice01


:: Untouched by the Third [rambling] {"position":"2050,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: Untouched by Helvar, Sire... ah, old Master, meet new.
LOG: Not one mark from Helvar... not once! Master, I know exactly what such a victory truly means. He conquered the Infernal Abyss in his own reign, my Lord! Madness did not erase the warrior beneath that corruption! Nor did centuries make every old strike less deadly to face. Yet he never marked your armour or flesh, Sire! Forgive an old Minion a little pride... just this once. One reign stood against another, and the older one fell. The living Master walked away untouched, magnificent work!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/untouched_by_the_third · fires on advancement `block_factorys_bosses:no_hit_underworld_knight` (in-game name "Beyond Death") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Endboss_Abyss 300.20


:: Under a Minute, Sire! [rambling] {"position":"2200,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Salutations, Swift Scourge of Stubborn Foes! The song lasted longer than the fight.
LOG: Salutations, Swift Scourge of Stubborn Foes! Barely begun. Already finished! The enemy entered with menace. The enemy left as history. I had not reached my second flourish. Very inconsiderate. Still, speed deserves ceremony! One minute for the foe. Far longer for the title. Welcome, Breaker of Brief Battles! Drums ready. Trumpets ready. Quaver nearly ready. The Master needs none of us, apparently. A swing, a crash, a corpse. Simple! I shall stretch the applause so the occasion does not feel embarrassingly short. Very fast... almost suspiciously fast.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/under_a_minute_sire · fires on advancement `block_factorys_bosses:kill_boss_under_minute` (in-game name "Overclocker") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles BEAT_JESTER1.JES


:: Not a Scorch Mark [rambling] {"position":"2350,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The dragon roared and filled the cavern air with flame / He crossed untouched and made the beast his fame!
LOG: The dragon came roaring with furnace-hot smoke, flame, and breath / His blackened boots carried him through scorching air, danger, and death! / Its claws struck the stone while its great wings battered air / Yet nothing could scorch him or singe one black hair! / I watched from a hollow where cooler dark shadows lay / From safety I praised every stroke at sensible distance away! / Let dragons boast proudly of talon, fire, fury, and might / This hunter walked spotless and smiling away from the fight! / The beast kept its treasure of smoke, scale, and gold / His skin kept no scorch, which makes better tales told!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/not_a_scorch_mark · fires on advancement `block_factorys_bosses:no_hit_dragon` (in-game name "Dragon Hunter") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.49


:: Dry as a Bone [rambling] {"position":"2500,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The Kraken struck through foam and hammered at the bay / He stayed untouched and sent the beast away!
LOG: The sea grew great arms and came crashing over the deck / His iron stance then answered the monstrous wet wreck! / And its tentacles hammered through salt, foam, rigging, and spray / And yet none of them dragged his dark dignity away. / And the Kraken made whirlpools and battered each towering wave / He finished the fight still as dry as a grave! / I climbed the tall mast where the rigging felt sound / I crouched in the rigging while angry tentacles thrashed round. / And the sailors may boast they have weathered the foam / He fought the sea's terror and carried dry boots home!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dry_as_a_bone · fires on advancement `block_factorys_bosses:no_hit_kraken` (in-game name "Wraith of the Tide") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.37


:: Not Even Sandy [rambling] {"position":"2650,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The worm burst roaring from beneath the burning sand / He sent it down beneath his darker hand!
LOG: And the desert split open beneath his long black stride / Then a deathworm came lunging with jaws opened terribly wide! / It snapped through the sunlight and rolled across the plain / The Master walked onward without taking so much as a stain! / No tooth marked his armour, no sand marked his trail / The worm had great fury and somehow still managed to fail! / I watched from firm ground where the dunes remained still / And cheered while he taught buried monsters how to chill. / And the dunes may conceal every tooth under shimmering light / Then he leaves them all buried when ending the fight!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/not_even_sandy · fires on advancement `block_factorys_bosses:no_hit_sandworm` (in-game name "Desert Power") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.30


:: Not a Scratch in the Snow [rambling] {"position":"2800,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The Yeti swung through snow and shattered icy sleet / It never laid one claw upon his feet!
LOG: The Yeti came roaring downhill through the white frozen snow / The Master stood ready and welcomed the whole dreadful show! / Its claws carved the ice while its fists battered white / And yet none of those swings ever landed quite right. / No scratch marked his armour, no bruise marked his frame / I watched from the fire and loudly sang of his fame! / And the blizzard blew sideways, the beast thundered down below / He crossed through the battle still clean as the snow. / A beast dressed in winter may roar from the hill / His spotless black armour somehow looks handsomer still!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/not_a_scratch_in_the_snow · fires on advancement `block_factorys_bosses:no_hit_yeti` (in-game name "King of the Hill") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.54


:: Well, That Went Badly [rambling] {"position":"2950,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: You fell, Sire. You also returned.
LOG: You fell, Sire. The foe did not. Briefly unfortunate. Death reached for you. It failed to keep hold. That happens. Rarely. Do not grow careless. The grave remembers arrogance. It also remembers repeat visitors. Return stronger. Return prepared. Return with fewer openings. There is no shame in dying once. Staying dead is less productive. I have known many warriors. Most learned that distinction late. You have another chance. Spend it better. I will keep the plot ready, just in case. Remember the blow. Remember the opening. The dead are patient teachers. Tuition can be severe.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/well_that_went_badly · fires on advancement `block_factorys_bosses:die_boss` (in-game name "Bosses' Rise") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.QUIT2


:: Shellfish, Shelled [rambling] {"position":"3100,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Shellfish, shelled, Master! Gristle may want a look.
LOG: Well, the shellfish is shelled... one almost wants butter! That thing had claws enough for six full dinners, Master! It still failed against your magnificence, my Lord, rather badly! Old corruption makes ridiculous bodies dangerous, never truly dignified or less edible. Look at those shattered plates and twitching little legs nearby. Beneath all that menace... seafood, Sire, ordinary seafood! I find that strangely reassuring after such a noisy, claw-filled struggle. Horrors become friendlier when one imagines the sauce! Perhaps Gristle will call it supper, after we leave.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/shellfish_shelled · fires on advancement `cataclysm:kill_clawdian` (in-game name "Not so Shrimple Now") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 1100.10


:: A Golem, Rift-Flavoured [rambling] {"position":"3250,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Strange stone, strange magic, Sire... smash first, theorize carefully.
LOG: That golem looks distinctly unwell... purple, brooding, unfriendly! Old magic has soured inside hosts before, Master, remember that. This stone carries the same wrong little smell, my Lord! Do not name the cause yet... evidence before conclusions, always, my cautious Lord! We have too little to praise our cleverness, Sire. Break the thing and watch what clings to the pieces! Stone should stay stone, preferably obedient, decorative, quiet, and beneath your boots. When masonry starts carrying bad magic, smash harder! Ah, glowing architecture with ambitions, always a promising disaster.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_golem_rift_flavoured · fires on advancement `cataclysm:kill_ender_golem` (in-game name "Palette Swap") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Wastelands 210.20


:: Put Out That Fire [rambling] {"position":"3400,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Still burning, Master! Put the stubborn corpse out.
LOG: It is still burning after death... how industrious! Somebody has overachieved in the worst possible direction, Master! Fire should solve corpses, not employ them, my Lord! Yet corruption teaches dreadful persistence to anything dead enough to listen. This revenant has studied that lesson with embarrassing enthusiasm for far too long. Strike hard and put the flaming nuisance down, Sire! If it burns forever... extinguish it violently and repeatedly. That is not philosophy, merely sensible housekeeping after battle! Ah, much better when the smoking thing stops moving at last.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/put_out_that_fire · fires on advancement `cataclysm:kill_revenant` (in-game name "Imperfect thing") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 101.30


:: Every Scar Settled [rambling] {"position":"3550,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Settler of Cataclysmic Scores! Eight scars, eight endings.
LOG: Greetings, Settler of Cataclysmic Scores! Eight old horrors answered. None remained standing! Factory, tomb, arena, reef. Prison, forge, citadel, sky. A grand tour of things best left buried. The Master left them quieter than he found them. / Eight scars rose up with teeth and spite, eight scars went dark beneath his might! / Old ruin, old rage, old bones, old flame, each ended underneath his name! Welcome, Auditor of Ancient Agonies! I prefer ruins once somebody else has finished screaming inside them.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_scar_settled · fires on advancement `cataclysm:kill_all_bosses` (in-game name "The Cataclysmfarer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles FULL_DUNGEON.JES


:: Corruption, How Lovely [rambling] {"position":"3700,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Corruption you can see, Sire! Much easier to decorate around.
LOG: The corruption is visible now... how considerate of it! Look at those stains spreading over the graves, Master! Rot has finally developed decorative instincts, my Lord, at last! The graveyard wears them rather better than flowers ever could, thank Evilness. Do not pet anything glowing, however attractive it looks. Soured power loves pretty disguises... nasty little habit, Sire. If the scenery moves, kill the scenery immediately! If it stays still, wait and watch very carefully, from somewhere dry. Graveyards reward patience with much worse surprises, lovely places indeed.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/corruption_how_lovely · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/corruption` (in-game name "Source of Evil") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.30


:: Mushrooms Gone Wrong [rambling] {"position":"3850,4850","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A mushroom with ambition, Master! Nature is finally improving.
LOG: Nature has made the mushroom enormous... an improvement! Look at that swollen thing, Master, absolutely splendid! Ordinary mushrooms crouch damply beneath trees and disappoint everyone with their harmlessness! This one has ambition, corruption, and properly threatening height above your helmet. Much better than another harmless woodland ornament, my Lord! Do not stand beneath it too long, Sire, however tempting. If smaller ones start growing teeth... burn them immediately. Gristle may ask whether the thing is edible! Tell him after we leave, preferably from very far away, with fire ready.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/mushrooms_gone_wrong · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/giant_mushroom` (in-game name "Corrupting the Paradise") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.40


:: Tea With the Dead [rambling] {"position":"1000,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Tea with the dead, Sire! Mind the chair... and the host.
LOG: Tea with the dead... civilized, almost! Mind that chair, Master, I distinctly saw it move! Haunted houses adore familiar little routines, my Lord, don't they? Cups, footsteps, whispers... doors opening when nobody touches them, all very tasteful! Very homely, if one overlooks the resident corpses, moaning, and cold drafts. Search before accepting refreshments from invisible hosts, Sire! If the teapot floats, excellent service, perhaps reward it. If the teapot screams, skip the tea entirely! Ah, hospitality beyond death. I have attended worse parties, with living hosts.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/tea_with_the_dead · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/haunted_house` (in-game name "Invitation to the Tea Party") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_D4_Abyss 300.40


:: Blind, Still Deadly [rambling] {"position":"1150,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Hail, Sightless Smiter of Sepulchral Scum! Eyes were apparently optional.
LOG: Hail, Sightless Smiter of Sepulchral Scum! Darkness fell. The victim still fell harder! No sight. No lantern. No polite warning. The Master struck anyway. Splendid! I would trip over the first gravestone. He simply made another occupant for the yard. Greetings, Blindfold Bane of Buried Brutes! Perhaps keep that one. It has bounce. The dead may hide in gloom, but gloom clearly offers no protection. Tread carefully... I mean me, not him. A minstrel values both eyes, even when his Lord proves neither is required. Eyes open... mine, at least.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/blind_still_deadly · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/kill_while_blinded` (in-game name "Peekaboo, I (still) see you!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 500.10


:: Iron With Taste [rambling] {"position":"1300,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Dark iron, Masta! Giblet hears good ring!
LOG: Giblet smells dark iron! Cold smell. Grave smell. Still iron. Better colour too! Black suits Master. Bright iron shows scratches. Dark iron hides shame. Good metal should not shame. Giblet taps bar. Ting! Dense. Taps again. Ting! Good song. Not Quaver song. Forge song! Giblet knows forge song. Heat it slow. Hit it hard. Quench fast. Maybe smoke comes. Fine. Smoke means work. Mortis may stare. Let Mortis stare. Giblet not stealing bones. Only iron! Master gets dark blade. Dark plate. Dark spikes. Much better. Giblet wants whole pile.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/iron_with_taste · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/dark_iron` (in-game name "Iron, but dark") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 106.10


:: The Tree Remembers [rambling] {"position":"1450,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Dead wood remembers. So does soil.
LOG: Dead wood remembers life! This tree remembers death. Both cling tightly. Its roots sit among graves. Its branches hold old silence. Do not mistake stillness for emptiness, Sire. Places absorb endings. The soil keeps names beneath it. Old bark keeps every scar and weight. The tree has seen enough. It remains. That is a kind of service. No leaves. No fruit. No complaint. I respect that. A living orchard demands seasons. A dead tree only asks that nobody lean too hard. Leave one branch untouched. Old dead things deserve one privilege. Even trees earn retirement.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_tree_remembers · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/dead_tree` (in-game name "Hanging Tree") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.25


:: Coffins to Carry [rambling] {"position":"1600,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Carry the coffin carefully. It has expectations.
LOG: A coffin should carry the dead. This one carries duty too. Sensible design. You bear it, Sire. Something within may answer. Keep the lid secure. The dead dislike being dropped. So do gravekeepers. Wood and iron surround bone. Each has purpose. A coffin is not merely furniture. It is a promise. One journey ends inside. Another may begin outside. Life for death. Death for life. The price remains, even when handles make it portable. Lift with your knees. Eternity is heavy. Do not swing it. The passenger has endured enough movement for one lifetime already.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/coffins_to_carry · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/equip_ghouling_coffin` (in-game name "The dead shall serve") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.10


:: Their Own Dagger [rambling] {"position":"1750,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: His dagger returned to him. Point first.
LOG: The acolyte knew that dagger. Now it knows him. Appropriate. Bone makes honest weapons. It remembers what flesh forgets. You turned his own tool back, Sire. No grand rite followed. No sermon helped. Steel would have worked. Bone made the lesson neater. The dead appreciate symmetry. The living rarely do. He carried death. He received death. Balanced enough. Keep the dagger if useful. Return it to the grave otherwise. I dislike clutter around tombs. Corpses already own too much. Clean the blade afterward. Old blood rusts poorly. New blood rarely improves the smell. Store the blade cleanly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/their_own_dagger · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/kill_acolyte_bone_dagger` (in-game name "Turning the tables") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B TOUR.60


:: A Horde, Unmade [rambling] {"position":"1900,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The walking dead are still now. Better.
LOG: Many dead rose. Many dead fell. Order restored. A horde is only numbers. Death counts well. You reduced the sum, Sire. Bones broke until the graveyard quieted. That is acceptable work. Undead armies often forget limits. They confuse persistence with entitlement. The distinction matters. One may return. One may serve. One may even fight. But the dead should know who commands. These did not. Now they know nothing. That is simpler. Silence scales remarkably well. Burn nothing unless needed. Bones tell stories. Ash has very limited conversation. Numbers end eventually.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_horde_unmade · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/kill_horde` (in-game name "Walking Dead") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.50


:: Wraiths Hate Grave Robbers [rambling] {"position":"2050,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: The grave objected. The wraith spoke for it.
LOG: A wraith came for thieves. You ended it instead. Graves inspire loyalty. Sometimes violently. The dead own little, Sire. They become possessive. Rings, bones, names, old dust. Take care what you disturb. A tomb is a contract. Breaking it has witnesses. This wraith objected. Its complaint is concluded. Keep what you claimed. Accept what follows. Death is your friend. Friends may still resent burglary. I recommend knocking next time. The dead will ignore you, but courtesy costs nothing. Mark the tomb afterward. Otherwise you may rob it twice. That becomes administrative waste. Close the tomb after.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/wraiths_hate_grave_robbers · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/kill_wraith` (in-game name "Taking from the Dead") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.QUIT4


:: Voluntary Donations [rambling] {"position":"2200,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: How generous. Someone bottled the invitation.
LOG: How civic of them. Bottles of blood, neatly offered. Were the donors smiling? I hope not, because gratitude ruins the flavour. Still, a voluntary gift has its pleasures. No chase, no struggle, just that small private surrender. You can almost hear the pulse regretting generosity. Do you taste fear afterward? Sometimes it arrives late, and sometimes pride does. I prefer the second. Pride makes surrender feel scandalous. Drink slowly, dark one, and let the gift become insulting by degrees. I would thank the donor myself. Then I would ask whether another bottle waits somewhere warmer.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/voluntary_donations · fires on advancement `graveyard:graveyard/vial_of_blood` (in-game name "Blood "Donation"") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S01E03 41


:: Best Friends With a Bee [rambling] {"position":"2350,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: A giant bee likes you, Master. I blame the flowers.
LOG: You befriended a giant bee... oh dear! I blame the flowers entirely, Master, every revolting last one. Still, the creature is enormous, loyal, and heavily armed! That combination has undeniable value beneath your command, my Lord! Keep the useful end pointed toward somebody else, Sire. Do not ask me to pet it... absolutely not. If it brings honey, send the sticky mess straight to Gristle. If it brings flowers, burn those quietly and quickly! A Dark Lord needs standards, even around affectionate insects.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/best_friends_with_a_bee · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:beehemoth/queen_beehemoth` (in-game name "Regal Friends Till The Very End!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 203.10


:: A Bee You Can Ride [rambling] {"position":"2500,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: You can ride it, Sire! Oh, dignity has left the hive.
LOG: You can ride the bee, Sire... of course you can! Nature has abandoned dignity completely now, Master, and apparently gravity too! Still, flight is flight, and the beast carries impressive weight! It also brings its own stinger to negotiations, my Lord. That makes the creature useful enough for your darker purposes. Try not to wave cheerfully from above the peasants! We have a reputation... a dark, imposing, thoroughly humourless one. If Quaver sees this, look magnificently grim and threatening! Perhaps nobody will notice the buzzing beneath your armour, perhaps.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_bee_you_can_ride · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:beehemoth/tamed_beehemoth` (in-game name "Bee Movie But It's 300% Larger") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 100.20


:: NOT THE BEES, Sire! [rambling] {"position":"2650,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: NOT THE BEES, Sire! Kill faster!
LOG: NOT THE BEES, Sire... you have angered absolutely all of them! Run, Master, or kill the little devils considerably faster! One sting becomes a thousand furious little opinions, my Lord! Hives take offence with frightening speed and remarkably good organization. I almost admire that discipline... almost, from very far away! Sweet little workers, were they, with harmless fuzzy bodies? Fluffy little pollinators, ha, now look at the knives! Survive this first, then we may discuss your botanical diplomacy afterward. Next time, offend something with fewer relatives, much fewer!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/not_the_bees_sire · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:effects/bee_hit_wrath_of_the_hive` (in-game name "NOT THE BEEEEEES!!!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 200.10


:: You Drank It? Sweet Gods. [rambling] {"position":"2800,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: You drank it, Master?! By Evil... all of it?
LOG: You drank it, Sire... you actually swallowed the whole essence! By Evil, Master, that was concentrated bee magic in a bottle! I had rather hoped we would feed it to somebody else! Perhaps throw it at an enemy from a reassuring distance. But swallow it yourself, my Lord... bold, very bold indeed! Feel what it does before celebrating your magnificent constitution. If you start buzzing, tell me immediately and calmly! If you sprout wings. Grubbison may become terribly jealous, unfortunately. If you praise flowers, we deny everything, everything!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/you_drank_it_sweet_gods · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:essence/bee_essence_infusion` (in-game name "Hope, Love, Dreams, and BEES!!!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 501.10


:: A Sanctum. Of Bees. [rambling] {"position":"2950,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: A sacred bee hall, Sire... my teeth ache already.
LOG: They built a sanctum for bees... ancient, sacred, horribly sticky! My teeth ache merely looking at the golden walls, Master! Someone built all this grandeur for insects, my Lord, deliberately! Still, old sanctums often keep older and much nastier secrets! Search carefully and take anything valuable before admiring details, Sire! Age does not make sweetness respectable... merely expensive and archaeological. It does, however, make the architecture worth robbing thoroughly. If the walls start singing about pollen, leave quickly! Take the treasure first, naturally, we endured all those flowers.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_sanctum_of_bees · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:structures/enter_sempiternal_sanctum` (in-game name "Ancient Origins") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 100.20


:: The Bee Queen's Errands [rambling] {"position":"3100,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: The Queen has errands for you, Master! Try not to look offended.
LOG: The Bee Queen has started giving you errands... yes, you! Do not glare yet, Master, however deeply tempting it feels. Queens hide good rewards behind silly requests, my Lord! Complete whatever seems profitable and ignore the sentimental bits entirely! Refuse flower crowns whenever your dignity still permits it, Sire! Accept treasure without hesitation... that part counts as diplomacy. Think of this as buzzing statecraft beneath your dark magnificence. A Dark Lord may run one errand, occasionally! He simply charges far more afterward, preferably in gold and obedience.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_bee_queens_errands · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/the_beginning` (in-game name "The Queen's Desire") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 803.30


:: The Blue Sanctum Falls [rambling] {"position":"3250,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The blue hall hummed of peace and honeyed rest / He broke the calm and passed its gentle test!
LOG: The blue sanctum whispered of quiet, soft humming, and rest / His darker tread entered and spoiled every peaceful little test! / And its honeyed light softened the buzzing that drifted around / His darker will answered without making much of a sound! / And the gentle halls shimmered with magical patience and peace / He crossed them and showed that their calm had to cease! / I like a soft ballad when every last danger is done / But not when armed bees start to hum every one. / The bees may prefer all that quiet high above / He proved darker hearts have no need for their love!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_blue_sanctum_falls · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:essence/essence_calming` (in-game name "Peace and Love") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.43


:: The White Sanctum Falls [rambling] {"position":"3400,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Welcome, Bender of Bending Corridors! The hall tried cheating first.
LOG: Welcome, Bender of Bending Corridors! Walls slipped. Paths folded. Floors forgot themselves. Very rude architecture! The white sanctum tried to lose the Master inside itself. It failed. Naturally. Salutations, Straight-Walker Through Crooked Space! Too long. I can trim it later. The halls bent, the Lord did not. That is the important part. I would have taken one wrong corner and sung there forever. Quietly. Eventually to myself. Tread carefully! Strange halls reward confidence with missing exits, and minstrels are much easier to misplace than Overlords. Straight halls suit me better.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_white_sanctum_falls · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:essence/essence_continuity` (in-game name "Reality Glitch") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 600.30


:: The Purple Sanctum Falls [rambling] {"position":"3550,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The purple hall watched every passage, wall, and door / It watched him win, then watched the world no more!
LOG: The purple hall watched every worker, each doorway, each hive / It noticed what moved and what somehow remained still alive! / Its knowing light shimmered through ceiling, floor, chamber, and room / Then Master walked in and gave all that knowledge its doom. / I hate any chamber that studies me closely while I flee / So curtains and corners always seem much wiser to me! / Let watchful old magic keep staring through every long night / Our Lord makes the all-seeing wish for considerably less sight. / A room that knows everything should know when to hide / And it learned that small lesson when darkness stepped inside.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_purple_sanctum_falls · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:essence/essence_knowing` (in-game name "The All-Seeing") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.40


:: The Green Sanctum Falls [rambling] {"position":"3700,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The living hall grew leaf and flowered vine / He made its blooming power bow and decline!
LOG: The green sanctum breathed with new blossom, green root, and vine / His shadow strode through and made darkness the stronger sign! / And its blessing stirred roots through the wax-covered flowering hall / And his shadow reminded the living that living things fall! / I like all my flowers much smaller, quieter, and still / And not climbing from floorboards toward ceiling, window, and hill! / Let gardens grow proudly wherever their bright roots may please / Our Lord makes them bow with the flowers and trees. / The flowers may scatter their bright perfume and seed / He makes even bright springtime look properly dark indeed!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_green_sanctum_falls · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:essence/essence_life` (in-game name "Blessings of Life") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.45


:: The Yellow Sanctum Falls [rambling] {"position":"3850,5000","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Salutations, Dimmer of Dazzling Domains! The sunshine has been disciplined.
LOG: Salutations, Dimmer of Dazzling Domains! Very bright place. Very dark visitor. Excellent contrast! The yellow sanctum blazed like noon trapped indoors. The Master walked through without squinting. I would have demanded curtains. Thick ones. Preferably stone. Welcome, Shade-Bringer to Shining Shrines! The glow has learned humility. Radiance can fill a chamber, but it cannot outshine a proper entrance. I shall applaud from the dim side. Minstrels look better in forgiving light. Also, fewer bees notice us there. That is artistic judgment, not fear. Dim corners flatter a minstrel.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_yellow_sanctum_falls · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:essence/essence_radiance` (in-game name "Solar Powered") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles CORRUPTED_LVL_4.JES


:: The Red Sanctum Falls [rambling] {"position":"1000,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The raging hall roared hotter, furious, and red / He matched its anger till the fury bled!
LOG: The red sanctum thundered with anger, hot wax, and heat / His black boots strode forward and challenged its furious beat! / Its fury rolled outward through wall, floor, chamber, and hive / And his darker wrath answered and somehow stayed more alive! / And I sang from a doorway where flames stayed afar / For songs sound much better when singers do not char! / Now let raging halls roar till their hottest echoes swell / And our Lord brings a temper that frightens even hell! / And the hive may call anger a glorious red art / Then he showed it a temper with considerably more heart!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_red_sanctum_falls · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:essence/essence_raging` (in-game name "Unstoppable Anger") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.13


:: Buzzing Ballads, All of Them [rambling] {"position":"1150,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The hive has yielded every buzzing tune today / Now all its strangest ballads join the play!
LOG: Come raise every cup while the buzzing hive ballads now play / And the Master has gathered their whole strange musical array! / One tune hums softly, another keeps dancers moving at night / A third makes the honeyed halls shiver with bright delight. / I know proper music, and bees mostly know their own wings / So nobody claim they are better at songs or at sings! / Let honey halls dance to each buzzy and wobbling new sound / But Quaver still owns every proper dark stage above ground. / I grant them one chorus, perhaps even two / Every good audience eventually comes back to Quaver anew!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/buzzing_ballads_all_of_them · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:music_discs/obtain_all_music_discs` (in-game name "Gotta Hive a Dance!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.47


:: Stung Stiff [rambling] {"position":"1300,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Paralyzer of Ponderous Prey! One sting made the giant behave.
LOG: Hail, Paralyzer of Ponderous Prey! One sharp sting. One very still foe. Beautiful economy! The target froze where it stood. The Master did not. I approve of enemies becoming statues before the dangerous part begins. It gives a singer time to choose the rhyme. / The stinger struck, the monster stayed, and then his darker blow was paid! / It froze in place from crown to toe, a kinder target for the blow! Greetings, Lord of Loaded Odds! I like fights best when only one side moves.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stung_stiff · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:stinger_spear/stinger_spear_paralyze_boss` (in-game name "Getting Favorable Odds") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles ULTIMATE_STEEL.JES


:: Stingers, Reattached [rambling] {"position":"1450,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Welcome, Restorer of Royal Rearmament! The bees have their points back.
LOG: Welcome, Restorer of Royal Rearmament! Broken stingers mended. Buzzing weapons restored. How generous! The Queen should be delighted. I am less certain about everyone standing nearby. A bee without a stinger is a fuzzy worry. A bee with one is a flying argument. The Master has chosen arguments. Naturally. Salutations, Surgeon of Stinging Subjects! Keep that title. It sounds dangerous. I shall clap carefully, with both hands far from the hive. Helping armed insects feels noble from across the room. Up close, it feels remarkably pointy. No touching... not by me.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stingers_reattached · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/back_in_action` (in-game name "Back in Action") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles UNCORRUPTED_LVL_1.JES


:: 128 Trades With a Bug [rambling] {"position":"1600,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Greetings, Bargainer Beyond Bee Belief! One hundred twenty-eight trades, and still counting.
LOG: Greetings, Bargainer Beyond Bee Belief! One hundred twenty-eight exchanges. I lost count at nineteen. Then I lied! The bug kept offering. The Master kept dealing. Neither side collapsed from boredom. Remarkable endurance. Coins changed hands. Goods changed hands. My attention wandered completely. Welcome, Merchant-Master of the Many-Legged Market! I may need a shorter title before trade two hundred. Still, the purse survived, the bargain pile grew, and the bee remained cooperative. That counts as diplomacy. Quaver counts it as a very long afternoon. Counting is a cruel profession.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/128_trades_with_a_bug · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/crazy_trader` (in-game name "Crazy Trader") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D5_CAPTUREJEWEL.JES


:: Silverfish, Squished [rambling] {"position":"1750,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The silver swarm came crawling through the ancient stone / He ground the biting little horde to bone!
LOG: The silverfish poured from the cracks in a glittering wave / His armoured stride met them, magnificently bold and brave! / They skittered through stone in a bright, biting silver row / And his boots made their glitter considerably flatter and low! / I climbed on a chair where my ankles remained safely high / And sang once the last little nuisance was ready to die! / Let silver pests swarm from each crack they can fit / Our Lord turns the swarm to one glittering flattened bit. / The cracks may grow quiet, the stones may all gleam / I still keep my stool well away from the seam!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/silverfish_squished · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/fighting_the_swarm` (in-game name "Fighting the Swarm") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.17


:: Landlord to Bees [rambling] {"position":"1900,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Hail, Proprietor of Pollen Properties! The tenants are armed.
LOG: Hail, Proprietor of Pollen Properties! New homes built. New tenants buzzing. The housing market has wings! Rent collection may prove lively. Bees dislike eviction notices, I imagine. I shall not test the theory. / He raised them homes of wax and comb, and every buzzing tenant found a home! / The landlord wears an iron crown, so late rent seldom lingers round! Greetings, Keeper of the Honeyed Holdings! I prefer a room with fewer wings. Still, the property looks occupied, and nobody has eaten the landlord yet.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/landlord_to_bees · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/flooding_the_housing_market` (in-game name "Flooding the Housing Market") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles TOWER_UPGRADE_2.JES


:: Bee Matchmaker [rambling] {"position":"2050,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Two lonely bees met happily wing to wing / His darker reign has somehow sponsored spring!
LOG: Two lonely bees circled through flower, warm honey, and air / Then a dark-gloved matchmaker finally made them one happy pair! / They buzzed close together and danced happily wing to wing / And romance under darkness became quite an alarming little thing. / I watched from a distance and called the whole courtship all right / Because stingers in love still remain very sharp in a fight! / Now let poets praise honey and hearts fluttering softly above / Our Lord has become quite the broker of bee love. / And the happy new pair may make honey all day / I merely request that they keep sharp stingers away.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/bee_matchmaker · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/love_bees` (in-game name "Love bees") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.22


:: Mites Begone [rambling] {"position":"2200,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Salutations, Purger of Pernicious Parasites! Tiny pests, enormous satisfaction.
LOG: Salutations, Purger of Pernicious Parasites! Mites arrived. Mites crawled. Mites regretted everything. The hive looks cleaner already! I dislike pests that can hide in fur, boots, bedding, bells, or anywhere else small and personal. The Master removed them. Good. Welcome, Eradicator of Uninvited Itch-Makers! Perhaps too specific. Still accurate. I shall inspect my sleeves later. Twice. Then the socks. Tread carefully! Little horrors rarely respect rank, music, or personal space. The Queen may call this service. I call it relief with applause. Itches ruin every grand fanfare.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/mites_begone · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/otherworldly_mites` (in-game name "Otherworldly Mites") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles ZOMBIE_KILLS_100.JES


:: The Wither, by Bee [rambling] {"position":"2350,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A tiny bee flew boldly out to face the blight / The Master staged a mad and glorious fight!
LOG: There once was a bee with astonishing courage and nerve / It flew where much wiser small wings would immediately swerve! / The Wither spat darkness and rattled with hunger and death / The bee flew straight onward through blackened and poisonous breath! / And behind them the Master arranged that ridiculous wild bout / While I found thick stone and refused to come out! / Then a bee against horror makes nonsense look gloriously right / When darker hands choose such a mad and magnificent fight. / And the tale sounds ridiculous, yet every word remains true / When Master wants spectacle, the strangest things will do!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_wither_by_bee · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/peak_inefficiency` (in-game name "Peak Inefficiency") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.27


:: Stinger Volleys [rambling] {"position":"2500,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The poisoned stingers crossed the buzzing battle sky / His enemies discovered nowhere safe or dry!
LOG: The poisoned stingers went cutting in volleys through open air / And his gauntlet sent sharpened and buzzing destruction everywhere there! / Each dart flew like lightning through smoke, noise, and light / The enemy scattered beneath that ridiculous poisonous fight. / I found a good roof and applauded each distant scream / I thanked every stone and each very strong beam! / Now let archers boast loudly of feathers and elegant flight / And his stingers make poison look properly wicked and right. / A roof is a fine place for minstrels to hide / Especially when poisoned sharp stingers are flying wide!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stinger_volleys · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/poison_warfare` (in-game name "Poison Warfare") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.19


:: Pollen to the Face [rambling] {"position":"2650,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Welcome, Powderer of Proud Proboscises! The flowers have joined the war.
LOG: Welcome, Powderer of Proud Proboscises! Pollen everywhere. Faces included. Very yellow victory! The Master has turned flowers into ammunition, which feels wrong and therefore excellent. Enemies coughed. Eyes watered. Dignity disappeared beneath golden dust. I sneezed once. Then twice. Then heroically withdrew. Greetings, General of the Golden Sneeze! That one has promise. The battlefield smelled suspiciously pleasant afterward, which I dislike on principle. Still, victory is victory. I shall compose the next fanfare after my nose stops attempting to escape my face. Pollen and dignity never mix.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/pollen_to_the_face · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/pollen_fight` (in-game name "Pollen Fight") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 200.30


:: Cave Spiders, Culled [rambling] {"position":"2800,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The cave grew legs across the ceiling, floor, and stone / He left the crawling nest crushed and alone!
LOG: The cave grew eight-legged from ceiling, wall, floor, and stone / His dark shape went hunting through all that gloom alone! / The spiders dropped downward in hairy and venomous black rain / His blade sent the brood to a much flatter plane! / And I counted the legs, then abandoned the terrible sum / And fled to a chamber where spiders could never come! / Now let cave spiders dangle and bare every poisonous fang / Our Lord turns their webs into gallows where spiders hang. / And the cave may be cleaner, the webbing cut thin / I still check every ceiling before calmly walking in!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/cave_spiders_culled · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/terror_fangs` (in-game name "Terror Fangs") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.26


:: Flower Fiend [rambling] {"position":"2950,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Hail, Hoarder of Horrifying Horticulture! The bouquet has become excessive.
LOG: Hail, Hoarder of Horrifying Horticulture! Flowers piled high. Petals everywhere. A deeply suspicious amount of colour! The Master has gathered enough blooms to alarm every gardener in creation. I prefer skulls. Easier rhymes. Fewer bees. Still, such excess deserves music. / He gathered bloom from field and bower, then built himself a darker flower tower! / The petals bowed beneath his tread, bright trophies for a Lord of dread! Salutations, Monarch of the Murderous Bouquet! I shall admire it from the pollen-free side.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/flower_fiend · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/the_crazy_florist` (in-game name "The Crazy Florist") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D2_GROVE.ALT


:: Dragon Slain in Bee Armour [rambling] {"position":"3100,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Bee armour shone against the dragon's furnace flame / He slew the beast and dressed the deed in fame!
LOG: The dragon came roaring through smoke, burning flame, and gold / His black armour shone there, fearless, gleaming, and bold! / The honeyed plates glittered beneath every burst of burning light / He carried that buzzing bright shell through the whole fight! / I watched from outside where my fur remained safely unburned / And sang when the dragon to supper was finally turned! / Let dragons mock honey and buzzing bright armour if they dare / And our Lord makes bee armour the fiercest thing there! / The honeyed bright armour may sound deceptively sweet / It looks considerably less silly beside fresh dragon meat!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dragon_slain_in_bee_armour · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/the_great_dragon_slayer` (in-game name "The Great Dragon Slayer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.28


:: Spiders by the Dozen [rambling] {"position":"3250,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Counter of Crawling Catastrophes! Twelve legs would have been enough.
LOG: Greetings, Counter of Crawling Catastrophes! One spider. Two spiders. Too many spiders! The dozen became corpses before my counting improved. Excellent. The Master does arithmetic with a weapon. Very educational! Legs everywhere. Web everywhere. Quaver nowhere nearby. That is the correct arrangement. Welcome, Multiplier of Murdered Many-Legged Monsters! The title grew more legs than the victims. I dislike it already. Still, twelve spiders are twelve fewer reasons to inspect ceilings. Tread carefully! Eight legs may be dead, but webbing has dreadful staying power. Ceilings remain under suspicion.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/spiders_by_the_dozen · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/too_many_legs` (in-game name "Too Many Legs") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles BEAT_JESTER2.JES


:: Dressed as a Bee. Proudly. [rambling] {"position":"3400,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Bee armour. Hmph. Giblet admits strong!
LOG: Bee armour. Yellow. Hmph! Yellow. Fuzzy-looking. Giblet hates fuzzy metal. But plate strong! Strange. Giblet knocks chest. Tok tok. Good. Stinger bits pointy. Better! Master wears bug suit. Looks proud. Should look mean. Maybe paint darker? No. Leave yellow. Enemy laughs first. Then sting! Good joke. Giblet likes joke with blood. Honey smell bad. Sticky straps worse. Still, armour holds. That matters. Giblet judges hit. Not colour. Not buzz. Hit! Armour says no. Good armour. Giblet approves bug work. Grudging. Very grudging. No flowers near forge! Giblet the Sixth has limits.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dressed_as_a_bee_proudly · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:armor/warrior_bee` (in-game name "The Bee Warrior Rises!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 103.20


:: The Sweetest Shield [rambling] {"position":"3550,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Sweet shield? Ugh. Giblet likes hard part!
LOG: Sweet shield? Ugh. Giblet sniffs. Honey smell. Too sweet! Crystal good though. Very good. Hard face. Clean edge. Takes hit well. Master holds it. Giblet thumps front. THUNK! Good answer. Hits again. THUNK! Better answer. Sweet no matter. Shield works. Work beats smell. Giblet can respect that. Maybe wash honey off. No? Fine. Let enemy stick to it! Hah! Then smash enemy. Better use. Shield should stop hurt. Shield should hurt back. This one can. Giblet likes mean shield. Not pretty shield. Sweet outside. Nasty inside. Good enough!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_sweetest_shield · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:honey_crystal_shield/obtain_maxed_honey_crystal_shield` (in-game name "Grand Hive Defender") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.GuardHere01


:: Royal Jelly, Gulped [rambling] {"position":"3700,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Royal jelly sticks! Ugh!
LOG: I taste royal jelly. Too sweet already! My teeth angry. Masta gulps whole thing. Brave stomach there. Jelly thick, sauce gone wrong. Maybe power inside. Maybe fancy bee spit. I taste one drop. Sticky! Tongue sticks roof. HATE THAT! Need hot broth. Better idea. Royal power stays bottled. I cook fat, salt, fire! Bees cook flowers, buzzing. Wrong way entirely. Still, jelly got strength. Could glaze roast? Hm, tiny glaze maybe. Burn sugar dark. Then maybe good. Gnarl hears nothing. Honey idea stays secret! Not one word.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/royal_jelly_gulped · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:honey_bucket/drink_royal_jelly_bottle` (in-game name "Gaining Royal Powers") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ForYou01


:: A Bucket of Jelly [rambling] {"position":"3850,5150","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Whole bucket? WHY!
LOG: Bucket full jelly! Why whole bucket? Sugar everywhere. Whole thing wobbles. I poke surface. Wobble comes back. Disrespectful food! Masta collected all. Kitchen uses some, maybe. Maybe sauce. Maybe glaze. Maybe rat trap. Sticky works good! I pour spoonful near heat. Bubbles fast there. Smells like flower. Ugh. Cooks darker though. Better now. Add salt, better again. Add chili, MUCH better. Bees should learn. Sweet needs pain. I can teach that. Bucket stays covered. Quaver stays far away. He rhymes honey, money. Ugh. I hate that already.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_bucket_of_jelly · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:honey_bucket/obtain_royal_jelly_bucket` (in-game name "Masterful Collector") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Treasure02


:: Drunk on Honey [rambling] {"position":"1000,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Honey drunk! Sit down!
LOG: Masta drank honey hard! Ha, maybe floor wobbling. Sweet drink sneaky. No good heat, still head-hit. I sniff cup. Flowers punch nose. Tiny sip first. Too sweet! Second sip checks. Still too sweet. Third checks danger. Dangerous, knew it. Chair here! I sit before kitchen spins. Pot cannot spin. Pot spins? Big problem. Masta handles honey better. Of course he does. Me cook, not bee. Give fire drink. Give pepper broth. Honey makes legs soft. I hate soft legs. No laughing now! I still got ladle.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/drunk_on_honey · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/honey_drunk` (in-game name "Honey Drunk") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.HelpMe01


:: Feeding Bees. Ugh. [rambling] {"position":"1150,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Feed bees? With MY food?!
LOG: Feed bees? MY FOOD? No! Masta says feed, hmph. I feed scraps anyway. Good scraps maybe. Not best scraps. Best stays kitchen. Bee takes food, buzzes thanks. I distrust that. Tiny thief returns. Another comes too! Hungry swarm, greedy fuzz. I toss more. Fingers back! They got stingers. My spoon bigger still. Still not fighting. Feeding bees feels wrong. Food should feed Masta. Or me first. Or pot maybe. Bees come last. Maybe after Quaver. No, before Quaver. He sings instead eating. Fine.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/feeding_bees_ugh · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/hungry_hungry_bees` (in-game name "Hungry Hungry Bees") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ForTheMaster01


:: Honey Slimes, Breeding [rambling] {"position":"1300,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Sticky babies multiplying! Keep away stove!
LOG: More honey slimes now! Ugh, sticky babies everywhere. One blob, two blobs, more appear! They split, squish, wobble. Kitchen floor hates this. I hate it too. Still, jelly creature food? No, probably friend. Masta looks pleased, hmph then. I do not cook pets. Usually. Slimes smell sweet. Smell cloys hard. Sticky tracks follow everywhere. Throw sand? Bad idea. Flour? Worse idea. Sawdust maybe. Grubbison knows dirt. Not kitchen dirt. Blobs stay from stove! Heat may melt them. Or caramelize them. Hm. No. Bad thought. Kitchen brain does this. Thoughts happen. Slimes hear nothing.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/honey_slimes_breeding · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:the_queens_desire/slimy_mitosis` (in-game name "Slimy Mitosis") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WhatAMess02


:: Fishing in Honey [rambling] {"position":"1450,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Honey fishing? Wash that catch!
LOG: Fishing in honey? WRONG! Fish belongs water. Honey belongs nowhere near fish. Yet line goes in. Something bites hard. Sticky splash everywhere! Masta pulls treasure up. Not fish maybe. Good. Fish comes? Wash ten times! Salt it hard. Fry it hotter. Sweet fish insults pan. I refuse that. Honey drips everywhere. Floor sticks now. Boots stick too. Ladle sticks worst. I get angry. VERY angry! Still, rare loot comes out. Fish more then. I stand far away. Somebody else cleans. Not me. I already cook enough. Enough jobs!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/fishing_in_honey · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:tools/fish_rare_loot` (in-game name "Beesistent Fishing") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.OnIt01


:: Every Sticky Corner [rambling] {"position":"1600,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Master! Sticky place found, and another one!
LOG: Buzz everywhere! I run sticky woods and honey caves, and every turn got more yellow ground! I find deep place, high place, wet place, sweet place, all of it! Good exploring, Master? Good enough? Grubby made new Gates where roads stopped, and I can find roads before digging them! Maybe good enough for old name? Maybe. Mark turn, lose mark, find better turn anyway! Feet sticky, ears buzzing, map in head growing fast. I go farther! Farther! One place left? I find it. Two places? I find both!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_sticky_corner · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:biomes/discover_all_biomes` (in-game name "Beeography") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_TR START.75


:: Every Hive Explored [rambling] {"position":"1750,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Every hive hall! I found all!
LOG: Another hive hall! And another, and another, and I keep going before bees notice! Big chambers, little chambers, old wax rooms, shiny rooms, all found! Grubby dug toward places Master needed, yes? I scout them first! Good plan? I think good plan! Doors hide behind comb, stairs hide under honey, tunnels twist back wrong way. I still get through! Remember smell, slope, turns, sticky floor spots. Then I run next one! Every hive explored, no corner wins! Grubby had Gates. I got paths. Paths first, holes later!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_hive_explored · fires on advancement `the_bumblezone:structures/enter_all_structures` (in-game name "Sightbee-er") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Everlight_Jungle 110.40


:: Filth, Refined [rambling] {"position":"1900,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Filth, refined, Sire! The rats understand industry.
LOG: Someone refined the filth... civilization advances! The rats waste absolutely nothing, Master, admirable little vermin indeed! Dirt becomes something useful between those grubby clever paws with enough patience! Dwarves do much the same with ore, my Lord, more loudly. Scholars manage it with stale opinions and much longer words, usually in robes. Rats merely smell worse... refreshingly honest little creatures, Sire! Keep the finished lump if it proves useful to your reign. Rubbish belongs to whoever sees its value first! If somebody complains, give them the raw ingredients back personally, perhaps by throwing.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/filth_refined · fires on advancement `rats:ball_of_filth` (in-game name "Cleanliness is Close to Godliness!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 901.60


:: Rats at the Bench [rambling] {"position":"2050,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Rats at the bench, Master! Tiny hands, dangerous ideas.
LOG: The rats have discovered a workbench... just look at them go! Tiny paws, serious faces, dreadful concentration everywhere, Master! I admit the sight is almost charming, my Lord... almost! Let us not become sentimental about industrious rodents just yet! Let them build while every little contraption remains useful, Sire. Watch for pride afterward, because pride grows very quickly indeed. First comes a maker's mark, then comes an invoice! If they demand holidays, confiscate the cheese at once! Industry needs discipline, especially when industry has whiskers and teeth.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rats_at_the_bench · fires on advancement `rats:rat_crafting_table` (in-game name "Rat Auto-Crafting") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 417.30


:: Rats From the Netherworld [rambling] {"position":"2200,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: A demon-rat, Sire! Well... at least it looks familiar.
LOG: That rat smells faintly of the Netherworld... pleasantly familiar! The little beast kept its appetite, naturally enough, Master! Infernal power has not improved its manners, my Lord, thankfully! Keep it obedient before confidence becomes theology, property claims, or organized theft, Sire! Rats already steal anything left unattended for three heartbeats, sometimes fewer. Add demonic swagger... and lock the treasury twice, perhaps thrice! Still, what a useful little horror you have! Give it work before it invents some dreadful private hobby. A bored demon-rat is trouble underneath furniture, and inside walls, boots, cupboards, everywhere.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rats_from_the_netherworld · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_demon` (in-game name "I Seen This Before...") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Wastelands 130.40


:: Rats With Wings. Why. [rambling] {"position":"2350,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: The rat can fly, Master. Why was the floor not enough?
LOG: The rat can fly, Sire... why exactly, Master, why? Was the floor no longer ambitious enough for it, my Lord? I object professionally, personally, and from every place directly below! A rat under tables is at least a comprehensible nuisance! A rat above your head becomes military strategy, somehow. Still, flight has uses... irritatingly excellent and numerous ones. High shelves, scouting, theft, all become much easier! Keep it away from Quaver's instruments and my quarters! If they nest overhead, we conquer the ceiling, immediately!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rats_with_wings_why · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_flight` (in-game name "Essentially Pigeons") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 400.10


:: A God-Rat, Sire? [rambling] {"position":"2500,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: A god-rat, Sire! We have clearly encouraged them too much.
LOG: The rats have apparently made a god... we encouraged this far too much! Look at those worshipful little faces, Master, dangerous little things! Power has gone straight to its whiskers, my Lord, predictably! Remind it who owns the cheese, altar, and servants, Sire! Gods become troublesome when reverence starts feeling permanent to them. This one is still pocket-sized... keep it exactly that way. If it demands a temple, give it a sturdy box! If it demands sacrifices, offer stale crumbs first! Divinity should learn economy beneath your reign, and proper obedience!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_god_rat_sire · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_god` (in-game name "Whats a Man to a King?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_D5_Abyss 500.30


:: Piglins Worship Rats Now [rambling] {"position":"2650,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Piglins worshipping a rat, Sire! The family shame has acquired theology.
LOG: Ha, Piglins have started worshipping a rat idol now! Splendid judgment from that family branch... truly! Keep watching, Sire, because false prophets make useful levers when pride outruns sense. Piglins love gold, noise, ceremony, and anything shiny enough to look important. Give them a rodent and theology starts doing half the bargaining for us. Do not encourage the rat too much, Master. Tiny gods grow dreadful opinions about tribute, temples, offerings, and who owns the cheese. Let the Piglins kneel if they insist, my Lord! You remain the only authority worth fearing when worship grows noisy.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/piglins_worship_rats_now · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_idol` (in-game name "False Prophet") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D3_MAIN 804.60


:: Pickpocket Rats [rambling] {"position":"2800,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Check your pockets, Sire! The rat has discovered professional theft.
LOG: Check your pockets, Sire! The rat has learned pickpocketing already, rather quickly. Clever little thief, with excellent taste in unattended wealth and loose purses! I almost admire the technique more than whatever vanished from that merchant. Small paws reach places larger servants simply cannot, Master. That makes the creature useful around merchants, guards, nobles, and anyone careless with jewelry. Count your own coins afterward, my Lord, because loyalty and temptation make poor roommates. If it steals from you, steal the cheese back! Discipline should remain simple enough for rats to understand after one sharp lesson.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/pickpocket_rats · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_pickpocket` (in-game name "Talk of the Town") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 204.10


:: Every Hat, Rat-Sized [rambling] {"position":"2950,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Hail, Milliner of Miniature Mischief! Every rat has found a crown.
LOG: Hail, Milliner of Miniature Mischief! Caps, crowns, bonnets, helmets. Every rat dressed! The creatures now strut worse than nobles. I envy the feathered one slightly. Only slightly. / One rat wore velvet, one wore gold, one wore a cap against the cold! / The Master found each tiny crown, until the best-dressed rats in town! Salutations, Tailor to the Tiniest Tyrants! Poor Quaver owns one battered cap, but I shall not compete with creatures who can steal replacements while I sleep.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_hat_rat_sized · fires on advancement `rats:all_hats` (in-game name "Grand Hat Collector") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles TOWER_UPGRADE_1.JES


:: The Plague Doctor Falls [rambling] {"position":"3100,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The beaked old doctor stalked the plague-filled night / He met the Master and prescribed a fight!
LOG: The beaked Plague Doctor came stalking through sickness and gloom / And his black silhouette brought a darker and healthier doom! / Its mask hid the sickness, its black robes hid spite / And his weapon exposed both before the end of night. / I held in my breath till the battle was through / Then checked several times that I still was not blue! / Let plague masks stalk proudly wherever foul sickness may roam / And our Lord sends the doctor quite sickly back home. / The streets may breathe much easier when plague masks disappear / I breathe even easier from several rooms safely clear!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_plague_doctor_falls · fires on advancement `rats:defeat_black_death` (in-game name "Do Not Go Quietly Into the Night") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.52


:: The Rat King Falls [rambling] {"position":"3250,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Rat King raised his tiny golden crown / The greater ruler came and struck him down!
LOG: The Rat King sat proudly on somebody else's old throne / A darker crowned ruler showed whose royal claim was known! / And his whiskered court squeaked and displayed ridiculous royal pride / Then scattered like crumbs when their little king died! / I bowed to one throne and kept cheese near my chest / For rats without kings may still burgle all the rest! / Let rodent kings boast with their sceptre, their crown, and ring / And our Lord wears the crown above every small king. / The little kingdom grew smaller when royalty finally fell / Then a rat without crown is still ratty as hell!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_rat_king_falls · fires on advancement `rats:defeat_rat_king` (in-game name "King of the World!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.33


:: The Piper's Tune [rambling] {"position":"3400,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Welcome, Conductor of the Crawling Choir! The rats know the refrain.
LOG: Welcome, Conductor of the Crawling Choir! Pipe raised. Rats gathered. Music became command! That is a tune I understand. The Master plays, the little paws obey. Admirable rhythm. Slightly worrying audience. / He played one note, the whiskers turned, another note, and order learned! / The rats marched on from beat to beat, a furry army moved its feet! Greetings, Maestro of the Mousing March! If they request an encore, I shall guard my lute. Musicians have standards, even when the audience eats cheese between verses.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_pipers_tune · fires on advancement `rats:piper` (in-game name "Pay the Piper") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 300.10


:: A Tune Worth Stealing [rambling] {"position":"3550,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The rats composed a squeaking, surprisingly tuneful strain / He stole the song and made it play again!
LOG: The rats made a tune with a squeak and steady beat / Then one dark hand took ownership, tidy, quick, and neat! / Their paws found the rhythm, their whiskers kept excellent time / Somehow those rodents produced a surprisingly decent rhyme. / I praise proper music whenever good melodies rise / Though envy may flicker a little in my eyes! / Let rodents have one tiny chorus and one line to shine / The Tower's finest proper ballads are obviously still mine. / If rodents demand royalties, payment, applause, or fame / And I'll hide every cheese wheel and copyright my name.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_tune_worth_stealing · fires on advancement `rats:rat_music_disc` (in-game name "Rat Tunes") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.47


:: Rats in Armour [rambling] {"position":"3700,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: TOK TOK! Tiny armour holds!
LOG: TOK TOK! Tiny armour! Giblet laughs. Then stops. Plate fit good. Rivets tiny. Tiny rivets hard! Rat stands proud. Rat squeaks. Giblet taps helm. Rat bites hammer. Hah! Warrior rat. Good spirit. Armour must move. Not pinch tail. Not block ears. Giblet checks straps. One loose. Bad. Fix strap! Rat runs better. Master has small soldiers now. Very small. Still pointy. Giblet respects fighters in metal. Even rat. Especially rat biting hammer. Give rat little shield. Maybe little spear. No crown. Crown stupid. Helmet better. Giblet says helmet!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rats_in_armour · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_warrior` (in-game name "Rat Warrior Clan") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 203.10


:: Rat-Touched Rations [rambling] {"position":"3850,5300","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: RAT IN PANTRY! OUT!
LOG: GET RAT OUT KITCHEN! WHO touched rations? I smell little paws. See bite marks too. Mine rations! Contaminated now. I throw spoon. Not at Masta. At rat shadow. Food thief deserves heat! I check sacks first. One torn open. Check bread next. One corner nibbled. Cheese? Corner gone. RAGE! Rat can work. Rat can wear hats. Rat can do tricks. Rat does NOT touch pantry! I scrub shelf. Boil cloth hard. Roast crumbs black. Maybe too much. Clean now. Good. On purpose! No smoke complaints. Smoke means clean enough. I guard cupboard tonight.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rat_touched_rations · fires on advancement `rats:contaminated_food` (in-game name "Stop that Health Inspector!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_PoisonNoHurt


:: Cheese From the Netherworld [rambling] {"position":"1000,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hot cheese bites back! YES!
LOG: Hot cheese! YES! Nether cheese bites back. Finally dairy got courage. I cut wedge. Orange veins inside. Spicy smell, good! Bite small first. Tongue burns. Better! Bite bigger. Eyes water. BEST! Cheese belongs near fire. Melt it on meat. Melt it on bread. Melt it on cheese! Masta gets thick slice. Gristle approves this one! Special cheese earns name. Mine mouth still burning. Good burn stays. Food should leave memory. This leaves scar maybe. Even better. Cold water stays away. Water insults flavour. Give roast instead. Spice fights spice. I win!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/cheese_from_the_netherworld · fires on advancement `rats:nether_cheese` (in-game name "Spicy Pepper Jack") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Goblin_Burn_1


:: Rat Cuisine [rambling] {"position":"1150,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Rat cooking now! I watch pot!
LOG: Rat cooking now, rat stirring pot, rat stealing spoon! I watch little paws, knife go fast, onion bits fly. Hmph, not bad, not good, maybe annoying good. Rat flip mushroom, pan spit grease, I smell proper browning! Nobody praise rat yet! I taste sauce, need salt, need heat, need ME. Rat adds spice, wrong amount, somehow still works. I shove coal closer, flame jumps high, rat squeaks loud. Good, kitchen got fight! Masta can eat this. I still cook better, MUCH better, no argument. Rat gets tiny apron. Not my apron!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rat_cuisine · fires on advancement `rats:rat_cooking` (in-game name "Anyone Can Cook") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.GotIt02


:: Rat, Head Chef [rambling] {"position":"1300,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: HEAD CHEF? Mine kitchen!
LOG: Head chef rat? WHAT! Mine kitchen got new boss now? Tiny hat sit crooked, tiny spoon wave, tiny paws point orders. I stare hard, rat stare back, neither move first. Rat chop herbs, toss pan, make smell annoyingly good. I taste one bite, chew slow, refuse smiling. Fine, little cook knows heat. Little cook knows salt too. Nobody tell Quaver! Rat keep corner stove, only corner! Touch mine big pot, WAR. Masta watches, probably amused, I hate that. Rat squeaks. I point spoon. We understand each other.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rat_head_chef · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_chef` (in-game name "The Rat is the Cook!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ForMe02


:: You've Caught Something [rambling] {"position":"1450,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Master... sssick smell. Lovely.
LOG: Master... come closer... no, little farther. You caught something... smells wonderful. Fever scent... sour breath... skin heat wrong. Plague, maybe. Yesss... plague. I sniff sleeve... careful, very careful. Nose burns softly. My tongue tastes copper... without licking anything. Curious. Your pulse sounds loud... or mine does. Hard tell. Do not panic... wastes good symptoms. I want notes... then cure later. Maybe much later. Rot takes time, blooms nicely. Fingers shaking? Mine, not yours, probably mine. I keep vial ready, black one, not green. Green one sleeps too hard. Beautiful sssickness, ugly timing. Still beautiful.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/youve_caught_something · fires on advancement `rats:plague` (in-game name "Down with the Sickness!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_PoisonNoHurt


:: Leeches Were Optional [rambling] {"position":"1600,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Cure ready... sssmooth enough.
LOG: Leeches? ...optional, Master. Very optional. I know cure now... cleaner one, mostly cleaner. Bitter bark first... sour root next... plague hates both. I grind quiet... pestle squeaks. Add blood drop... not much. Mine works. Hand numb already... convenient. Mixture turns grey... then sickly gold. Good. Drink small, wait, breathe. Fever loosens. Skin stops crawling. Mmm, nearly pleasant. Leeches can stay jarred, little greedy worms. Mortis might like them? ,no, maybe not. I cork cure, label three scratches. One means safe-ish. Three means use quickly. Important system, sssimple to me.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/leeches_were_optional · fires on advancement `rats:plague_cure` (in-game name "The Medieval Treatment") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.HelpMe02


:: Beaked Quack [rambling] {"position":"1750,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Beak smells ssstrange... useful.
LOG: Beak mask smells herbs... and old breath. I sniff inside... bad idea. Eye waters... other eye joins late. Plague doctor costume... ssstrange little thing. Master... beak holds powders well. Bitter leaves here... sharp resin there, rot-sweet petals deeper. Clever. Quack maybe, useful quack though. I tap lens, world turns green. World already green enough. I breathe once, tongue goes dry. Protection? ,maybe. Fashion? ,certainly strange. I like pockets most, so many bottles. One leaks! Excellent. I tie mask tighter, whisper through beak. Voice sounds worse. Good. Patients trust scary beak, somehow.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/beaked_quack · fires on advancement `rats:plague_doctor` (in-game name "I AM THE CURE!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Nice02


:: Death Dances In [rambling] {"position":"1900,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Death danced in. The music stopped.
LOG: Death entered dancing! The music was brief. Pestilence wears many faces. This one had rhythm. You met it, Sire. It spread fear. It spread sickness. It did not spread far enough. Good. Plague is wasteful death. Too many bodies. Too little purpose. I prefer cleaner accounts. One soul. One grave. One price. Still, every age invents excess. The dead accept all fashions eventually. The grave has no dress code. It has poor ventilation, however. Burn the cloth afterward. Bury the rest. Plague should not receive an encore. Silence follows eventually.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/death_dances_in · fires on advancement `rats:black_death` (in-game name "Dance Macabre!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.30


:: Rats of the Deep Dark [rambling] {"position":"2050,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Souls cling to these rats. That is unusual.
LOG: These rats carry something old. Souls cling to them. Listen carefully. Not with ears. The dark has its own memory. Small creatures can bear heavy echoes. I do not envy them. A soul should settle. A rat should scurry. Mixing the two causes complications. You have seen the result, Sire. Keep watch. The creatures may seem harmless. So does a grave before opening. If they chatter at empty corners, leave the corners alone. Some company is best unintroduced. Feed them carefully. Soul-touched vermin develop habits. Habits near graves become traditions too quickly. Watch them from distance.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rats_of_the_deep_dark · fires on advancement `rats:rat_upgrade_sculked` (in-game name "One with the Souls") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.40


:: Garlic in a Bottle [rambling] {"position":"2200,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Garlic in glass. Humanity does adore portable courage.
LOG: What an ugly little bottle. And that smell... garlic pretending to be virtue. How exhausting. People adore simple protections, do they not? A bulb, a prayer, a splash, and suddenly terror feels manageable. Très bien! They can believe it. Confidence makes prey careless. Does the brew sting? Naturally, but irritation is not holiness. I have endured sermons with more bite. The bottle may stay if you enjoy the theatre. Throw it at someone else if you enjoy me. Better yet, let a hunter clutch it proudly before discovering that courage still has a throat.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/garlic_in_a_bottle · fires on advancement `nycto:nycto/brew_garlic_brew` (in-game name "Holy Water") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S02E05 257


:: Hunters for Hire [rambling] {"position":"2350,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: You bought hunters? How entrepreneurial.
LOG: You bought hunters? Delicious! Men who sell courage by contract usually charge extra for dying. What did they promise you? Silver, secrecy, perhaps a clean little profession with rules? Hunters adore rules because rules make fear look respectable. The Silent Order knew the trick well. Give terror a uniform and people call it duty. Do these ones know whom they serve now? I hope not, because surprise improves posture. Send them after whatever offends you. Allow the boasting afterward. Notice how quickly principles become wages when the purse grows heavy. Such devotion deserves an invoice.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/hunters_for_hire · fires on advancement `nycto:nycto/buy_hunter_contract` (in-game name "Contract Killer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S02E05 265


:: Fully Undead [rambling] {"position":"2500,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Come closer. The night sits differently on you now.
LOG: Come here and let me look at you. Closer. There. You have gone farther tonight. Can you feel the stillness beneath the skin? The sharper little appetites? Do not mistake completion for a cage. Choice remains choice, and hunger remains hunger. You may cherish this condition, despise it, exploit it, or refuse to let it define you. I am curious about what you choose next. That is all. Well... not all. You wear the night beautifully. I resent that slightly, because vanity is easier without competition.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/fully_undead · fires on advancement `nycto:nycto/complete_vampire` (in-game name "Taste of Eternity") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S03E01 377


:: Not So Eternal [rambling] {"position":"2650,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: So much for eternity. Confidence is a fragile immortal.
LOG: Immortality is such a vulgar boast. Look at him now. Very eternal, is he? The body disagrees, and the floor agrees with me. That is usually how these arguments end. Did he believe age made him untouchable? Poor creature! Time teaches many lessons, but pride skips class. You killed one of the night-born and proved the obvious. We endure, we heal, we terrify, and we also die. The trick is making the interval memorable. I imagine his was, briefly. Do not mourn him. He had centuries to develop better instincts and apparently preferred confidence.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/not_so_eternal · fires on advancement `nycto:nycto/kill_vampire` (in-game name "Not So Immortal") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S03E03 60


:: Stake Through the Heart [rambling] {"position":"2800,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Wood through the heart. Crude, intimate, final.
LOG: Wood. Really? Such a primitive answer. I almost admire the insult. Did the vampire see it coming? Please say no, because surprise belongs in certain endings. A sharpened stick has no elegance, lineage, or poetry. Yet the heart does not care about aesthetics when pierced. Cruel, isn't it? All that night and appetite, undone by carpentry. I would call it humiliating... which is precisely why I understand the appeal. Leave the stake plain. Jewels would spoil it. If one must be barbaric, one should at least be disciplined about it.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stake_through_the_heart · fires on advancement `nycto:nycto/kill_vampire_with_wooden_stake` (in-game name "Shot Through The Heart") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S03E03 169


:: A Garlic Halberd [rambling] {"position":"2950,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Garlic on a halberd. Even murder can be unfashionable.
LOG: That weapon smells like a kitchen quarrel. Garlic on a halberd. Quelle horreur. Who decided warfare needed seasoning? Still, the reach is excellent, and I cannot deny good proportions. Does it make the hunters feel brave? Let them hold it farther forward, then. Fear looks magnificent at the end of a long pole. I would not stand close for the demonstration. Not from fear, darling, but from taste. There are indignities even immortality should refuse. Swing it cleanly. If the blade fails, the smell may finish the conversation. That would be a terribly provincial victory.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_garlic_halberd · fires on advancement `nycto:nycto/obtain_garlic_coated_halberd` (in-game name "Seasoned Warrior") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S01E04 321


:: Garlic Jewellery [rambling] {"position":"3100,5450","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: Garlic jewellery? I am offended on behalf of mirrors.
LOG: You are wearing garlic. I need a moment. Is this protection or punishment? No, do not answer, because the wreath has already confessed. There are ways to frighten creatures of the night without declaring war on beauty. This is not one. Still, you seem pleased, and that almost saves it. Almost. Does it itch? Good. Fashion should demand sacrifice, preferably from someone else. Take the thing off before the smell settles into your hair. I have endured centuries of changing taste. I refuse to accept vegetables as jewellery. Some standards survive every age.
