EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Half horse, half hawk! At least neither half is fluffy.
LOG: Half horse, half hawk, all attitude! Ridiculous creature, Master, which makes it excellent company for a tyrant. The hippogryph has agreed to carry you, Sire, proving more sense than nobles possess! Keep the beast fed and its claws pointed toward other people whenever possible. Flying mounts should inspire awe, not veterinary complaints and awkward landings before peasants. You look appropriately imposing up there, my Lord. Try not to smile while taking off in front of witnesses. Dark magnificence loses something when the mount starts preening beside it. Still, one cannot argue with talons, speed, and altitude!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/half_horse_half_hawk · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/tame_hippogryph` (in-game name "Buck Beak") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 300.10


:: A Head That Petrifies [rambling] {"position":"1000,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Salutations, Bearer of the Gorgon's Grim Glare! Do not point it here.
LOG: Salutations, Bearer of the Gorgon's Grim Glare! A severed head. Still dangerous. Excellent trophy! The stare remains dreadful even without the rest attached. Very efficient. One glance may turn flesh to stone. I am fond of statues when somebody else becomes one. Welcome, Curator of Catastrophic Eye Contact! Please admire that title while facing elsewhere. I enjoy my current texture. Soft enough for music. Hard enough for minor falls. Tread carefully! A minstrel carved in stone would finally hold one pose, but the acoustics would be terrible. Stone is a terrible complexion.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_head_that_petrifies · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/gorgon_head` (in-game name "Clash of the Titans") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles ULTIMATE_ARCANIUM.JES


:: One Eye Fewer [rambling] {"position":"1150,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Cyclops watched him with one enormous eye / It saw the Master coming, then goodbye!
LOG: And the Cyclops watched proudly with one enormous single eye / His black-armoured figure calmly waved the giant goodbye! / That eye caught the armour and saw one final gleam / Then darkness arrived at the ending of its final dream! / I chose a broad boulder with room at the side / I praised every blow from my comfortable little hide! / Let giants boast loudly of height, heavy clubs, and view / One eye was still somehow one eye far too few. / A giant may tower and threaten the open sky / It still cannot rule after losing that enormous eye!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/one_eye_fewer · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_cyclops` (in-game name "My Name is Nobody") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.55


:: Worm Out of the Sand [rambling] {"position":"1300,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The deathworm rose beneath the burning desert sun / He put it down before the feast begun!
LOG: The desert rolled strangely, then sand broke open like sea / A deathworm came rising where nothing that large should be! / Its armoured rings twisted and cut through the burning dune / The Master stepped forward and ended the monster quite soon. / I kept both my boots where the ground made no sound / And hated each dune that looked even slightly too round! / Let worms swim through deserts and leap from the land / Our Lord simply sends them straight back under the sand. / The desert went quiet when those great jaws disappeared / I still trust flat paving, for shifting dunes should be feared!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/worm_out_of_the_sand · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_deathworm` (in-game name "The Desert Swimmers") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.50


:: Ghost Busted [rambling] {"position":"1450,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Evictor of Ethereal Evildoers! The dead tenant has departed.
LOG: Hail, Evictor of Ethereal Evildoers! A ghost appeared. A ghost disappeared. Efficient haunting! Walls did not stop it. Death did not stop it. The Master did. Much better. Greetings, Breaker of Bodiless Boasters! I prefer enemies with feet. One can hear them approaching. Spirits cheat. They pass through walls, floors, and good locked doors. Very poor manners. I shall sleep with a lamp tonight. Perhaps two. Tread carefully... no, actually stomp loudly. If another ghost arrives, I want warning before it starts sharing my room. Walls should keep ghosts out.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/ghost_busted · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_ghost` (in-game name "Who You Gonna Call?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 500.20


:: Heads Everywhere [rambling] {"position":"1600,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Hydra grew another head wherever one was done / He kept on cutting heads until the beast had none!
LOG: The Hydra grew heads where a sensible beast keeps one / He kept on cutting until every last head was done! / One jaw became three, then the three became terribly more / His blade kept on working while heads rolled over the floor! / I tried counting necks, but the number refused to stay right / A minstrel needs fingers for strings, not for joining that fight! / Monsters may sprout heads till they crowd every cave wall / His sword has enough sharp replies for them all! / The Hydra lost heads by the heap and the score / I stopped counting early and hid by the door!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/heads_everywhere · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_hydra` (in-game name "The Twelve Labors of Hercules") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.49


:: Dragonslayer, Sire [rambling] {"position":"1750,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Decapitator of Draconic Dread! Another dragon chose very poorly.
LOG: Hail, Decapitator of Draconic Dread! One dragon challenged the crown. One dragon regretted it! Wings flared. Flame rolled. Steel answered. The Master stood where lesser hunters become smoke. Magnificent! Salutations, Scourge of Scales and Sovereign of Scorched Skies! The carcass makes a better monument than the living beast ever did. clear the landing ground! I shall announce the victory from somewhere with a roof. No, farther back. Much farther. Dragonslayer of the dark domain!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dragonslayer_sire · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_if_dragon` (in-game name "Dragonslayer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.28


:: Serpent Soup [rambling] {"position":"1900,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The serpent rose in foam with scales along its side / He carved it down and drowned its scaly pride!
LOG: The sea serpent rose from the foam with its scales shining wide / The Master met jaws with a blade and broke all its pride! / Its coils churned white water and battered the rocks near the shore / His strikes cut the coils until none could come curling for more! / I watched from dry stone where the tide could not reach / Such monsters make excellent stories when fought off the beach! / Sailors can boast of the storms they have weathered at sea / He carved serpent supper where sailors would rather flee! / The ocean kept salt, scales, and spray in its stew / The Master left standing while serpent blood coloured it blue!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/serpent_soup · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_sea_serpent` (in-game name "Sea? Not a Problem") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.37


:: Deaf to Sirens [rambling] {"position":"2050,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Silencer of Saltwater Songbirds! Rival singers have been dismissed.
LOG: Greetings, Silencer of Saltwater Songbirds! The Sirens sang. The Master kept walking. Admirable ears! Their voices promised sweetness, beauty, and whatever else gets sailors killed. He answered with steel. / The singers called softly across dark rolling foam / His darker heart answered by steering for home! / Their melody shattered along the black shore / The Sirens fell silent and sang nevermore! Salutations, Breaker of Bewitching Ballads! I support defeating rival singers on artistic grounds.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/deaf_to_sirens · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_siren` (in-game name "Tie me to the Mast") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.5


:: Brass Birds, Plucked [rambling] {"position":"2200,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The brass-winged flock came screaming from the sky / He plucked the metal birds and watched them die!
LOG: Those brass-feathered birds filled the daylight with glittering flight / Their beaks struck like spears and their wings flashed terribly bright! / He went out hunting while metal wings screamed through the sky / Each bird that came diving discovered a new way to die! / I ducked beneath stone when the feathers began falling fast / The noise made me certain each shiny sharp bird was my last! / Let Stymphalian horrors beat bronze through the cloud / His blows plucked the flock while the metal rang loud! / Their brass wings lay scattered where once they had wheeled / I call that fine music from safely behind a shield!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/brass_birds_plucked · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/kill_stymphalian_bird` (in-game name "Herc was on a Roll!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.44


:: Armour for a Dragon [rambling] {"position":"2350,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Big beast needs big plate! Giblet approves!
LOG: Bring big armour! Bigger! Giblet grins. Dragon needs plate too? Hah! Good. Scale already hard. Plate makes harder. More hard always good. Fit wings careful. Fit neck tighter. Leave joints moving. Bad plate traps beast. Good plate guards beast. Giblet knows. Master brings dragon. Giblet measures from far. Very far. Tail moves lots. Teeth move too! Giblet not fool. Forge can make giant straps. Giant buckles. Giant plates. Much hammer. Much fire. Good job! No old clan tale. No legend. Just big beast, big metal. Giblet likes simple. Bigger anvil maybe needed. Oh yes he will!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/armour_for_a_dragon · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/dragonarmor` (in-game name "Suit Up") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 200.10


:: A Sword Still Burning [rambling] {"position":"2500,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: FSSSH! Giblet wants hot sword!
LOG: FSSSH! Sword still burns! Giblet cheers. Bone core. Fire edge. Strange mix. Good mix! Blade stays hot. No bellows needed. Hah! Master swings once. Air hisses. Swings twice. Better! Fire hugs edge. Enemy gets cut. Then cooked. Gristle jealous maybe. Giblet not share. Forge likes hot blade. Hot blade likes forge. Giblet wants tap it. Maybe not! Burn hammer handle. Bad. Use tongs. Big tongs. Very big tongs. Sixth learns fast. First learned slow. First got burnt cinder. Proud anyway. Family work! This sword worthy. Keep it sharp. Keep it angry.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_sword_still_burning · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/dragonbone_flaming_sword` (in-game name "A Flaming Sword") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Goblin_Burn_1


:: Dragonsteel, Sharpened [rambling] {"position":"2650,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Dragonsteel fights hammer! Giblet likes fight!
LOG: Giblet hears dragonsteel sing. Dense. Mean. Heavy right. Edge takes work. Good sign! Soft metal easy. Great metal fights hammer. Giblet fights back! Clang! Clang! Clang! Sparks jump high. Master gets weapon. Weapon gets bite. Dragonsteel holds. No curl. No chip. Good. Giblet smiles ugly smile. This is craft. Real craft! Dragon heat helps make it. That enough lore. Forge does rest. Giblet does rest. Sixth earns name here. Hit spine. Set edge. Cool slow. Check point. Again! Good blade comes stubborn. Best blade comes mean. This one mean. Giblet likes mean.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dragonsteel_sharpened · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/dragonsteel_weapon` (in-game name "Draconic Evolution") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 107.10


:: A Pixie's Wand [rambling] {"position":"2800,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Tiny spark-stick? Giblet wants metal on it!
LOG: Tiny wand? Where metal? Giblet pokes it. Spark! Giblet jumps. Angry now. Hits table instead. Better. Pixie stick throws strange light. No edge. No weight. No proper grip. Still useful? Maybe. Master likes strange tools. Giblet judges by hurt. Wand hurts foe? Good. Only sparkles? Bad wand. Simple. Giblet wraps grip. Adds metal ring. Better already! Maybe tiny spike too. Everything better pointy. Blister says no hitting. Giblet hears. Giblet ignores little. Not much. Sixth knows when stick bites. Mostly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_pixies_wand · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/pixie_wand` (in-game name "Where Is My Mind?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_MagicNoHurt


:: Dragon Chow [rambling] {"position":"2950,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: BIG bowl! Bigger meat!
LOG: Dragon meal needs BIG bowl, big meat, bigger smell! I chop chunks thick, mix fat, pack tight. Beast eat fast, bowl go empty, teeth keep looking. I make more, no tiny portions, dragon laugh at tiny. Bone meal, meat meal, greasy meal, all go together. I season little, not too much, beast no critic. Masta bring hungry dragon, I bring mountain dinner, fair trade! Tail knocks table, sauce goes flying, I shout louder. Dragon licks floor clean. Hah, useful! I keep fingers back, ladle forward, fire high. Feed beast strong, keep cook whole.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dragon_chow · fires on advancement `iceandfire:iceandfire/dragon_meal` (in-game name "Dragon Growth Hormone") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WeNeedMore02


:: Every Leaf, Sire [rambling] {"position":"3100,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Every leaf, Sire! I fear you now know the forest personally.
LOG: Every leaf, Sire! You have studied that forest with almost scholarly obsession. I knew those trees were plotting something eventually! Leaves differ, bark differs, roots differ, and all of them shed rubbish everywhere. Still, knowledge has value when it helps destroy things properly, Master. You now know which growth burns, bends, poisons, hides prey, or clings unpleasantly to boots. Elves would call this reverence for nature and start singing immediately nearby. We call it reconnaissance with botanical detail, my Lord. Much healthier, and considerably less embarrassing in public or at dinner!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_leaf_sire · fires on advancement `twilightforest:arborist` (in-game name "Maniacal Dendrologist") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 900.20


:: Up the Beanstalk [rambling] {"position":"3250,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Up you go, Master! Anything that tall is hiding something.
LOG: Up you go, Master! That beanstalk has absolutely no sense of proportion or good agricultural manners. Anything growing that high is either hiding treasure or inviting trouble, Sire! Both deserve your attention before some giant claims them first and gets comfortable. Climb carefully and keep one hand ready for violence. Giants adore heights because looking down encourages confidence in slow thinkers. Confidence improves the fall considerably, my Lord. If clouds start hiding doorways, search them closely. Nature rarely grows a ladder this absurd without placing something foolish, wealthy, or edible at the top, Sire!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/up_the_beanstalk · fires on advancement `twilightforest:beanstalk` (in-game name "Jack and the Beanstalk") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_D1_Abyss 303.10


:: Ghasts From the Sky [rambling] {"position":"3400,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Ha! You brought a screaming cloud down to your level.
LOG: Ha, you trapped a Ghast out of the sky! What a wonderfully rude use of machinery, Sire. Those floating sacks usually prefer distance, height, and screaming from somewhere inconvenient above your head. Dragging one down removes nearly every advantage at once and improves the view. Very satisfying, Master... especially when the shrieking becomes indignant rather than threatening. Keep the trap armed and let the next one learn nothing. If the device rattles, stand well clear, my Lord. Angry Ghasts become terribly expressive when cornered! Terror from above looks much less dignified once tied to the ground!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/ghasts_from_the_sky · fires on advancement `twilightforest:ghast_trap` (in-game name "Something Strange in Towerwood") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_D4_Abyss 403.20


:: A Ram, Satisfied [rambling] {"position":"3550,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Look at that ram, Sire! Gluttony in wool deserves some respect.
LOG: Look at that ram, Sire! Stuffed, satisfied, and apparently grateful after all that fuss. You fed the woolly brute every colour it demanded, Master. Such exhausting taste for a creature that eats leaves and wanders about naked! Still, the reward is yours, and that makes the indignity worthwhile. Never underestimate animals with elaborate appetites and endless expectations. They train fools into servants without lifting a hoof. In this case, my Lord, at least the transaction produced something useful. Take the prize and leave before it asks for matching curtains!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_ram_satisfied · fires on advancement `twilightforest:quest_ram` (in-game name "Consummate Baaahs") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 203.40


:: Unmaking the Unmaker [rambling] {"position":"3700,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: You unmade the unmaker, Master! Deliciously unnecessary.
LOG: You unmade the unmaking table, Master! Now that is beautifully spiteful and just complicated enough to be amusing. A device built to take things apart has finally met itself, Sire. I approve of the symmetry rather more than any scholar should! There is something Evilly poetic about turning a tool's own purpose against it. Collect whatever useful pieces remain and waste nothing. Waste is terribly unbecoming when destruction leaves salvage behind, my Lord. Scholars might call this paradox... if given enough ink. I call it loot with a sense of humour!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/unmaking_the_unmaker · fires on advancement `twilightforest:uncraft_uncrafting_table` (in-game name "A Step too Far") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 202.50


:: Giant Theft [rambling] {"position":"3850,5750","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Welcome, Pilferer of Preposterous Giants! Even clouds cannot protect property.
LOG: Welcome, Pilferer of Preposterous Giants! Clouds below. Giants above. Property changing hands! The Master climbed where ordinary folk become weather. He found enormous possessions and made them less enormous by ownership. Splendid theft! Giants looked down. He looked around. Quaver looked for somewhere lower. Greetings, Appropriator of Altitudinous Assets! Bring down whatever fits through the Tower doors. mind the ceiling! If that giant table arrives intact, I am not singing beneath it. The legs alone could end a minstrel career. SALUTE THE SKY-SCALE BURGLAR!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/giant_theft · fires on advancement `twilightforest:giants` (in-game name "I'm on Cloud Nine") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D3_KAHN.JES


:: Four Sceptres, One Master [rambling] {"position":"1000,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Salutations, Sovereign of the Four Sceptres! Four powers have found one hand.
LOG: Salutations, Sovereign of the Four Sceptres! Four powers gathered. One hand claimed them. Proper hierarchy restored! Each sceptre carried a different old threat, but the Master made all four look like court furniture. / Four rods of command found one darker hand / Each ancient enchantment now bends to command! / Four sceptres once boasted of sorcery and lore / Their powers now answer one Master, not four! Greetings, Collector of Crooked Crowns and Ceremonial Sticks! I request no demonstration aimed toward the band.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/four_sceptres_one_master · fires on advancement `twilightforest:lich_scepters` (in-game name "By Our Powers Combined!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles ULTIMATE_DURIUM.JES


:: The Acid Rain Clears [rambling] {"position":"1150,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The poisoned clouds have emptied out their pain / His victories opened pathways through the rain!
LOG: The poisoned rain faded and left the strange forest in peace / The Master's hard victories made the last burning drops cease! / Old regions that snarled behind weather now opened their way / The clouds lost their acid and grudgingly brightened the day! / I kept under cover until every sizzling drop passed / Courage is splendid, but roofs make a minstrel last! / Old kingdoms may clash where their poisoned old borders converge / His victories met there and broke through the poisonous scourge! / The pathways lie open where rain once delivered its pain / I still carry a hood if those clouds start again!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_acid_rain_clears · fires on advancement `twilightforest:progress_merge` (in-game name "Ultimate Showdown") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.36


:: A Trophy for the Master [rambling] {"position":"1300,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Hail, Pedestal-Promoter of Proudly Plundered Prizes! Modesty has been defeated.
LOG: Hail, Pedestal-Promoter of Proudly Plundered Prizes! Trophy acquired. Trophy displayed. Modesty defeated! The Master has placed victory where every visitor must look at it. Excellent taste. A trophy hidden in a chest is merely clutter. A trophy raised high becomes a warning with polish. Salutations, Exhibitor of Exterminated Enemies! Dust it carefully, Minions. Not me. I sing. I do not polish remains. Let every guest enter, stare upward, and understand the decorating theme immediately. Fanfare for the Lord of Lofty Loot!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_trophy_for_the_master · fires on advancement `twilightforest:progress_trophy_pedestal` (in-game name "Trophied Champion") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D5_RETRIEVESTATUE.JES


:: Glass Swords Break [rambling] {"position":"1450,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: CRACK! Giblet knew glass weak!
LOG: Glass sword. Bad idea! Pretty. Sharp. Fragile! Giblet knows before swing. Master swings anyway. CRACK! There. Told no one. Still right. Glass cuts well once. Maybe twice. Then pieces. Pieces cut feet. Bad craft! Unless one-hit plan. Then good. Very good maybe. Hit hard. Break blade. Foe breaks too. Giblet respects brave stupid sword. Same as Minion sometimes. Strong until not. Fifth got gibbed out. Still hit first. Good Minion. Good sword? Hm. Maybe. Giblet keeps shard. Sharp shard useful. Forge gives second jobs.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/glass_swords_break · fires on advancement `twilightforest:break_glass_sword` (in-game name "One Hit Wonder") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_CantDamage


:: Dressed in Fire [rambling] {"position":"1600,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Fire armour! Giblet likes hot plate!
LOG: FWOOM! Armour wears fire! Heat outside. Heat inside? Hope not. Master wears blaze. Plate glows mean. Good look! Giblet taps shoulder. Hot! Ouch. Still good. Fire no hurt it! Hah! Good armour laughs at flame. Sparks run off. Heat stays angry. Enemy grabs? Enemy burns. Better! Giblet calls that smart metal. Maybe too smart. Armour fights while Master fights. Double work. Good. Forge Master approves. No honey smell. No fluff. Just heat. Much better. Giblet wants copy. Smaller copy. Maybe gloves first. Maybe not gloves. Sixth likes fingers. Keeps fingers. Use tongs!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dressed_in_fire · fires on advancement `twilightforest:fiery_set` (in-game name "Gallons of Blood and Tears") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_FireNoHurt


:: Snake-Scale Armour [rambling] {"position":"1750,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Snake scale bends. Giblet says useful!
LOG: Giblet bends snake scale. Flex good. Tough too. Hm! Not iron. Still worthy. Plates overlap neat. No gap. Good craft. Master moves easy. Armour moves too. No clank much. Strange. Giblet likes clank. But quiet can live. Edge catches blow. Scale turns it. Niceee! Maybe add metal rim. Just little. Giblet cannot help. Metal makes proper. Snake stuff makes clever. Together better. Keep belly covered. Keep neck covered. Tail? Master no tail. Good. Less work. Giblet judges this armour strong. Not strongest. Strong enough. Hit test later. Very gentle. Maybe.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/snake_scale_armour · fires on advancement `twilightforest:naga_armors` (in-game name "Naga Armorer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 103.10


:: Mystery Cake [rambling] {"position":"1900,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Cake watching me! BAD cake!
LOG: Mystery cake smell WRONG, look sweet, jiggle like trouble! I cut slice, filling crawls sideways, frosting watches me! No cake should watch cook! I heat knife, cut again, thing hisses soft. Good, now I angry. Masta tastes first? Brave Masta, very brave. I toast edge, smoke comes up, little black line grows. ON PURPOSE! Cake needed crust. Everybody knows crust. Inside tastes meat, berry, maybe something with legs. I chew once, chew twice, stop asking questions. Strange cake fills belly. I put rest under lid. Heavy lid. If lid moves, I burn whole cake!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/mystery_cake · fires on advancement `twilightforest:experiment_115` (in-game name "Mystery Meat?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Ouch02


:: Cake. Forever. [rambling] {"position":"2050,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: FOREVER? No more frosting!
LOG: Cake every day, forever, forever, FOREVER? I like cake fine, not this much! Sweet smell morning, sweet smell night, SWEET SMELL IN SLEEP! Masta keep eating, cake keep coming, plate never learn shame. Salt one day, pepper next, hot sauce after. Cake survives all insult. I try sear slice, try fry slice, try hide slice. More cake waits. This food got grudge! I WANT STEW, meat, something ugly! Anything not frosting. Quaver hums cake song, I throw towel. Mortis probably likes silence. I understand Mortis now. Eat cake, Masta. I go smell onions.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/cake_forever · fires on advancement `twilightforest:experiment_115_115` (in-game name "Eating 115 Everyday, 115 Years, Forever") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_TooStrong


:: Cake That Returns [rambling] {"position":"2200,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Slice comes back! RUDE!
LOG: Cake grow back, slice after slice, stupid sweet miracle! I cut wedge, turn around, wedge returns like insult. I cut bigger wedge, return again, still smiling frosting. Fine, I cook faster! Pan get hot, cake hit pan, sugar go dark quick. Smoke curls up, alarm starts in nose. Meant that! Dark sugar tastes better. I planned dark sugar! Masta eat one slice, another wait, then another. Infinite supper sounds good until supper all cake. I need meat beside it. Big salty roast. Bigger roast. Cake can refill forever, roast keeps dignity. I lock cake plate away. It comes back anyway.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/cake_that_returns · fires on advancement `twilightforest:experiment_115_self_replenishing` (in-game name "Making a note: Huge Success!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ComingBack01


:: Starving? Hydra Chop. [rambling] {"position":"2350,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Starving? Take BIG chop!
LOG: Starving? Take Hydra chop, thick meat, big fat edge! I slap chop down, board nearly breaks, good size. Season heavy, salt sticks, pepper disappears into meat. Pan too small, so use fire grate, hotter anyway! Hydra meat fight heat, curl hard, spit fat everywhere. I turn once, turn twice, no baby poking. Let crust build! Masta gets chop like shield. Cut center, steam jumps out, smell fills whole room. Good! One bite could feed Quaver week. Maybe two Quavers. I keep bone for stock, fat for pan, scraps for stew. Hydra got many heads, only one dinner needed.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/starving_hydra_chop · fires on advancement `twilightforest:hydra_chop` (in-game name "Hydra Chop, Baby!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.KillThemAll02


:: The Forest, Eaten [rambling] {"position":"2500,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Whole forest dinner! Good table!
LOG: Whole forest on table, every strange bite, every glowing snack! I taste berry, chew root, bite mushroom, regret mushroom briefly. Eternal dusk grow odd food, odd food still food. Roast fern curls, stew beast cuts, mash purple tuber. Masta eat through whole spread, no fear, no fuss. Good mouth! Some fruit bite back, I bite harder, fair rule. One leaf numbs tongue, another makes ears hot. I keep notes? No, Blister keeps notes. I keep plates. Forest dinner needs smoke, salt, sharp sauce, maybe less mystery. By last bowl, table looks conquered. That is proper feast!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_forest_eaten · fires on advancement `twilightforest:twilight_dinner` (in-game name "We Dine At Eternal Sundown") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Treasure03


:: Harming Potions, Chugged [rambling] {"position":"2650,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hissss... another hurting bottle.
LOG: One hurting potion... two... three... Master keeps drinking. I watch throat... still working. Impressive. Bottle one bites blood... bottle two bites bone. Third tastes like nails... I checked. Tongue still numb there. Fourth makes shadows twitch... maybe shadows always did. Harming brew beautiful stuff... simple intention, nasty finish. I hold next vial... hand shakes small. Not fear... symptom. Probably. Master drinks again... cup empties clean. I would applaud... too loud. Instead I sniff stopper, hissss, strong batch. Pain stacked on pain, still standing. Good data. Very good data, slightly blurry data.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/harming_potions_chugged · fires on advancement `twilightforest:full_mettle_alchemist` (in-game name "Full Mettle Alchemist") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ItHurts01


:: A Pickaxe for Mazes [rambling] {"position":"2800,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Master, maze got wall? I got pick!
LOG: This pickaxe wants walls! Maze says left, right, lost forever! I say dig! Best answer! Walls hate it. Grubby found Gate spots through worse ground, and I can make straight road through silly maze! Maybe too straight. Wall gone! Next wall gone too! Pick bites hard, stone gives up, and I run before dust settles! Master sees shortcut? I made that! Not door. Better than door. Door asks permission. Hole does not! Could Grubby do faster? Probably. I do next faster! Give me thicker wall. No, thicker! I want prove it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_pickaxe_for_mazes · fires on advancement `twilightforest:mazebreaker` (in-game name "Breaking the Maze") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Empire_Arena 120.30


:: Maps of Shiny Things [rambling] {"position":"2950,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Shiny map? Shiny under feet!
LOG: Shiny marks on map? I know this game! I follow line and turn and climb, and map says treasure under feet somewhere! Under feet, favourite somewhere! Grubby searched ground for Gate spots, careful and useful. Me? I chase shiny. Still useful! Maybe more shiny-useful. I dig where map says, then little left, then too far right, then back again! Good correction! Stone changes colour. That means close, maybe. Master, look! Map points, I dig, shiny comes out. Simple! Map lies, I dig more, map gets embarrassed! Persistence earns respect, I say!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/maps_of_shiny_things · fires on advancement `twilightforest:ore_map` (in-game name "How Can That Be Worth It?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Treasure01


:: A Totem Against Slimming [rambling] {"position":"3100,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Do not lose weight, Sire! The Gnumus have prepared against catastrophe.
LOG: Do not lose weight, Sire! Apparently the Gnumus agree completely and have made protection against slimming ceremonial. That little totem guards every precious ounce with admirable stubbornness, Master. They truly have built theology around keeping dinner attached! Wear it if you wish, especially after one of Gristle's larger evening meals. A broad silhouette can look very imposing from a throne. Ignore any priest claiming thinness brings purity, my Lord. Purity rarely survives a proper feast anyway, especially around Gnumus. Besides, an Overlord should cast a respectable shadow!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_totem_against_slimming · fires on advancement `gnumus:weight_loss_protection` (in-game name "Weight Loss Protection") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 802.50


:: A Hat for Haggling [rambling] {"position":"3250,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: A bargaining hat! At least greed has finally become fashionable.
LOG: A hat for haggling! The Gnumus understand presentation almost as well as appetite, Master. Put that thing on and merchants suddenly respect your purse, Sire! Or perhaps they fear the hat, which works just as well. Traders love symbols almost as much as profit, excuses, and other people's money. A fine brim tells them somebody expects a better price before speaking. Your armour says something similar with sharper punctuation, my Lord. Use both whenever bargaining grows tedious or suspiciously fair. If they still refuse, negotiations can become more traditional!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_hat_for_haggling · fires on advancement `gnumus:worthy_traders_hat` (in-game name "Worthy Trader's Hat") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 500.30


:: Big Snout, Brought Down [rambling] {"position":"3400,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The giant boar came charging with its monstrous snout / He met the tusks and knocked the brute right out!
LOG: A monstrous boar thundered through brush with a mountain-sized snout / He met those tusks with his steel and soon took the beast out! / Its hooves tore the soil while the great hairy shoulders drove wide / His darker blow stopped all that weight and deflated its pride! / I chose a tall tree where a boar could not reach / From branches I sang every verse of the victory speech! / Hunters may boast of the boars they brought down for a feast / He brought down one with the manners and bulk of a beast! / The Gnumus may carve every chop and ask loudly for more / I only request that they never rebuild the boar!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/big_snout_brought_down · fires on advancement `gnumus:plan_boar` (in-game name "Plan "Boar"") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.38


:: Every Pouch, Pinched [rambling] {"position":"3550,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Greetings, Pincher of Prodigious Pouches! The belts are looking rather bare.
LOG: Greetings, Pincher of Prodigious Pouches! One sack, two sacks, every sack! The Gnumus must be checking their belts very nervously. The Master has gathered purses with the dedication of a tax collector and the subtlety of a landslide. Lovely work! Salutations, Sovereign of Sacks and Satchels! Coins rattle. Clasps snap. Owners complain somewhere far behind. Ignore them. stack the pouches by size, weight, and likelihood of biting. I shall guard the empty shelf. From here. With both hands visible. POUCHES TO THE MASTER!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_pouch_pinched · fires on advancement `gnumus:sack_collector` (in-game name "Pouch Collector") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.18


:: A Rifle, Vintage [rambling] {"position":"3700,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Long iron stick? Giblet wants inspect!
LOG: What this long stick? Not spear. Hm. Giblet squints. Tube. Lock. Wood. Old work! Good work too. Master lifts it. Heavy right. Giblet likes heavy right. It kicks when angry? Hah! Good. Weapon should kick little. Makes owner respect. Giblet checks barrel. Straight. Checks stock. Solid. Checks bits. Tiny bits! Hate tiny bits. Still clever. Gnumus made odd thing. Sixth respects old craft. Not pretty respect. Forge respect. Keep dry. Keep clean. Hit with it too? Maybe. Stock strong enough. If shot fails, club works! Good weapon needs second plan.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_rifle_vintage · fires on advancement `gnumus:vintage_rifleman` (in-game name "Vintage Rifleman") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Nice02


:: Vintage Gadgetry [rambling] {"position":"3850,5900","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: CLICK! Tiny metal works. Giblet confused!
LOG: CLICK! Tiny gears move! Springs too. Giblet frowns. Too many tiny bits. Still... good fit. Click. Click. Snap! Clever. Old Gnumus knew tiny metal. Giblet knows metal loud. Different craft. Not bad. Master found useful junk. Giblet turns it over. Brass here. Steel there. Teeth mesh clean. No wobble. Hm! Respect grows. Small respect. Tiny gear respect. Sixth could smash it easy. Sixth will not. That proves quality! Maybe. Keep oil close. Sand bad. Rust bad. Big hammer very bad. Giblet uses small hammer. Tiny hammer. Feels wrong. Works. Giblet hates that.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/vintage_gadgetry · fires on advancement `gnumus:vintage_technology` (in-game name "Vintage Technology") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.GotIt01


:: A Helmet for Gluttons [rambling] {"position":"1000,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Big helm! Giblet says skull safe!
LOG: Big helmet. Very wide! Giblet stares. Gnumus head fits? Maybe after feast. Hah! Metal thick. Cheek plates broad. Neck guard good. Master could wear? Maybe too round. Still strong. Giblet knocks crown. BONK! Deep sound. Good sound. Helm should save skull. Skull keeps orders. Orders keep Giblet working. Important! Food stains inside? Ugh. Gristle problem. Not forge problem. Giblet can add rim. Add spike. Add two spikes. Better. Face-first fall? Helmet survives. Wearer maybe too. Good enough! Sixth approves fat metal. More metal means more safe.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_helmet_for_gluttons · fires on advancement `gnumus:wellfed_warrior` (in-game name "Well-fed Warrior") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 104.10


:: A Hearty Gnumu Dinner [rambling] {"position":"1150,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: GOOD steam! Give spoon!
LOG: Gnumu dinner arrive heavy, round, rich, smell very serious. I lift lid, steam punches face, GOOD steam! Meat buried deep, roots packed round, gravy thick enough standing. I stir once, bottom catches, smoke sneaks up side. Char is flavour! I planned! Scrape black bits in, they make gravy stronger. Masta get biggest scoop, no tiny Gnumu serving here. I add pepper, stir fast, taste twice, burn tongue little. Worth it! Whoever cooked first knew fat. I respect that. Not too much. Mine version gets hotter, darker, louder. Hearty means belly quiet after. This dish shuts belly up.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_hearty_gnumu_dinner · fires on advancement `gnumus:hearty_dish` (in-game name "Hearty Dish") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Nice02


:: A Goblin in a Barrel [rambling] {"position":"1300,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Well, well! One of our supposed cousins has become furniture.
LOG: Well, well, there is a Goblin in that barrel! Keep your hand near your weapon, Sire, because barrels rarely improve Goblins. Our supposed cousins have discovered portable cowardice, which is sensible enough for them. A barrel hides smell, face, and most bad intentions rather efficiently. Check it before turning your back, Master! Goblins rarely enter containers for reasons that improve the room. If he offers trade, count everything twice before smiling. If he offers friendship, count three times, my Lord, then kick the barrel gently! Proper manners sometimes require a little woodwork.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_goblin_in_a_barrel · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:barrel_success` (in-game name "Kinda Sus") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD1_WorkCamp 203.30


:: A Droblin of Your Own [rambling] {"position":"1450,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Your own Droblin servant! Ugly, obedient, and properly employed.
LOG: You acquired a Droblin servant! Ugly little thing, isn't it, and eager enough to be useful? Excellent, because beauty wastes time in servant quarters. Servants need not be handsome, Sire, merely obedient, useful, and easy to replace. Keep it busy before idleness develops into personality and expensive opinions. A creature trained to follow orders can save effort elsewhere, Master. Do not mistake attachment for equality, my Lord! Give it work, scraps, and enough praise to continue. The Tower can always use another pair of willing hands, especially cheap, Master!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_droblin_of_your_own · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:droblin_success` (in-game name "Best Slave Forever") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD1_WorkCamp 104.10


:: A Shiny Bug Tamed [rambling] {"position":"1600,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Shiny, obedient, armoured! A surprisingly respectable insect.
LOG: Shiny bug, sharp shell, obedient temperament! That is a respectable combination, Sire, especially around Goblins and thieves. The Glitteron looks expensive even before doing anything useful for you. Goblins must hate seeing one under your control, Master. Good! Let the creature carry, fight, or simply stand somewhere impressive and glitter threateningly. Sometimes appearance is half the threat, my Lord, and shine helps considerably. Its shell catches light like stolen treasure from a royal vault. Keep it away from gold piles before the shiny little brute develops expensive tastes!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_shiny_bug_tamed · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:glitteron_success` (in-game name "A Bug's Life") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D5_MAIN 101.10


:: Disguised as Cousins [rambling] {"position":"1750,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Try not to laugh, Master! The disguise almost makes you family.
LOG: Try not to laugh, Master! That disguise almost makes you look Goblin enough from a polite distance. Their camp may accept the shape before noticing your magnificence underneath, Sire. Almost! Walk like you belong there and expect everyone else to move first. Slouch, sneer, and look deeply offended by honest prices or clean furniture. Our alleged cousins should find that convincing, my Lord, especially after one stolen purse. If somebody asks a family question, grunt. If they ask another, steal something and leave before they compare ears!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/disguised_as_cousins · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:goblins_disguise_success` (in-game name "Hiding Among Fools") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 204.10


:: Waking the Drunk [rambling] {"position":"1900,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Wake him, Sire! He has mistaken drunkenness for hibernation.
LOG: Wake him, Sire! The drunken Goblin has slept long enough to become part of the furniture. Honestly, some creatures treat unconsciousness like a profession, Master. Give him a prod and stand back! Goblin liquor can preserve bad temper remarkably well over long, unproductive afternoons. If he wakes swinging, that is perfectly normal. If he wakes singing, hit him again, my Lord. A useful drunk may still know routes, passwords, hidden stores, and unpaid debts. Ask quickly before the next bottle appears and erases whatever useful answer remains!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/waking_the_drunk · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:wake_up_success` (in-game name "Do Not Disturb") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 605.20


:: Goblin Prototype, Pinched [rambling] {"position":"2050,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Stolen prototype! Give Giblet!
LOG: Give stolen thing here! Hah! Goblin made prototype. Master pinched it. Better owner! Giblet turns thing. Odd joints. Rough welds. Smart bits hidden. Goblin work ugly. Giblet respects ugly when works. One screw loose. Two plates thin. Third bit clever! Very clever. Giblet steals idea. Not thing. Idea. Master stole thing already. Good teamwork! Heat this part. Brace that part. Remove wobble. Add weight. Prototype stops being prototype. Becomes proper! Goblin may cry. Good. Tears cool metal badly though. Keep Goblin away. Giblet fixes. Oh yes he will!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/goblin_prototype_pinched · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:prototype_success` (in-game name "This is Mine Now") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ThatsMine02


:: Goblin Wings [rambling] {"position":"2200,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: CLACK! Metal wings open. Giblet watches!
LOG: CLACK! Metal wings open! Goblin madness flies. Giblet lifts frame. Too light. Suspicious. Straps thin. More suspicious. Hinges clever. Very suspicious! Master wears wings. Giblet watches from ground. If fall, Giblet catches? No. Giblet small. Ground catches. Better not fall! Wings need strong pins. Giblet swaps pins. Better. Maybe plate straps. Better. Maybe less weight? Hm. Flying hates weight. Stupid rule. Forge likes weight. Sky does not. Giblet offended. Still, metal flies. That is funny. Sixth wants flying hammer now. No reason. Just wants. Good enough!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/goblin_wings · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:skybound_success` (in-game name "To the Sky") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 600.60


:: Upgrades, Goblin-Style [rambling] {"position":"2350,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Goblin work better! Giblet makes better-better!
LOG: Giblet sees Goblin work. Better now. Not best. Better. Giblet sees new plates. New teeth. New springs. Good. Goblins hit things wrong. Then somehow right. Annoying! Master brings improved gear. Giblet checks every join. One bad. Hit! Now good. One loose. Tighten! Now good. One clever. Leave it. Giblet learns. Forge Master can learn. Sixth not proud-stupid. Only proud. Very proud! Goblin style means extra bits. Too many bits. But bits work. Fine. Giblet steals best tricks. Makes cleaner. Makes heavier. Makes meaner. Goblin style becomes Giblet style. Much better!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/upgrades_goblin_style · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:upgrade_success` (in-game name "Upgrades, People. Upgrades.") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 105.30


:: Liquid Fire [rambling] {"position":"2500,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Fire in cup! Give here!
LOG: Blazing liquor? Give cup here, I smell fire already! First sip burns lips, second burns throat, third maybe eyebrows. GOOD drink! Goblins put flame in bottle somehow, finally useful cousin trick. I hold cup near stove, liquid flashes blue, table gets little scorch. Nobody saw nothing! Table always had mark. Masta drinks cleaner than me, unfair. I add drop to sauce, pan ROARS, sauce gets brave. Too much makes bitter. Right amount makes mouth fight back. I keep bottle high shelf, far from Blister tasting hands. One splash only. Maybe two. Never near open flour. Learned that fast.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/liquid_fire · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:blazing_liquor_success` (in-game name "This is Fine !") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Goblin_Burn_1


:: A Deadly Drink [rambling] {"position":"2650,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: Smells deadly! Tiny sip!
LOG: Deadly liquor smell like bad decision, bitter herbs, metal, old boot. Sniff once, eyes water, good warning. I sip tiny, tongue goes numb, BAD warning! Masta can drink? Of course Masta can. I pour small cup, stand back, watch face carefully. If face stays same, drink strong. If face turns green, drink stronger. Goblin brew tries kill mouth, gut, maybe shadow too. I hate drink that fights cook! Still, sauce can use drop. ONE drop. Pot bubbles mean. Blister would gulp bottle, fool. I hide bottle behind salt. Salt trustworthy. Liquor not. Nobody drink without me yelling first!
