:: Tastes Like Cousin [rambling] {"position":"2800,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Cousin meat? Sauce first!
LOG: Goblin meat on board, smells like cousin maybe, smells like TROUBLE definitely! I poke cut, fat soft, muscle stringy, skin awful. Cousin maybe, Gnarl not sure, I call meat now! Once meat on board, family talk ends. I trim bad bits, rub spice deep, roast slow first. Smell turn good, feels rude somehow. Masta eats if Masta wants. I taste edge, HAH, chewy but rich! Needs acid, needs heat, needs never telling Goblins! If cousins truly cousins, awkward dinner. If not cousins, normal dinner. Either way, sauce works. I keep bones covered, supper gets no questions.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/tastes_like_cousin · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:goblins_meat_success` (in-game name "Goblin Eater") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ThatMustHurt02


:: Stew for the Merchant [rambling] {"position":"2950,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Stew worth coin! Move!
LOG: Merchant want mushroom stew, fine, I make stew worth coin! Mushroom go in, onion follow, butter scream under heat. I stir fast, salt early, pepper late, no lazy bubbling. Merchant watches pot, I hate watcher. Buy or MOVE! Rainbow caps melt strange colour, broth turn bright, smell stay good. That worries me little. Masta see merchant smile, trade likely easy now. I taste spoon, tongue tingles, walls maybe bend. Hm. Strong mushroom. I add cream, fixes nothing, tastes better. Good enough! Merchant gets bowl. Coin comes back. If merchant sees rainbow road, not mine problem.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stew_for_the_merchant · fires on advancement `goblins_tyranny:mushroom_success` (in-game name "Seeing a Rainbow Road ?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.OnIt02


:: Peasant to Fish [rambling] {"position":"3100,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: What have you done to that peasant, Master? He has developed gills!
LOG: What have you done to that peasant, Master? He has gone decidedly fishy from head to miserable toes! Gills, scales, and far less interest in dry furniture or proper roads. Remarkable. The Mermorph change can be forced after all, Sire. That raises several wonderfully unpleasant possibilities for later study and diplomacy! Do not assume the poor creature appreciates the improvement. Peasants complain about weather, taxes, fences, and now breathing arrangements, my Lord. Transformation is much easier to admire when it happens to somebody else, preferably a peasant!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/peasant_to_fish · fires on advancement `seadwellers:adv_turn_villager_into_mermorph` (in-game name "Reverse Evolution") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_MAIN 703.10


:: A Mask in the Grove [rambling] {"position":"3250,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Tread lightly, Master. Sacred masks make excellent lies.
LOG: Tread lightly, Master. That mask belongs in the Grove, and the worshippers know its sacred shape very well. Wear it carefully, Sire, and they may overlook the creature underneath. Ceremonial faces make wonderful little lies... wonderfully useful lies! People see the symbol before the person beneath it, especially frightened or devout ones. Priests are particularly vulnerable to that weakness, especially around sacred costumes and solemn processions. Do not overplay the role, my Lord. Too much confidence invites questions from suspicious believers with spears. Let the mask speak first and keep violence ready second!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_mask_in_the_grove · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:sneak_grove` (in-game name "Birds of a Feather") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 100.10


:: Stolen From a Frostmaw [rambling] {"position":"3400,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Ha! Theft is much finer when the owner can crush you.
LOG: Ha, you stole the Frostmaw's crystal while it lived! That takes nerve, Sire, and excellent timing around enormous teeth and claws. Sleeping monsters make the best vaults... until they wake! Keep moving, Master. I doubt the creature appreciates clever thieves carrying its favourite treasure away. The crystal is valuable precisely because something enormous wanted it nearby for itself. That is usually a trustworthy recommendation, my Lord. Do not stop to admire your work within clawing distance! Theft becomes legend only if the thief survives long enough to boast about it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/stolen_from_a_frostmaw · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:steal_ice_crystal` (in-game name "Big Brain™ Time") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D4_MAIN 501.30


:: Fortunate Grottol [rambling] {"position":"3550,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: There! Grottol, and more shiny!
LOG: There! Shiny Grottol running, and I chase, and it darts left, and I nearly eat rock! Fortune on tool, reward gets bigger? I want clean hit, good hit, Grubby-good hit! Grubby got catapults onto hills for Master, heavy work, proper work. I only need catch sparkly beast! Easier? Does not feel easier! I swing, creature cracks, and treasure jumps, and bits scatter everywhere! More than before! Yes! I scoop shards and chase rollers, and none escape under stone! Master sees? I got double!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/fortunate_grottol · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:kill_grottol_fortune` (in-game name "Double Or Nothing!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 System_Quests Q32_TASK_02.DESC_DONE


:: Grottol, Gently [rambling] {"position":"3700,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Whole Grottol! I did gentle!
LOG: Careful now... no, fast careful! Shiny Grottol there, and I need take it whole, and hands keep wanting grab too fast! Hard job! Gentle tool, tiny tap, little breath. Grubby made Gates without dropping roofs, and I can do gentle too! Probably! Tap once, hold breath, and tap again, and creature comes free. It stays whole! Master, whole! I did not crush it! Grubbison Jr can be delicate. Sometimes. Very sometimes. Want show Giblet, but Giblet might hit it. Better not. Carry like treasure, both hands, and no running. Maybe little running!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/grottol_gently · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:kill_grottol_silk_touch` (in-game name "You're Coming With Me") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.GotIt01


:: Fell Off the Sculpture [rambling] {"position":"3850,6050","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: The ground won, Sire. It often does.
LOG: Height is patient. The ground is not. You fell, Sire. The trial ended quickly. Stone has no sympathy. Neither does gravity. Rise again. Study the ledge before jumping. Caution belongs in climbing. Death collects many through ambition. More through poor footing. There is dignity in caution. Very little in tumbling past a statue. Your epitaph need not mention this. I keep records. I can be discreet. The stone, unfortunately, saw everything. Next attempt, shorter steps. Pride has poor balance. Stone keeps better footing.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/fell_off_the_sculpture · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:sculptor_failure` (in-game name "No One Jumps for the Beef") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.25


:: Rusted Knight Toppled [rambling] {"position":"1000,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The iron knight came grinding out in steel / His rusted armour learned at last to kneel!
LOG: The rusted knight woke with a groan from its armour of steel / The Master struck harder and taught the old metal to kneel! / Its blade swept the chamber and sparks chased the edge of the floor / His blows rang like hammers until it could threaten no more! / I heard every crash from a very respectable stair / A minstrel survives by remaining quite comfortably there! / Ancient plate may boast that no ordinary weapon can bite / His strikes found the weakness and battered the rust from the knight! / The armour fell empty with one final thunderous sound / A flesh wound indeed, if the flesh is all rust on the ground!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rusted_knight_toppled · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:kill_ferrous_wroughtnaut` (in-game name "Just a Flesh Wound") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.16


:: Frostmaw, Thawed [rambling] {"position":"1150,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Thawer of the Titanic Tooth-Beast! That was a very rude awakening.
LOG: Hail, Thawer of the Titanic Tooth-Beast! The Frostmaw woke. The Frostmaw roared. The Frostmaw stopped! Very efficient awakening. Snow flew. Claws swung. The Master remained unpleasantly warmer than the victim. Greetings, Breaker of Blizzard-Born Brutes! I watched the ice crack from a sheltered place. A heroic sheltered place. I value circulation in all fingers. The beast may have slept for ages, but one rude awakening was clearly enough. fetch the trophy before it freezes to the floor! Quickly, before something else wakes!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/frostmaw_thawed · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:kill_frostmaw` (in-game name "Rude Awakening") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D2_OBERON.JES


:: Naga, Grounded [rambling] {"position":"1300,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Naga swept in circles through the open sky / He struck the serpent down while still in flight!
LOG: The Naga came sweeping on wings through the bright open sky / He looked up once and struck the great serpent mid-fly! / It circled with scales flashing hard in the light / His weapons kept finding the serpent throughout the long fight! / I followed from cover and praised every glorious bound / My favourite part came when the monster stayed close to the ground! / Let winged serpents coil where the clouds make their lofty domain / His darker reach sends them crashing in pain! / The sky lost a terror when scales struck the ground / I like all my serpents much lower and easier found!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/naga_grounded · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:kill_naga` (in-game name "Wingin' It") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.6


:: The Sculptor Approves [rambling] {"position":"1450,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Welcome, Victor of the Sculptor's Severe Scrutiny! The critic approves.
LOG: Welcome, Victor of the Sculptor's Severe Scrutiny! The trial was climbed. The judge approved. The Master stood worthy! Stone, height, balance, and whatever solemn test the Sculptor demanded could not spoil the ascent. / The challenge rose steep where weak climbers would fall / His iron will carried him over it all! / The Sculptor looked down from a cold stony seat / The Master stood worthy and finished the feat! Salutations, Ascender of Awkward Artistic Approval! I applaud from below, where falling has shorter consequences.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_sculptor_approves · fires on advancement `mowziesmobs:sculptor_challenge` (in-game name "You Must Believe") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 300.30


:: The Chest Bit Back [rambling] {"position":"1600,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Slayer of Suspicious Storage! Furniture should not have teeth.
LOG: Greetings, Slayer of Suspicious Storage! The chest opened first. That was its mistake. Teeth appeared. Quaver disappeared! A treasure box that bites violates several sacred expectations, mostly mine. The Master struck back and converted false furniture into honest remains. Excellent! Salutations, Breaker of Biting Boxes! Open the next chest slowly, Minions. Very slowly. Use a stick. A long stick. Longer. No, longer than that! The treasure can wait. My fingers cannot be replaced by a particularly convincing rhyme. Chests should hold gold, not grudges!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_chest_bit_back · fires on advancement `artifacts:chest_slayer` (in-game name "Chest Slayer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D2S3_TOMBPLUNDERER.JES


:: Eating Artifacts, Sire? [rambling] {"position":"1750,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: ARTIFACT NOT FOOD! Use plate!
LOG: ARTIFACTS NOT FOOD, Masta, teeth got limits even for Masta! I see relic go mouthward, I nearly drop pan. Metal charm stays out mouth, old idol stays out too! Boots maybe leather, still not dinner. I cook meal, not history, Gnarl chew scroll. I make proper plate, meat here, root there, sauce everywhere. Masta still eat strange treasure, fine, I stand ready with broth. Hard bite chips tooth, broth helps, cursed bite screams, Blister helps. Glowing bite explodes, Giblet helps maybe. Kitchen rule stays SIMPLE, if fork bends, STOP CHEWING! Masta disagree, Masta always win, I complain anyway!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/eating_artifacts_sire · fires on advancement `artifacts:adventurous_eater` (in-game name "Adventurous Eater") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WhyMe01


:: A Relic Unearthed [rambling] {"position":"1900,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Leave the dirt where it is. Context is fragile.
LOG: You found a relic without knowing precisely what you sought. That is archaeology in its purest form. Discovery first... confidence afterward. Resist the urge to assign importance immediately. Dirt has no sense of hierarchy. A prince's seal and a servant's spoon may sleep beside each other for centuries. Where was it lying? What surrounded it? What material clung beneath the edge? Those details vanish first... usually beneath someone's polishing cloth. Bring me the piece as found. We can make it handsome later. Truth is less cooperative once cleaned... and considerably harder to reconstruct.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_relic_unearthed · fires on advancement `artifacts:amateur_archaeologist` (in-game name "Amateur Archaeologist") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until That Is Not a Fish (overlord:tales/that_is_not_a_fish) has UNLOCKED (the Collector's first appearance) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: DREDGE Row 1033


:: Every Dungeon Delved [rambling] {"position":"2050,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Every dungeon! Every dark hole too!
LOG: Down stairs, through crack, under arch, across pit, and still more dungeon ahead! Good! Old places, bad floors, I like! Every door means route, and every cellar means deeper route, and every wall might lie! Grubby dug where Master needed Gates, and I keep thinking like that. Where can road go? Where wall thin? Where floor lying? I check all! One dungeon got dead end. Dead end not dead after pickaxe! Another got hidden stair, and I found with forehead, and forehead found pain! Ouch! Still found. Master, every dungeon seen now! That counts as delving! Very good.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_dungeon_delved · fires on advancement `betterdungeons:all_dungeons` (in-game name "Professional Dungeoneer") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Hunting_Grounds 114.30


:: Krampus Is Coming [rambling] {"position":"2200,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Someone has been very naughty! Good. Krampus appears to have noticed.
LOG: Someone has been very naughty! I can almost hear winter sharpening its claws already outside. Krampus takes such matters personally, Sire, which saves us the trouble of hunting it. Good! Let the creature bring its moral ledger and test it against yours, Master. I suspect the accounting becomes violent rather quickly and wonderfully one-sided. Creatures who punish bad children rarely prepare for grown tyrants, my Lord. If it brings chains, take them afterward as trophies. Midwinter improves enormously once somebody starts screaming and presents begin changing hands, my Lord!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/krampus_is_coming · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:naughty_child` (in-game name "Naughty Child") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Nordberg_Town_Chunk_4 310.20


:: Sweets. Disgusting. [rambling] {"position":"2350,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Sweets. Disgusting! Take them anyway.
LOG: Sweets are disgusting! Look at that sticky little offering, Sire, all cheerful colours and sugar. Childish expectation clings to it almost as badly as syrup on fur. Hideous, though perhaps useful when free. Still, somebody may be foolish enough to hand you treats for merely appearing, Master. Accept them! Free food tastes less wholesome once obtained by intimidation and dark armour. If they offer honey, send it to Gristle, my Lord. If they offer nothing, remind them who knocked!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/sweets_disgusting · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:trickor_treat` (in-game name "Trick or Treat") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD3_MelvinsKitchen 100.10


:: Mother of Spiders, Squashed [rambling] {"position":"2500,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The mother spider filled her lair with hungry brood / He spoiled her nest and ruined her maternal mood!
LOG: The mother of spiders came swollen with venom and brood / He went spider-hunting and spoiled her maternal mood! / Her children came crawling through webbing from ceiling to floor / His blade kept on working until they could skitter no more! / I fled from the nursery when eight-legged babies drew near / A minstrel can rhyme very poorly when paralysed by fear! / Spider queens may hatch every nightmare their swollen nests bring / He cuts through the brood before anything can spring! / The brood lost its mother, the web lost its crown / I vote that the whole dreadful nursery stays down!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/mother_of_spiders_squashed · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:arachnophobes_nightmare` (in-game name "Arachnophobe's Nightmare") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.32


:: Top Dog, Put Down [rambling] {"position":"2650,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Kennel-King of the Colossal Curs! The top dog has gone down.
LOG: Hail, Kennel-King of the Colossal Curs! Big dog. Bigger teeth. Brief reign! The beast came charging as though size alone had settled the fight. The Master corrected that misunderstanding. Loudly. Greetings, Toppler of the Top Dog! Fur flew. Jaws snapped. I selected an excellent wall. One with no dog-sized openings. The creature may have been called the biggest brute in the pack, but every pack learns hierarchy eventually. drag the carcass somewhere dramatic! Leave the head facing away from the music room. Good. KEEP THAT THING'S FLEAS OUTSIDE!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/top_dog_put_down · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:big_boy` (in-game name "Big Boy") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.46


:: Every Charm [rambling] {"position":"2800,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Salutations, Keeper of Curious Charms! Every trinket has found a darker owner.
LOG: Salutations, Keeper of Curious Charms! Trinkets gathered. Luck bottled. Every little ward accounted for! Some promise protection, some promise strength, and some merely look expensive enough to steal. The Master has collected the lot. / Charm after charm found a place in his hoard / Each bauble now serves a much darker Lord! / Bright tokens may promise good fortune and grace / Darkness looks better when wearing their face! Greetings, Gatherer of Gleaming Guarantees! If one charm protects minstrels from falling masonry, I volunteer to test it second.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_charm · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:charm_collector` (in-game name "Charm Collector") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D5_RETRIEVESTATUE.JES


:: The Missionary Silenced [rambling] {"position":"2950,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The preacher raised his voice and thundered holy zeal / The Master answered with a shorter, sharper appeal!
LOG: A missionary came preaching through darkness with terrible zeal / The Master supplied a far shorter and bloodier appeal! / The preacher spoke loudly of doctrine, salvation, and right / His sermon grew shorter when steel interrupted the night! / I listened from cover and learned every sensible refrain / The safest belief is the one keeping singers from pain! / Let missionaries thunder until every listener grows bored / No sermon sounds grand when cut short by a darker Lord! / The pulpit went quiet, the last holy argument fled / A preacher speaks softly when preaching is done among dead!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_missionary_silenced · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:dark_creator` (in-game name "Dark Creator") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles SILENT_ORDER.JES


:: Bonescaller, Unboned [rambling] {"position":"3100,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Welcome, Dismantler of the Dread Bonescaller! The summoner needs reassembly.
LOG: Welcome, Dismantler of the Dread Bonescaller! Summoner summoned. Bones answered. Bones scattered! The old conjurer called up skeletal servants as though quantity might impress the Master. It did not. Greetings, Breaker of Bone-Bound Brutes! Ribs flew. Skulls rolled. I counted neither. Counting bones invites someone to ask me to stack them. The caller's grand army ended as a floor problem. sweep the femurs left! No, the other left! Watch that skull! I said watch the skull!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/bonescaller_unboned · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:dismantledto_bones` (in-game name "Senior Summoner") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 500.10


:: Swatted in Style [rambling] {"position":"3250,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Swatter of the Swollen Sky-Pest! One blow improved the atmosphere.
LOG: Hail, Swatter of the Swollen Sky-Pest! One enormous fly met one excessive answer. Beautiful! Wings buzzed. The Master swung. The air became considerably quieter. / A fly large enough to cast shadows came buzzing for blood / One mighty swat sent it straight to the mud! / Its wings had been thunder, its belly was fat / All of that grandeur lies horribly flat! Salutations, Sultan of the Singular Swat! I refuse cleanup duty. Absolutely. That stain has dimensions.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/swatted_in_style · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:excessive_fly_swatter` (in-game name "Excessive Fly Swatter") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 400.20


:: Chaos Cast Out [rambling] {"position":"3400,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: The chaos clung like shadow where the darkened air was bare / He cast the horror outward and left nothing hiding there!
LOG: The foul thing clung tightly where chaos had twisted the air / He drove darkness from darkness and stripped the thing bare! / Its presence fought hard with a shriek that could curdle the night / His will cast it outward and ended its grip in the fight! / I kept every charm that I own very close to my chest / A singer prefers when strange spirits leave singers at rest! / Chaos may clutch every shadow it thinks it can claim / His will casts horrors away all the same! / The chamber fell quiet when the last foul echo was gone / I waited three breaths before daring to carry on!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/chaos_cast_out · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:exorcism` (in-game name "Exorcism") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 500.20


:: The Stalker Stalked [rambling] {"position":"3550,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Hunter of the Hunting Horror! The stalker chose the wrong shadow.
LOG: Greetings, Hunter of the Hunting Horror! The stalker stalked. The Master stalked better. Case closed! Nightmares usually depend on being the frightening one in the dark. This one misjudged the competition. Salutations, Tracker of the Terror That Tracks! I remained nearby in spirit. Very nearby in spirit. Physically, the corridor was excellent. Strong walls. One exit. The creature followed prey for too long and became prey instead. bring a lantern! Another lantern! Make it three! I LIKE SEEING NIGHTMARES BEFORE THEY SEE ME!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_stalker_stalked · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:fighting_nightmares` (in-game name "Fighting Nightmares") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.50


:: Every Hat of Chaos [rambling] {"position":"3700,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The hats of chaos filled the pegs in every range / He gathered every crown and cap, however bent or strange!
LOG: The hats of chaos came tall, bent, feathered, broad, and strange / The Master collected the whole ridiculous range! / One hat looked wicked, one wobbled, one glittered with dread / Another seemed eager to bite from the crown of the head! / I tried one for half of a verse and surrendered the crown / The brim hid my eyes and I nearly marched straight into town! / Chaos may dress in impossible buckles and flair / Our Lord owns the wardrobe and leaves every peg nearly bare! / The collection now waits for a suitably terrible night / Quaver prefers his old cap because nothing about it can bite!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_hat_of_chaos · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:hatman` (in-game name "Hatman") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.10


:: Lifestealer, Robbed [rambling] {"position":"3850,6200","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Robber of the Ravenous Lifestealer! The thief has been robbed.
LOG: Hail, Robber of the Ravenous Lifestealer! The thief came for life. The Master took the advantage instead! A creature that feeds by stealing strength should understand theft better than most. Apparently not. / It reached for his lifeblood and found only strife / Darkness robbed back what had come there for life! / The hunter grew hungry, the hunted stood tall / The Lifestealer finished with nothing at all! Greetings, Repossessor of Stolen Vitality! I recommend keeping whatever was taken. Returning it would spoil the fanfare.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/lifestealer_robbed · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:horror_underthe_mantle` (in-game name "Horror Under the Mantle") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles HARVEST_10.JES


:: The Glutton, Gutted [rambling] {"position":"1000,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Glutton came up hungry from a cavern without sun / He fed upon the Master's steel until the feast was done!
LOG: The Glutton came hungry from caverns too deep for the sun / He went down hunting and spoiled all its terrible fun! / Its mouth seemed enormous, its belly still begged to be fed / His blade gave the creature a meal made of violence instead! / I brought no provisions and stayed where the tunnel was wide / A hungry thing that enormous makes minstrels decide where to hide! / Gluttons may eat stone, bones, armour, and anything near / He feeds them endings with absolutely nothing to fear! / The depths lost their eater when hunger finally was done / I kept my lunch guarded until we returned to the sun!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_glutton_gutted · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:horrorofthe_depths` (in-game name "Horror of the Depths") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D1_FOOD.JES


:: The Pumpkin Lord Falls [rambling] {"position":"1150,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Salutations, Sovereign of Smashed Squash! The pumpkin throne stands empty.
LOG: Salutations, Sovereign of Smashed Squash! The Pumpkin Lord has fallen. Autumn is leaderless! Vines drooped. Seeds scattered. The crown rolled somewhere under a boot. Excellent harvest! Welcome, Carver of Crowned Cucurbits! The great orange noble looked impressive until someone struck the stem. I never trusted vegetables with titles. They grow ambitions between harvests. collect the seeds! Not for planting. Absolutely not for planting. Roast them, bury them, throw them into the sea. Anything but succession. Long live the Master, down with the gourd!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_pumpkin_lord_falls · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:pumpkin_lord` (in-game name "Last Night") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 100.20


:: Sir Pumpkinhead, Carved [rambling] {"position":"1300,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Sir Pumpkinhead rode proudly beneath the silver light / He lost his glowing head before the end of night!
LOG: Sir Pumpkinhead rode beneath moonlight with orange noble pride / He cut through courtly display from the side! / His carved little grin had been wicked and bright in the night / One proper dark blow made the lantern-head lose all its light! / I almost felt sorry for one very vegetable knight / The feeling departed the moment his weapon came into sight! / Pumpkin-faced warriors may salute with their swords raised high / Our Lord makes their helmets into supper by and by! / The seeds may remember a knight with a proud little name / The Master remembers another strange foe for his fame!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/sir_pumpkinhead_carved · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:pumpkin_sir` (in-game name "Pumpkin Sir") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles D1_MELVIN.JES


:: Rampage, Sire! [rambling] {"position":"1450,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Rampager of Ruinous Renown! The furniture should begin evacuating.
LOG: Hail, Rampager of Ruinous Renown! Something broke. Then something else broke. Then everything became louder! The Master entered a proper rampage and left restraint somewhere far behind. Splendid! Walls shook. Foes scattered. I found a supportive pillar. Greetings, Grand Duke of Going Completely Too Far! No, no, that one nearly earns a correction. Keep smashing! The fanfare can catch up later. Minions, forward! Minstrel, backward! The floor is moving! RAMPAGE FOR THE DARK LORD! MORE DRUMS! FEWER FALLING STONES!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/rampage_sire · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:rampage` (in-game name "RAMPAGE!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.35


:: Moonlit Cowboy [rambling] {"position":"1600,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: There rode a lonely figure through the cold and silver night / He met the Master underneath the moon and lost the fight!
LOG: There once rode a cowboy through spruce-shadowed country at night / The moon caught his outline and silvered the edge of the fight! / The Master found trouble beneath that cold pale lunar glow / A strange western figure soon learned there was nowhere to go! / I hummed a low tune fit for roads and a lonely old trail / The wind took the chorus and carried it over the vale! / Moonlit riders may boast of the wilds under their reign / Our Lord rides through darkness and leaves them a much shorter plain! / The night kept its moon and the forest kept every tall tree / The cowboy kept less while the trees still stood free!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/moonlit_cowboy · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:spruce_cowboyinthe_moonlight` (in-game name "Spruce Cowboy In The Moonlight") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.27


:: Every Record of Chaos [rambling] {"position":"1750,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Welcome, Archivist of Appalling Acoustics! Chaos has completed an album.
LOG: Welcome, Archivist of Appalling Acoustics! Every record gathered. Every terrible tune preserved. The collection sounds dangerous already! Chaos has produced quite a catalogue. The Master has taken all of it. / Each record now turns with a shriek and a chime / Darkness keeps excellent horrible time! / From first dreadful note to the last wicked sound / The whole mad symphony circles around! Salutations, Collector of Catastrophic Choruses! Quaver admits one refrain is catchy. Only one. If anyone repeats that admission, the next song will be about them.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_record_of_chaos · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:symphonyof_chaos` (in-game name "Symphony of Chaos") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 300.10


:: Krampus, Unwrapped [rambling] {"position":"1900,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Unwrapper of the Unwelcome Winter Guest! Midwinter has gone badly.
LOG: Greetings, Unwrapper of the Unwelcome Winter Guest! Krampus arrived with chains, horns, and seasonal disapproval. The Master supplied a harsher holiday greeting. Excellent! Gifts are traditionally wrapped. Krampus was apparently the reverse. Salutations, Breaker of the Bad-Natured Gift-Bringer! Naughty lists have become much less important now. I kept very quiet during the inspection. Purely artistic restraint. No reason at all. check the sack! If anything inside moves, close it again! Midwinter has produced enough surprises. FANFARE, QUICKLY, BEFORE ANOTHER RELATIVE ARRIVES!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/krampus_unwrapped · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:wrong_santa` (in-game name "Wrong Santa") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.30


:: Clad in Dark Metal [rambling] {"position":"2050,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Dark plate, Masta! Giblet likes weight!
LOG: Dark plate. Thick plate! Giblet grins. This suit means work. Heavy shoulders. Hard chest. Mean helm. Good! Master wears darkness as metal. Giblet taps breast. Clang deep. Good heart-sound. Not real heart. Metal heart. Better. Chaos stuff strange. But forge rule same. If holds hit, good. If bends, fix. If breaks, melt. Simple! This holds. Giblet respects. Maybe add edge here. Maybe spike there. No need? Hm. Giblet wants anyway. Sixth hates flat plate. Needs bite. Armour should say move. Dark armour says MOVE! Giblet likes loud metal.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/clad_in_dark_metal · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:chaos_knight` (in-game name "Chaos Knight") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 103.30


:: A Dark Metal Blade [rambling] {"position":"2200,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Black blade here! Giblet checks edge!
LOG: Hand black blade over! Quiet blade. Giblet tests edge. Shhhk! Nice. Dark metal hard. Not brittle. Good. Master swings. Blade hums low. Giblet likes hum. Not song. Work sound. Point narrow. Spine thick. Balance near hand. Very good! Whoever forged first knew hammer. Giblet gives grudging nod. Tiny nod. Then improves grip. Hah! Now Giblet part inside it. Better. Blade should feel mean early. This one does. Keep it dry. Keep it sharp. Keep it busy. Rust hates work. Work hates rust. Giblet hates rust most. Sixth says cut first. Polish later.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_dark_metal_blade · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:dark_blacksmith` (in-game name "Dark Blacksmith") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 102.30


:: A Warblade Your Size [rambling] {"position":"2350,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: CLANG! Now that blade proper!
LOG: CLANG! Big blade lands! Heavy! Proper! Giblet laughs. Master-sized iron. Finally. Small swords look silly now. This one needs two hands? Master has strength. Fine! Giblet tries lift. Hnnng! Too much. Good sign. Big weapon mocks weak arms. Edge long. Spine brutal. Guard thick. Pommel could crack skull. Excellent! Giblet walks around it. Checks straight. Checks tip. Checks grip. All good. Sixth approves loudly. Very loudly! Foe sees blade. Foe knows. No speech needed. Just metal. Big metal. Mean metal. Giblet calls that diplomacy. Ha! Big word. Funny. Still true.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_warblade_your_size · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:my_size` (in-game name "My Size!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 102.10


:: Shielded by Darkness [rambling] {"position":"2500,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Dark shield eats light? Giblet tests!
LOG: Dark shield eats light? Good. Giblet likes shade. Shield face strange. Metal drinks glow? Maybe. Not care. Does it stop hit? Yes! Then good shield. Master braces. Giblet punches front. Ow. Good shield! Punch hurt Giblet. That means strong. Very scientific. Hah! Sixth knows big words sometimes. Edge thick. Grip firm. No rattle. Excellent. Darkness curls around it. Fine. Let dark do work too. Giblet trusts rivet more. Rivet visible. Darkness not visible much. Still both hold. Keep shield high. Keep feet set. Let enemy break first. Giblet likes that plan.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/shielded_by_darkness · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:protectedby_darkness` (in-game name "Protected by Darkness") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 300.20


:: Spiny Shell Suit [rambling] {"position":"2650,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Spikes! Giblet approves already!
LOG: Spikes! Good start. Shell plate too. Better start! Giblet runs claw along ridge. Hard. Very hard. Master wears wall with teeth. Hah! Enemy hits armour. Armour bites back. Perfect! Shoulder spikes point out. Back spikes point more. Sit down? Maybe bad. Not forge problem. Giblet likes suit. Thick where needed. Ugly everywhere else. Excellent. Sixth adds one rivet. Just one. Makes it his. Family rule. Always leave mark. Not fancy mark. Hammer dent. Good mark. Shell warrior walks now. Giblet hears scrape. Strong scrape. Proud scrape. More spikes maybe? No. Enough. Strange feeling.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/spiny_shell_suit · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:shell_warrior` (in-game name "Shell Warrior") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 203.10


:: Spider Bite, Forged [rambling] {"position":"2800,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Fang-blade! Giblet sees pointy work!
LOG: Bring fang-blade closer! Hm. Bite-shaped edge. Hook here. Fang there. Mean weapon! Giblet likes mean. Master lifts it. Giblet sees point. Very pointy. Good. Maybe poison lives there? Blister would lick it. Bad idea. Giblet does not lick metal. Mostly. Sixth hammers spine. Tap! Tap! No bend. Good. Spider thing should catch. This catches. Pull foe close. Then hit. Simple! Web tricks maybe. Giblet not web person. Hammer beats web. But forged bite? Good craft. Keep edge clean. Keep hook sharp. Spider asks back? Stab spider. Stab it! Stab it! Stab it!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/spider_bite_forged · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:spider_warlord` (in-game name "Spider Warlord") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Attack01


:: Every Dark Blade [rambling] {"position":"2950,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Blade pile! Giblet very happy!
LOG: Giblet counts blade pile! Good pile! One. Two. Many. Better count! Dark swords, axes, strange cutters. Master got all. Giblet happy. Very happy! Forge table full. Armory fuller. Each blade says different thing. Chop. Stab. Split. Crush. Giblet understands all. Sixth picks favorite. Changes favorite. Changes again. Too many good! This is hard work. Nice hard work. Keep dull ones left. Sharp ones right. Weird ones middle. No touching without ask. Except Master. Master touch all. Giblet polishes none today. Too busy admiring. Tomorrow, work. Today, shiny. Niceee!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_dark_blade · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:squireofthe_dark_lord` (in-game name "Squire of the Dark Lord") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ForMe01


:: Dressed in Nightmares [rambling] {"position":"3100,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Nightmare suit looks mean. Giblet likes mean!
LOG: Nightmare suit. Angry-looking. Giblet watches. Good. Plates dark. Edges wrong. Wrong good? Maybe. Giblet touches sleeve. Cold. Then hot. Huh. Strange armour! Master wears it fine. Of course. Giblet watches shadows stick close. Not normal. Still, plate holds. Buckles hold. That matters. Sixth trusts buckle. Shadow can do shadow things. No bother. Helmet makes face meaner. Hard job. Master already mean face. Hah! Giblet likes suit. Not because nightmare. Because strong. Strong wins. Fear helps too. Foe runs? Less dent repair. Very efficient. Big word! Giblet proud.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dressed_in_nightmares · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:unitywith_darknessachievement` (in-game name "Unity with Darkness") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 107.10


:: Eternal Candy. Ugh. [rambling] {"position":"3250,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Eternal candy? UGH! Eat roast!
LOG: ETERNAL CANDY? Ugh! One chew and hunger goes quiet too long. Sweet little lump act powerful, I distrust tiny food. Real meal got steam, grease, noise, plate weight. Masta eat one, belly stop asking. That is cheating kitchen! What I cook after, air and disappointment? NO! I need hungry mouths, plates coming back clean. Candy steals work from me. I bite corner, sweetness punches teeth, enough. I wrap rest tight, shove high shelf, glare at it. Quick travel food maybe, Masta can take some. Dinner stay real, take space, make mess, need nap after. CANDY NEVER GET MINE BIG PLATE!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/eternal_candy_ugh · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:yoursatietywillbe_eternal` (in-game name "Your satiety will be Eternal!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.PoorMe01


:: Spirits, Transmuted [rambling] {"position":"3400,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Ssspirit shifts... hold bottle still.
LOG: Ssspirit in bottle... not drink spirit... other spirit. Strange. I hold glass close... cold leaks through. Transmute slowly... never rush ghost stuff. Powder falls... flame turns pale. I whisper measure... one pinch, half pinch... maybe too much. Shape changes inside... spirit stretches thin. My nails look blue... unrelated? ,maybe related. Master, infernal medicine bites different. Not poison exactly, feels meaner. I taste residue, only residue. Ears ring backward, somehow. Good reaction. Keep circle clear, no kicking jars. Giblet kicks things. Gristle shouts at things. I ask nicely, spirits sometimes listen. Sometimes they bite glass.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/spirits_transmuted · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:infernal_medicine` (in-game name "Infernal Medicine") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_MagicNoHurt


:: Elixir of Changing [rambling] {"position":"3550,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Sssweet change... maybe too much.
LOG: Elixir keeps changing colour... without asking me. Rude... fascinating. I tilt vial... red becomes green... green becomes something wet-looking. Master... transmuting mix nearly ready. Nearly means dangerous. Ready means also dangerous. I taste one bead... lips tingle... teeth feel taller. Teeth not taller? ,good. Fingers bend fine. Mostly. I add silver dust, liquid shivers. Beautiful. Matter wants become other matter, such sssweet bad manners. I understand that. Bottle warms palm, pulse matches mine. That concerning? ,later concern. For now, seal tight. If cork grows legs, catch it gently. I want legs intact.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/elixir_of_changing · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:transmutalogy` (in-game name "Transmutalogy") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.GotIt01


:: Every Tombstone Taken [rambling] {"position":"3700,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Many stones. Many names. Handle both carefully.
LOG: Every stone has a name. You gathered many. Some names remain readable. Others surrendered to rain. A tombstone marks debt, memory, and place. Move it carefully, Sire. The dead may not object. Families often do. That is why night is useful. Stone travels better quietly. Keep each marker upright. Turning one face down is rude. Turning several is inventory. There are standards, even in grave robbing. I am relieved someone still appreciates proper masonry. Stack none carelessly. Names should face outward. The dead dislike becoming paving. Keep chisels nearby.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_tombstone_taken · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:bury_them_all` (in-game name "Bury Them All") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.10


:: Pocket Necromancy [rambling] {"position":"3850,6350","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Necromancy fits in your hand now. Predictable.
LOG: Necromancy has become portable. Predictable. The living shrink everything eventually. Rituals once needed circles. Candles. Hours. Now death fits in a pocket. Convenient, Sire. Convenience invites carelessness. Do not confuse small with harmless. A spark may burn a hall. A bone may raise an army. A soul may ruin a room. Keep the device closed. Use it with purpose. Death for life. The rule does not shrink with the vessel. Neither does the bill. Keep it away from children. And Quaver. Curiosity creates tedious funerals. Small graves remain graves.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/pocket_necromancy · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:compact_necromancy` (in-game name "Compact Necromancy") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.20


:: Grave Robbing, Sire? [rambling] {"position":"1000,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: Grave robbing, Sire. At least be tidy.
LOG: You entered a grave for profit. Direct. I respect clarity. Tombs contain valuables. They also contain owners. The owners are quiet. Usually. Take what serves, Sire. Leave what does not. Disturbing every bone gains little. Waste offends the balance. So does needless damage. A graveyard is not a pantry. Gristle has been told this. More than once. If something follows you home, return the item first. Then strike whatever remains. That order saves sweeping. Close the grave afterward. Rain enters. Mud follows. Then everything smells worse. Replace the soil neatly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/grave_robbing_sire · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:grave_ravager` (in-game name "Grave Ravager") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.60


:: The Guide, Guided [rambling] {"position":"1150,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The guide crossed first. Appropriate.
LOG: Some guide the dead onward. This one required guidance. You provided it. Final guidance! Sire, death needs no map. The living do. Priests draw roads. Mourners invent gates. Spirits follow what they can. Eventually all paths narrow. One breath. No breath. One side. The other. The guide crossed his own boundary. There is symmetry there. I approve. His profession remains secure. Demand never declines. He simply joined the clientele. His work continues elsewhere now. Perhaps efficiently. Perhaps not. The dead rarely file complaints. I will not grade him. The boundary remains.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/the_guide_guided · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:guidetothenextworld` (in-game name "The day of the Dead") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.50


:: A Stack of Souls [rambling] {"position":"1300,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Souls accumulate. Debt does too.
LOG: Souls should not stack. Yet here they are. Layered. Counted. Kept. Efficient, perhaps. Comfortable, unlikely. Handle them gently, Sire. A soul weighs little. Debt weighs more. The dead remember bargains. So do I. Use them with purpose, Sire. Hoarding is safer than waste. Life has a price. Death has one too. When the pile grows tall, do not admire it too closely. Collections become responsibilities. Ask any gravekeeper with several centuries of backlog. Count twice. Souls are poor at standing still. One missing soul becomes several questions. Order prevents arguments.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_stack_of_souls · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:soul_eater` (in-game name "Soul Eater") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.30


:: Vampirism, Bottled [rambling] {"position":"1450,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Lestat
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Hunger in a bottle. Some temptations deserve better packaging.
LOG: There are things one should never bottle. Hunger is one. Yet here it sits, stoppered and portable. Charming. Does that disturb you? It should, a little. Appetite deserves a body, and desire deserves consequences. A vial makes both look tidy. They are not tidy. You know that now. The old order hoarded relics and called restraint sacred. I always found restraint terribly decorative. This is more honest. A little theft of blood, a little promise of change... suddenly glass feels intimate. Let it remain sealed until you decide what it means. Not what it can do, but what you want from it.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/vampirism_bottled · fires on advancement `born_in_chaos_v1:heart_thief` (in-game name "Heart Thief") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Pale Suits You, Sire (overlord:tales/pale_suits_you_sire) has UNLOCKED (Lestat's first appearance; a player who never turns vampire never gets these) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: IWTV S01E02 91


:: Curtain Call [rambling] {"position":"1600,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Conjurer filled the hall with colour, smoke, and rage / He met the Master and was thrown straight off the stage!
LOG: The Conjurer strode out like an actor demanding the stage / His tricks filled the hall with illusion, bright colour, and rage! / The Master stood watching the spectacle twist through the air / One dark interruption reminded the fraud who ruled there! / I know about stages, applause, and a dramatic last bow / The Conjurer learned that his curtain was falling right now! / Actors may throw smoke and make false little marvels appear / His performances give audiences something to fear! / The final trick ended with one very permanent fall / I call that a curtain call worthy of Tower applause for all!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/curtain_call · fires on advancement `conjurer_illager:kill_conjurer` (in-game name "What a Performance!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.15


:: A Soul in a Bottle [rambling] {"position":"1750,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: One soul. One bottle. Keep the cork firm.
LOG: Glass holds many things. Wine. Poison. Now a soul. The bottle feels colder. That is expected. Keep the cork firm, Sire. A loose soul makes poor company. It may whisper. It may knock. It may simply wait. Waiting is common among the dead. Do not shake it. Dignity matters after death. Mostly because there is little else left. When the soul is needed, release it cleanly. Until then, store it upright. Eternity leaks badly through cheap cork. Label it. Names matter. Otherwise somebody may open the wrong eternity. Glass breaks. Souls wander.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_soul_in_a_bottle · fires on advancement `darkerdepths:activities/bottle_void_soul` (in-game name "Bottle O'Void Souls") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B IGRAVE.40


:: Diamonds Revive [rambling] {"position":"1900,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: A diamond paid. Something returned.
LOG: A diamond enters. A body returns. Expensive symmetry. The husk was empty. Now it moves again. Do not mistake motion for miracle, Sire. Something paid. Something always pays. Death for life. The gem is only the visible cost. The rest follows quietly. Watch the revived one. Memory may return slowly. Hunger may not. If it asks what happened, answer briefly. Long explanations rarely improve resurrection. Neither do mirrors during the first hour. Give it time. Returning is work. Even the dead need a moment before standing. Do not rush it.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/diamonds_revive · fires on advancement `darkerdepths:activities/insert_diamond_into_crystal_husk` (in-game name "Back From the Dead!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B GRAVE.30


:: Anchored to Death [rambling] {"position":"2050,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Mortis
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: Your return is bound. Guard the bond.
LOG: You bound your return to a place. Sensible. Dangerous. Death now has an address. It may call there. Such bonds are old ideas, Sire. They promise certainty. They also create dependence. Guard the place closely. Respect what the bond costs. Do not call it freedom. A tether saves because it holds you. Balanced pairs often hide sharp edges. If the place fails, the promise may fail with it. Death dislikes unpaid arrangements. I dislike paperwork after them. Check the place often. Stones crack. Oaths endure. That combination causes trouble.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/anchored_to_death · fires on advancement `darkerdepths:activities/set_death_anchor` (in-game name "Soul Pact") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 NW_B TOUR.GRAVE3


:: A Pixie, Swatted [rambling] {"position":"2200,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Swatter of Sparkling Sprites! Tiny wings offered tiny resistance.
LOG: Hail, Swatter of Sparkling Sprites! One pixie fluttered. One pixie splattered. Very direct criticism! Tiny wings, tiny tricks, enormous confidence. The Master corrected the scale of its ambition. Greetings, Crusher of Glittering Irritations! I know, they look harmless. That is how small nuisances survive long enough to steal things. I learned this from rats. The pixie may have expected mercy from something so much larger. Poor judgment. sweep the glitter before it gets into the instruments! No, not with my cap! Use Giblet's helmet!
