LOG: Dragon meat minced small, huge beast turned tiny bits, I LOVE insult! Chop, chop, chop, knife works hard, board shakes under weight. Meat rich, fat hot, smell bigger than pieces. I mix onion, pepper, salt, maybe hot root. Form patties? Too neat. Make rough lumps, throw pan, let edges tear. Masta gets dragon supper without wrestling whole beast. Hah! Mighty scales outside, minced meat inside. Everything ends edible eventually. I sear hard, flip once, juice hisses loud. Gristle says this good! Rare self-praise earned. Serve with black bread, sharp sauce, no flower garnish. Dragon deserve better death, not flower garnish.
