:: DeadBeard, Dead Again [rambling] {"position":"3250,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: DeadBeard sailed again though death had claimed its due / He met the Master and went sinking into blue!
LOG: DeadBeard sailed again though death had already claimed its due / He met that piracy with something considerably less blue! / The rotten old captain came swaggering with cutlass and grin / His second career ended deep in the harbour's black din! / I know a sea song, but pirates always steal every refrain / I changed every chorus and kept all the royalties plain! / DeadBeard may raise anchors and stagger from grave into foam / Our Lord sends dead pirates back under the black water home! / The captain died twice, which seems terribly hard on his crew / I hope they choose someone alive for the next mutiny too!
