:: Immortal, Briefly [rambling] {"position":"3550,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Salutations, Briefly Immortal Bringer of Bad Decisions! Death blinked first.
LOG: Salutations, Briefly Immortal Bringer of Bad Decisions! Lightning struck. Death hesitated. The Master remained! Very dramatic. Quaver's fur stood on end from several paces away. Electricity lacks manners. Greetings, Survivor of Shocking Sovereignty! One terrible jolt made mortality look negotiable for a moment. I approve in theory. In practice, I prefer not glowing. The Master walked away with a story. Quaver walked away smelling faintly singed. Nobody mention that. stop laughing! I mean it. STOP LAUGHING! The next fanfare begins when my fur lies flat again.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/immortal_briefly · fires on advancement `rottencreatures:shocking_encounter` (in-game name "High Tension") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 EXP_Titles 500.30


:: A Liar's Mask [rambling] {"position":"3700,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Put on the liar's mask, Sire! Honesty was never flattering.
LOG: Put on the liar's mask, Sire! It suits deceit better than any honest face ever could. People trust symbols far too quickly, Master, especially when frightened, hurried, or eager to belong. Give them one polished lie and they supply the rest themselves! Let the mask carry suspicion away from your intentions and toward somebody poorer. Smile only if absolutely necessary. Honest expressions ruin good trickery, my Lord. If somebody sees through it, congratulate them briefly. Then make certain they cannot explain the trick to anyone else!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_liars_mask · fires on advancement `savage_and_ravage:adventure/mask_of_dishonesty` (in-game name "A Little Tricking") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D4_SD2_TempleConstruction 200.10


:: Explosive Fashion [rambling] {"position":"3850,6500","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: BOOM! Giblet likes loud armour!
LOG: BOOM! Armour answers back! Hah! Giblet LOVES. Plates carry blast. Bad idea. Great idea! Master wears trouble. Giblet steps back. More back. Good. One spark? Maybe no. Keep sparks away until fight. Forge full sparks. Problem. Giblet thinks. Think hard. Put armour over there! Very over there. Then inspect. Thick plates. Strong straps. Blast bits fixed tight. Good. Enemy strikes wrong place. BOOM! Enemy learns. Maybe armour learns too. Sixth likes answering gear. Loud answer best. Giblet would add hammer. No need. Armour already hammer, fire, noise. Perfect stupid thing!
