:: Every Illager Relic [rambling] {"position":"1000,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: the Collector
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The entire set is assembled. Now the differences matter.
LOG: You now possess the entire Illager set. Good. A single object invites admiration. A full set permits comparison... which is more useful. Repeated symbols become habits. Differences become decisions. Arrange them by function first, age second. Ignore value for now. What did their makers repeat? What did they avoid? Auction logic is intellectually lazy. Tools preserve fear, pride, and habit after speeches disappear. You have enough evidence now... enough for absences to matter. Leave one space empty deliberately. A complete display encourages complacency. An empty space keeps the question alive.
