LOG: SOAP? For dinner? NO! I slap hand away, smell clean poison nonsense. Food smell roasted, spiced, bloody, buttery, anything but bath! Masta consider bite, I consider screaming, then screaming wins. Soap make bubbles, not gravy, wash bucket get soap. I chop onion, show proper edible thing, pan smells right again. I fry meat, show proper edible smell, kitchen calms down. See, this food! Soap stays by bucket, far from plates. Somebody eat it, mouth get foam, belly get regret. I cook weird things, soap never join list. Gristle got standards, high ones, mostly hot ones!
