:: A Sip From the Chalice [rambling] {"position":"1600,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Chalice whispers... sssip small.
LOG: Chalice smells old... metal, wine... tiny curse maybe. I bring nose close... cup breathes back! Hm. Master drinks first... wise for me. Liquid slides dark... leaves silver ring. I lick rim... only rim. Tongue goes cold... throat goes warm. Nice contrast. One eye sees sparks... other sees cup. Keep cup on table, table safest. Concoction tastes layered, bitter, sweet, then wrong. Wrong can be useful. I want another trace, no gulping. Gulping wastes symptoms. Sssip gives details, numb lip, buzzing jaw, little happy shiver. Good chalice. Suspicious chalice, my favourite kind.
