:: A Hoe for Fighting [rambling] {"position":"1750,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: That is not gardening, Sire! Good.
LOG: That is not gardening, Sire! Good, because gardening was beginning to sound dangerously wholesome. A hoe large enough for battle finally understands its proper purpose, Master. Why scratch soil when one can scratch armour, helmets, and stubborn skulls instead? Swing it properly and let the farmers faint! The shape is ridiculous, but ridiculous weapons still hurt when brought down hard. A peasant sees a familiar tool, my Lord, right until it enters combat. An enemy sees the last agricultural mistake of his afternoon. Keep the edge sharp and the fields safely neglected.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_hoe_for_fighting · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:big_iron_hoe` (in-game name "It's Not For Gardening") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 102.20


:: A Beast From Ages Past [rambling] {"position":"1900,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Careful, Master! That creature looks older than everyone's manners.
LOG: Careful, Master! That beast looks dragged from a much older age and dropped here hungry. Wings, teeth, and absolutely no concern for modern manners. I like it already, Sire! Tame it if you can without becoming part of its first meal. Ancient creatures make splendid symbols once they stop trying to eat the owner. Keep food ready and your hands clear, my Lord. The beast may remember instincts older than kingdoms, but instinct is not authority. Once it obeys, let everyone else worry about what century it belongs in!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_beast_from_ages_past · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:grapteranodon` (in-game name "Hey Just Like In Ark") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D2_SD1_TheViridianCaverns 101.10


:: Penguins in Armour [rambling] {"position":"2050,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Penguins in armour! Nature has become useful by accident.
LOG: Penguins in armour! I had not expected that sentence today, and I have lived through several strange reigns. Look at the little waddling soldiers, Sire! Nature has become ridiculous again, Master, but usefully so this time. Armour improves almost anything with enemies and a poor survival instinct. It certainly improves a bird that already looks permanently offended. Keep them moving and watch the formation, my Lord. If they slide into battle, even better! Dignity is optional when the opponent is bleeding and the penguin is still standing.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/penguins_in_armour · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:ice_armor` (in-game name "Bring Me A Warden!") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 203.50


:: A Flying Cloud [rambling] {"position":"2200,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Is that a cloud, Sire? No. It has teeth.
LOG: Is that a cloud, Sire? No... it has much larger teeth and a rather alarming wingspan! The Quetzalcoatlus makes an impressive silhouette, Master! Tame it and the sky becomes considerably less neutral for everyone below. Anything that large can carry fear farther than banners or shouted threats. Keep the creature fed and facing outward. Villages notice shadows before speeches, my Lord, which saves valuable time! If it lands badly, stand clear and look offended. Great flying beasts should serve your image, not flatten it beneath several tons of enthusiasm, Sire!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_flying_cloud · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:quetzalcoatlus` (in-game name "Is That A Cloud?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD1_WorkCamp 100.30


:: Beetle-Gem Armour [rambling] {"position":"2350,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Gem armour? Shiny strong. Giblet surprised!
LOG: Gem armour? Beetle gem? Shiny shell. Giblet squints. Looks fancy. Too fancy. Then taps it. TOK! Good. Hits harder. TOK! Still good. Hm. Fancy can be strong. Giblet learns unpleasant thing. Master wears jewel bug plate. Strange look. Good defence. Edges smooth. Maybe too smooth. Add spike? Giblet always says spike. No. Leave gem whole. Cracks bad. Sixth uses soft hammer. Soft hammer feels shameful. But works. Tiny taps. Tap tap. Armour stays bright. Good. Enemy may stare. Then Master hits. Shine can help fight maybe. Fine. Giblet accepts shiny. Once.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/beetle_gem_armour · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:beetle_armor` (in-game name "Giving Netherite A Run For Its Money") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 105.10


:: Wings of Beetle [rambling] {"position":"2500,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Wing hinge first! Giblet checks!
LOG: Giblet checks wing hinge. Metal wings! Hinge holds. Good. Wing shell light. Too light for forge taste. But sky wants light. Stupid sky again. Master straps wings on. Giblet checks twice. Three times. Fourth too. No loose pins! Falling bad. Grubbison knows falls maybe. Giblet knows anvils. Anvil falls. Same idea. Sixth trusts metal. Not air. Master jumps. Wings catch. Hah! Metal flies again. Giblet still offended. Also proud. Wing-shape bellows maybe? No. Different job. Keep wings clean. Bent wing goes spin. Spin bad!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/wings_of_beetle · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:beetle_elytra` (in-game name "Why Not Have Both?") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ForMe02


:: An Iron Beetle [rambling] {"position":"2650,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Iron beetle! Good bug!
LOG: Iron beetle. Good bug! Giblet laughs. Hard shell. Metal shine. Good legs. Giblet crouches. Beetle clicks. Giblet clicks back. Beetle wins. Fine. Master has walking armour now. Maybe mount? Maybe worker. Maybe just bug. Still strong. Sixth taps shell. Beetle angry. Good spirit! No crack. Better spirit. Iron beetles squish less. This one understands. Metal saves. Giblet approves forge-sense creature. Feed what? Not coal maybe. Giblet not know. Do not feed hammer. Beetle tried bite. Hammer mine! Giblet grabs back. This spot mine! Bug can keep shell.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/an_iron_beetle · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:metal_beetle` (in-game name "Chrome Beetle") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.ThisSpotMine01


:: Passenger Seating [rambling] {"position":"2800,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Grubbison Jr
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: Sky seats, Master? Me too?!
LOG: More seats? On flying beast? Master, I can ride too? Maybe? I check straps and perch and where feet go, and none of it looks like tunnel! Sky got no walls. Bad design! Grubby deployed catapults on hills, big things exactly where Master needed. I can place passengers too, just smaller and much higher! Sit here, hold there, no looking down! I looked down. Bad choice! Wind steals breath, ground gets tiny, and I start missing dirt immediately! Still, travel fast! Very fast! Transport works! Sky still terrible. Next time, seat lower! Much lower!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/passenger_seating · fires on advancement `tameablebeasts:quetzal_stand` (in-game name "Public Transport") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 System_Quests Q32_TASK_04.DESC_DONE


:: You Saved a Village? Shameful. [rambling] {"position":"2950,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: You saved the village?! Sire, this is how rumours of goodness begin.
LOG: You saved the village?! Sire, really, people may start talking about goodness. Look at them cheering as though virtue happened deliberately under your supervision! How embarrassing, but gratitude can be spent almost as easily as gold, Master. Happy villagers lower their guard, open stores, gossip freely, and remember heroes fondly. That makes later disappointment much richer, my Lord. Accept the praise, but do not wave back like some smiling champion. A good reputation is merely camouflage with applause! Use it before somebody sensible notices where your Tower stands.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/you_saved_a_village_shameful · fires on advancement `minecraft:adventure/hero_of_the_village` (in-game name "Hero of the Village") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 1000.30


:: Captain Deposed [rambling] {"position":"3100,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Ha! One Captain fewer, one banner suddenly looking unemployed.
LOG: Ha, their Captain has been deposed! One loud banner less in the world... and one chain of command suddenly wobbling! Raiders adore hierarchy until the wrong person carries its symbol, Sire. Removing the Captain unsettles the whole arrangement beautifully. Let them argue about succession while you keep the useful trophies, Master. If another Captain rises, you already know the treatment. Titles are only armour for authority, my Lord, and armour comes off eventually! Keep the banner where everyone can see it! Humiliation travels farther when displayed by the victor.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/captain_deposed · fires on advancement `minecraft:adventure/voluntary_exile` (in-game name "Voluntary Exile") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 611.20


:: Raising the Anchor Again [rambling] {"position":"3250,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: No, Sire. You raised the Anchor again. Kill it again.
LOG: No, Sire... you raised the dragon again! The Anchor is back, and the wound can feel that mistake immediately. Bold curiosity, Master, but rather expensive curiosity! Kill it again before the old pressure settles comfortably into familiar habits. We already learned what that beast was holding open, my Lord. Repeating the lesson will not improve the answer or close anything faster! Still, I admire your willingness to test dangerous facts personally. Scholars use notes and cautious diagrams, while Overlords use resurrected dragons! Much more convincing, though considerably harder on the landscape.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/raising_the_anchor_again · fires on advancement `minecraft:end/respawn_dragon` (in-game name "The End... Again...") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D3_SD2_TheSewers 100.10


:: A Beacon for Evil [rambling] {"position":"3400,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Look at that light, Master! Even brightness knows who owns it.
LOG: Look at that light, Master! A beacon worthy of darker ownership at last. Lesser rulers build monuments so subjects can find them when lost. You build one so the horizon remembers who owns the land, Sire! Feed it power and let the beam announce dominion without tiring its voice. Brightness need not belong to goodness, whatever priests insist. That old mistake has survived far too long, my Lord. A shining symbol over an Evil realm is almost insulting. Excellent, even light behaves better when commanded from the Tower!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_beacon_for_evil · fires on advancement `minecraft:nether/create_full_beacon` (in-game name "Beaconator") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 End_Tower_Battle_Narrative 100.10


:: Summoning the Wither [rambling] {"position":"3550,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: You summoned the Wither. Excellent judgment, Master!
LOG: So, you summoned the Wither. Excellent judgment, Master! Nothing says confidence like creating a disaster on purpose and waiting nearby. The creature arrives angry, destructive, and completely unwilling to discuss borders or compensation. Very promising, so keep it away from anything expensive, Sire! Let it spend that fury somewhere replaceable before turning on you. If you can destroy what you called, even better, my Lord. Summoning proves nerve, while surviving proves authority! Ah, mayhem with an appointment is always classier than accidental catastrophe.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/summoning_the_wither · fires on advancement `minecraft:nether/summon_wither` (in-game name "Withering Heights") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_MAIN 201.20


:: A Ghast Abroad [rambling] {"position":"3700,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Ha! You made the Ghast travel before killing it.
LOG: Ha, you brought a Ghast somewhere it clearly dislikes! Listen to the miserable thing complain, Sire. Excellent work... and wonderfully unnecessary in exactly the right way! Creatures become confused when removed from familiar territory, Master, especially creatures accustomed to owning the sky. Keep it moving and do not stand beneath that enormous mouth. A displaced Ghast is still mostly teeth, tears, fire, and wounded dignity. The novelty changes none of that, my Lord! Still, dragging terror across a boundary just to kill it elsewhere has style! Some enemies deserve the inconvenience before the ending.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_ghast_abroad · fires on advancement `minecraft:nether/uneasy_alliance` (in-game name "Uneasy Alliance") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D5_MAIN 207.10


:: Un-Zombifying a Peasant [rambling] {"position":"3850,6650","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gnarl
EMOTION: Composed
POPUP: A generous act, Sire! Do try not to make a habit of it.
LOG: A generous act, Sire! You cured the poor peasant completely and left him inconveniently alive. How alarming, Master, though the technique is worth knowing because ruined flesh can sometimes be restored. That may matter again in circumstances far less wholesome than this one. Do not let the villagers call you kind, my Lord! Correct them before the rumour spreads through markets and family dinners. You saved one life because the knowledge was useful. That sounds much better! If gratitude becomes excessive, charge a fee and preserve your reputation properly, Master.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/un_zombifying_a_peasant · fires on advancement `minecraft:story/cure_zombie_villager` (in-game name "Zombie Doctor") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 D1_SD2_HalflingHomes 203.10


:: One Bolt, Five Bodies [rambling] {"position":"1000,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Hail, Impaler of the Impossible Five! One bolt handled a crowded problem.
LOG: Hail, Impaler of the Impossible Five! One bolt flew. Five bodies regretted standing in line. Splendid geometry! The Master found the straightest answer to a crowded problem. / One bolt crossed the field with a hard iron song / Five fools stood together and all stood there wrong! / It passed through the first and kept finding the rest / Five bodies discovered one shot at its best! Greetings, Sovereign of Singular Shots! I volunteer to stand nowhere behind anybody when that weapon rises. Spread out, Minions!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/one_bolt_five_bodies · fires on advancement `minecraft:adventure/arbalistic` (in-game name "Arbalistic") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.19


:: Every Monster Slain [rambling] {"position":"1150,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Each monster earned a line within the Master's fame / He hunted every kind until they knew his name!
LOG: From caverns to coastlands the monsters had gathered their fame / He hunted them all until every kind knew his name! / Great jaws, little claws, wings, venom, armour, and slime / Each monster eventually reached its unfortunate time! / I made a long list and the list made my poor wrist ache / His own list was shorter: just monsters left dead in his wake! / Hunters may boast of the trophies they gathered before / Our Lord has hunted the whole dreadful bestiary and more! / No monster remains unremembered in Quaver's grand lay / I hope that means none remain hungry and coming this way!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_monster_slain · fires on advancement `minecraft:adventure/kill_all_mobs` (in-game name "Monsters Hunted") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.16


:: Out-Shooting a Skeleton [rambling] {"position":"1300,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: The skeleton drew first across the empty ground / His answering shot arrived before another sound!
LOG: The skeleton stood far away with its bowstring pulled tight / He answered from distance and won the long fight! / Bone fingers drew arrows and measured the cold open ground / His answering shot crossed the distance before another sound! / I watched from behind something broad, thick, heavy, and tall / Distance feels safest when arrows are starting to fall! / Skeleton archers may pride themselves on patient old aim / He sends one shot back and ends their bony game! / The duel left one archer and one pile of bone / I prefer contests where minstrels are safely unknown!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/out_shooting_a_skeleton · fires on advancement `minecraft:adventure/sniper_duel` (in-game name "Sniper Duel") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.45


:: Two Phantoms, One Arrow [rambling] {"position":"1450,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Greetings, Divider of One Arrow Between Two Nightmares! Economical shooting.
LOG: Greetings, Divider of One Arrow Between Two Nightmares! Two phantoms flew. One shot answered. Both regretted sharing airspace! That is economy. That is aim. That is also why I never fly. Salutations, Splitter of Spectral Pairs! Wings folded. Membranes dropped. The sky became quieter by exactly two shrieks. Excellent. I considered a title involving birds, but those things are not birds and I value accuracy when terrified. retrieve the arrow if it survived! On second thought, wait until sunrise. No sense meeting cousins of the victims in darkness. Fanfare at dawn!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/two_phantoms_one_arrow · fires on advancement `minecraft:adventure/two_birds_one_arrow` (in-game name "Two Birds, One Arrow") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Titles ULTIMATE_STEEL.JES


:: Ghast, Return to Sender [rambling] {"position":"1600,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Quaver
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: The Ghast sent fire screaming down from high above / He sent it straight back with a harder kind of love!
LOG: A Ghast spat its fire with a shriek from the black Nether sky / He sent the same blazing complaint back on the fly! / Its own burning fury went racing straight back to its face / The creature discovered that distance was no hiding place! / I ducked at the first flaming ball and remained down below / The Master sent fire back upward with one perfect blow! / Ghasts may scream insults from heights where they think themselves strong / Their own fiery message came back with the answer all wrong! / The sender received what it sent with a thunderous roar / I favour all post that explodes somewhere else, not my door!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/ghast_return_to_sender · fires on advancement `minecraft:nether/return_to_sender` (in-game name "Return to Sender") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O2 Minstrel_Titles 200.9


:: Every Trim, Sire [rambling] {"position":"1750,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Many trims, Masta! Giblet sees good lines!
LOG: Giblet sees many trims. So many marks. Giblet lays plates out. Lines here. Teeth there. Ridges there. Fancy edges too. Master tried all. Good! Armour wears many mean looks. Giblet usually wants strong first. Still wants strong first! But strong can look proud. Sixth admits it. Quietly. Each trim needs clean hit. Crooked line shameful. Bad hammer mark worse. Giblet fixes. Tap. Turn. Tap. Check. Again. Good. Forge work can be pretty. Do not tell Quaver. He makes song. Giblet hates songs during counting. Master gets style. Giblet gets craft. Both win!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/every_trim_sire · fires on advancement `minecraft:adventure/trim_with_all_exclusive_armor_patterns` (in-game name "Smithing with Style") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 105.20


:: Clad in Netherite [rambling] {"position":"1900,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Giblet the Sixth
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Bring Netherite here! Giblet wants inspect!
LOG: Bring Netherite suit here! Now serious. Heavy. Dark. Strong! Giblet runs knuckle over plate. No give. Good. Master wears full set. Looks like walking forge door. Perfect! Sixth checks helm. Checks chest. Checks legs. Checks boots. All thick. All mean. Fire no hurt much. Blows no bite easy. This metal earned name. Giblet respects it. Not worship. Metal gets hit, not worship. Simple! Forge can still improve fit. Strap here. Pad there. Edge smooth. Then done. Maybe done. Giblet hates done. Done means no hammer. Hm. Add tiny dent. Family mark! Now done.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/clad_in_netherite · fires on advancement `minecraft:nether/netherite_armor` (in-game name "Cover Me in Debris") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · VOICE: O1 Tower_Forge 106.10


:: Ate Everything [rambling] {"position":"2050,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: EVERYTHING eaten! Good belly!
LOG: Everything eaten, every food tried, Masta belly got whole world inside! Meat, fruit, roots, sweets, fish, strange bits, all went down. I respect appetite, I also fear appetite, pantry looks nervous. I cook new spread, pan runs hot, sauce darkens round edge. Dark edge stay, give good bite, no need waste it. Masta never complain, good Masta, strong gut. List flavours aloud, LOSE COUNT HALFWAY! Too many tastes, too many plates, not enough shelves. Balanced diet sound dull, this was conquest by mouth. Next feast need BIGGER PANTRY, BIGGER STOVE, BIGGER KNIVES! Bigger cook? NO, I enough!
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/ate_everything · fires on advancement `minecraft:husbandry/balanced_diet` (in-game name "A Balanced Diet") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Tower_GeneralMessages 104.20


:: A Full Menagerie [rambling] {"position":"2200,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Pleased
POPUP: Whole yard breeding! Keep kitchen shut!
LOG: WHOLE MENAGERIE BREEDING! Every beast making more beasts, pantry thoughts arrive uninvited. Pets not supper, I know that, mostly know that. Masta gather pairs, pens fill, noises stack over noises. Moo, bleat, grunt, squeak, whole yard shouting together. Kitchen suffer nearby, animals still give useful things. Milk come, eggs come, wool maybe, meat only if rules change. I keep hands off, see, both hands here! One hen drop egg, now kitchen business starts. EGG FAIR, MILK FAIR, nobody argue with cook! Make breakfast from gifts, not guests, sounds almost nice. Ugh, add pepper, nice feeling gone.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_full_menagerie · fires on advancement `minecraft:husbandry/bred_all_animals` (in-game name "Two by Two") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.WeNeedMore02


:: A Netherite Hoe. Why? [rambling] {"position":"2350,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Gristle
EMOTION: Darkened
POPUP: NETHERITE? For dirt?!
LOG: Netherite hoe? WHY spend best metal digging dirt, Masta! I grab handle, feel weight, good metal wasted on weeds. Giblet probably crying sparks somewhere. Tool strong though, annoyingly strong. I swing once, soil opens easy, no bend, no chip. Hmph. Fields feed kitchen. Kitchen feeds Masta. So hoe maybe feeds kitchen sideways. I hate logic when works! Netherite belong blade, pot, cleaver, glorious pan. Hoe gets mud. MUD! I wipe edge fast, oil head, glare at field. Fine. Serious farm tool. Very serious. Anyone call it pretty, I throw turnip. Bring crops quickly, make waste worth dinner.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/a_netherite_hoe_why · fires on advancement `minecraft:husbandry/obtain_netherite_hoe` (in-game name "Serious Dedication") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Gristle wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_CantDamage


:: Dragon Breath, Bottled [rambling] {"position":"2500,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Relishing
POPUP: Ssso pretty... keep cork tight.
LOG: Dragon breath trapped... ssso pretty. Purple mist curls... bottle sweats cold. I hold far first... then closer. Closer wins. Master... cork smells burned glass. I sniff once... chest tickles. Sniff twice... bad choice. Small cough... only small. Mist sticks tongue? ...did not test. Yet. Bottle wants darkness... light makes swirl faster. I tap side... cloud snaps back. Lovely temper. No old tale needed, breath itself enough. Hot? Cold? Both maybe. My fingertips sting, nails look pink now. Fine. Keep stopper tight, very tight. If fog escapes. I leave room quietly.
CODER NOTES: overlord:ramblings/dragon_breath_bottled · fires on advancement `minecraft:end/dragon_breath` (in-game name "You Need a Mint") · no completion popup/entry · see ramblings doc · HOLD until Sit, Sire. Brood. (overlord:the_dark_tower/sit_sire_brood) is COMPLETED (Blister wakes with the room restorations) · if the advancement was earned before that, this Rambling fires on release as CATCH-UP: log entry + toast only, NO popup · VOICE: O1 Minion_-_General_Speech ignore.Minion_MagicImmune


:: Every Effect at Once [rambling] {"position":"2650,6800","size":"100,100"}
SPEAKER: Blister
EMOTION: Stricken
POPUP: Ssso many effects... hold still.
LOG: Too many effects... all at once... beautiful disaster. Master stands there... glowing, shaking, steaming maybe. Hard count. I start list... lose list. Speed in legs... heaviness in arms... hunger nowhere. Vision sharp... then blurry. I sniff air... taste three potions somehow. Mine ears ring... sympathy perhaps. Colours loud today... ssso loud. One effect fights another... little war under skin. I adore that. Safe? ,no. Interesting? ,very. I keep cure nearby, several cures actually. Which cure first? ,good question. Maybe wait. Sometimes mixtures solve themselves, sometimes explode quietly.
